window.KT_I18N=window.KT_I18N||{};window.KT_I18N["ms"]={"About | KungfuTutor":"Tentang | KungfuTutor","About KungfuTutor.com — interactive movement lessons for kung fu, martial arts, self-defence and sports.":"Tentang KungfuTutor.com — pelajaran pergerakan interaktif untuk kung fu, seni mempertahankan diri dan sukan.","Bow-stance punch":"Tumbukan lurus kuda-kuda busur","FRONT KNEE OVER TOES · BACK LEG STRAIGHT":"LUTUT DEPAN LURUS MELEPASI JARI KAKI · KAKI BELAKANG LURUS","Kung Fu":"Kung Fu","Fighting":"Seni Lawan","Self-Defence":"Pertahanan Diri","Sports":"Kemahiran Sukan","Fitness":"Kecergasan","Interactive movement lab":"Makmal pergerakan interaktif","See the movement. Understand the technique. Master the art.":"Lihat pergerakannya. Fahami tekniknya. Kuasai seninya.","Kung fu, fighting, self-defence and sports skills — every move shown as an animation you can slow down and step through, with clear explanations and common mistakes.":"Kung fu, seni lawan, pertahanan diri dan kemahiran sukan — setiap pergerakan ditunjukkan sebagai animasi yang boleh diperlahankan dan dilalui langkah demi langkah, dengan penerangan yang jelas serta kesilapan biasa.","Try the HYROX explainer →":"Cuba penerangan HYROX →","Bow-stance straight punch · Gong Bu Chong Quan":"Tumbukan lurus kuda-kuda busur · Gong Bu Chong Quan","Sports skills":"Kemahiran sukan","HYROX: 8 stations":"HYROX: 8 stesen","Animated demos, loads for every division, judging rules and training tips.":"Demonstrasi animasi, beban untuk setiap kategori, peraturan penilaian dan tip latihan.","Badminton smash":"Smash badminton","The full chain from backswing and trunk rotation to contact point.":"Rangkaian pergerakan lengkap dari ayunan belakang dan putaran badan ke titik sentuhan.","Golf swing":"Ayunan golf","Setup, backswing, downswing, impact and finish — plus driver, chip and putt.":"Kedudukan, ayunan naik, ayunan turun, hentaman dan penamat — serta driver, chip dan putt.","Traditional kung fu":"Kung fu tradisional","The five stances":"Lima kuda-kuda asas","Horse, bow, empty, drop and cross: front/side animation, foot map and stance timer.":"Kuda-kuda kuda, busur, kosong, jatuh dan silang: animasi depan/sisi, peta kedudukan kaki dan pemasa berdiri.","Basic punches & kicks":"Asas tumbukan & tendangan","Straight punch, palm strike, snap, heel, side and stretch kicks — step by step.":"Tumbukan lurus, tolakan tapak, tendangan snap, tendangan tumit, tendangan sisi dan tendangan regang — diuraikan langkah demi langkah.","Wing Chun basics":"Asas Wing Chun","Stance, vertical & chain punch, tan/bong/fuk/pak sao, with a centreline guide.":"Kuda-kuda, tumbukan menegak & berantai, tan/bong/fuk/pak sao, dengan panduan garis tengah.","Tai Chi 24-form":"Tai Chi 24 jurus","All 24 postures animated, with a breathing cue and play-the-whole-form mode.":"Semua 24 postur dianimasikan, dengan isyarat pernafasan dan mod main keseluruhan rangkaian.","Fighting skills":"Kemahiran lawan","Filipino martial arts":"Seni mempertahankan diri Filipina","MMA basics":"Asas MMA","Stance, striking, double-leg, sprawl, ground and pound and the technical stand-up.":"Kedudukan, pukulan, double-leg, sprawl, ground and pound, dan cara bangun yang selamat.","Lethwei basics":"Asas Lethwei","Bare knuckles, headbutt, rising elbow, flying knee and catch-and-sweep — the art of nine limbs.":"Tinju tanpa sarung, sundulan kepala, siku naik, lutut melayang, dan tangkap-kemudian-sapu — seni sembilan anggota.","Boxing basics":"Asas tinju 10 pelajaran","Jab, cross, hook, uppercut, slip, bob and weave, parry and footwork.":"Jab, cross, hook, uppercut, slip, bob and weave, parry dan kerja kaki.","Muay Thai basics":"Asas Muay Thai 10 teknik","Teep, roundhouse, low kick, elbow, clinch, knee and check — shown against an opponent.":"Teep, tendangan roundhouse, tendangan rendah, siku, clinch, lutut dan check kick — ditunjukkan terhadap lawan.","Roundhouse kick":"Tendangan sabit","Support-foot pivot and knee path.":"Pusingan kaki sokongan dan laluan lutut.","Self-defence":"Pertahanan diri","Krav Maga basics":"Asas Krav Maga","Defend and counter at once, front-choke release, non-stop counters — then get away.":"Pertahan dan balas serentak, lepaskan cengkaman leher dari depan, balasan tanpa henti — kemudian larikan diri.","Self-defence basics":"Asas pertahanan diri","The fence, keeping distance, palm heel, elbow, wrist-grab release and head cover — every move ends with getting away.":"Posisi siaga, menjaga jarak, tapak tangan, siku, melepaskan cengkaman pergelangan tangan dan melindungi kepala — setiap pergerakan berakhir dengan melarikan diri.","Falling safely":"Jatuh dengan selamat","Back and side breakfalls.":"Jatuh belakang dan sisi.","Fitness & mobility":"Kecergasan & mobiliti","10 essential gym exercises":"10 senaman gim penting","Squat, deadlift, bench, press, row, pull-up and more — with beginner versions and bar path.":"Squat, deadlift, bench press, overhead press, row, pull-up dan lain-lain — dengan versi pemula dan laluan bar.","Stretches for high kicks":"Regangan untuk tendangan tinggi","Safe hip and hamstring stretches.":"Regangan pinggul dan hamstring yang selamat.","Balance training":"Latihan keseimbangan","Weight-shift drills for every age.":"Latihan peralihan berat badan untuk setiap peringkat umur.","About":"Tentang","Privacy":"Privasi","Terms & Safety":"Terma & Keselamatan","Contact":"Hubungi","Content is for education only. Check your health before training and practise under a qualified instructor where possible.":"Kandungan ini hanya untuk tujuan pendidikan. Periksa kesihatan anda sebelum berlatih dan berlatihlah di bawah jurulatih yang layak jika boleh.","KungfuTutor — Interactive Kung Fu, Martial Arts & Sports Movement Lessons":"KungfuTutor — Pelajaran Interaktif Kung Fu, Seni Mempertahankan Diri & Gerakan Sukan","Learn kung fu, fighting, self-defence and sports skills from animated, interactive movement demos. Slow it down, step through it, and understand why it works.":"Pelajari kung fu, pertarungan, pertahanan diri dan kemahiran sukan melalui demonstrasi pergerakan beranimasi dan interaktif. Perlahankan, teliti setiap langkah, dan fahami mengapa ia berkesan.","Privacy Policy | KungfuTutor":"Dasar Privasi | KungfuTutor","How KungfuTutor.com handles data, cookies and advertising.":"Cara KungfuTutor.com mengendalikan data, kuki dan pengiklanan.","Terms & Safety | KungfuTutor":"Terma & Keselamatan | KungfuTutor","Terms of use and training safety notice for KungfuTutor.com.":"Terma penggunaan dan notis keselamatan latihan untuk KungfuTutor.com.","Clearest from the other view":"Paling jelas dilihat dari sudut pandangan lain","MASTERED":"DIKUASAI","✓ Marked as mastered":"✓ Ditandakan sebagai dikuasai","Mark as mastered":"Tandakan sebagai dikuasai","Progress is saved in your browser only":"Kemajuan hanya disimpan dalam pelayar anda"," — demo":"— demo","Your best hold: ":"Pegangan terbaik anda:","Finish a hold to record your best time":"Selesaikan satu pegangan untuk merekod masa terbaik anda","Stop":"Berhenti","Start hold":"Mula pegangan","Stance & Guard":"Kedudukan & Pertahanan","Foundation":"Asas","Side-on, chin down":"Badan menyerong, dagu ke bawah","Balance and defence":"Keseimbangan dan pertahanan","SIDE-ON · SOFT KNEES · GLOVES AT CHEEKS · CHIN DOWN":"MENYERONG · LUTUT LENTUR · SARUNG TANGAN DI PIPI · DAGU KE BAWAH","Right-handers stand left foot forward (orthodox), feet about shoulder-width, lead toes pointing forward and the back foot turned out about 45° with the heel slightly raised. Turn a little side-on to present a smaller target, knees soft, weight even. Keep the gloves by your cheeks, elbows in front of the ribs, chin tucked, eyes on the opponent over your gloves.":"Peninju tangan kanan berdiri dengan kaki kiri di hadapan (ortodoks), kaki lebih kurang selebar bahu, jari kaki hadapan menghala ke depan dan kaki belakang dipusingkan ke luar kira-kira 45° dengan tumit sedikit terangkat. Badan sedikit menyerong supaya sasaran lebih kecil, lutut lembut, berat badan sama rata. Letakkan sarung tangan di pipi, siku di hadapan rusuk, dagu ditarik ke dalam, dan pandang lawan di atas sarung tangan.","Feet on one line (no balance); chin up; elbows flared, exposing the body; locked knees.":"Kaki sebaris (hilang imbangan); dagu terangkat; siku terkembang, mendedahkan badan; lutut dikunci.","Hold your stance in a mirror and bounce lightly, 3 × 1 minute, checking chin and hands.":"Kekalkan kedudukan di hadapan cermin dan bergerak ringan, 3 × 1 minit, sambil periksa dagu dan tangan.","A good stance lets you attack, defend and move at the same time.":"Kedudukan yang baik membolehkan anda menyerang, bertahan dan bergerak serentak.","Jab":"Jab","Straight punch":"Tumbukan lurus","Face":"Muka","Fast out, fast back":"Cepat keluar, cepat tarik balik","Speed and range":"Kelajuan dan jarak","STRAIGHT OUT · TURN PALM-DOWN · SAME LINE BACK":"LURUS KELUAR · PUSINGKAN TAPAK KE BAWAH · KEMBALI SELARAS","From your stance, shoot the lead hand straight out, turning it palm-down just before impact, with the lead shoulder raised to protect the chin and the rear glove by your chin. Bring it back along the same line, fast. A small step with the lead foot adds reach.":"Dari kedudukan, lontarkan tangan hadapan lurus ke depan, pusingkan tapak ke bawah sebelum hentaman, dengan bahu hadapan dinaikkan untuk melindungi dagu dan sarung tangan belakang di sisi dagu. Tarik balik sepanjang garis yang sama dengan pantas. Langkah kecil dengan kaki hadapan menambah jangkauan.","Pulling back before punching (telegraphing); dropping the hand on the way back; flaring the elbow; leaning forward.":"Menarik ke belakang sebelum menumbuk (memberi isyarat); menurunkan tangan semasa menarik balik; siku terkembang; condong ke hadapan.","3 × 2-minute rounds of jabs only, in the air or on the bag — the return as fast as the punch.":"Hanya jab 3 pusingan × 2 minit, di udara atau pada beg. Tarik balik secepat tumbukan.","The jab finds range, distracts, breaks the opponent's rhythm and sets up every combination.":"Jab mencari jarak, mengalih perhatian, memecahkan irama lawan dan menyediakan setiap kombinasi.","Cross":"Cross","Chin, face":"Dagu, muka","Turn foot, hip, shoulder":"Pusing kaki, pinggul, bahu","Rotational power":"Kuasa putaran","PIVOT THE BACK HEEL · TURN THE HIPS · LEAD GLOVE ON THE CHIN":"PUSING TUMIT BELAKANG · PUSING PINGGUL · SARUNG DEPAN DI DAGU","From your stance, pivot the back heel out so the hips and shoulders turn forward, and drive the rear hand straight out — power travels from the floor through the hips to the fist. The lead glove stays by your chin; return along the same line.":"Dari kedudukan, pusingkan tumit belakang ke luar supaya pinggul dan bahu berpusing ke depan, dan hulurkan tangan belakang lurus. Kuasa mengalir dari lantai melalui pinggul ke penumbuk. Tangan depan kekal di dagu; tarik balik melalui laluan yang sama.","Arm-only punching; not turning the back heel; dropping the lead hand; leaving the weight out front.":"Hanya tumbukan dengan lengan; tumit belakang tidak dipusing; tangan depan jatuh; berat badan tertinggal di hadapan.","10 slow reps of pivot → hip → punch, then 3 rounds on the bag.":"10 ulangan perlahan pusing → pinggul → tumbukan, kemudian 3 pusingan pada beg.","The cross usually follows the jab and is the most common power punch.":"Cross biasanya mengikuti jab dan merupakan tumbukan kuat yang paling lazim.","Lead Hook":"Kait depan","Hook":"Kait","Side of the jaw":"Sisi rahang","Elbow level, turn the body":"Siku sama tinggi, pusing badan","Short-range rotation":"Putaran jarak dekat","ELBOW LEVEL WITH THE FIST · PIVOT · ARM AT ~90°":"SIKU SAMA TINGGI DENGAN PENUMBUK · PUSING · LENGAN ~90°","Shift a little weight to the lead foot, pivot on it and turn the hips and shoulders together. Bend the arm to about 90° with the elbow raised level with the fist and swing it across into the side of the jaw. The arm shape stays fixed — the power comes from turning. Return to the guard. (In this side view the fist travels across, into the screen.)":"Alihkan sedikit berat badan ke kaki depan, pusing di atasnya dan pusingkan pinggul serta bahu bersama. Bengkokkan lengan kira-kira 90° dengan siku diangkat sama tinggi dengan penumbuk, dan ayunkan melintang ke sisi rahang. Bentuk lengan kekal tetap; kuasa datang daripada pusingan. Kembali ke kedudukan pertahanan. (Dalam animasi sisi ini, penumbuk bergerak melintang ke dalam skrin.)","Winding up wide into a looping swing; dropping the elbow; arm-only with no body turn; the other hand leaving the chin.":"Menarik lengan terlalu luas menjadi ayunan melingkar; siku jatuh; hanya lengan tanpa pusingan badan; tangan satu lagi meninggalkan dagu.","Hooks on pads, 3 × 10, then add them after a jab and cross (1-2-3).":"Hook pada pads, 3 × 10, kemudian tambahkan selepas jab dan cross (1-2-3).","The hook comes from outside the opponent's line of sight and is a classic knockout punch.":"Hook datang dari luar garisan pandangan lawan dan merupakan pukulan knockout klasik.","Rear Uppercut":"Uppercut tangan belakang","Uppercut":"Uppercut","Under the chin":"Di bawah dagu","Dip, then drive up":"Rendahkan badan, kemudian tolak ke atas","Leg drive and rotation":"Tujahan kaki dan putaran","DIP THE KNEES · DRIVE AND TURN · FIST TRAVELS UP":"TUNDUKKAN LUTUT · TOLAK DAN PUSING · PENUMBUK NAIK KE ATAS","At close range, dip the knees and lower the rear hand slightly (don't pull it behind you), then drive up through the legs and turn the hips so the fist travels upward into the chin, palm facing you. Snap back to the guard.":"Pada jarak dekat, tekukkan lutut dan rendahkan sedikit tangan belakang (jangan tarik ke belakang), kemudian tolak ke atas melalui kaki dan pusingkan pinggul supaya penumbuk bergerak ke atas menuju dagu, telapak menghadap anda. Tarik balik ke posisi guard dengan pantas.","Dropping the hand low and back (telegraphing); lifting with the arm only; throwing from too far; leaving the face open afterwards.":"Menurunkan tangan terlalu rendah dan ke belakang (memberi isyarat); hanya mengangkat dengan lengan; membaling dari jarak terlalu jauh; membiarkan muka terbuka selepas itu.","On pads or an uppercut bag, 3 × 10, feeling the legs drive.":"Pada pads atau beg uppercut, 3 × 10, rasakan tujahan kaki.","Uppercuts punish an opponent who ducks or leans in, especially in close exchanges.":"Uppercut menghukum lawan yang menunduk atau condong ke depan, terutamanya dalam pertukaran jarak dekat.","The 1-2 (Jab–Cross)":"1-2 (Jab–Cross)","Combination":"Gabungan","Face, chin":"Muka, dagu","One returns as the other fires":"Satu tangan kembali ketika yang lain dilepaskan","Combination rhythm":"Irama gabungan","THE JAB OPENS · THE CROSS FIRES AS IT RETURNS":"JAB MEMBUKA · CROSS DILEPASKAN SEMASA JAB KEMBALI","Throw the jab, and as it comes back pivot the back foot and turn the hips to fire the cross. No pause between the two, and never have both hands away from your face at once. Finish with both hands back in the guard.":"Lepaskan jab, dan apabila ia kembali, pusingkan kaki belakang dan pusingkan pinggul untuk melepaskan cross. Jangan berhenti antara kedua-duanya, dan jangan sekali-kali biarkan kedua tangan jauh dari muka serentak. Akhiri dengan kedua tangan kembali ke guard.","Pausing between punches; firing the cross before the jab returns; not guarding afterwards; falling forward off balance.":"Berhenti antara tumbukan; melepaskan cross sebelum jab kembali; tidak mengawal selepas itu; jatuh ke depan hilang imbangan.","3 × 2-minute rounds in the air or on the bag, moving your feet after every 1-2.":"3 pusingan × 2 minit di udara atau pada beg, bergerak dengan kaki selepas setiap 1-2.","The 1-2 is the base of every combination; hooks and uppercuts follow from it.":"1-2 ialah asas setiap gabungan; hook dan uppercut mengikutinya.","Slip":"Slip (elak ke sisi)","Defence":"Pertahanan","Make the punch miss":"Buat tumbukan tersasar","Small move, use the knees":"Gerakan kecil, guna lutut","Reaction and timing":"Reaksi dan masa","BEND THE KNEES · HEAD OFF THE LINE · EYES ON THEM":"LENTURKAN LUTUT · KEPALA KELUAR DARI GARISAN · MATA PADA LAWAN","As a straight punch comes, bend the knees and shift the upper body slightly forward and to the side, moving your head off the punch's line so it slides over your shoulder. Keep it small, keep your eyes on them, and come straight back to stance or counter. (The side view can't show the sideways part — only the dip and lean.)":"Apabila tumbukan lurus datang, lenturkan lutut dan alihkan badan atas sedikit ke hadapan dan ke sisi, gerakkan kepala keluar dari garisan tumbukan supaya ia meluncur di atas bahu. Buat gerakan kecil, pandang lawan, dan terus kembali ke kedudukan atau balas. (Pandangan sisi tidak dapat menunjukkan bahagian sisi, hanya tunduk dan condong.)","Slipping too far and losing balance; closing your eyes; bending only at the waist; never countering.":"Mengelak terlalu jauh dan hilang imbangan; memejamkan mata; hanya membongkok di pinggang; tidak pernah membalas.","Slip along a rope line, 3 × 1 minute, then have a partner throw slow jabs.":"Latih mengelak ke kiri dan kanan di sepanjang tali, 3 × 1 minit, kemudian minta rakan melontarkan jab perlahan.","Slipping keeps both hands free to counter immediately.":"Mengelak membolehkan kedua-dua tangan kekal bebas untuk membalas serta-merta.","Bob & Weave":"Bob & Weave","Duck under the hook":"Tunduk di bawah cangkuk","Use the legs, not the waist":"Guna kaki, bukan pinggang","Leg strength and rhythm":"Kekuatan kaki dan irama","BEND THE KNEES · UNDER THE PUNCH · HANDS UP":"LENTURKAN LUTUT · MELALUI BAWAH TUMBUKAN · TANGAN NAIK","As a hook swings in, bend your knees and sink so your head passes under the punch, moving in a U shape and rising on the other side. Keep your back fairly straight, eyes on the opponent and hands up throughout.":"Apabila cangkuk datang mengayun, lenturkan lutut dan rendahkan badan supaya kepala melepasi bawah tumbukan, bergerak dalam bentuk U dan bangkit di sebelah lain. Kekalkan belakang agak tegak, pandang lawan, dan tangan sentiasa naik.","Bending at the waist and looking at the floor (blind, open to uppercuts); sinking so deep you can't come up; dropping the hands.":"Membongkok dan menunduk (tidak nampak lawan, mudah terkena uppercut); mencangkung terlalu dalam sehingga tidak boleh bangun; tangan jatuh.","Weave back and forth under a rope line, 3 × 1 minute.":"Bergerak ke kiri dan kanan di bawah tali yang diregangkan, 3 × 1 minit.","Bobbing and weaving takes you under hooks and into position to counter from the side.":"Tunduk dan mengelak membolehkan anda terlepas dari cangkuk dan berada dalam kedudukan untuk membalas dari sisi.","Parry":"Parry","Their glove":"Sarung tangan lawan","Small, fast, straight back":"Kecil, pantas, terus kembali","Reaction and hand control":"Reaksi dan kawalan tangan","SHORT TAP · DON'T REACH · BACK TO THE CHIN":"TEPUK PENDEK · JANGAN MENJULUR · TERUS KE DAGU","As the jab comes, tap it aside with the palm of your rear glove just in front of your face. Don't reach out to meet it — move only a short distance in front of the face — then snap the glove back to your chin and counter.":"Apabila jab datang, tepis ke sisi dengan tapak sarung tangan tangan belakang betul-betul di hadapan muka. Jangan hulurkan tangan untuk menyambutnya, bergerak hanya dalam jarak pendek di hadapan muka, kemudian tarik sarung tangan kembali ke dagu dan balas.","Reaching out for the punch (leaves an opening); too big a movement; not bringing the hand back; parrying without countering.":"Menghulurkan tangan untuk menyambut tumbukan (membuka ruang); gerakan terlalu besar; tidak menarik tangan balik; menangkis tanpa membalas.","Partner throws slow jabs while you parry, 3 × 1 minute; then add a counter cross after each parry.":"Rakan melontarkan jab perlahan semasa anda menangkis, 3 × 1 minit; kemudian tambah cross balas selepas setiap tangkisan.","Parrying neutralises straight punches without stepping back and creates instant counters.":"Menangkis meneutralkan tumbukan lurus tanpa berundur dan mewujudkan balasan serta-merta.","Footwork: Step & Drag":"Kerja kaki: Langkah & Seret","Footwork":"Kerja kaki","Control distance":"Kawal jarak","The foot nearest the direction moves first":"Kaki yang paling dekat dengan arah bergerak dahulu","Distance and balance":"Jarak dan keseimbangan","FORWARD: LEAD FOOT FIRST · BACK: REAR FOOT FIRST · SAME WIDTH":"MAJU: KAKI HADAPAN DAHULU · UNDUR: KAKI BELAKANG DAHULU · LEBAR SAMA","To move forward, step the lead foot a short distance and bring the rear foot up the same amount; to move back, step the rear foot first and let the lead foot follow. Every step keeps your stance width, soft knees and hands up — never cross or bring the feet together.":"Untuk bergerak ke hadapan, langkahkan kaki hadapan sedikit, dan bawa kaki belakang naik sejauh yang sama; untuk berundur, langkahkan kaki belakang dahulu dan biarkan kaki hadapan mengikuti. Setiap langkah mengekalkan lebar kedudukan, lutut lembut dan tangan di atas. Jangan silangkan atau rapatkan kaki.","Crossing or closing the feet; steps too big; bouncing up and down; dropping the hands as you move.":"Kaki bersilang atau rapat; langkah terlalu besar; badan melambung semasa bergerak; tangan jatuh.","Along a line on the floor, 10 steps forward and back, 3 sets; then add punches as you move.":"Di sepanjang garisan di lantai, maju dan undur masing-masing 10 langkah, 3 set; kemudian tambah tumbukan semasa bergerak.","Footwork controls distance — in range when you want to punch, out of range when you need to be.":"Kerja kaki mengawal jarak: berada dalam jangkauan apabila mahu menumbuk, di luar jangkauan apabila perlu mengelak.","Everything starts here":"Semuanya bermula di sini","Balance · protect the chin":"Keseimbangan · lindungi dagu","The most important punch in boxing":"Tumbukan paling penting dalam tinju","Measures distance, sets up":"Mengukur jarak, membuka laluan","The main power punch":"Tumbukan kuasa utama","Power comes from the ground":"Kuasa datang dari tanah","A short-range power punch":"Tumbukan berkuasa jarak dekat","The whole body turns":"Seluruh badan berpusing","An upward close-range punch":"Tumbukan ke atas jarak dekat","Power from the legs":"Kuasa dari kaki","Boxing's basic combination":"Gabungan asas tinju","Smooth rhythm":"Irama yang lancar","Defence without the hands":"Pertahanan tanpa tangan","Slip, then counter":"Elak, kemudian balas","The answer to a hook":"Jawapan kepada hook","A U-shaped path":"Laluan berbentuk U","Stops straight punches with minimal effort":"Menghalang tumbukan lurus dengan tenaga minimum","Redirect, don't block":"Alihkan, jangan sekat","The root of good boxing":"Asas tinju yang baik","Never cross the feet":"Jangan sekali-kali silangkan kaki","Stand side-on, feet about shoulder-width, knees soft, weight even":"Berdiri secara mengiring, kaki kira-kira selebar bahu, lutut lembut, berat badan sama rata","Gloves by the cheeks, elbows in front of the ribs":"Sarung tangan di sisi pipi, siku di hadapan rusuk","Chin down, eyes on the opponent over your gloves":"Dagu ditunduk, mata memandang lawan di atas sarung tangan","Stance":"Kedudukan","Snap the lead hand straight out, turning it palm-down":"Lontarkan tangan hadapan lurus, pusingkan telapak ke bawah","Bring it straight back to the face":"Tarik semula lurus ke muka","Turn the back heel, hips and shoulders and throw the rear hand straight":"Pusingkan tumit belakang, pinggul dan bahu, kemudian lontarkan tangan belakang lurus","Return — the lead glove guards the chin the whole time":"Kembali — sarung tangan hadapan sentiasa melindungi dagu","Stance, at close range":"Kedudukan, jarak dekat","Shift a little weight onto the lead foot":"Alihkan sedikit berat badan ke kaki hadapan","Pivot the lead foot and turn the hips; elbow up level with the fist, which swings across":"Pusingkan kaki hadapan dan pinggul; siku naik sama aras dengan penumbuk, yang diayun melintang","Back to the guard":"Kembali ke pertahanan","Dip the knees and drop the rear hand slightly":"Tekukkan lutut sedikit dan turunkan tangan belakang sedikit","Drive up through the legs, turn the hips and bring the fist up under the chin":"Tolak ke atas melalui kaki, pusingkan pinggul dan naikkan penumbuk ke bawah dagu","\"One\": the jab":"\"Satu\": jab","\"Two\": the cross fires as the jab comes back":"\"Dua\": kros dilontarkan ketika jab ditarik balik","Both hands back to the guard":"Kedua-dua tangan kembali ke pertahanan","Stance; watch their shoulders":"Kedudukan; perhatikan bahu lawan","They throw a jab":"Mereka melontarkan jab","Bend the knees and shift forward and to the side so the punch slides over your shoulder":"Tekukkan lutut dan alihkan badan ke hadapan dan ke sisi supaya tumbukan meluncur melepasi bahu","Keep your eyes on them":"Terus pandang mereka","Back to stance, ready to counter":"Kembali ke kedudukan, bersedia membalas","They swing a hook":"Mereka mengayunkan hook","Bend the knees and drop under the punch — legs, not the waist":"Tekukkan lutut dan turun di bawah tumbukan — gunakan kaki, bukan pinggang","Move in a U shape and come up on the other side":"Bergerak dalam bentuk U dan bangun di sisi yang satu lagi","Back to stance; the hands stay up throughout":"Kembali ke kedudukan; tangan kekal di atas sepanjang masa","A short tap forward with the rear glove knocks the jab off line":"Tepukan pendek ke hadapan dengan sarung tangan belakang menolak jab dari laluannya","The glove snaps straight back to the chin":"Sarung tangan segera kembali ke dagu","Counter straight after the parry":"Balas dengan tumbukan lurus selepas menangkis","Advance: the lead foot steps first, a small step":"Maju: kaki hadapan melangkah dahulu, langkah kecil","The rear foot follows the same distance — stance width stays the same":"Kaki belakang mengikut dengan jarak yang sama — lebar kedudukan kekal","Retreat: the rear foot steps back first":"Undur: kaki belakang melangkah ke belakang dahulu","The lead foot follows — never cross the feet":"Kaki hadapan mengikut — jangan sekali-kali menyilang kaki","TARGET: ":"SASARAN:","Balance":"Keseimbangan","Relaxation":"Relaksasi","Speed":"Kelajuan","Range":"Jarak jangkau","Shoulder endurance":"Daya tahan bahu","Rotation":"Putaran","Pivot":"Pusingan kaki","Shoulder & arm":"Bahu & lengan","Arm structure":"Struktur lengan","Lead-foot pivot":"Pusingan kaki hadapan","Leg drive":"Dorongan kaki","Close range":"Jarak dekat","Timing":"Waktu yang tepat","Rhythm":"Irama","Reaction":"Reaksi","Legs":"Kaki","Leg strength":"Kekuatan kaki","Hand control":"Kawalan tangan","Distance control":"Kawalan jarak","Leg endurance":"Daya tahan kaki","Current speed: ":"Kelajuan semasa:","Learning (slow motion)":"Pembelajaran (gerakan perlahan)","Fight speed":"Kelajuan pertarungan","Lesson {n} of 10 · {type}":"Pelajaran {n} daripada 10 · {type}","Punch numbers":"Nombor tumbukan","Coaches call combinations by number: 1 jab, 2 cross, 3 lead hook, 4 rear hook, 5 lead uppercut, 6 rear uppercut. \"1-2-3\" means jab, cross, lead hook. Some gyms number them slightly differently.":"Jurulatih biasanya menyebut gabungan dengan nombor: 1 jab, 2 cross, 3 hook depan, 4 hook belakang, 5 uppercut depan, 6 uppercut belakang. \"1-2-3\" bermaksud jab, cross, kemudian hook depan. Sesetengah gim menomborkannya sedikit berbeza.","The ten lessons at a glance":"Sepuluh pelajaran sepintas lalu","Lesson":"Pelajaran","Type":"Jenis","Target":"Sasaran","Key point":"Perkara utama","A beginner session":"Sesi untuk pemula","Skip rope for 3 × 3-minute rounds to warm up.":"Lompat tali 3 pusingan × 3 minit untuk memanaskan badan.","Shadowbox for 2 rounds, focusing on stance, footwork and returning the hands.":"Shadowbox 2 pusingan, fokus pada kedudukan, kerja kaki dan menarik tangan kembali.","Heavy bag for 3 rounds: jabs, 1-2s and 1-2-3s.":"Beg berat 3 pusingan: jab, 1-2 dan 1-2-3.","Defence: 1 minute each of slips and bob-and-weaves.":"Pertahanan: masing-masing 1 minit slip dan bob-and-weave.","Finish with core work and stretching.":"Tamatkan dengan latihan teras dan regangan.","Gear and safety":"Peralatan dan keselamatan","Always wrap your hands and wear gloves on the bag to protect wrists and knuckles; add a mouthguard and headgear to spar, and only spar under a coach's supervision. Stop and see a doctor after any blow to the head that leaves you dizzy, with a headache or nauseous.":"Sentiasa balut tangan dan pakai sarung tangan semasa memukul beg untuk melindungi pergelangan dan buku jari; pakai pelindung gigi dan topi keledar semasa sparring, dan hanya sparring di bawah pengawasan jurulatih. Berhenti dan dapatkan rawatan doktor selepas sebarang pukulan di kepala yang menyebabkan pening, sakit kepala atau loya.","Want kicks, knees and elbows too? See <a href=\"../muay-thai/\">Muay Thai basics</a>.":"Mahu tendangan, lutut dan siku juga? Lihat <a href=\"../muay-thai/\">Asas Muay Thai</a>.","Frequently asked questions":"Soalan lazim","What does \"1-2\" mean?":"Apakah maksud \"1-2\"?","A jab followed by a cross — boxing's basic combination.":"Jab diikuti cross, gabungan asas dalam tinju.","Slip or bob and weave — what's the difference?":"Slip atau bob and weave, apakah bezanya?","A slip moves the head slightly sideways to beat a straight punch; a bob and weave bends the knees to duck under a hook in a U shape.":"Slip menggerakkan kepala sedikit ke sisi untuk mengelak tumbukan lurus; bob and weave membengkokkan lutut untuk menunduk di bawah cangkuk dalam bentuk U.","Can I practise without a partner?":"Bolehkah saya berlatih tanpa pasangan?","Yes — shadowboxing, the heavy bag and skipping are all solo, and you can practise bobbing under a rope. Sparring needs a coach and partner.":"Boleh. Shadowboxing, beg berat dan lompat tali boleh dibuat seorang diri, dan anda boleh berlatih menunduk di bawah tali. Sparring memerlukan jurulatih dan pasangan.","Boxing":"Tinju","FIGHTING SPORTS · BOXING FOR BEGINNERS":"SUKAN PERTAHANAN DIRI · TINJU UNTUK PEMULA","Boxing Basics: Punches, Defence & Footwork in 10 Lessons":"Asas Tinju: Tumbukan, Pertahanan & Pergerakan Kaki dalam 10 Pelajaran","Start with the stance, then learn the four basic punches, the first combination, three ways to defend — slip, bob and weave, parry — and how to step in and out. The grey figure is the opponent and the red ring shows where a punch lands; lefties press SOUTHPAW.":"Mulakan dengan kedudukan, kemudian pelajari empat tumbukan asas, gabungan pertama, tiga cara mempertahankan diri (slip, bob and weave, parry), dan cara melangkah masuk dan keluar. Figura kelabu ialah lawan dan bulatan merah menunjukkan tempat tumbukan mendarat; pemain kidal tekan SOUTHPAW.","Lead hook":"Cangkuk depan","Rear hook":"Cangkuk belakang","Lead uppercut":"Uppercut depan","Rear uppercut":"Uppercut belakang","Basic punches":"Tumbukan asas","Jab · cross · hook · uppercut":"Jab · cross · hook · uppercut","Key point, this lesson":"Perkara utama pelajaran ini","Amateur bout":"Format perlawanan amatur","3 rounds × 3 minutes (varies by category)":"3 pusingan × 3 minit (berbeza mengikut kategori)","Lessons you have mastered":"Pelajaran yang telah anda kuasai","Mark each lesson as mastered below":"Tandakan setiap pelajaran sebagai telah dikuasai di bawah","Choose the speed (the animation updates instantly)":"Pilih kelajuan (animasi dikemas kini serta-merta)","Learning · slow motion":"Pembelajaran · gerakan perlahan","Reset mastered marks":"Tetapkan semula tanda yang telah dikuasai","Pick a lesson (best learned in order)":"Pilih pelajaran (paling baik dipelajari mengikut urutan)","Click a card or use the ← / → keys":"Klik kad atau gunakan kekunci ← / →","What it builds":"Apa yang dibina","How to do it":"Cara melakukannya","Common mistakes":"Kesilapan biasa","Drill":"Latihan","In the ring":"Di gelanggang","SIDE · GREY = OPPONENT":"SISI · KELABU = LAWAN","ORTHODOX":"ORTODOKS","SOUTHPAW":"KIDAL","NEXT STEP ▸":"LANGKAH SETERUSNYA ▸","What this lesson trains":"Apa yang dilatih dalam pelajaran ini","Relative importance":"Kepentingan relatif","For education only; the animations are simplified. Boxing is a contact sport: train under a qualified coach, wrap your hands and wear gloves on the bag, and wear a mouthguard and headgear to spar.":"Untuk tujuan pendidikan sahaja; animasi dipermudah. Tinju ialah sukan sentuhan: berlatihlah di bawah bimbingan jurulatih yang berkelayakan, balut tangan dan pakai sarung tangan semasa memukul beg, serta pakai pelindung gigi dan topi keselamatan semasa sparring.","Boxing Basics: Stance, Jab, Cross, Hook, Uppercut & Defence — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"Asas Tinju: Kedudukan, Jab, Cross, Hook, Uppercut & Pertahanan — Panduan Interaktif | KungfuTutor","Learn 10 boxing fundamentals with animated demos against an opponent: stance and guard, jab, cross, lead hook, rear uppercut, the 1-2, slip, bob and weave, parry and footwork — with mistakes and drills.":"Pelajari 10 asas tinju dengan demonstrasi animasi menentang lawan: kedudukan dan kawalan, jab, cross, lead hook, rear uppercut, 1-2, slip, bob and weave, parry dan footwork — dengan kesilapan dan latihan.","Boxing Basics — Punches, Defence & Footwork, Step by Step":"Asas Tinju — Pukulan, Pertahanan & Footwork, Langkah demi Langkah","What are the basic punches in boxing?":"Apakah pukulan asas dalam tinju?","The jab, the cross, the hook and the uppercut. Coaches often number them: 1 jab, 2 cross, 3 lead hook, 4 rear hook, 5 lead uppercut, 6 rear uppercut.":"Jab, cross, hook dan uppercut. Jurulatih selalunya memberi nombor: 1 jab, 2 cross, 3 lead hook, 4 rear hook, 5 lead uppercut, 6 rear uppercut.","What does 1-2 mean in boxing?":"Apakah maksud 1-2 dalam tinju?","A jab followed immediately by a cross — the most basic boxing combination.":"Jab yang diikuti serta-merta dengan cross — gabungan tinju yang paling asas.","What is the difference between a slip and a bob and weave?":"Apakah perbezaan antara slip dan bob and weave?","A slip moves the head a little to the side to make a straight punch miss; a bob and weave bends the knees to duck under a hook in a U-shaped path.":"Slip menggerakkan kepala sedikit ke sisi untuk menjadikan tumbukan lurus tersasar; bob and weave membengkokkan lutut untuk mengelak di bawah hook dalam laluan berbentuk U.","Stance & Grip":"Kedudukan & Pegangan","Single stick":"Tongkat tunggal","Control and balance":"Kawalan dan keseimbangan","BUTT SHOWING · FIRM, NOT TENSE · LIVE HAND UP":"HUJUNG PEGANGAN NAMPAK · KUAT, TIDAK TEGANG · TANGAN HIDUP NAIK","Hold the stick in a full grip with two or three finger-widths of the butt (punyo) showing below your little finger — it is used for close strikes and hooking. Grip firmly but not rigidly so the wrist can turn freely. Keep the weapon hand in front with the stick up; the other hand, the \"live hand\", stays by your chest ready to check, push or grab. Stand with feet staggered and knees soft.":"Pegang tongkat dengan genggaman penuh, dengan dua atau tiga lebar jari hujung pegangan (punyo) kelihatan di bawah jari kelingking anda — ia digunakan untuk serangan jarak dekat dan kait. Genggam kukuh tetapi tidak kaku supaya pergelangan tangan boleh berpusing dengan bebas. Letakkan tangan senjata di hadapan dengan tongkat tegak; tangan satu lagi, \"tangan hidup\", kekal di dada anda, sedia untuk memeriksa, menolak atau mencengkam. Berdiri dengan kaki bersilang selang-seli dan lutut lembut.","Holding the very end (poor control, easy to knock away); gripping so hard the wrist locks; letting the live hand hang; standing too upright.":"Memegang hujung paling akhir (kawalan lemah, mudah dipukul jatuh); menggenggam terlalu kuat sehingga pergelangan terkunci; membiarkan tangan hidup terjuntai; berdiri terlalu tegak.","Hold the ready stance with the stick and move forward and back for a minute, checking the butt and the live hand.":"Kekalkan kedudukan sedia dengan tongkat dan bergerak ke depan dan ke belakang selama 1 minit, sambil memeriksa hujung pegangan dan tangan hidup.","FMA usually teaches the weapon first; a correct grip and an active live hand underpin everything else.":"FMA biasanya mengajar senjata dahulu; pegangan yang betul dan tangan hidup yang aktif menjadi asas kepada semua yang lain.","Forehand Diagonal Strike":"Pukulan Serong Forehand","Strike":"Serangan","Upper part of the stick":"Bahagian atas tongkat","Hip turn and wrist":"Pusingan pinggul dan pergelangan tangan","COCK OVER THE SHOULDER · DIAGONAL DOWN · FOLLOW THROUGH":"SENGET DI ATAS BAHU · SERONG KE BAWAH · TERUSKAN HINGGA TEMBUS","Cock the stick over the shoulder on your weapon side, then turn the hips so the body drives the arm and the stick travels down a diagonal to the side of the head or the collarbone, following through past the opposite hip instead of stopping on the target. The live hand stays by your chest. Many systems call this line \"angle 1\", though the numbering varies between styles.":"Angkat kayu ke atas bahu di sebelah senjata, kemudian pusingkan pinggul supaya badan menggerakkan lengan dan kayu bergerak menyerong ke sisi kepala atau tulang kolar, teruskan sehingga melepasi pinggul bertentangan dan jangan berhenti pada sasaran. Tangan aktif kekal di dada. Banyak sistem memanggil garisan ini \"sudut 1\", walaupun penomboran berbeza antara gaya.","Arm only, no hip turn; stopping on the target (weak, easy to grab); dropping the live hand; a big telegraphed loop behind you.":"Hanya lengan, tanpa pusingan pinggul; berhenti pada sasaran (lemah, mudah dipegang); tangan aktif jatuh; gelung besar di belakang yang memberi isyarat.","20 slow strikes on a tyre or striking post, then speed up; train both hands.":"20 pukulan perlahan pada tayar atau tiang tumbukan, kemudian laju; latih kedua-dua tangan.","The forehand diagonal is the most natural, powerful line, and almost every FMA style starts with it.":"Pukulan serong forehand ialah garisan yang paling semula jadi dan kuat, dan hampir setiap gaya FMA bermula dengannya.","Backhand Diagonal Strike":"Pukulan Serong Backhand","Turning back the other way":"Berpusing semula ke arah bertentangan","TO THE OTHER SHOULDER · BACK OF HAND OUT · TURN BACK THROUGH":"KE BAHU SEBELAH · BELAKANG TANGAN KE LUAR · PUSING BALIK MENEMBUS","Bring the stick across to your opposite shoulder with the back of the hand facing out, then turn the body back so the stick travels down the opposite diagonal to the other side of the head, following through to your weapon side. Forehand and backhand are usually thrown together. (In the side view the two diagonals look alike — the difference is which shoulder they start from.)":"Bawa kayu ke bahu bertentangan dengan belakang tangan menghadap ke luar, kemudian pusingkan badan kembali supaya kayu bergerak menyerong berlawanan ke sisi kepala yang satu lagi, dan teruskan ke sebelah senjata. Forehand dan backhand biasanya dilakukan bersama. (Dalam pandangan sisi, kedua serong kelihatan serupa; bezanya ialah bahu mana ia bermula.)","Lifting the elbow too high in a big wind-up; flicking from the wrist only; no body turn; the live hand getting in the way.":"Mengangkat siku terlalu tinggi dalam ayunan besar; hanya mengibas dari pergelangan tangan; tiada pusingan badan; tangan aktif menghalang laluan sendiri.","Forehand + backhand pairs, 20 per set, 3 sets.":"Pasangan forehand + backhand, 20 setiap set, 3 set.","Paired with the forehand, it lets you strike from both sides without a gap.":"Digandingkan dengan pukulan forehand, ia membolehkan anda menyerang dari kedua-dua belah tanpa ruang kosong.","Thrust to the Body":"Tusukan ke Badan","Thrust":"Tusukan","Stick tip":"Hujung kayu","Range and speed":"Jarak dan kelajuan","DRAW TO THE HIP · STEP IN · STRAIGHT LINE":"TARIK KE PINGGANG · MELANGKAH MASUK · GARIS LURUS","Draw the stick back to your hip with the tip forward, then step in with the lead foot and extend the arm so the tip drives straight into the stomach, and recover to the ready stance. The thrust takes the shortest path and is often used to interrupt the opponent.":"Tarik kayu ke pinggang dengan hujung menghala ke depan, kemudian melangkah masuk dengan kaki hadapan dan lanjutkan lengan supaya hujung kayu menusuk lurus ke perut, dan kembali ke kedudukan sedia. Tusukan mengambil laluan terpendek dan sering digunakan untuk mengganggu lawan.","The tip wobbling up and down; reaching without stepping; leaving the stick out where it can be grabbed.":"Hujung kayu bergoyang naik turun; menghulur tangan tanpa melangkah; membiarkan kayu terkeluar di hadapan supaya boleh dirampas.","Thrust at a hanging ball or soft target, 3 × 10, hitting the same spot every time.":"Tusuk bola tenis yang digantung atau sasaran lembut, 3 × 10, mengenai titik yang sama setiap kali.","In FMA the thrust also underpins blade work; it trains a straight line and distance.":"Dalam FMA, tusukan juga menjadi asas kerja bilah; ia melatih garisan lurus dan rasa jarak.","Figure-8 Flow":"Aliran Angka 8","Flow drill":"Latihan aliran","Flow and wrist":"Kelancaran dan pergelangan tangan","FOREHAND → ROLL THE WRIST → BACKHAND → NON-STOP":"FOREHAND → PUSING PERGELANGAN → BACKHAND → TANPA HENTI","Throw a forehand diagonal, roll the wrist as you follow through so the stick loops up to the other shoulder, throw a backhand diagonal, then roll back again — the two diagonals cross in front of you in a figure 8 that never stops. Start slowly and speed up as it becomes smooth.":"Libas serong dengan forehand, pusingkan pergelangan semasa mengikut hayunan supaya kayu berputar naik ke bahu sebelah lain, libas serong dengan backhand, kemudian pusing semula. Kedua-dua serong bersilang di hadapan badan membentuk angka 8 yang tidak henti. Mula perlahan dan laju apabila sudah lancar.","Pausing between strikes; drawing big circles with the arm instead of the wrist; a stiff body; watching the stick instead of looking ahead.":"Berhenti di antara pukulan; membuat bulatan besar dengan lengan, bukan pergelangan; badan kaku; memandang kayu, bukan ke hadapan.","3 × 1 minute a day, alternating hands, adding steps forward and back.":"3 × 1 minit sehari, bergilir antara kedua-dua tangan, sambil menambah langkah ke depan dan ke belakang.","Flow drills make your attacks continuous and lead into the double-stick weaving drills (sinawali).":"Latihan aliran menjadikan serangan berterusan dan menjadi asas latihan anyaman dua kayu (Sinawali) dalam FMA.","Roof Block & Counter":"Tangkisan Bumbung & Serangan Balas","Defend + counter":"Pertahanan + balasan","The sloping stick":"Permukaan condong kayu","Timing and flow":"Masa dan Aliran","HAND OVERHEAD · TIP SLOPES DOWN AND BACK · FLOW INTO THE COUNTER":"TANGAN DI ATAS KEPALA · HUJUNG TONGKAT CONDONG KE BAWAH DAN KE BELAKANG · MENGALIR KE SERANGAN BALAS","As a strike comes down from above, raise your weapon hand above your head with the tip sloping down and back, like a roof, so their stick slides off along yours instead of meeting it head-on. Let the stick flow on round to your shoulder and counter at once with a forehand.":"Apabila serangan turun dari atas, angkat tangan pemegang senjata ke atas kepala dengan hujung tongkat condong ke bawah dan ke belakang, seperti bumbung, supaya tongkat lawan meluncur sepanjang tongkat anda dan tidak bertembung terus. Biarkan tongkat mengalir ke bahu dan balas serta-merta dengan forehand.","Blocking flat and square (jars the hand and can break the stick); not raising the hand high enough; stopping after the block.":"Menangkis mendatar dan tegak lurus (menggegarkan tangan dan boleh mematahkan tongkat); tidak mengangkat tangan cukup tinggi; berhenti selepas menangkis.","Partner strikes slowly from above while you roof-block and counter, sets of 10 — with protective gear and slow speed.":"Pasangan menyerang perlahan dari atas manakala anda menangkis bumbung dan membalas, set 10 kali — dengan peralatan pelindung dan kelajuan perlahan.","The roof block turns defence and attack into one flowing move — a good example of FMA's \"the block is the strike\" idea.":"Tangkisan bumbung menggabungkan pertahanan dan serangan menjadi satu gerakan yang mengalir — contoh yang baik bagi idea FMA «tangkisan ialah serangan».","Live-Hand Check & Disarm":"Semakan Tangan Hidup & Pelucutan","Control":"Kawalan","Live hand on their weapon hand":"Tangan hidup pada tangan senjata lawan","Control and coordination":"Kawalan dan koordinasi","BLOCK · CHECK WITH THE LIVE HAND · STRIP DOWN · GET DISTANCE":"TANGKIS · PERIKSA DENGAN TANGAN HIDUP · LUCUTKAN KE BAWAH · WUJUDKAN JARAK","Block their strike with your stick, then immediately pin their weapon hand or wrist with your live hand (the \"check\") so they cannot pull back for another strike. Use your stick to strip theirs downward out of their hand, then step back to a safe distance. It is one of the most basic disarms — always practise it slowly and with protective gear.":"Tangkis serangan lawan dengan tongkat anda, kemudian segera tekan tangan atau pergelangan tangan pemegang senjata dengan tangan hidup anda («semakan») supaya mereka tidak dapat menarik balik untuk serangan seterusnya. Gunakan tongkat anda untuk melucutkan tongkat mereka ke bawah daripada tangan mereka, kemudian undur ke jarak selamat. Ini antara pelucutan paling asas — sentiasa latih dengan perlahan dan memakai peralatan pelindung.","Remembering the live hand only after the block (too slow); grabbing their stick instead of their hand (easily pulled away — and a blade would cut); staying close after the disarm.":"Baru teringat tangan hidup selepas menangkis (terlalu perlahan); mencengkam tongkat mereka dan bukan tangan (mudah ditarik lepas — dan jika bilah, akan terluka); kekal rapat selepas pelucutan.","Partner strikes very slowly while you block → check → strip, 10 reps; speed up only once it is smooth.":"Rakan memukul dengan sangat perlahan semasa anda menangkis → menyemak → melucutkan, 10 kali; tingkatkan kelajuan hanya apabila lancar.","The live hand is a hallmark of FMA: the weapon hand attacks and defends, the live hand controls.":"Tangan hidup ialah ciri khas FMA: tangan senjata menyerang dan mempertahankan, tangan hidup mengawal.","Empty-Hand Application":"Aplikasi Tangan Kosong","Empty hand":"Tangan kosong","Bottom of the fist or the palm":"Bahagian bawah penumbuk atau telapak tangan","Transfer and understanding":"Pemindahan dan pemahaman","SAME DIAGONAL · HAMMER FIST OR PALM · LIVE HAND STILL WORKS":"PEPENJURU SAMA · TUMBUKAN PALU ATAU TELAPAK · TANGAN HIDUP TETAP BERFUNGSI","A hallmark of FMA is that weapon and empty hand use the same angles and movements. Put the stick down and the forehand diagonal becomes a downward hammer fist or slashing palm, the backhand becomes a backhand slap or elbow, and the live-hand check works just the same. Train the stick well and your empty-hand skills improve at the same time.":"Ciri khas FMA ialah senjata dan tangan kosong menggunakan sudut dan pergerakan yang sama. Apabila tongkat diletakkan, pepenjuru forehand menjadi tumbukan palu ke bawah atau tetakan telapak, pepenjuru backhand menjadi tamparan backhand atau siku, dan semakan tangan hidup berfungsi sama. Latih tongkat dengan baik, kemahiran tangan kosong anda turut meningkat.","Thinking empty hand is a separate system; hitting with the knuckles instead of the bottom of the fist; forgetting the live hand.":"Menganggap tangan kosong ialah sistem berasingan; memukul dengan buku jari dan bukannya bahagian bawah penumbuk; melupakan tangan hidup.","Do a drill 10 times with the stick, then 10 times empty-handed, feeling that the movement is identical.":"Buat latihan 10 kali dengan tongkat, kemudian 10 kali dengan tangan kosong, dan rasakan bahawa pergerakannya sama.","This \"one set of angles, many tools\" principle is what makes FMA such a practical self-defence system.":"Prinsip \"satu set sudut, banyak alat\" inilah yang menjadikan FMA sistem pertahanan diri yang sangat praktikal.","Leave a little butt showing":"Biarkan sedikit hujung pangkal kelihatan","The live hand is always working":"Tangan hidup sentiasa berfungsi","Angle 1 in many systems":"Sudut 1 dalam banyak sistem","High to low on a diagonal":"Dari atas ke bawah secara pepenjuru","Angle 2 in many systems":"Sudut 2 dalam banyak sistem","The mirror of the forehand":"Pantulan forehand","The fastest, straightest attack":"Serangan paling pantas dan paling lurus","Step with it":"Melangkah bersama-sama dengannya","Forehand and backhand joined up":"Forehand dan backhand bersambung dalam satu garisan","The key to a loose wrist":"Kunci pergelangan tangan yang lentur","Let their stick slide off":"Biarkan tongkat lawan tergelincir","Counter straight after":"Balas serta-merta selepas itu","Block → check → strip":"Tangkis → semak → lucut","What the live hand is for":"Tujuan sebenar tangan hidup","Weapon and hand share the same angles":"Senjata dan tangan kosong berkongsi sudut yang sama","A core FMA idea":"Idea teras FMA","Grip the stick with two or three finger-widths of butt showing below the hand":"Pegang kayu dengan 2 atau 3 lebar jari pangkal kelihatan di bawah tangan","Weapon hand forward with the stick up; the other, \"live\" hand guards the chest":"Tangan senjata di hadapan dengan kayu tegak; tangan satu lagi, tangan “hidup”, melindungi dada","Feet staggered, knees soft, weight even":"Kaki berselang-seli, lutut lembut, berat badan sama rata","Ready stance":"Kedudukan sedia","Cock the stick over the shoulder on the weapon side":"Angkat kayu ke atas bahu di sebelah tangan senjata","Turn the hips and swing down on a diagonal to the side of the head":"Pusingkan pinggul dan ayun kayu turun secara serong ke sisi kepala lawan","Follow through past the opposite hip — don't stop on the target":"Teruskan ayunan melepasi pinggul sebelah bertentangan, jangan berhenti pada sasaran","Recover to the ready stance":"Kembali ke kedudukan sedia","Bring the stick across to the opposite shoulder, back of the hand facing out":"Bawa kayu ke bahu sebelah bertentangan, belakang tangan menghadap ke luar","Swing back down on the opposite diagonal, the body turning back with it":"Ayun semula turun secara serong berlawanan, badan turut berpusing balik","Follow through and finish on the weapon side":"Teruskan ayunan dan berakhir di sebelah tangan senjata","Draw the stick back to the hip, tip pointing forward":"Tarik kayu ke pinggang, hujung kayu menghala ke hadapan","Step in and drive the tip straight into the stomach, arm extending":"Melangkah ke depan dan tusukkan hujung kayu lurus ke perut, lengan dilanjutkan","Back to the ready stance":"Kembali ke kedudukan sedia","Forehand: from the shoulder, diagonally down":"Forehand: dari bahu, serong ke bawah","Roll the wrist and loop the stick up to the other shoulder":"Pusingkan pergelangan tangan dan lingkarkan kayu ke bahu sebelah lain","Backhand: diagonally down — the two strikes join into a non-stop figure 8":"Backhand: serong ke bawah; kedua-dua pukulan bersambung menjadi angka 8 tanpa henti","They raise the stick to strike down":"Lawan mengangkat kayu untuk memukul dari atas","Raise the weapon hand overhead with the tip sloping down and back, so their stick slides off":"Angkat tangan senjata ke atas kepala dengan hujung kayu condong ke belakang dan bawah, supaya kayu lawan tergelincir","Let the stick flow on round to the shoulder":"Biarkan kayu mengalir berpusing ke bahu","Counter straight away with a forehand":"Balas serta-merta dengan forehand","Ready stance at close range":"Kedudukan sedia pada jarak dekat","They swing down":"Lawan mengayun kayu ke bawah","Block with your stick first":"Tahan dahulu dengan kayu anda","The live hand immediately checks their weapon hand":"Tangan hidup segera mengawal tangan lawan yang memegang kayu","Use your stick to strip theirs downward out of their hand":"Gunakan kayu anda untuk menanggalkan kayu lawan dari tangannya dengan menekannya ke bawah","Step back to a safe distance":"Undur ke jarak yang selamat","Put the stick down — same ready stance":"Letakkan kayu, kekal dalam kedudukan sedia yang sama","The hand moves exactly as in the forehand stick strike":"Pergerakan tangan sama persis dengan pukulan kayu forehand","The same diagonal becomes a hammer fist or a slashing palm":"Pepenjuru yang sama menjadi tumbukan tukul atau tetakan tapak","Weapon and empty hand share the same angles":"Senjata dan tangan kosong berkongsi sudut yang sama","CONTACT: ":"SENTUHAN:","Grip control":"Kawalan genggaman","Live-hand awareness":"Kesedaran tangan hidup","Hip rotation":"Putaran pinggul","Wrist":"Pergelangan tangan","Accuracy":"Ketepatan","Follow-through":"Teruskan hingga menembusi sasaran","Coordination":"Koordinasi","Flow":"Kelancaran","Wrist mobility":"Kelenturan pergelangan tangan","Angles":"Sudut","Counter":"Serangan balas","Safety":"Keselamatan","Transfer":"Keupayaan peralihan","Angle awareness":"Kefahaman sudut","Live hand":"Tangan hidup","Real speed":"Kelajuan sebenar","Contact: ":"Kontak:","Lesson {n} of 8 · {type}":"Pelajaran {n} daripada 8 · {type}","Kali, Eskrima, Arnis — what is the difference?":"Kali, Eskrima, Arnis: apakah bezanya?","All three are names for the Filipino martial arts (FMA); which one is used depends mostly on region and school, and the content overlaps a great deal. In 2009 the Philippines made arnis its national martial art and sport. What every style shares is weapons first — usually stick and blade — with the same angles then applied to the empty hand.":"Ketiga-tiga nama ini merujuk kepada seni mempertahankan diri Filipina (FMA). Nama mana yang digunakan bergantung terutamanya pada wilayah dan perguruan, dan kandungannya banyak bertindih. Pada 2009 Filipina menjadikan arnis seni mempertahankan diri dan sukan kebangsaannya. Setiap aliran berkongsi ciri utama: senjata dahulu, biasanya kayu dan bilah, kemudian sudut yang sama digunakan pada tangan kosong.","The eight lessons at a glance":"Lapan pelajaran sepintas lalu","Tool":"Alat","The angle system":"Sistem sudut","Instead of memorising individual techniques, FMA sorts attacks into a few \"angles\": forehand and backhand diagonals from above, horizontal strikes, rising diagonals from below, and thrusts. Each style numbers them differently (commonly 5 to 12), but the principle is the same: learn to defend each angle and you can answer a stick, a blade or an empty hand the same way.":"Daripada menghafal teknik satu demi satu, FMA mengelaskan serangan kepada beberapa “sudut”: pepenjuru forehand dan backhand dari atas, pukulan mendatar, pepenjuru menaik dari bawah, dan tusukan. Setiap aliran menomborkannya secara berbeza (biasanya 5 hingga 12), tetapi prinsipnya sama: pelajari cara mempertahankan setiap sudut, maka anda boleh menjawab kayu, bilah atau tangan kosong dengan cara yang sama.","Practise safely":"Berlatih dengan selamat","Train alone or on a tyre or striking post before partner drills.":"Berlatih sendirian atau pada tayar atau tiang pukul sebelum latihan berpasangan.","Wear a helmet, hand and eye protection for partner drills, starting very slowly.":"Pakai topi keledar, pelindung tangan dan mata untuk latihan berpasangan, mulakan dengan sangat perlahan.","Use rattan or foam training sticks — never hardwood or metal for partner work.":"Gunakan kayu latihan rotan atau span, jangan sekali-kali kayu keras atau besi untuk latihan berpasangan.","Blade work uses blunt trainers only, under an instructor.":"Latihan bilah hanya menggunakan alat latihan tumpul, di bawah bimbingan jurulatih.","Related: <a href=\"../../self-defence/krav-maga/\">Krav Maga basics</a> and <a href=\"../../kungfu/wing-chun/\">Wing Chun basics</a>.":"Berkaitan: <a href=\"../../self-defence/krav-maga/\">Asas Krav Maga</a> dan <a href=\"../../kungfu/wing-chun/\">Asas Wing Chun</a>.","Why learn the weapon first?":"Mengapa belajar senjata dahulu?","A weapon magnifies mistakes, making distance, angles and timing easier to learn — and the same movements carry straight over to the empty hand.":"Senjata membesarkan kesilapan, menjadikan jarak, sudut dan masa lebih mudah dipelajari — dan pergerakan yang sama terus digunakan untuk tangan kosong.","What is the live hand?":"Apakah tangan hidup?","The hand without the weapon, used to check, push or control the opponent's weapon hand.":"Tangan yang tidak memegang senjata, digunakan untuk memeriksa, menolak atau mengawal tangan lawan yang memegang senjata.","What equipment do I need?":"Apakah peralatan yang saya perlukan?","One or two rattan sticks of about 70 cm to start; add a helmet and hand protection for partner work.":"Satu atau dua batang rotan kira-kira 70 cm untuk permulaan; tambah topi keledar dan pelindung tangan untuk latihan berpasangan.","Kali / Eskrima / Arnis":"Kali / Eskrima / Arnis","FIGHTING ARTS · FILIPINO MARTIAL ARTS FOR BEGINNERS":"SENI PERTARUNGAN · SENI BELA DIRI FILIPINA UNTUK PEMULA","Filipino Martial Arts Basics: Kali, Eskrima & Arnis Stick in 8 Lessons":"Asas Seni Bela Diri Filipina: Kali, Eskrima & Tongkat Arnis dalam 8 Pelajaran","Filipino martial arts teach the weapon first and the empty hand second, using the same angles for stick, blade and hand. These 8 lessons use the single stick (baston): stance, diagonal strikes, the thrust, figure-8 flow, the roof block, the live-hand check and disarm, and finally the same angles with the empty hand. The brown stick is yours; the grey figure is your training partner.":"Seni bela diri Filipina mengajar senjata dahulu dan tangan kosong kemudian, menggunakan sudut yang sama untuk kayu, bilah dan tangan kosong. 8 pelajaran ini menggunakan kayu tunggal (baston): kedudukan, serangan pepenjuru, tusukan, aliran angka lapan, tangkisan bumbung, pemeriksaan tangan hidup dan pelucutan, kemudian sudut yang sama dengan tangan kosong. Kayu coklat ialah milik anda; figura kelabu ialah rakan latihan anda.","Three names":"Tiga nama","Depends on region and school":"Bergantung pada wilayah dan sekolah","Tool in this lesson":"Alat dalam pelajaran ini","Stick length":"Panjang kayu","Traditionally rattan":"Secara tradisional rotan (rattan)","Pick a technique (best learned in order)":"Pilih satu teknik (paling baik dipelajari mengikut susunan)","Contact point":"Titik sentuhan","In a fight":"Dalam pertarungan","SIDE · GREY = PARTNER":"SISI · KELABU = RAKAN","RIGHT HAND":"TANGAN KANAN","LEFT HAND":"TANGAN KIRI","What this technique trains":"Apa yang dilatih oleh teknik ini","For education only; the animations are simplified. Train stick work under a qualified instructor, wear a helmet, hand and eye protection for partner drills and start slowly. This page does not cover live-blade training.":"Untuk tujuan pendidikan sahaja; animasi dipermudahkan. Berlatih kerja kayu di bawah bimbingan jurulatih yang layak, pakai topi keledar, pelindung tangan dan mata untuk latihan berpasangan, dan mulakan dengan perlahan. Halaman ini tidak merangkumi latihan bilah tajam.","Filipino Martial Arts Basics: Kali, Eskrima & Arnis Stick Fighting — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"Asas Seni Mempertahankan Diri Filipina: Pertarungan Kayu Kali, Eskrima & Arnis — Panduan Interaktif | KungfuTutor","Learn 8 Filipino martial arts (Kali, Eskrima, Arnis) basics with animated stick demos: stance and grip, forehand and backhand diagonal strikes, thrust, figure-8 flow, roof block and counter, live-hand check and disarm, and empty-hand application.":"Pelajari asas 8 seni mempertahankan diri Filipina (Kali, Eskrima, Arnis) melalui demonstrasi kayu beranimasi: kedudukan dan genggaman, serangan serong forehand dan backhand, tusukan, aliran angka lapan, sekatan bumbung dan balasan, semakan tangan hidup dan pelucutan senjata, serta aplikasi tangan kosong.","Kali, Eskrima & Arnis Basics — Stick Fighting, Step by Step":"Asas Kali, Eskrima & Arnis — Lawan Kayu, Langkah demi Langkah","What is the difference between Kali, Eskrima and Arnis?":"Apakah perbezaan antara Kali, Eskrima dan Arnis?","They are three common names for the Filipino martial arts; which name is used depends largely on region and school. All of them train weapons first, usually sticks and blades, and apply the same angles to empty-hand fighting.":"Ketiga-tiganya ialah tiga nama lazim bagi seni mempertahankan diri Filipina; nama yang digunakan banyak bergantung pada kawasan dan sekolah. Semuanya melatih senjata dahulu, biasanya kayu dan bilah, dan menggunakan sudut yang sama untuk pertarungan tangan kosong.","Why do Filipino martial arts start with weapons?":"Mengapa seni mempertahankan diri Filipina bermula dengan senjata?","Because the same angles and movements carry over to the empty hand: a forehand stick strike becomes a hammer fist or palm strike, and the live-hand check works the same way.":"Kerana sudut dan pergerakan yang sama dibawa ke tangan kosong: pukulan kayu forehand menjadi tumbukan tukul atau tamparan telapak tangan, dan semakan tangan hidup berfungsi dengan cara yang sama.","What is the live hand in FMA?":"Apakah tangan hidup dalam FMA?","The hand that does not hold the weapon. It checks, pushes, grabs and controls the opponent's weapon hand while the weapon hand attacks and defends.":"Tangan yang tidak memegang senjata. Ia menyemak, menolak, memegang dan mengawal tangan senjata lawan, manakala tangan senjata menyerang dan mempertahankan diri.","Technique {n} of 10 · {type}":"Teknik {n} daripada 10 · {type}","What is Lethwei?":"Apakah itu Lethwei?","Lethwei is Myanmar's traditional combat sport, known as the \"art of nine limbs\". Fighters wear no gloves — only gauze and tape on the hands — and may strike with fists, elbows, knees, feet and the head, while throws and sweeps are also allowed, which makes it one of the most intense stand-up fighting sports in the world.":"Lethwei ialah sukan tempur tradisional Myanmar, dikenali sebagai “seni sembilan anggota”. Pemain tidak memakai sarung tangan, hanya kain kasa dan pita pada tangan, dan boleh menyerang dengan penumbuk, siku, lutut, kaki dan kepala. Bantingan dan sapuan juga dibenarkan, menjadikannya antara sukan tarung berdiri paling sengit di dunia.","How is it different from Muay Thai?":"Apakah bezanya dengan Muay Thai?","Lethwei":"Lethwei","Muay Thai":"Muay Thai","Gloves":"Sarung tangan","None — gauze and tape":"Tiada — kain kasa dan pita","Yes":"Ya","Headbutts":"Tandukan kepala","Allowed":"Dibenarkan","Not allowed":"Tidak dibenarkan","Weapons":"Senjata","Throws & sweeps":"Bantingan & sapuan","Part of the game":"Sebahagian daripada permainan","Limited":"Terhad","Rules vary between events — always check the rules of the event you are watching or entering.":"Peraturan berbeza mengikut acara. Sentiasa semak peraturan acara yang anda tonton atau sertai.","The ten techniques at a glance":"Sepuluh teknik sepintas lalu","Technique":"Teknik","Starting out safely":"Bermula dengan selamat","Build the basics first — stance, straight punches, kicks and checks from boxing and Muay Thai.":"Bina asas dahulu: kedudukan badan, tumbukan lurus, tendangan dan tangkisan tendangan daripada tinju dan Muay Thai.","Learn to wrap your hands properly, and still wear gloves for most pad and bag work.":"Pelajari cara membalut tangan dengan betul, dan tetap pakai sarung tangan untuk kebanyakan latihan pad dan beg.","Practise headbutts and elbows only on pads or protective gear, under a coach.":"Latih tandukan kepala dan siku hanya pada pad atau peralatan pelindung, di bawah pengawasan jurulatih.","Stop and see a doctor after any blow to the head that causes dizziness, headache or nausea.":"Berhenti dan dapatkan rawatan doktor selepas sebarang hentakan di kepala yang menyebabkan pening, sakit kepala atau loya.","Related: <a href=\"../muay-thai/\">Muay Thai basics</a> and <a href=\"../boxing/\">boxing basics</a>.":"Berkaitan: <a href=\"../muay-thai/\">Asas Muay Thai</a> dan <a href=\"../boxing/\">asas tinju</a>.","Why \"the art of nine limbs\"?":"Mengapa dipanggil “seni sembilan anggota”?","It adds the headbutt to Muay Thai's eight limbs of fists, elbows, knees and shins.":"Ia menambah tandukan kepala kepada lapan anggota Muay Thai, iaitu penumbuk, siku, lutut dan tulang kering.","Do Lethwei fighters wear gloves?":"Adakah pemain Lethwei memakai sarung tangan?","No — the hands are wrapped only in gauze and tape.":"Tidak. Tangan hanya dibalut dengan kain kasa dan pita.","Can beginners learn headbutts?":"Bolehkah pemula belajar tandukan kepala?","Only from a qualified coach, following their progression and with protective equipment — never on your own or with friends.":"Hanya daripada jurulatih yang layak, ikut perkembangan latihannya dan dengan peralatan pelindung. Jangan sekali-kali berlatih sendiri atau bersama rakan.","FIGHTING SPORTS · MYANMAR'S ART OF NINE LIMBS":"SUKAN PERTARUNGAN · SENI SEMBILAN ANGGOTA BADAN MYANMAR","Lethwei Basics: Bare Knuckles and the Art of Nine Limbs":"Asas Lethwei: Tinju Tanpa Sarung Tangan dan Seni Sembilan Anggota Badan","Lethwei is fought without gloves — just gauze and tape on the hands — and adds the head to Muay Thai's weapons: fists, elbows, knees, feet and the headbutt make nine, and throws and sweeps are allowed. The grey figure is the opponent; the red ring marks the point of contact.":"Lethwei dibuat tanpa sarung tangan, hanya kain kasa dan pita pada tangan, dan menambah kepala pada senjata Muay Thai: tumbukan, siku, lutut, kaki dan sondol kepala menjadi sembilan, serta bantingan dan sapuan dibenarkan. Figura kelabu ialah lawan; bulatan merah menandakan titik sentuhan.","Fists (bare)":"TUMBUKAN (TANPA SARUNG)","Elbows":"SIKU","Knees":"LUTUT","Feet & shins":"KAKI & TULANG KERING","Head":"KEPALA","Safety: ":"Keselamatan:","Lethwei is one of the most dangerous combat sports. Headbutts, bare-knuckle punches and elbows must only be trained under a qualified coach, on pads and with protective equipment — never try a headbutt on a partner or anyone else. These animations are for understanding only.":"Lethwei adalah antara sukan pertarungan paling berbahaya. Sondol kepala, tumbukan tanpa sarung tangan dan siku hanya boleh dilatih di bawah jurulatih yang layak, pada pad atau dengan peralatan pelindung. Jangan sekali-kali cuba sondol kepala pada rakan atau sesiapa. Animasi ini hanya untuk kefahaman.","Fists · elbows · knees · feet · head":"Tumbukan · siku · lutut · kaki · kepala","Contact point, this technique":"Titik sentuhan, teknik ini","Hands wrapped in gauze and tape only":"Tangan hanya dibalut kain kasa dan pita","Techniques you have mastered":"Teknik yang telah dikuasai","Mark each technique as mastered below":"Tandakan setiap teknik sebagai telah dikuasai di bawah","Pick a technique":"Pilih teknik untuk melihat butirannya","How it works":"Cara ia berfungsi","For education only; the animations are simplified. Lethwei is a high-risk contact sport — train only under a qualified coach with proper protective equipment.":"Hanya untuk tujuan pendidikan; animasi dipermudahkan. Lethwei ialah sukan sentuhan berisiko tinggi. Berlatihlah hanya di bawah jurulatih yang layak dengan peralatan pelindung yang sesuai.","Lethwei Basics: Burmese Bare-Knuckle Boxing, the Art of Nine Limbs | KungfuTutor":"Asas Lethwei: Tinju Tangan Kosong Burma, Seni Sembilan Anggota | KungfuTutor","An animated introduction to Lethwei, Myanmar's bare-knuckle art of nine limbs: stance, bare-knuckle punches, the headbutt, rising elbow, flying knee, kicks, catch-and-sweep and the high cover — with safety notes.":"Pengenalan beranimasi kepada Lethwei, seni sembilan anggota tinju tangan kosong dari Myanmar: kedudukan, tumbukan tangan kosong, sondolan kepala, siku naik, lutut melayang, tendangan, tangkap-dan-sapu dan pertahanan tinggi — dengan nota keselamatan.","Lethwei Basics — The Art of Nine Limbs, Step by Step":"Asas Lethwei — Seni Sembilan Anggota, Langkah demi Langkah","Why is Lethwei called the art of nine limbs?":"Mengapa Lethwei dipanggil seni sembilan anggota?","Because it adds the head to the eight weapons of Muay Thai: two fists, two elbows, two knees, two shins or feet, and headbutts.":"Kerana ia menambah kepala kepada lapan senjata Muay Thai: dua penumbuk, dua siku, dua lutut, dua tulang kering atau kaki, dan sondolan kepala.","No. Lethwei is fought bare-knuckle, with the hands wrapped in gauze and tape.":"Tidak. Lethwei dilakukan dengan tangan kosong, dengan tangan dibalut kain kasa dan pita pelekat.","What is the difference between Lethwei and Muay Thai?":"Apakah perbezaan antara Lethwei dan Muay Thai?","Lethwei is bare-knuckle and allows headbutts, and throws and sweeps are part of the game; Muay Thai is fought in gloves and does not allow headbutts.":"Lethwei dilakukan dengan tangan kosong dan membenarkan sondolan kepala, serta bantingan dan sapuan adalah sebahagian daripada permainan; Muay Thai dilakukan dengan sarung tangan dan tidak membenarkan sondolan kepala.","HANDS HIGH · ELBOWS TIGHT · CHIN DOWN":"TANGAN TINGGI · SIKU RAPAT · DAGU KE BAWAH","Stand with feet staggered about shoulder-width, weight slightly back, knees soft. With bare fists there is no padding to hide behind, so hold the hands higher and closer to the head and use the forearms as shields; keep the elbows in and the chin tucked. Watch their chest — and their head, because headbutts are legal in Lethwei.":"Berdiri dengan kaki sedikit berjarak kira-kira lebar bahu, berat badan sedikit ke belakang, lutut lembut. Dengan penumbuk tanpa sarung, tiada alas untuk berlindung, jadi angkat tangan lebih tinggi dan lebih rapat ke kepala serta gunakan lengan bawah sebagai perisai; rapatkan siku dan tundukkan dagu. Perhatikan dada lawan — dan kepalanya, kerana sondolan kepala dibenarkan dalam Lethwei.","Hiding behind the hands as if wearing gloves (bare fists don't cover enough); chin up; poking the head forward (an easy headbutt target); weight on the front foot.":"Bersembunyi di belakang tangan seolah-olah memakai sarung tangan (penumbuk tanpa sarung tidak menutup cukup); dagu terangkat; menjulurkan kepala ke hadapan (sasaran sondolan yang mudah); berat badan di kaki depan.","Hold and move in your stance in a mirror, 3 × 1 minute, checking hands, elbows and chin.":"Tahan dan bergerak dalam kedudukan di hadapan cermin, 3 × 1 minit, semak tangan, siku dan dagu.","Lethwei has the most weapons of any striking art, so the stance must defend fists, elbows, knees, feet and the head.":"Lethwei mempunyai senjata serangan paling banyak berbanding seni tumbukan mana-mana, maka kedudukan mesti mempertahankan penumbuk, siku, lutut, kaki dan kepala.","Bare-knuckle Straight Punch":"Tumbukan Lurus Tanpa Sarung","Punch":"Tumbukan","First two knuckles":"Dua buku jari pertama","Fist structure":"Struktur penumbuk","PIVOT & TURN · FIRST TWO KNUCKLES · STRAIGHT WRIST":"PUSING KAKI & PINGGUL · DUA BUKU JARI PERTAMA · PERGELANGAN LURUS","Throw it like a boxing cross — pivot and turn the hips — but with no glove you must land on the first two knuckles with the wrist and forearm in one straight line and the fist tightly closed. Snap it straight back to guard.":"Lontarkannya seperti pukulan silang tinju — pusing kaki dan pinggul — tetapi tanpa sarung tangan anda mesti mendarat pada dua buku jari pertama dengan pergelangan dan lengan bawah dalam satu garisan lurus serta penumbuk digenggam rapat. Tarik semula dengan pantas ke kedudukan pertahanan.","Landing on the little-finger knuckles (a common fracture); a bent wrist; a loose fist; punching hard skull bone.":"Mendarat dengan buku jari kelingking (patah tulang yang biasa); pergelangan bengkok; penumbuk longgar; menumbuk tulang tengkorak yang keras.","With wraps and gauze, slow reps on pads, 3 × 10, feeling the first two knuckles connect.":"Dengan balutan tangan dan kasa, ulang perlahan pada pad, 3 × 10, rasakan dua buku jari pertama mengena.","Bare-knuckle punches cut and concentrate force — but hands break easily, so where you hit matters.":"Tumbukan tanpa sarung menyebabkan luka dan memfokuskan daya — tetapi tangan mudah patah, jadi di mana anda menumbuk adalah penting.","ELBOW LEVEL · TURN · STRAIGHT WRIST":"SIKU SEPARAS · PUSING · PERGELANGAN LURUS","Shift a little weight to the lead foot, pivot and turn the hips with the arm bent about 90° and the elbow level with the fist, hooking across into the side of the jaw. With bare fists keep the wrist straight to avoid spraining it. (In the side view the fist travels into the screen.)":"Alihkan sedikit berat badan ke kaki depan, pusingkan kaki dan pinggul dengan lengan dibengkokkan kira-kira 90° dan siku sama aras dengan penumbuk, kaitkan penumbuk ke sisi rahang. Dengan penumbuk tanpa pelindung, kekalkan pergelangan lurus untuk elak terseliuh. (Dalam pandangan sisi, penumbuk bergerak ke dalam skrin.)","A wide, telegraphed swing; dropping the elbow; bending the wrist; the other hand leaving the face.":"Ayunan lebar yang mudah dikesan; siku jatuh; pergelangan tangan melentur; tangan sebelah meninggalkan muka.","Hooks on pads, 3 × 10, then chain them after the straight punch.":"Tumbukan kait pada pad, 3 × 10, kemudian gandingkan selepas tumbukan lurus.","Hooks come from outside the line of sight and are a common knockout punch up close.":"Kait datang dari luar garisan pandangan dan merupakan tumbukan KO yang biasa pada jarak dekat.","Headbutt":"Hentakan kepala","Forehead near the hairline":"Dahi berhampiran garis rambut","Close-range control":"Kawalan jarak dekat","GRIP THE NECK · DRIVE FROM THE LEGS · USE THE FOREHEAD":"GENGGAM LEHER · TOLAK DARI KAKI · GUNAKAN DAHI","The headbutt is what sets Lethwei apart from other stand-up fighting. At very close range a fighter often grips the back of the opponent's neck to control the distance, then drives from the legs to strike with the hard part of the forehead near the hairline — not the face or the top of the head. This animation is only here so you understand the rule and the movement: headbutts are extremely dangerous and must only be learned under a qualified coach with suitable equipment. Never try one on a training partner or anyone else.":"Hentakan kepala ialah yang membezakan Lethwei daripada pertarungan berdiri yang lain. Pada jarak yang sangat dekat, pejuang selalunya menggenggam belakang leher lawan untuk mengawal jarak, kemudian menolak dari kaki untuk menyerang dengan bahagian keras dahi berhampiran garis rambut, bukan muka atau bahagian atas kepala. Animasi ini hanya untuk anda memahami peraturan dan pergerakan: hentakan kepala sangat berbahaya dan hanya boleh dipelajari di bawah jurulatih bertauliah dengan peralatan yang sesuai. Jangan sekali-kali mencubanya ke atas rakan latihan atau sesiapa pun.","Hitting with the face or the top of the head (you get hurt); charging in head-down and blind; lunging from out of range.":"Menghentak dengan muka atau bahagian atas kepala (anda sendiri akan cedera); meluru dengan kepala tertunduk dan buta; menerkam dari luar jarak.","This page gives no headbutt drill — learn it only from a qualified Lethwei coach.":"Halaman ini tidak memberikan latihan hentakan kepala; pelajari hanya daripada jurulatih Lethwei yang bertauliah.","Headbutts make close range far more dangerous — and are why Lethwei fighters guard their head so carefully.":"Sondulan kepala menjadikan jarak dekat jauh lebih berbahaya, dan itulah sebabnya pejuang Lethwei menjaga kepala mereka dengan teliti.","Rising Elbow":"Siku Naik","Elbow":"Siku","Point of the elbow":"Hujung siku","Close-range explosiveness":"Letupan kuasa jarak dekat","DIP · DRIVE UP · ELBOW SPEARS UP":"TUNDUK · TOLAK KE ATAS · SIKU MENUSUK KE ATAS","At close range, dip the knees and drop the rear elbow, then drive up through the legs so the elbow spears upward into the chin, with your hand finishing near your own ear. The other hand guards your head; return to stance.":"Pada jarak dekat, tunduk sedikit dan turunkan siku belakang, kemudian tolak dengan kaki supaya siku menusuk ke atas ke dagu, dengan tangan berakhir dekat telinga anda. Tangan satu lagi melindungi kepala; kembali ke kedudukan.","Throwing from too far; lifting the arm without the legs; flaring the elbow out; leaving an opening afterwards.":"Menyerang dari jarak terlalu jauh; mengangkat lengan tanpa kaki; melebarkan siku ke luar; meninggalkan bukaan selepas itu.","Slow reps on pads, 3 × 8, then add it after a hook.":"Ulang perlahan pada pad, 3 × 8, kemudian tambah selepas cangkuk.","When an opponent ducks and charges in, the rising elbow meets them on the way.":"Apabila lawan menunduk dan meluru masuk, siku naik akan menyambut mereka di tengah jalan.","Flying Knee":"Lutut Terbang","Knee":"Lutut","Point of the knee":"Hujung lutut","Chest, chin":"Dada, dagu","Explosiveness and timing":"Letupan dan masa","STEP & JUMP · REAR KNEE UP & FORWARD · LAND GUARDED":"LANGKAH & LOMPAT · LUTUT BELAKANG KE ATAS & HADAPAN · MENDARAT BERJAGA","Step in with the lead foot to take off and jump forward and up, driving the rear knee up and forward into the chest or chin, with the hands reaching out for balance or control. Land balanced and get straight back into your guard.":"Langkah masuk dengan kaki depan untuk melompat, lompat ke depan dan ke atas, tolak lutut belakang ke atas dan ke depan ke dada atau dagu, dengan tangan dihulur untuk imbangan atau kawalan. Mendarat seimbang dan terus kembali ke kawalan.","Jumping from too far; pausing before take-off (telegraphing); landing off balance; getting countered after a miss.":"Melompat dari jarak terlalu jauh; berhenti seketika sebelum melompat (memberi isyarat); mendarat hilang imbangan; diserang balas selepas tersasar.","Practise jumping knee lifts on the spot, 10 reps, then 3 × 5 on the bag, focusing on a balanced landing.":"Latih angkat lutut sambil melompat di tempat, 10 ulangan, kemudian 3 × 5 pada beg, fokus pada pendaratan yang seimbang.","The flying knee is a classic finisher in Lethwei and Muay Thai — but costly if it misses.":"Lutut terbang ialah penamat klasik dalam Lethwei dan Muay Thai, tetapi mahal harganya jika tersasar.","Roundhouse Kick":"Tendangan Sisi","Kick":"Tendangan","Shin":"Tulang hadapan kaki","Side of the body":"Sisi badan","Explosive hip turn":"Pusingan pinggul yang meletup","PIVOT · TURN THE HIP · SHIN · ARM SWINGS BACK":"PUSING · PUSINGKAN PINGGUL · TULANG KERING · LENGAN AYUN KE BELAKANG","Turn the lead foot out, swing the rear leg up and turn the hip over, landing the shin on the side of the body. The arm on the kicking side swings down and back while the other hand guards the head. Recover to stance.":"Pusingkan kaki depan ke luar, ayunkan kaki belakang ke atas dan pusingkan pinggul, mendaratkan tulang kering di sisi badan. Lengan di sebelah tendangan ayun ke bawah dan ke belakang manakala tangan satu lagi melindungi kepala. Kembali ke kedudukan asal.","Not pivoting; kicking with the foot; dropping both hands.":"Tidak memusing; menendang dengan kaki; kedua-dua tangan jatuh.","10 slow pivots holding a wall, then 3 × 10 per leg on the bag.":"10 pusingan perlahan sambil berpegang pada dinding, kemudian 3 × 10 setiap kaki pada beg tinju.","Body kicks add up and draw the hands down, opening the head.":"Tendangan badan mengumpul kesan dan menurunkan tangan lawan, membuka bahagian kepala.","Push Kick":"Tendangan Tolak","Sole of the foot":"Tapak kaki","Stomach, hips":"Perut, pinggul","KNEE UP · PUSH THE HIPS · SOLE":"LUTUT NAIK · TOLAK PINGGUL · TAPAK","Lift the lead knee, push the hips forward and drive the sole of the foot into them, leaning back slightly with the hands up; re-chamber before putting the foot down.":"Angkat lutut hadapan, tolak pinggul ke hadapan dan tolak tapak kaki ke arah lawan, condongkan badan sedikit ke belakang dengan tangan diangkat; tarik semula lutut sebelum meletakkan kaki.","Swinging without the knee lift; no hip push; dropping the hands.":"Mengayun tanpa mengangkat lutut; tiada tolakan pinggul; tangan jatuh.","3 × 10 per leg on the bag.":"3 × 10 setiap kaki pada beg tinju.","When they try to close in for headbutts or the clinch, the push kick restores the distance.":"Apabila lawan cuba mendekat untuk tandukan kepala atau klinch, tendangan tolak memulihkan jarak.","Catch Kick & Sweep":"Tangkap Tendangan & Sapuan","Lead arm traps the leg":"Lengan hadapan memerangkap kaki","Their standing leg":"Kaki penyokong lawan","Timing and control":"Masa dan kawalan","STEP IN · TRAP THE LEG · SWEEP THE STANDING LEG":"MASUK · PERANGKAP KAKI · SAPU KAKI PENYOKONG","As the body kick comes, step into it to take the sting out and scoop the leg up under your lead arm. Then sweep their standing leg with your rear leg so they lose balance, and reset to your stance.":"Apabila tendangan badan datang, masuk ke dalamnya untuk mengurangkan kesan dan cedok kaki ke atas di bawah lengan hadapan. Kemudian sapu kaki penyokong lawan dengan kaki belakang supaya mereka hilang imbangan, dan kembali ke kedudukan asal.","Catching while backing away (you take the full kick); grabbing with the hand instead of trapping; losing your own balance on the sweep.":"Menangkap sambil berundur (anda menerima penuh tendangan); mencengkam dengan tangan dan bukan memerangkap; hilang imbangan sendiri semasa menyapu.","Partner throws slow, light kicks while you step in and trap, 10 reps; then add the sweep, on mats only.":"Rakan melontar tendangan perlahan dan ringan manakala anda melangkah masuk dan memerangkap, 10 kali; kemudian tambah sapuan, di tilam sahaja.","Catching and sweeping makes a kicker think twice.":"Menangkap dan menyapu membuatkan penendang berfikir dua kali.","High Cover & Counter":"Perlindungan Atas & Balas","Forearm and elbow":"Lengan bawah dan siku","Block the hook":"Sekat tumbukan kait","Reaction and structure":"Reaksi dan struktur","ARM TIGHT TO THE HEAD · CHIN DOWN · COUNTER":"LENGAN RAPAT KEPALA · DAGU KE BAWAH · BALAS","As a hook comes in, raise the arm on that side tight against the side of your head so the forearm and elbow take the blow, chin down and leaning in slightly. Fire back immediately with a straight punch from the other hand.":"Apabila kait datang, angkat lengan sebelah itu rapat ke tepi kepala supaya lengan bawah dan siku menerima hentaman, dagu ke bawah dan badan sedikit condong ke hadapan. Balas segera dengan tumbukan lurus daripada tangan satu lagi.","Holding the arm away from the head (the punch drives through); closing your eyes and turning away; blocking without countering.":"Menahan lengan terlalu jauh dari kepala (tumbukan menembusi); memejam mata dan memalingkan kepala; hanya menyekat tanpa membalas.","Partner swings slowly from both sides with pads; block and counter, 3 × 1 minute.":"Rakan mengayun dengan pad perlahan dari kedua-dua belah; sekat dan balas, 3 × 1 minit.","Without gloves only the structure of the arm can absorb a heavy shot, so this cover is vital.":"Tanpa sarung tangan, hanya struktur lengan yang boleh menahan tumbukan berat, jadi pertahanan ini amat penting.","Defending without gloves":"Mempertahankan diri tanpa sarung tangan","Hands higher and tighter":"Tangan lebih tinggi dan lebih rapat","No gloves — structure matters more":"Tanpa sarung tangan — struktur lebih penting","A straight wrist":"Pergelangan tangan lurus","Driven by the body turn":"Didorong oleh pusingan badan","Lethwei's signature ninth weapon":"Senjata kesembilan yang menjadi ciri khas Lethwei","For understanding only — never practise on a person":"Untuk kefahaman sahaja — jangan sekali-kali berlatih ke atas orang","Upward at close range":"Ke atas pada jarak dekat","Punishes a ducking opponent":"Menghukum lawan yang menunduk","High risk, high reward":"Risiko tinggi, ganjaran tinggi","When the opponent dips":"Apabila lawan menunduk","The same hip-turning kick as Muay Thai":"Tendangan memusingkan pinggul yang sama seperti Muay Thai","Lands with the shin":"Mendarat dengan tulang kering","Controls distance":"Mengawal jarak","Stops a rush":"Menghentikan serbuan","Turns their kick into your chance":"Menjadikan tendangan lawan peluang anda","Lethwei allows throws and sweeps":"Lethwei membenarkan lontaran dan sapuan","Key bare-knuckle defence":"Pertahanan utama dalam tinju tanpa sarung tangan","Block, then counter at once":"Sekat, kemudian balas serta-merta","Feet staggered, weight a little back, knees soft":"Kaki berdiri berselang depan-belakang, berat badan sedikit ke belakang, lutut lembut","Hands high and tight with the chin tucked — there are no gloves to hide behind":"Tangan tinggi dan rapat dengan dagu dirapatkan — tiada sarung tangan untuk berlindung","Elbows in to cover the body; eyes on their chest":"Siku rapat untuk melindungi badan; mata pada dada lawan","Pivot and turn the hips; land on the first two knuckles":"Pusingkan kaki dan pinggul; mendarat dengan dua buku jari pertama","Keep the wrist straight and snap it back":"Kekalkan pergelangan tangan lurus dan tarik balik dengan pantas","Stance at close range":"Kedudukan jarak dekat","Turn the body and hook the fist across into the side of the jaw":"Pusingkan badan dan kaitkan penumbuk melintang ke sisi rahang","The opponent is very close":"Lawan sangat dekat","Grip behind their neck and sway back slightly":"Genggam belakang leher lawan dan condongkan badan sedikit ke belakang","Drive from the legs and strike with the forehead near the hairline":"Tolak dari kaki dan hentam dengan dahi berhampiran garis rambut","Release and return to the guard":"Lepaskan dan kembali ke kedudukan pertahanan","Close-range stance":"Kedudukan jarak dekat","Dip the knees and drop the rear elbow":"Tekukkan lutut sedikit dan turunkan siku belakang","Drive up and spear the elbow upward under the chin":"Tolak ke atas dan hunjamkan siku ke atas ke bawah dagu","Stance; the opponent dips or comes forward":"Kedudukan kuda-kuda; lawan menunduk atau maju ke hadapan","Step in with the lead foot to take off":"Langkah dengan kaki depan untuk melompat","Jump and drive the rear knee up and forward, hands reaching out":"Lompat dan tolak lutut belakang ke hadapan dan atas, tangan dihulurkan ke hadapan","Land balanced and get the hands up":"Mendarat seimbang dan segera angkat tangan ke pertahanan","Pivot the lead foot and swing the rear leg up":"Pusingkan kaki depan dan ayunkan kaki belakang ke atas","Turn the hip over and land the shin on the body":"Pusingkan pinggul dan hentamkan tulang kering ke badan","Recover the leg":"Tarik balik kaki","Back to stance":"Kembali ke kedudukan kuda-kuda","Stance; the opponent steps in":"Kedudukan kuda-kuda; lawan melangkah rapat","Lift the lead knee":"Angkat lutut hadapan","Push the hips and drive the sole into them":"Tolak pinggul dan tolak lawan dengan tapak kaki","Re-chamber":"Tarik balik kaki ke kedudukan asal","They throw a body kick":"Lawan melepaskan tendangan ke badan","Step into the kick and scoop the leg under your lead arm":"Masuk ke dalam tendangan dan sauk kaki dari bawah dengan lengan hadapan","Sweep their standing leg with your rear leg":"Sapu kaki penyokong lawan dengan kaki belakang","They lose their balance; you reset to stance":"Lawan hilang imbangan; anda kembali ke kedudukan kuda-kuda","Arm tight to the side of the head, forearm takes it, chin down, lean in a little":"Lengan rapat ke sisi kepala, lengan bawah menahan, dagu dirapatkan, badan condong sedikit ke hadapan","Counter straight away with the rear hand":"Balas serta-merta dengan tangan belakang selepas menahan","Awareness":"Kesedaran","Wrist stability":"Kestabilan pergelangan tangan","Close control":"Kawalan jarak dekat","Head defence":"Pertahanan kepala","Explosiveness":"Daya letupan","Flexibility":"Kelenturan","Hip drive":"Dorongan pinggul","One-leg balance":"Keseimbangan satu kaki","Commitment":"Komitmen","Phase: ":"Fasa:","Technique {n} of 8 · {type}":"Teknik {n} daripada 8 · {type}","What is MMA?":"Apakah itu MMA?","Mixed martial arts (MMA) is a combat sport that allows striking, clinching, takedowns and ground fighting; fighters usually blend boxing, Muay Thai, wrestling and Brazilian jiu-jitsu. Bouts take place in a cage or ring and are won by knockout, submission (the opponent taps out) or the judges' decision.":"Mixed martial arts (MMA) ialah sukan tempur yang membenarkan pukulan, clinch, bantingan dan pertarungan di lantai; pejuang biasanya menggabungkan tinju, Muay Thai, gusti dan Brazilian jiu-jitsu. Perlawanan berlangsung di dalam sangkar atau gelanggang dan dimenangi melalui knockout, submission (lawan menepuk tanda menyerah) atau keputusan hakim.","The eight techniques at a glance":"Lapan teknik sepintas lalu","Phase":"Fasa","How do striking and wrestling connect?":"Bagaimanakah pukulan dan gusti saling berkait?","MMA's key idea is that strikes set up takedowns and the threat of takedowns sets up strikes: when they raise their hands to block punches, the double-leg gets easier; when they drop low to stop takedowns, the overhand and knees land more easily. That is why the stance must handle both threats at once.":"Idea utama MMA ialah pukulan membuka jalan untuk bantingan, dan ancaman bantingan membuka jalan untuk pukulan: apabila lawan mengangkat tangan untuk menahan tumbukan, double-leg menjadi lebih mudah; apabila lawan menurunkan badan untuk menghalang bantingan, overhand dan lutut lebih mudah mengena. Sebab itu, kedudukan mesti mampu menangani kedua-dua ancaman serentak.","Learn a boxing stance, basic wrestling and how to fall safely (breakfalls) first.":"Pelajari dahulu kedudukan tinju, gusti asas dan cara jatuh dengan selamat (breakfall).","Practise takedowns and ground work only on mats, with a coach.":"Latih bantingan dan kerja lantai hanya di tikar, dengan jurulatih.","Spar with MMA or boxing gloves and a mouthguard, starting with light technical sparring.":"Berlatih tanding dengan sarung tangan MMA atau tinju dan pelindung gigi, bermula dengan sparring teknikal ringan.","Tap early when caught in a choke or joint lock — never fight through it.":"Tepuk awal apabila terperangkap dalam cekikan atau kunci sendi — jangan sekali-kali bertahan.","Related: <a href=\"../boxing/\">boxing basics</a> and <a href=\"../muay-thai/\">Muay Thai basics</a>.":"Berkaitan: <a href=\"../boxing/\">asas tinju</a> dan <a href=\"../muay-thai/\">asas Muay Thai</a>.","What should an MMA beginner learn first?":"Apakah yang patut dipelajari oleh pemula MMA dahulu?","The stance, basic punches, the sprawl and getting up safely — they keep you safe in sparring.":"Kedudukan, pukulan asas, sprawl dan cara bangun dengan selamat — semuanya memastikan kamu selamat semasa sparring.","What is a sprawl?":"Apakah itu sprawl?","A takedown defence: throw your legs back and drop your hips onto their back as they shoot.":"Pertahanan terhadap lontaran: campakkan kaki ke belakang dan turunkan pinggul ke belakang lawan ketika dia menyerbu.","Can I learn MMA without a wrestling background?":"Bolehkah saya belajar MMA tanpa latar belakang gusti?","Yes — most MMA classes teach the stance, breakfalls and basic takedowns from scratch.":"Ya — kebanyakan kelas MMA mengajar kedudukan, teknik jatuh dan lontaran asas dari permulaan.","MMA":"Seni Mempertahankan Diri Campuran","FIGHTING SPORTS · MIXED MARTIAL ARTS FOR BEGINNERS":"SUKAN PERTEMPURAN · SENI BELA DIRI CAMPURAN UNTUK PEMULA","MMA Basics: Striking, Takedowns and the Ground in 8 Lessons":"Asas MMA: Serangan, Lontaran dan Pertarungan di Lantai dalam 8 Pelajaran","MMA joins boxing, Muay Thai, wrestling and jiu-jitsu. These 8 lessons start with the stance, then basic strikes, a takedown and how to stop one, control on the ground and getting back up safely. The grey figure is the opponent; the red ring marks the point of contact.":"MMA menggabungkan tinju, Muay Thai, gusti dan jiu-jitsu. 8 pelajaran ini bermula dengan kedudukan, kemudian pukulan asas, lontaran dan cara menghalangnya, kawalan di lantai, dan bangun semula dengan selamat. Figura kelabu ialah lawan; bulatan merah menandakan titik sentuhan.","Striking":"Serangan berdiri","Punches and kicks":"Tumbukan dan tendangan","Wrestling":"Gusti","Takedowns and the sprawl":"Lontaran dan sprawl","Ground":"Lantai","Control and getting up":"Kawalan dan bangun","Phases of a fight":"Fasa-fasa pertarungan","Standing · clinch and takedowns · ground":"Berdiri · klinc dan lontaran · lantai","This technique's phase":"Fasa teknik ini","Pro bout":"Format perlawanan profesional","3 rounds × 5 minutes (title fights 5 rounds)":"3 pusingan × 5 minit (perlawanan kejuaraan 5 pusingan)","For education only; the animations are simplified. MMA is a high-impact contact sport: train under a qualified coach on mats, with gloves and a mouthguard for sparring. Practise takedowns and ground work only on mats with a coach.":"Untuk tujuan pendidikan sahaja; animasi dipermudah. MMA ialah sukan sentuhan berimpak tinggi: berlatih di bawah jurulatih bertauliah di tikar, dengan sarung tangan dan pelindung gigi untuk sparring. Latih lontaran dan kerja lantai hanya di tikar dengan jurulatih.","MMA Basics: Stance, Striking, Takedowns, Sprawl & Ground Game — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"Asas MMA: Kedudukan, Serangan, Jatuhan, Sprawl & Permainan Lantai — Panduan Interaktif | KungfuTutor","Learn 8 mixed martial arts fundamentals with animated demos against an opponent: MMA stance, jab-cross, overhand, low kick, double-leg takedown, sprawl, ground and pound from mount and the technical stand-up.":"Pelajari 8 asas seni mempertahankan diri campuran dengan demonstrasi animasi menentang lawan: kedudukan MMA, jab-cross, overhand, tendangan rendah, jatuhan double-leg, sprawl, ground and pound dari mount, dan bangkit berdiri secara teknikal.","MMA Basics — Striking and Grappling, Step by Step":"Asas MMA — Pukulan dan Gusti, Langkah demi Langkah","What are the basics of MMA?":"Apakah asas-asas MMA?","A stance that defends both strikes and takedowns, basic punches and kicks, a takedown such as the double-leg, takedown defence such as the sprawl, and control on the ground, plus getting back to your feet safely.":"Kedudukan yang melindungi daripada serangan dan jatuhan, pukulan dan tendangan asas, jatuhan seperti double-leg, pertahanan jatuhan seperti sprawl, dan kawalan di lantai, serta cara bangun semula dengan selamat.","What is a sprawl in MMA?":"Apakah itu sprawl dalam MMA?","A takedown defence: as the opponent shoots for your legs, you throw your legs back and drop your hips onto their upper back so they cannot reach your legs, then get back up.":"Pertahanan terhadap jatuhan: apabila lawan menyerbu kaki anda, anda lontarkan kaki ke belakang dan turunkan pinggul ke belakang badan atas mereka supaya mereka tidak dapat mencapai kaki anda, kemudian bangun semula.","What is a technical stand-up?":"Apakah itu bangun teknikal?","A safe way to get up from the floor: post one hand behind you, plant the opposite foot, lift the hips, swing the straight leg back underneath you and stand up at a distance, eyes on the opponent.":"Cara selamat untuk bangun dari lantai: letakkan satu tangan di belakang anda, pacakkan kaki bertentangan, angkat pinggul, ayunkan kaki yang lurus ke belakang di bawah badan dan bangun dengan jarak, mata tertumpu pada lawan.","MMA Stance":"Kedudukan MMA","Standing":"Berdiri","Balance and all-round defence":"Keseimbangan dan pertahanan menyeluruh","MORE KNEE BEND · HIPS LOW · HANDS UP":"LUTUT LEBIH TUNDUK · PINGGUL RENDAH · TANGAN NAIK","The MMA stance sits between boxing and wrestling: feet a little wider than in boxing, knees more bent and hips lower, so you can react when someone shoots for your legs. Hands guard the face but sit slightly lower than in boxing, elbows close, so they can block punches and fight off grips. Keep your weight fairly even and the lead leg light against low kicks.":"Kedudukan MMA terletak di antara tinju dan gusti: kaki sedikit lebih luas daripada tinju, lutut lebih tunduk dan pinggul lebih rendah, supaya anda boleh bertindak balas apabila lawan cuba menyerang kaki anda. Tangan melindungi muka tetapi sedikit lebih rendah daripada tinju, siku rapat, supaya boleh menyekat tumbukan dan menepis cengkaman. Kekalkan berat badan agak seimbang dan kaki depan ringan untuk mengelak tendangan rendah.","Standing tall like a boxer (easy to take down); head too low like a wrestler (open to knees); dropping the hands; too much weight on the lead leg.":"Berdiri terlalu tegak seperti peninju (mudah dijatuhkan); kepala terlalu rendah seperti pegusti (terdedah kepada lutut); menurunkan tangan; terlalu banyak berat di kaki depan.","Move in all directions in your stance for 3 × 1 minute, dropping your level every time a partner calls it.":"Bergerak ke segala arah dalam kedudukan selama 3 × 1 minit, dan rendahkan badan setiap kali pasangan memberi arahan.","An MMA fighter faces punches, kicks, knees, elbows and takedowns at once — the stance is where every exchange starts.":"Pejuang MMA perlu menghadapi tumbukan, tendangan, lutut, siku dan bantingan serentak; kedudukan ialah titik permulaan setiap pertukaran.","Jab–Cross (1-2)":"Jab–Cross (1-2)","Knuckles":"Buku jari","Speed and rhythm":"Kelajuan dan irama","JAB OPENS · CROSS TURNS THE HIPS · MOVE AFTER":"JAB MEMBUKA · SILANG MEMUTAR PINGGUL · BERGERAK SELEPAS ITU","Find range with the jab and, as it returns, pivot the back foot and turn the hips to fire the cross. MMA gloves are much smaller than boxing gloves, so keep the hands working hard to protect your face. Move straight after, or chain into a kick or takedown.":"Cari jarak dengan jab, dan apabila tangan kembali, pusingkan kaki belakang dan pinggul untuk melepaskan silang. Sarung tangan MMA jauh lebih kecil daripada sarung tangan tinju, jadi kekalkan tangan aktif melindungi muka. Bergerak terus selepas itu, atau sambung kepada tendangan atau bantingan.","Standing still afterwards; both hands away from the face; no body turn; falling forward and giving them a takedown.":"Kekal kaku selepas memukul; kedua-dua tangan jauh dari muka; tidak memusingkan badan; condong ke hadapan dan memberi peluang lawan untuk membanting.","3 × 3-minute rounds of shadowboxing or bag work, moving in a new direction after every 1-2.":"3 pusingan × 3 minit latihan bayang atau kerja beg, bergerak ke arah baharu selepas setiap 1-2.","The 1-2 is the base of MMA striking and often hides a takedown.":"1-2 ialah asas pukulan berdiri dalam MMA dan selalu menyembunyikan takedown.","Overhand":"Pukulan Overhand","Arcing power and head movement":"Kuasa melengkung dan pergerakan kepala","HEAD OFF LINE · LOOP UP AND OVER · OVER THEIR GUARD":"KEPALA KELUAR GARIS · AYUN NAIK DAN ATAS · MELEPASI PERTAHANAN MEREKA","Dip your head forward and off the centre line while the rear hand loops up and over the top of their lead hand onto the side of the head. Pivot and turn the hips so your weight follows, with the other hand guarding your face. It is often thrown just as they jab.":"Tundukkan kepala ke depan dan keluar dari garisan tengah, manakala tangan belakang berayun naik dan melepasi atas tangan depan lawan, lalu mengena sisi kepala. Pusing kaki dan pinggul supaya berat badan turut bergerak, dengan tangan satu lagi melindungi muka. Ia sering dilepaskan ketika lawan melepaskan jab.","A huge, obvious loop; leaving the head on the centre line; losing balance on a miss; dropping the other hand.":"Ayunan terlalu besar dan jelas; kepala kekal di garisan tengah; hilang imbangan apabila tersasar; tangan satu lagi jatuh.","Partner throws slow jabs while you slip and counter with the overhand, 3 × 10.":"Rakan melontar jab perlahan manakala anda mengelak dan membalas dengan overhand, 3 × 10.","With small gloves and the threat of takedowns, guards sit lower in MMA — which is why the overhand lands so often.":"Dengan sarung tangan kecil dan ancaman takedown, pertahanan dalam MMA lebih rendah, itulah sebabnya overhand sering mengena.","Low Kick":"Tendangan Rendah","Hip turn and accuracy":"Pusingan pinggul dan ketepatan","PIVOT · SHIN · HANDS UP AFTER":"PUSING · TULANG KERING · TANGAN NAIK SELEPAS ITU","Turn the lead foot out, swing the rear leg and turn the hip to land the shin on the outside of their thigh or calf. In MMA a high kick can be caught for a takedown, so the low kick is one of the safest, most used kicks. Recover the leg with the hands up.":"Pusingkan hujung kaki depan ke luar, ayunkan kaki belakang dan pusingkan pinggul supaya tulang kering mendarat di luar paha atau betis lawan. Dalam MMA, tendangan tinggi boleh ditangkap untuk dijatuhkan, jadi tendangan rendah antara yang paling selamat dan kerap digunakan. Tarik kaki balik dengan tangan terangkat.","Throwing it when they are set (checked or caught); kicking with the foot; dropping the hands afterwards.":"Melontarkannya ketika lawan sudah bersedia (ditahan atau ditangkap); menendang dengan belakang kaki; tangan jatuh selepas itu.","1-2 plus low kick on the bag, 3 × 3-minute rounds.":"1-2 ditambah tendangan rendah pada beg tinju, 3 × pusingan 3 minit.","Steady low kicks hurt the legs, slow the opponent down and make them wary of stepping in.":"Tendangan rendah yang berterusan melukakan kaki, melambatkan lawan dan membuat mereka berhati-hati untuk melangkah masuk.","Double-Leg Takedown":"Takedown Dua Kaki","Takedown":"Takedown","Hands behind both thighs":"Kedua-dua tangan di belakang kedua-dua paha","Standing → ground":"Berdiri → lantai","LEVEL CHANGE · PENETRATE · HEAD TIGHT · DRIVE":"TURUNKAN BADAN · TUSUKKAN LUTUT DEPAN · KEPALA RAPAT · TOLAK","First change levels — bend the knees with a straight back and eyes forward — then step deep between their feet, dropping the lead knee to the mat with your head tight to their side and both hands wrapping behind their thighs. Bring the back foot up and drive forward off your legs until they fall, and land on top. It works best straight after punches, when their hands come up to guard the head.":"Mula-mula tukar aras — bengkokkan lutut dengan belakang tegak dan mata ke hadapan — kemudian melangkah dalam di antara kaki mereka, turunkan lutut depan ke tikar dengan kepala rapat ke sisi mereka dan kedua-dua tangan membalut di belakang paha mereka. Bawa kaki belakang ke depan dan tolak ke hadapan menggunakan kaki sehingga mereka jatuh, dan mendarat di atas. Ia paling berkesan selepas tumbukan, apabila tangan mereka naik untuk melindungi kepala.","Bending at the waist instead of the knees (easy to sprawl on); shooting from too far; looking at the floor; grabbing the legs and stopping instead of driving.":"Membongkok di pinggang dan bukan di lutut (mudah ditindih); meluru dari jarak terlalu jauh; memandang ke lantai; memegang kaki dan berhenti dan bukannya menolak.","On mats, drill the level change and penetration step 10 times each, then slow full reps with a partner — only on mats with a coach.":"Di atas tikar, latih tukar aras dan langkah penembusan masing-masing 10 kali, kemudian ulang penuh secara perlahan bersama pasangan — hanya di tikar dengan jurulatih.","Good wrestlers decide whether the fight stays standing or goes to the ground; the double-leg is the basic takedown.":"Pegusat yang baik menentukan sama ada pertarungan kekal berdiri atau turun ke tanah; double-leg ialah teknik jatuhan asas.","Sprawl":"Menindih","Takedown defence":"Pertahanan terhadap jatuhan","Hips and body weight":"Pinggul dan berat badan","Reaction and hip strength":"Reaksi dan kekuatan pinggul","LEGS BACK · HIPS DOWN · HANDS ON HEAD AND SHOULDERS":"KAKI KE BELAKANG · PINGGUL KE BAWAH · TANGAN DI KEPALA DAN BAHU","The moment they shoot for your legs, throw both legs back and drive your hips down onto their upper back, putting your whole weight on them, with your hands pushing on their head and shoulders so they can't reach your legs. Once they stall, get back up to your stance.":"Sebaik sahaja mereka meluru ke arah kaki anda, lontarkan kedua-dua kaki ke belakang dan tekan pinggul anda ke belakang bahagian atas badan mereka, dengan seluruh berat badan anda, sambil tangan menolak kepala dan bahu mereka supaya mereka tidak dapat mencapai kaki anda. Apabila mereka terhenti, bangun semula ke kedudukan anda.","Reacting late; bending forward without throwing the legs back; landing on your knees (they can still reach); staying down instead of getting up.":"Bertindak balas lewat; membongkok ke hadapan tanpa melontarkan kaki ke belakang; mendarat atas lutut (mereka masih boleh mencapai); kekal menunduk dan bukannya bangun.","On mats, sprawl and pop back up on command, 3 × 10; then have a partner shoot slowly.":"Di tikar, turun ke bawah dan bangun semula apabila diberi arahan, 3 × 10; kemudian minta rakan melakukan tembakan (shoot) perlahan.","The sprawl lets a striker keep the fight standing.":"Sprawl membolehkan pemukul mengekalkan pertarungan dalam keadaan berdiri.","Ground and Pound (Mount)":"Ground and Pound (Kedudukan Mount)","Fists":"Penumbuk","KNEES TIGHT · WEIGHT LOW · SHORT STRIKES":"LUTUT RAPAT · BERAT BADAN RENDAH · PUKULAN PENDEK","In the mount you sit on an opponent lying on their back, knees tight to their sides and the tops of the feet on the mat. Get your weight low and balanced first, then posture up a little and throw short, fast strikes downward, bringing the hands back each time and staying balanced so they can't roll you. Many amateur events and most training sessions restrict or ban strikes to the head on the ground.":"Dalam kedudukan mount, anda duduk di atas lawan yang terlentang, lutut rapat ke sisi badannya dan belakang kaki di atas tikar. Rendahkan berat badan dan imbangkan dahulu, kemudian duduk sedikit tegak dan lepaskan tumbukan pendek dan pantas ke bawah, tarik tangan balik setiap kali dan kekal seimbang supaya anda tidak boleh diguling. Kebanyakan pertandingan amatur dan kebanyakan sesi latihan menghadkan atau melarang tumbukan ke kepala di lantai.","Sitting too tall (easy to roll); big swings that lose balance; striking without control; knees spread wide.":"Duduk terlalu tegak (mudah diguling); ayunan besar yang menyebabkan hilang imbangan; memukul tanpa kawalan; lutut terbuka luas.","On mats with a grappling dummy or a padded partner: hold the mount for 30 seconds while tapping light strikes.":"Di tikar dengan patung latihan gusti atau rakan yang memakai pelindung: tahan kedudukan mount selama 30 saat sambil mengetuk tumbukan ringan.","The mount is one of the best positions in MMA, and many fights end there.":"Mount ialah salah satu kedudukan terbaik dalam MMA, dan banyak pertarungan berakhir di situ.","Technical Stand-up":"Bangun Teknikal","Ground → standing":"Dari lantai → berdiri","Coordination and safety":"Koordinasi dan keselamatan","POST · LIFT THE HIPS · LEG BACK · STAND AT DISTANCE":"TOLAK · ANGKAT PINGGUL · KAKI KE BELAKANG · BANGUN DENGAN JARAK","Sitting on the floor, post one hand on the mat behind you with that leg straight, plant the other foot and guard your face with the free hand. Push off the posted hand and planted foot to lift your hips, swing the straight leg back underneath you and plant it, then rise into your stance at a safe distance. Keep your eyes on the opponent the whole time.":"Semasa duduk di lantai, letakkan sebelah tangan di tikar di belakang anda dengan kaki di sebelah itu lurus, jejakkan kaki yang satu lagi dan lindungi muka dengan tangan yang bebas. Tolak dengan tangan dan kaki yang menjejak untuk mengangkat punggung, ayunkan kaki yang lurus ke belakang di bawah badan dan jejakkan, kemudian bangun ke kedudukan dengan jarak yang selamat. Pandang lawan sepanjang masa.","Turning your back to crawl up; standing up head-first (easy to kick); ending up too close; posting the hand in front instead of behind.":"Membelakangkan lawan untuk merangkak bangun; bangun dengan kepala dahulu (mudah ditendang); berakhir terlalu dekat; meletakkan tangan di hadapan dan bukannya di belakang.","10 reps each side; once smooth, try it with a partner calling the side.":"10 ulangan setiap sisi; apabila sudah lancar, cuba dengan rakan yang menyebut sisinya.","Getting up safely after going down matters in MMA and in self-defence alike.":"Bangkit dengan selamat selepas jatuh adalah penting dalam MMA dan pertahanan diri.","Defends strikes and takedowns":"Mempertahankan diri daripada serangan dan jatuhan","Lower and wider than boxing":"Lebih rendah dan lebih lebar daripada tinju","The basic punching combination":"Gabungan tumbukan asas","Punch, then move":"Tumbuk, kemudian bergerak","One of MMA's most common power punches":"Antara tumbukan kuasa paling lazim dalam MMA","The head moves off line as you throw":"Kepala bergerak keluar dari garisan tengah semasa anda menumbuk","Slows the opponent's movement":"Melambatkan pergerakan lawan","Thigh or calf":"Paha atau betis","Takes the fight to the ground":"Membawa pertarungan ke lantai","Level change → penetrate → drive":"Tukar aras → tembus masuk → tolak","The basic takedown defence":"Pertahanan asas terhadap jatuhan","Legs back, hips down":"Kaki ke belakang, pinggul ke bawah","A dominant ground position":"Kedudukan dominan di lantai","Control first, then strike":"Kawal dahulu, kemudian serang","Getting up safely from the floor":"Bangun dengan selamat dari lantai","Useful in self-defence too":"Turut berguna dalam pertahanan diri","Feet a little wider than boxing, knees more bent, hips lower":"Kaki sedikit lebih lebar daripada tinju, lutut lebih ditekuk, pinggul lebih rendah","Hands guard the face but sit a little lower, ready to stop takedowns":"Tangan melindungi muka tetapi sedikit lebih rendah, sedia menghalang jatuhan","Ready for punches, kicks and takedowns at once":"Sedia untuk tumbukan, tendangan dan jatuhan sekaligus","Cross — pivot the back foot and turn the hips":"Tumbukan lurus — pusing kaki belakang dan pusing pinggul","Hands back up, ready to move":"Tangan kembali ke posisi, bersedia bergerak","Dip the head forward and off the centre line":"Tunduk kepala ke hadapan dan keluar dari garisan tengah","The rear hand loops up and over":"Tangan belakang melengkung ke atas dan ke hadapan","Come down over their guard onto the side of the head":"Turun melangkaui pertahanan lawan dan mengena di sisi kepala","Pivot the lead foot and swing the rear leg":"Pusingkan kaki hadapan dan ayunkan kaki belakang","Land the shin on their thigh or calf":"Daratkan tulang kering pada paha atau betis lawan","Recover the leg, hands up":"Tarik kaki kembali, tangan naik","Stance, at punching range":"Kedudukan, dalam jarak tumbukan","Level change: bend the knees, back straight, eyes forward":"Tukar aras: tekuk lutut, belakang lurus, mata ke hadapan","Penetration step: drop the lead knee between their feet, head tight to their side":"Langkah tembus: turunkan lutut depan di antara kaki lawan, kepala rapat ke sisinya","Grab behind both thighs and drive forward off your feet":"Pegang belakang kedua-dua paha dan tolak ke hadapan dengan kaki","They go down; you land on top in control":"Mereka jatuh; anda mendarat di atas dan mengawal keadaan","Stance; watch their hips":"Kuda-kuda; perhatikan pinggul lawan","They shoot low for your legs":"Mereka meluru rendah untuk menyerang kaki anda","Throw the legs back and drop the hips, putting your weight on their back":"Lontarkan kaki ke belakang dan turunkan pinggul, letakkan berat badan anda pada belakang mereka","Hands push down on their head and shoulders so they can't reach your legs":"Tolak tangan ke bawah pada kepala dan bahu mereka supaya mereka tidak dapat mencapai kaki anda","Get back up to your stance":"Bangkit semula ke kedudukan kuda-kuda anda","Mount: knees either side of their body, weight low":"Mount: lutut di kedua-dua belah badan mereka, berat badan rendah","Posture up a little and raise the rear hand":"Tegakkan badan sedikit dan angkat tangan belakang","Short, fast strikes downward, then bring the hand back":"Pukulan pendek dan laju ke bawah, kemudian tarik tangan kembali","Stay balanced so they can't roll you":"Kekal seimbang supaya mereka tidak dapat menggulingkan anda","Sitting: one hand posted behind, that leg straight, the other foot planted, front hand guarding the face":"Duduk: sebelah tangan menongkat di belakang, kaki itu lurus, kaki satu lagi dijejak, tangan depan melindungi muka","Push off the posted hand and planted foot to lift the hips":"Tolak dari tangan yang menongkat dan kaki yang dijejak untuk mengangkat pinggul","Swing the straight leg back under you and plant it behind":"Ayunkan kaki yang lurus ke belakang di bawah badan dan jejakkan di belakang","Stand up into your stance at a safe distance":"Bangun ke kedudukan kuda-kuda pada jarak yang selamat","Takedown readiness":"Kesediaan menahan bantingan","Arcing power":"Kuasa lengkung","Head movement":"Pergerakan kepala","Posture":"Postur","Hip strength":"Kekuatan pinggul","Conditioning":"Kecergasan","Hip pressure":"Tekanan pinggul","Accurate strikes":"Pukulan tepat","What is Muay Thai?":"Apakah itu Muay Thai?","Muay Thai is Thailand's national sport, known as the \"art of eight limbs\" because it strikes with eight points — two fists, two elbows, two knees and two shins — plus its own stand-up clinch. Before a fight, boxers perform the traditional Wai Kru Ram Muay to honour their teachers and tradition. Today it is one of the world's most popular stand-up combat sports and a key striking base for MMA.":"Muay Thai ialah sukan kebangsaan Thailand, dikenali sebagai “seni lapan anggota” kerana menyerang dengan lapan titik: dua penumbuk, dua siku, dua lutut dan dua betis, serta klinch berdiri tersendiri. Sebelum perlawanan, petinju mempersembahkan tarian tradisional Wai Kru Ram Muay untuk menghormati guru dan tradisi mereka. Kini ia antara sukan tempur berdiri paling popular di dunia dan asas serangan penting untuk MMA.","How is the stance different from boxing?":"Apakah bezanya pendirian dengan tinju?","Boxers only defend punches, so they stand more side-on with even weight. In Muay Thai you also face kicks, knees and elbows, so the stance is squarer, taller and weighted to the back leg, keeping the lead foot light to check kicks or teep.":"Peninju hanya perlu menahan tumbukan, jadi mereka berdiri lebih menyerong dengan berat badan sama rata. Dalam Muay Thai, anda juga perlu menghadapi tendangan, lutut dan siku, jadi pendirian lebih tegak, lebih tinggi dan berat badan ke kaki belakang, dengan kaki depan ringan untuk menahan tendangan atau teep.","Warm up with 5–10 minutes of skipping or jogging, then mobilise hips, ankles and shoulders.":"Panaskan badan 5–10 minit dengan melompat tali atau berjogging, kemudian gerakkan pinggul, buku lali dan bahu.","Get each technique right in the air or on the bag before adding speed and power.":"Betulkan setiap teknik di udara atau pada samsak sebelum menambah kelajuan dan kuasa.","Spar in gloves, a mouthguard and shin guards; throw elbows and knees only on pads or bags.":"Bersparring dengan sarung tangan, pelindung gigi dan pelindung betis; lontarkan siku dan lutut hanya pada pad atau samsak.","Shins toughen gradually with normal training — never strike hard objects to \"condition\" them.":"Betis akan menjadi kebal secara beransur-ansur melalui latihan biasa; jangan sekali-kali memukul objek keras untuk “melatihnya”.","Want stronger basic strikes? See <a href=\"../../kungfu/strikes/\">basic punches &amp; kicks</a>; for conditioning, try <a href=\"../../fitness/gym/\">the 10 gym basics</a>.":"Mahu tumbukan dan tendangan asas yang lebih kukuh? Lihat <a href=\"../../kungfu/strikes/\">tumbukan &amp; tendangan asas</a>; untuk kecergasan, cuba <a href=\"../../fitness/gym/\">10 asas gim</a>.","Why \"the art of eight limbs\"?":"Mengapa dipanggil “seni lapan anggota”?","Because it strikes with eight points: two fists, two elbows, two knees and two shins.":"Kerana ia menyerang dengan lapan titik: dua penumbuk, dua siku, dua lutut dan dua betis.","Do you kick with the foot or the shin?":"Adakah anda menendang dengan kaki atau betis?","The roundhouse and low kick land with the shin — far tougher than the foot and more powerful when the hip turns over.":"Tendangan roundhouse dan tendangan rendah dilakukan dengan tulang kering — jauh lebih tahan daripada kaki dan lebih kuat apabila pinggul diputar.","When can a beginner start sparring?":"Bilakah pemula boleh mula bersparing?","Usually after a few months of technique, pads and bag work, when your coach is happy you can control power and defend yourself — starting with light technical sparring.":"Biasanya selepas beberapa bulan latihan teknik, pad dan beg, apabila jurulatih berpuas hati bahawa anda boleh mengawal kekuatan dan mempertahankan diri — bermula dengan sparing teknikal yang ringan.","FIGHTING SPORTS · THAILAND'S ART OF EIGHT LIMBS":"SUKAN PERTARUNGAN · SENI LAPAN ANGGOTA DARI THAILAND","Muay Thai Basics: 10 Core Techniques, Step by Step":"Asas Muay Thai: 10 Teknik Utama, Langkah demi Langkah","Muay Thai strikes with eight limbs — fists, elbows, knees and shins — plus the clinch up close. Every technique is animated against a grey opponent, with a red ring at the point of contact. Click a step to freeze it; southpaws press SOUTHPAW.":"Muay Thai menyerang dengan lapan anggota — tinju, siku, lutut dan tulang kering — serta clinch pada jarak dekat. Setiap teknik dianimasikan terhadap lawan kelabu, dengan bulatan merah pada titik sentuhan. Klik satu langkah untuk membekukannya; pemain kidal tekan SOUTHPAW.","Fists — jab and cross":"Penumbuk — jab dan cross","Elbows — close range":"Siku — jarak dekat","Knees — from the clinch":"Lutut — dari clinch","Shins — kick and check":"Tulang kering — tendang dan tahan","Striking limbs":"Anggota serangan","Fists · elbows · knees · shins":"Penumbuk · siku · lutut · tulang kering","Pro bout format":"Format perlawanan profesional","5 rounds × 3 minutes (varies by event)":"5 pusingan × 3 minit (berbeza mengikut acara)","For education only; the animations are simplified. Muay Thai is a high-impact contact sport: train under a qualified coach and wear gloves, a mouthguard and shin guards for sparring; throw elbows and knees only on pads or bags.":"Untuk tujuan pendidikan sahaja; animasi dipermudah. Muay Thai ialah sukan kontak berimpak tinggi: berlatih di bawah jurulatih bertauliah dan pakai sarung tangan, pelindung gigi dan pelindung kaki semasa bersparing; siku dan lutut hanya dilancarkan pada pad atau beg.","Muay Thai Basics: Stance, Teep, Roundhouse, Elbow, Knee & Clinch — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"Asas Muay Thai: Kedudukan, Teep, Tendangan Sabit, Siku, Lutut & Clinch — Panduan Interaktif | KungfuTutor","Learn 10 Muay Thai fundamentals with animated demos against an opponent: stance, jab, cross, teep, roundhouse kick, low kick, elbow, clinch, knee and shin check — with common mistakes and drills.":"Pelajari 10 asas Muay Thai dengan demonstrasi animasi menentang lawan: kedudukan, jab, cross, teep, tendangan sabit, tendangan rendah, siku, clinch, lutut dan tangkisan tulang kering — dengan kesilapan lazim dan latihan.","Muay Thai Basics — The Art of Eight Limbs, Step by Step":"Asas Muay Thai — Seni Lapan Anggota, Langkah demi Langkah","Why is Muay Thai called the art of eight limbs?":"Mengapa Muay Thai dipanggil seni lapan anggota?","Because it strikes with eight points of contact: two fists, two elbows, two knees and two shins, plus clinch work to control the opponent.":"Kerana ia menyerang dengan lapan titik sentuhan: dua penumbuk, dua siku, dua lutut dan dua tulang kering, serta kerja clinch untuk mengawal lawan.","What is a teep in Muay Thai?":"Apakah teep dalam Muay Thai?","A push kick: lift the knee, then push the hips forward and drive the ball of the foot into the opponent's stomach or hips to stop them and restore distance.":"Tendangan tolak: angkat lutut, kemudian tolak pinggul ke hadapan dan tujah bahagian depan tapak kaki ke perut atau pinggul lawan untuk menghentikannya dan memulihkan jarak.","Do you kick with the foot or the shin in Muay Thai?":"Dalam Muay Thai, adakah anda menendang dengan kaki atau tulang kering?","The roundhouse and low kick land with the shin, which is far tougher than the foot and carries more power when the hip turns over.":"Tendangan sabit dan tendangan rendah mendarat dengan tulang kering, yang jauh lebih kuat daripada kaki dan membawa kuasa lebih besar apabila pinggul berpusing.","WEIGHT BACK · LIGHT LEAD FOOT · HANDS AT THE BROWS":"BERAT KE BELAKANG · KAKI HADAPAN RINGAN · TANGAN DI KENING","Stand with feet about shoulder-width, one foot ahead of the other (left foot forward for right-handers), facing the opponent more squarely than in boxing. Keep roughly 60–70% of your weight on the back leg so the lead foot is light and ready to check kicks or teep. Hold your hands up at brow height, elbows tight to the body, chin tucked, eyes on their chest and hips.":"Berdiri dengan kaki kira-kira selebar bahu, satu kaki di hadapan yang lain (kaki kiri di hadapan bagi pengguna tangan kanan), menghadap lawan lebih tegak berbanding tinju. Kekalkan kira-kira 60–70% berat badan pada kaki belakang supaya kaki hadapan ringan dan sedia menahan tendangan atau teep. Angkat tangan setinggi kening, siku rapat ke badan, dagu dirapatkan, dan mata tertumpu pada dada serta pinggul lawan.","Weight on the front foot (hard to check low kicks); dropping the hands; feet on one line so you lose balance; standing too side-on so the legs are easy targets.":"Berat di kaki hadapan (sukar menahan tendangan rendah); tangan jatuh; kaki sebaris sehingga hilang imbangan; berdiri terlalu menyerong sehingga kaki mudah disasar.","Hold your stance in a mirror for a minute, then bounce lightly forward and back without dropping the hands — 3 rounds.":"Tahan kedudukan di hadapan cermin selama 1 minit, kemudian lompat ringan ke depan dan ke belakang tanpa menurunkan tangan — 3 pusingan.","A Muay Thai stance has to deal with punches, kicks, elbows and knees, so it is squarer and more weighted to the back than a boxing stance.":"Kedudukan Muay Thai perlu menangani tumbukan, tendangan, siku dan lutut, jadi ia lebih tegak dan lebih berat ke belakang daripada kedudukan tinju.","Knuckles, lead hand":"Buku jari, tangan hadapan","Speed and distance":"Kelajuan dan jarak","STRAIGHT OUT · STRAIGHT BACK · SHOULDER COVERS CHIN":"LURUS KE HADAPAN · LURUS KEMBALI · BAHU MELINDUNGI DAGU","From your stance, shoot the lead hand straight out, turning it palm-down as it lands, with the lead shoulder raised to cover your chin and the other hand by your face. Snap it straight back to guard. A small step with the lead foot adds reach.":"Dari kedudukan, hulurkan tangan hadapan lurus ke depan, pusingkan telapak menghadap ke bawah ketika mendarat, dengan bahu hadapan dinaikkan untuk melindungi dagu dan tangan satu lagi di sebelah muka. Tarik balik lurus ke kedudukan pertahanan. Langkah kecil dengan kaki hadapan menambah jarak capaian.","Pulling back before punching (telegraphing); dropping the hand afterwards; the rear hand leaving the face; leaning forward.":"Menarik tangan ke belakang sebelum menumbuk (memberi isyarat); menurunkan tangan selepas itu; tangan belakang meninggalkan muka; condong ke hadapan.","3 × 2-minute rounds of jabs on a bag or in a mirror — fast out, fast back.":"3 pusingan × 2 minit jab pada beg tumbuk atau di hadapan cermin — cepat keluar, cepat balik.","The jab measures distance, blinds the opponent and sets up the cross or a kick.":"Jab digunakan untuk mengukur jarak, mengganggu penglihatan lawan dan membuka peluang untuk cross atau tendangan.","Knuckles, rear hand":"Buku jari, tangan belakang","PIVOT THE BACK HEEL · TURN THE HIPS · LEAD HAND GUARDS":"PUSINGKAN TUMIT BELAKANG · PUSINGKAN PINGGUL · TANGAN DEPAN MELINDUNGI","From your stance, turn the back heel out so the hips and shoulders rotate forward, and drive the rear hand straight out — power travels from the floor through the hips to the fist. The lead hand stays by your face. Return along the same line to your stance.":"Dari kedudukan, pusingkan tumit belakang ke luar supaya pinggul dan bahu berpusing ke hadapan, dan tolak tangan belakang lurus ke hadapan — kuasa mengalir dari lantai melalui pinggul ke penumbuk. Tangan depan kekal di hadapan muka. Tarik balik mengikut laluan yang sama ke kedudukan asal.","Arm-only punching; not turning the back heel; dropping the lead hand; leaving your weight out front.":"Hanya menumbuk dengan lengan; tidak memusingkan tumit belakang; menurunkan tangan depan; berat badan tertinggal di hadapan.","Jab–cross combinations on the bag, 3 × 2-minute rounds.":"Kombinasi jab–cross pada beg, 3 pusingan × 2 minit.","The cross is the most common power punch and often leads straight into a rear kick.":"Cross ialah tumbukan kuat yang paling biasa, dan sering terus diikuti tendangan belakang.","Teep (Push Kick)":"Teep (Tendangan Tolak)","Ball of the foot":"Bahagian depan tapak kaki","KNEE UP FIRST · PUSH THE HIPS · BALL OF THE FOOT":"LUTUT DINAIKKAN DAHULU · TOLAK PINGGUL · BAHAGIAN DEPAN TAPAK KAKI","From your stance, lift the lead knee to waist height, then push the hips forward and straighten the leg, driving the ball of the foot into their stomach or hips. Lean back slightly and keep the hands up. Re-chamber the knee before setting the foot down.":"Dari kedudukan, angkat lutut depan hingga paras pinggang, kemudian tolak pinggul ke hadapan dan luruskan kaki, tolak dengan bahagian depan tapak kaki ke perut atau pinggul lawan. Condongkan badan sedikit ke belakang dan kekalkan tangan di atas. Tarik semula lutut ke kedudukan angkat sebelum meletakkan kaki.","Swinging the leg without lifting the knee (like kicking a ball); no hip push; dropping the hands; slow recovery.":"Mengayunkan kaki tanpa mengangkat lutut (seperti menendang bola); tiada tolakan pinggul; tangan jatuh; pemulihan lambat.","On a bag or pad, 3 × 10 per leg, feeling the hips push.":"Pada beg atau sasaran, 3 set × 10 bagi setiap kaki, rasai tolakan pinggul.","The teep stops the opponent coming forward, restores distance and breaks balance — Muay Thai's key defensive and offensive kick.":"Teep menghentikan lawan yang menerpa, memulihkan jarak dan memecahkan keseimbangan — tendangan utama bertahan dan menyerang dalam Muay Thai.","Explosive hip rotation":"Putaran pinggul yang meletup","PIVOT · TURN THE HIP OVER · LAND THE SHIN · ARM SWINGS BACK":"PUSINGKAN KAKI · PUSINGKAN PINGGUL · MENDARAT DENGAN TULANG KERING · LENGAN AYUN KE BELAKANG","Turn the lead foot out onto the ball of the foot and swing the rear leg up and across while turning the hip right over, landing with the shin on the side of their body. The arm on the kicking side swings down and back to help you turn while the other hand guards your head. Let the leg return to your stance.":"Pusingkan kaki depan ke luar ke bahagian bola kaki dan ayunkan kaki belakang ke atas dan melintang sambil memusingkan pinggul sepenuhnya, mendarat dengan batang kaki di sisi badan lawan. Lengan di sebelah tendangan diayun ke bawah dan ke belakang untuk membantu pusingan, manakala tangan satu lagi melindungi kepala. Biarkan kaki kembali ke kedudukan asal.","Not pivoting the lead foot (no power, strains the knee); kicking with the top of the foot (easy to injure); not turning the hip over; dropping both hands.":"Tidak memusingkan kaki depan (tiada kuasa, tegang pada lutut); menendang dengan atas kaki (mudah cedera); tidak memusingkan pinggul; kedua-dua tangan jatuh.","Slow pivots and hip turns holding a wall, 10 reps, then 3 × 10 per leg on the bag.":"Latihan perlahan memusing kaki dan pinggul sambil berpaut pada dinding, 10 kali, kemudian pada beg tinju 3 × 10 setiap kaki.","The Muay Thai roundhouse lands with the shin and carries huge power — a main scoring weapon in fights.":"Tendangan roundhouse Muay Thai mendarat dengan batang kaki dan menghasilkan kuasa yang besar, senjata utama untuk mendapat mata dalam pertarungan.","Outside of the thigh":"Bahagian luar paha","PIVOT · CHOP DOWN · OUTSIDE OF THE THIGH":"PUSING · TEBAS KE BAWAH · BAHAGIAN LUAR PAHA","Pivot and turn the hip just like the roundhouse, but angle the kick slightly downward and chop the lower shin into the outside of their thigh. It works best straight after punches, while their attention is up high.":"Pusingkan kaki dan pinggul seperti tendangan roundhouse, tetapi condongkan tendangan sedikit ke bawah dan tetak bahagian bawah batang kaki ke bahagian luar paha lawan. Paling berkesan dilakukan selepas tumbukan, ketika perhatian lawan tertumpu ke atas.","Throwing it when they are set to check; kicking with the foot or ankle; losing balance afterwards.":"Melepaskannya ketika lawan bersedia menahan; menendang dengan kaki atau buku lali; hilang imbangan selepas itu.","Jab–cross–low kick combinations, 3 × 2-minute rounds.":"Gabungan jab–cross–tendangan rendah, 3 pusingan × 2 minit.","Low kicks add up — heavy legs and lost balance — a key way to wear an opponent down.":"Tendangan rendah terkumpul kesannya: kaki lawan menjadi berat dan hilang imbangan, cara utama untuk melemahkan lawan.","Horizontal Elbow":"Siku Mendatar","Side of the face, brow":"Sisi muka, kening","ARM FOLDED · ELBOW LEVEL · TURN THE HIPS":"LENGAN DILIPAT · SIKU SEPARAS · PUSING PINGGUL","At closer than punching range, fold the arm tight with the hand near your own head, turn the hips and shoulders, and slice the elbow level across the side of their face or brow. The other hand guards your head. Return to the guard immediately.":"Pada jarak yang lebih dekat daripada jarak tumbukan, lipat lengan rapat dengan tangan berhampiran kepala sendiri, pusing pinggul dan bahu, dan hiris siku secara mendatar ke sisi muka atau kening lawan. Tangan satu lagi melindungi kepala. Kembali ke posisi pertahanan dengan segera.","Throwing from too far (it falls short); not folding the arm; swinging the arm without turning the body; not returning to guard.":"Melontar dari jarak terlalu jauh (tidak sampai); tidak melipat lengan; mengayun lengan tanpa memusingkan badan; tidak kembali ke posisi pertahanan.","Slow horizontal elbows on pads, 10 each side; later chain them after hooks or from the clinch.":"Latih siku mendatar perlahan pada pad, 10 kali setiap sisi; kemudian sambungkan selepas cangkukan atau dari clinch.","Elbows cut easily and can end fights up close; many amateur events ban or restrict them.":"Siku mudah menyebabkan luka koyak dan boleh menamatkan pertarungan dari jarak dekat; banyak acara amatur melarang atau menghadkannya.","The Clinch (Plum)":"Clinch (Plum)","Clinch":"Clinch","Hands behind the head":"Tangan di belakang kepala","Head control":"Kawalan kepala","HANDS INSIDE · ONE OVER THE OTHER · ELBOWS SQUEEZE":"TANGAN DI DALAM · SATU DI ATAS SATU LAGI · SIKU DIHIMPIT","When chest to chest, bring both hands up the inside of their arms and cup them one over the other behind their head (don't interlace the fingers). Squeeze the elbows together onto their collarbones and pull the head down so they lose posture and balance.":"Apabila dada bertemu dada, angkat kedua-dua tangan di bahagian dalam lengan lawan dan letakkan satu di atas yang lain di belakang kepalanya (jangan jalinkan jari). Himpit siku ke dalam pada tulang selangka lawan, dan tarik kepalanya ke bawah supaya dia hilang postur dan keseimbangan.","Interlacing the fingers (they get hurt); flaring the elbows so they slip out; pulling with the arms only; letting your posture drop below theirs.":"Menjalinkan jari (jari boleh cedera); siku terbuka sehingga lawan boleh terlepas; hanya menarik dengan lengan tanpa badan; badan lebih rendah daripada lawan.","With a partner, take turns: enter the clinch → pull down → release, slowly and gently, a minute at a time.":"Bersama pasangan, bergilir-gilir berlatih: masuk ke clinch → tarik ke bawah → lepaskan, perlahan dan lembut, selama seminit setiap kali.","The clinch controls the opponent up close and sets up knees and off-balancing sweeps.":"Clinch membolehkan anda mengawal lawan dari jarak dekat dan membuka peluang untuk tendangan lutut serta sapuan menjatuhkan.","Straight Knee":"Lutut Lurus","Stomach, ribs":"Perut, rusuk","PULL THE HEAD DOWN · HIPS FORWARD · KNEE UP AND IN":"TARIK KEPALA KE BAWAH · PINGGUL KE HADAPAN · LUTUT NAIK DAN MASUK","In the clinch, pull their head down while drawing the rear leg back to load, then drive the hips forward and the knee up and in to their stomach or ribs, toes pointing down. Lean back slightly for balance and keep controlling the head with both hands.":"Dalam clinch, tarik kepala lawan ke bawah sambil menarik kaki belakang ke belakang untuk mengumpul tenaga, kemudian tolak pinggul ke hadapan dan naikkan lutut ke hadapan-atas ke perut atau rusuk lawan, hujung kaki menghala ke bawah. Condongkan badan sedikit ke belakang untuk imbangan dan terus kawal kepala dengan kedua-dua tangan.","Lifting the leg without pushing the hips; leaning forward into a head clash; letting go of the head; an unstable support leg.":"Hanya mengangkat kaki tanpa menolak pinggul; condong ke hadapan sehingga kepala berlanggar; melepaskan kawalan kepala; kaki penyokong yang tidak stabil.","3 × 10 knees per leg on a bag or knee pad, then light touch knees with a partner in the clinch.":"3 × 10 lutut setiap kaki pada beg atau pad lutut, kemudian latihan lutut ringan dengan rakan dalam clinch.","Straight knees are short and powerful; many Muay Thai fights are won with them in the clinch.":"Lutut lurus itu pendek dan bertenaga; banyak perlawanan Muay Thai dimenangi dengannya dalam clinch.","Check (Shin Block)":"Check (Tangkisan Tulang Kering)","Shin, lead leg":"Tulang kering, kaki depan","Block their kick":"Tangkis tendangan lawan","Reaction and balance":"Reaksi dan imbangan","KNEE UP · TURN IT OUT · HANDS STAY UP":"LUTUT NAIK · PUSING KELUAR · TANGAN KEKAL DI ATAS","As soon as you see their hip turn for a kick, lift the knee on that side and turn it slightly outward so your shin meets their kick. Keep the support leg slightly bent and both hands up. Plant the foot and fire back straight away.":"Apabila melihat pinggul lawan berpusing untuk menendang, angkat lutut di sebelah yang disasarkan dan pusingkan sedikit ke luar supaya tulang kering anda menahan tendangan lawan. Kekalkan kaki penyokong sedikit bengkok dan kedua-dua tangan di atas. Selepas menahan, jejakkan kaki dan balas serta-merta.","Watching the foot instead of the hips (too slow); a low knee so the thigh gets hit; dropping the hands; losing balance after the block.":"Hanya melihat kaki, bukan pinggul (terlalu perlahan); lutut terlalu rendah sehingga paha terkena; tangan jatuh; hilang imbangan selepas menahan.","Your partner throws slow, light kicks while you check, 10 each side; then add a counter after each check.":"Rakan anda menendang perlahan dan ringan semasa anda berlatih menahan dengan lutut, 10 kali setiap sisi; apabila mahir, tambah serangan balas selepas setiap tahanan.","Checking protects your legs and hurts the kicker's shin, making them think twice.":"Menahan tendangan melindungi kaki anda dan membuatkan tulang kering penendang sakit, sehingga lawan tidak berani menendang sewenang-wenangnya.","Where every technique starts":"Titik permulaan setiap teknik","High guard · weight back":"Pertahanan tangan tinggi · berat badan ke belakang","The fastest, most-used punch":"Tumbukan paling pantas dan paling kerap digunakan","Measures distance, sets things up":"Mengukur jarak, menyediakan laluan","The power straight punch":"Tumbukan lurus yang berkuasa","Turn foot, hip and shoulder":"Pusingkan kaki, pinggul dan bahu","Muay Thai's \"jab with the leg\"":"\"Jab dengan kaki\" Muay Thai","Pushes distance, breaks rhythm":"Menolak jarak, memecah irama","The signature Muay Thai kick":"Tendangan ikonik Muay Thai","Shin, not the foot":"Guna tulang kering, bukan kaki","Breaks down the legs":"Melemahkan kaki lawan","Chops downward":"Mencincang ke bawah","The sharpest close-range weapon":"Senjata paling tajam dalam jarak dekat","Driven by the hips":"Digerakkan oleh pinggul","Muay Thai's unique stand-up grappling":"Gusti berdiri khas Muay Thai","Control the head, control the body":"Kawal kepala, kawal badan","The main attack from the clinch":"Serangan utama dari clinch","Drive the hips forward":"Tolak pinggul ke hadapan","The standard defence to leg kicks":"Pertahanan standard terhadap tendangan kaki","Shin meets shin":"Tulang kering bertemu tulang kering","Feet about shoulder-width, one in front of the other, weight mostly on the back leg":"Kaki kira-kira selebar bahu, satu di hadapan yang lain, berat badan kebanyakannya pada kaki belakang","The lead foot stays light, ready to lift for a check or a teep":"Kaki hadapan kekal ringan, bersedia diangkat untuk menahan atau Teep","Hands up by the brows, elbows tight, chin tucked":"Tangan naik ke kening, siku rapat, dagu dirapatkan","Snap the lead hand straight out, shoulder up to protect the chin":"Hentam pantas dengan tangan hadapan lurus ke depan, bahu dinaikkan melindungi dagu","Bring it straight back to guard the face":"Tarik balik lurus untuk melindungi muka","Turn the back heel, hips and shoulders and drive the rear hand straight out":"Pusingkan tumit belakang, pinggul dan bahu, dan hentak tangan belakang lurus ke depan","Return — the lead hand guards the face the whole time":"Kembali — tangan hadapan sentiasa melindungi muka","Push the hips forward and drive the ball of the foot into their stomach":"Tolak pinggul ke hadapan dan tolak bebola kaki ke perut lawan","Re-chamber the knee":"Tarik semula lutut ke kedudukan sedia","Back to stance with the distance restored":"Kembali ke kedudukan asal dengan jarak yang dipulihkan","Pivot on the lead foot (toes turn out) and swing the rear leg up":"Pusingkan kaki hadapan (hujung kaki menghala ke luar) dan ayunkan kaki belakang ke atas","Turn the hip over and land with the shin on the body; the rear arm swings down and back":"Pusingkan pinggul dan mendarat dengan tulang kering pada badan lawan; lengan belakang berayun ke bawah dan ke belakang","Let the leg come back":"Biarkan kaki kembali","Back to stance, hands up":"Kembali ke kedudukan, tangan naik","Chop down with the shin into the outside of their thigh":"Libas ke bawah dengan tulang kering ke bahagian luar paha lawan","Close range — the opponent is inside punching distance":"Jarak dekat — lawan berada dalam jarak tumbukan","Draw the lead elbow back and load the hips":"Tarik siku hadapan ke belakang dan sediakan pinggul","Turn the hips and slice the elbow level across the side of the face":"Pusingkan pinggul dan hiris siku secara mendatar merentasi sisi muka","The opponent is chest to chest":"Lawan berada dada ke dada","Slide both hands up the inside and cup them, one over the other, behind their head":"Luncurkan kedua-dua tangan ke atas dari bahagian dalam, dan satukan dengan satu di atas yang lain di belakang kepalanya","Squeeze the elbows together on their collarbones and pull the head down":"Rapatkan siku pada tulang kolar lawan dan tarik kepalanya ke bawah","Hold the control — they lose their posture and balance":"Kekalkan kawalan, lawan akan hilang postur dan imbangannya","Control the head in the clinch":"Kawal kepala lawan dalam klinc","Draw the rear leg back to load":"Tarik kaki belakang ke belakang untuk bersedia","Drive the hips forward and the knee up and in to the stomach":"Tolak pinggul ke hadapan dan naikkan lutut ke atas, masuk ke perut","Return the leg, keep the clinch":"Kembalikan kaki, kekalkan klinc","They start a low kick":"Lawan mula menendang rendah","Lift the lead knee, turn it out and block with the shin":"Angkat lutut depan, pusingkan ke luar dan tangkis dengan batang kaki","Hands stay up the whole time":"Tangan kekal di atas sepanjang masa","Plant the foot, ready to fire back":"Pijakkan kaki, bersedia membalas","Distance":"Jarak","Shoulders":"Bahu","Setting it up":"Menyediakan serangan","Grip & squeeze":"Genggaman & himpitan","Core":"Teras (core)","Shin structure":"Struktur batang kaki","Squat":"Squat","Legs · push":"Kaki · tolak","Quads, glutes, core":"Quad, punggung (glutes), teras","Barbell (beginner: bodyweight to a box)":"Bar berat (pemula: berat badan ke kotak)","3–5 sets × 5–10 reps":"3–5 set × 5–10 ulangan","FLAT BACK · KNEES OVER TOES · WHOLE-FOOT DRIVE":"BELAKANG LURUS · LUTUT MENGHALA KE HUJUNG JARI · TOLAK DENGAN SELURUH KAKI","Stand with feet about shoulder-width, toes turned slightly out, and the bar resting on your upper back. Breathe in and brace your core, then sit the hips back and down while pushing the knees out over the toes until your thighs are at least parallel to the floor. Keep your back flat and heels down, then drive up through the whole foot as you breathe out. The bar should stay over the middle of your foot.":"Berdiri dengan kaki kira-kira selebar bahu, hujung jari sedikit terkeluar, dan bar diletakkan di belakang bahagian atas badan. Tarik nafas dan kukuhkan teras badan, kemudian tolak pinggul ke belakang dan ke bawah sambil menolak lutut ke luar melewati hujung jari sehingga paha sekurang-kurangnya selari dengan lantai. Kekalkan belakang lurus dan tumit di lantai, kemudian tolak ke atas melalui seluruh kaki sambil menghembus nafas. Bar hendaklah kekal di atas bahagian tengah kaki.","Knees caving in; heels lifting; rounding the back or cranking the head up; half-depth reps; hips shooting up first so it turns into a good-morning.":"Lutut masuk ke dalam; tumit terangkat; belakang membongkok atau kepala didongakkan; ulangan separuh kedalaman; pinggul naik dahulu sehingga bertukar menjadi good-morning.","Start with bodyweight squats to a box, 3 × 10; once steady, learn with an empty bar (20 kg) and add weight in small steps.":"Mulakan dengan squat berat badan ke kotak, 3 × 10; apabila sudah stabil, belajar dengan bar kosong (20 kg) dan tambah berat sedikit demi sedikit.","Squats build leg and core strength and underpin everyday movements like sitting, standing and lifting.":"Squat membina kekuatan kaki dan teras badan, dan menjadi asas pergerakan harian seperti duduk, berdiri dan mengangkat.","Deadlift":"Deadlift","Posterior chain · pull":"Rantai posterior · tarik","Glutes, hamstrings, back":"Gluteus, hamstring, belakang","Barbell":"Bar besi","3–5 sets × 3–6 reps":"3–5 set × 3–6 ulangan","BAR OVER MID-FOOT · FLAT BACK · BAR STAYS CLOSE":"BAR DI ATAS TENGAH KAKI · BELAKANG LURUS · BAR KEKAL DEKAT","Stand with feet hip-width and the bar over the middle of your feet. Hinge and bend the knees to grip the bar with shins touching it, back flat and shoulders just in front of the bar. Brace and stand up as if pushing the floor away, keeping the bar against your legs. Once past the knees, drive the hips forward to stand tall. To lower, push the hips back first and follow the same path down.":"Berdiri dengan kaki selebar pinggul dan bar di atas tengah kaki. Engsel pinggul dan bengkokkan lutut untuk memegang bar dengan tulang kering menyentuhnya, belakang lurus dan bahu sedikit di hadapan bar. Kuatkan badan dan berdiri seolah-olah menolak lantai ke bawah, sambil memastikan bar sentiasa rapat dengan kaki. Selepas melepasi lutut, tolak pinggul ke hadapan untuk berdiri tegak. Untuk menurunkan, tolak pinggul ke belakang dahulu dan ikut laluan yang sama.","Rounding the back; letting the bar drift away from the body; hips rising first; leaning back at the top; pulling with the arms.":"Membongkokkan belakang; membiarkan bar menjauhi badan; pinggul naik dahulu; condong ke belakang di bahagian atas; menarik dengan lengan.","Practise the hip hinge with a broomstick or empty bar, 3 × 10, before adding weight; start every rep from a dead stop.":"Latih engsel pinggul dengan batang penyapu atau bar kosong, 3 × 10, sebelum menambah berat; mulakan setiap ulangan dari keadaan pegun sepenuhnya.","The deadlift trains the whole back of the body and is the safe way to pick heavy things off the floor.":"Deadlift melatih seluruh bahagian belakang badan dan merupakan cara selamat untuk mengangkat barang berat dari lantai.","Bench Press":"Tekan bangku","Upper body · push":"Badan atas · tolak","Chest, triceps, front shoulders":"Dada, trisep, bahu hadapan","Barbell, bench (use a spotter)":"Bar besi, bangku (gunakan pembantu keselamatan)","BLADES SQUEEZED · ELBOWS ~45° · TOUCH THE LOWER CHEST":"BELIKAT DIRAPATKAN · SIKU ~45° · SENTUH BAHAGIAN BAWAH DADA","Lie on the bench with your eyes under the bar and feet planted. Grip a little wider than shoulder-width and squeeze your shoulder blades back and down. Unrack the bar over your shoulders, lower it under control to touch the lower chest with elbows about 45° from your body, then press it back up, drifting slightly towards the shoulders.":"Baring di atas bangku dengan mata di bawah bar dan kaki kukuh di lantai. Genggam sedikit lebih lebar daripada bahu dan kuncupkan bilah bahu ke belakang dan ke bawah. Angkat bar dari rak di atas bahu, turunkan dengan terkawal hingga menyentuh dada bawah dengan siku kira-kira 45° dari badan, kemudian tolak kembali ke atas, sedikit ke arah bahu.","Flaring elbows to 90° (hard on the shoulders); bouncing the bar off the chest; lifting the hips off the bench; bending the wrists back.":"Siku melebar hingga 90° (membebankan bahu); memantulkan bar di dada; mengangkat punggung dari bangku; melentur pergelangan tangan ke belakang.","Start with an empty bar or dumbbells, 3 × 10; always use a spotter or a rack with safety bars.":"Mulakan dengan bar kosong atau dumbel, 3 × 10; sentiasa gunakan pembantu (spotter) atau rak dengan bar keselamatan.","The bench press is one of the most effective builders of chest and arm pushing strength.":"Tekan bangku ialah antara cara paling berkesan untuk membina kekuatan tolakan dada dan lengan.","Overhead Press":"Tekan Atas Kepala","Shoulders, triceps, core":"Bahu, trisep, teras","Barbell (or dumbbells)":"Bar (atau dumbel)","3–5 sets × 5–8 reps":"3–5 set × 5–8 ulangan","GLUTES & CORE TIGHT · STRAIGHT BAR PATH · HEAD THROUGH":"PUNGGUNG & TERAS KETAT · LALUAN BAR LURUS · KEPALA MENEMBUS","Stand with feet hip-width, the bar resting on the front of your shoulders and elbows under and slightly in front of it. Squeeze glutes and core, tip your head back slightly to clear a path, and press the bar straight up. Once it passes your forehead, bring your head through between your arms and lock out directly overhead.":"Berdiri dengan kaki selebar pinggul, bar diletakkan di hadapan bahu dan siku berada di bawah serta sedikit ke hadapan bar. Kuncupkan punggung dan teras, dongakkan kepala sedikit ke belakang untuk memberi laluan, dan tolak bar lurus ke atas. Apabila bar melepasi dahi, bawa kepala ke hadapan melalui celah lengan dan kunci di atas kepala betul-betul di atasnya.","Leaning back and arching the lower back; pressing the bar forward around the face; flared elbows; dipping the knees to cheat.":"Condong ke belakang dan melengkungkan pinggang bawah; menolak bar ke hadapan melepasi muka; siku terbuka luas; menekuk lutut untuk menipu.","Start with an empty bar or light dumbbells, 3 × 8, and check side-on in a mirror that the bar travels straight up.":"Mulakan dengan bar kosong atau dumbel ringan, 3 × 8, dan semak dari sisi di hadapan cermin sama ada bar bergerak lurus ke atas.","The press builds shoulder strength and core stability — the same move as lifting a case into an overhead locker.":"Tekanan menguatkan bahu dan kestabilan teras, gerakan yang sama seperti mengangkat beg ke ruang simpanan atas kepala.","Bent-over Row":"Dayung Membongkok","Upper body · pull":"Badan atas · tarik","Lats, mid-back, biceps":"Latissimus, belakang tengah, bisep","3–4 sets × 8–12 reps":"3–4 set × 8–12 ulangan","HINGE · FLAT BACK · ELBOWS DRIVE BACK":"PINGGUL MEMBONGKOK · BELAKANG RATA · SIKU DITARIK KE BELAKANG","Hold the bar, soften the knees and hinge at the hips until your torso is about 45° with a flat back and the arms hanging. Drive the elbows back and up, squeezing the shoulder blades, until the bar touches your upper stomach, then lower slowly. Your torso angle stays the same throughout.":"Pegang bar, lenturkan lutut sedikit dan bongkokkan pinggul sehingga badan condong sekitar 45° dengan belakang rata dan lengan tergantung. Tarik siku ke belakang dan ke atas sambil rapatkan bilah bahu, sehingga bar menyentuh bahagian atas perut, kemudian turunkan perlahan. Sudut badan kekal sama sepanjang pergerakan.","Swinging the body to heave the weight; rounding the back; shrugging the shoulders; cutting the range short.":"Mengayun badan untuk mengangkat beban; membundarkan belakang; menjongkitkan bahu; memendekkan julat pergerakan.","Learn the elbow drive with one-arm dumbbell rows, one hand on a bench, 3 × 10 each side.":"Pelajari tarikan siku dengan dayung dumbel satu lengan, satu tangan di atas bangku, 3 × 10 setiap sisi.","Rows balance all the pushing (like the bench press), keeping shoulders healthy and posture upright.":"Dayung mengimbangi semua gerakan tolak (seperti bench press), menjaga bahu kekal sihat dan postur tegak.","Pull-up":"Tarik Atas","Lats, biceps, grip":"Latissimus, bisep, genggaman","Pull-up bar (beginner: box for negatives)":"Palang tarik (pemula: kotak untuk negatif)","3–5 sets × as many good reps as you can":"3–5 set × seberapa banyak ulangan yang baik boleh dilakukan","SHOULDERS DOWN · ELBOWS DOWN & BACK · CHIN OVER":"BAHU TURUN DAHULU · SIKU TURUN & KE BELAKANG · DAGU MELEPASI PALANG","Grip the bar a little wider than your shoulders, palms facing forward, and hang with straight arms. First pull your shoulders down away from your ears, then drive the elbows down and back until your chin clears the bar, and lower under control to straight arms.":"Genggam palang sedikit lebih lebar daripada bahu, telapak tangan menghadap ke depan, dan gantung dengan lengan lurus. Mula-mula turunkan bahu menjauhi telinga, kemudian tarik siku ke bawah dan ke belakang sehingga dagu melepasi palang, dan turunkan perlahan-lahan dengan terkawal hingga lengan lurus.","Kicking and swinging for momentum; half reps; dropping down fast; shrugging the shoulders up.":"Menendang dan mengayun untuk momentum; ulangan separuh; turun terlalu pantas; menjongkitkan bahu.","Can't do one yet? Choose Beginner: step up to the top and lower slowly over 3–5 seconds, 3 × 5, or use a resistance band.":"Belum mampu satu pun? Pilih Pemula: naik ke atas dan turun perlahan selama 3–5 saat, 3 × 5, atau gunakan tali rintangan.","The pull-up is one of the best upper-body pulling exercises and builds a strong grip.":"Tarik-up ialah antara latihan tarikan badan atas yang terbaik dan membina genggaman yang kuat.","Push-up":"Tekan tubi","Chest, triceps, core":"Dada, trisep, teras","None (beginner: from the knees)":"Tiada peralatan (pemula: dari lutut)","3 sets × 8–20 reps":"3 set × 8–20 ulangan","HANDS UNDER SHOULDERS · ONE STRAIGHT LINE · ELBOWS 45°":"TANGAN DI BAWAH BAHU · SATU GARIS LURUS · SIKU 45°","Place your hands just wider than and under your shoulders, with a straight line from head to heels and your stomach and glutes tight. Bend the elbows back at about 45° and lower your whole body together until your chest is just above the floor, then push the floor away to return.":"Letakkan tangan sedikit lebih lebar daripada dan di bawah bahu, dengan garisan lurus dari kepala ke tumit serta perut dan punggung bawah diketatkan. Bengkokkan siku ke belakang kira-kira 45° dan turunkan seluruh badan bersama-sama sehingga dada hampir dengan lantai, kemudian tolak lantai untuk kembali.","Hips sagging or piking up; elbows flared into a T; dipping only the head; not going low enough.":"Pinggul terkulai atau terangkat; siku terkembang membentuk T; hanya menunduk kepala; tidak turun cukup rendah.","If full push-ups are too hard, choose Beginner (from the knees) or put your hands on a table edge, 3 × 10.":"Jika tekan tubi penuh terlalu sukar, pilih Pemula (dari lutut) atau letakkan tangan di tepi meja, 3 × 10.","Push-ups train pushing strength and core stability together — the best equipment-free upper-body move.":"Tekan tubi melatih kekuatan tolak dan kestabilan teras serentak, pergerakan badan atas tanpa peralatan yang terbaik.","Reverse Lunge":"Lunge Undur","Legs · single-leg":"Kaki · satu kaki","Quads, glutes, balance":"Kuadriseps, punggung, keseimbangan","None (dumbbells optional)":"Tiada peralatan (dumbbell pilihan)","3 sets × 8–12 per leg":"3 set × 8–12 setiap kaki","STEP BACK · DROP STRAIGHT DOWN · FRONT KNEE OVER ANKLE":"LANGKAH KE BELAKANG · TURUN LURUS KE BAWAH · LUTUT HADAPAN DI ATAS PERGELANGAN KAKI","Stand with feet hip-width. Take a long step back with one foot and, keeping the front foot planted, drop straight down until the back knee nearly touches the floor and the front thigh is about parallel, front knee over the ankle. Push through the whole front foot to return to standing, then switch legs.":"Berdiri dengan kaki selebar pinggul. Ambil langkah panjang ke belakang dengan satu kaki dan, dengan kaki hadapan kekal di tempatnya, turunkan badan lurus ke bawah sehingga lutut belakang hampir menyentuh lantai dan paha hadapan kira-kira selari, lutut hadapan di atas buku lali. Tolak melalui keseluruhan tapak kaki hadapan untuk kembali berdiri, kemudian tukar kaki.","Too short a step so the front knee shoots far forward; folding the chest down; front knee caving in; slamming the back knee into the floor.":"Langkah terlalu pendek menyebabkan lutut depan tertolak jauh ke hadapan; dada membongkok ke bawah; lutut depan masuk ke dalam; lutut belakang terhentak ke lantai.","Hold a wall or chair for balance, 3 × 8 per leg; once steady, hold dumbbells for extra load.":"Pegang dinding atau kerusi untuk imbangan, 3 × 8 setiap kaki; setelah stabil, pegang dumbel untuk menambah beban.","Single-leg work builds balance and evens out left–right strength — great for running and climbing stairs.":"Latihan satu kaki membina imbangan dan menyamakan kekuatan kiri-kanan — bagus untuk berlari dan menaiki tangga.","Plank":"Plank","Core · hold":"Teras · tahan","Abs, glutes, shoulders":"Abdomen, punggung bawah, bahu","Exercise mat":"Tikar senaman","3 sets × 20–60 seconds":"3 set × 20–60 saat","ELBOWS UNDER SHOULDERS · HEAD TO HEELS IN LINE · BREATHE":"SIKU DI BAWAH BAHU · KEPALA HINGGA TUMIT SELARAS · BERNAFAS","Rest on your forearms with elbows directly under your shoulders, start on your knees, then lift them so head, shoulders, hips and heels form one straight line. Squeeze your stomach and glutes, look at the floor, breathe normally and hold.":"Bertumpu pada lengan bawah dengan siku tepat di bawah bahu, mulakan dengan lutut di lantai, kemudian angkat supaya kepala, bahu, pinggul dan tumit membentuk satu garis lurus. Kecutkan perut dan punggung bawah, pandang lantai, bernafas seperti biasa dan tahan.","Letting the hips sag (hurts the lower back); hips piked up high; holding your breath; lifting or dropping the head.":"Pinggul terjatuh (menyakitkan punggung bawah); pinggul terangkat terlalu tinggi; menahan nafas; mengangkat atau menjatuhkan kepala.","Use the timer below starting at 20 seconds and add 5–10 seconds a week; stop when your form slips — quality beats time.":"Gunakan pemasa di bawah bermula dari 20 saat dan tambah 5–10 saat setiap minggu; berhenti apabila postur mula longgar — kualiti lebih penting daripada masa.","The plank trains your core to resist movement, which protects the lower back and steadies every other lift.":"Plank melatih teras untuk menahan pergerakan, yang melindungi punggung bawah dan menstabilkan setiap angkatan lain.","Glute Bridge":"Jambatan Punggung","Glutes · hip extension":"Punggung · lanjutan pinggul","Glutes, hamstrings":"Otot punggung besar, hamstring","3 sets × 12–15 reps":"3 set × 12–15 ulangan","HEELS DOWN · SHOULDERS TO KNEES IN LINE · NO ARCHING":"TUMIT DITEKAN KE BAWAH · BAHU KE LUTUT SELARAS · JANGAN MELENGKUNG","Lie on your back with knees bent, feet hip-width and heels close to your seat, arms by your sides. Press through your heels to lift the hips until shoulders, hips and knees form a straight line, squeeze the glutes for 1–2 seconds, then lower slowly.":"Baring terlentang dengan lutut dibengkokkan, kaki selebar pinggul dan tumit rapat dengan punggung, lengan di sisi badan. Tolak melalui tumit untuk mengangkat pinggul sehingga bahu, pinggul dan lutut membentuk garis lurus, ketatkan punggung bawah (glutes) selama 1–2 saat, kemudian turunkan perlahan.","Arching the lower back instead of using the glutes; pushing through the toes; knees falling out or in; dropping down fast.":"Melengkungkan pinggang dan bukannya menggunakan punggung bawah (glutes); menolak dengan hujung jari kaki; lutut jatuh ke luar atau ke dalam; turun terlalu pantas.","3 × 15; once easy, try single-leg bridges or hip thrusts with your shoulders on a bench.":"3 × 15; apabila sudah mudah, cuba jambatan sebelah kaki atau hip thrust dengan bahu di atas bangku.","Long sitting \"switches off\" the glutes; bridges wake them up and take strain off the lower back and knees.":"Duduk lama membuatkan punggung bawah (glutes) \"tidur\"; jambatan mengaktifkannya dan mengurangkan tekanan pada pinggang dan lutut.","The king of lifts":"Raja segala angkatan","Hips back, knees over toes":"Pinggul ke belakang, lutut mengikut hujung jari kaki","Lifting a weight off the floor":"Mengangkat beban dari lantai","A flat back comes first":"Belakang yang lurus adalah keutamaan","The classic upper-body press":"Tolakan badan atas yang klasik","Shoulder blades back, elbows 45°":"Bilah bahu ditarik ke belakang, siku 45°","Pressing a weight overhead standing":"Menolak beban ke atas kepala sambil berdiri","Whole body tight, no leaning back":"Seluruh badan ketat, jangan condong ke belakang","The basic back builder":"Latihan asas untuk membina ketebalan belakang","Torso angle stays fixed":"Sudut badan kekal","The bodyweight pulling king":"Raja tarikan dengan berat badan sendiri","Shoulders down first, then pull":"Turunkan bahu dahulu, kemudian tarik","Do it anywhere":"Boleh dilakukan di mana-mana","Body like a plank":"Badan seperti papan","Easier on the knees than a forward lunge":"Lebih mesra lutut daripada lunge ke hadapan","Drop straight down":"Turun secara menegak","The basic core exercise":"Latihan teras yang paling asas","Use the hold timer below":"Gunakan pemasa tahan di bawah","A beginner glute activator":"Gerakan permulaan untuk mengaktifkan punggung bawah (glutes)","Squeeze and pause at the top":"Ketatkan dan tahan 1–2 saat di puncak","Feet shoulder-width, toes slightly out, arms forward":"Kaki selebar bahu, hujung jari kaki sedikit ke luar, tangan dihulurkan ke hadapan","Bar on the upper back; breathe in and brace":"Bar di belakang atas; tarik nafas dan ketatkan teras badan","Sit the hips back and down; knees track over the toes":"Tolak pinggul ke belakang dan ke bawah; lutut mengikut arah hujung jari kaki","Lightly touch the box, then stand":"Duduk di atas kotak, sentuh ringan, kemudian bangun","Thighs at least parallel; back stays flat":"Peha sekurang-kurangnya selari dengan lantai; belakang kekal lurus","Drive up through the whole foot; breathe out":"Tolak dengan seluruh tapak kaki untuk bangun; hembus nafas","Bar over mid-foot; flat back, shoulders just in front of the bar":"Bar di atas tengah kaki; belakang rata, bahu betul-betul di hadapan bar","Brace and \"push the floor away\"":"Kencangkan badan dan \"tolak lantai menjauh\"","Bar slides up the shins; past the knees, drive the hips forward":"Bar meluncur ke atas betis; selepas melepasi lutut, dorong pinggul ke hadapan","Stand tall and lock out — don't lean back":"Berdiri tegak dan kunci — jangan condong ke belakang","Hips back first, lower along the same path":"Tolak pinggul ke belakang dahulu, turun mengikut laluan yang sama","Feet planted, shoulder blades squeezed, arms straight":"Kaki tegap di lantai, tulang belikat dirapatkan, lengan lurus","Lower under control, elbows about 45° — not flared out":"Turun dengan terkawal, siku kira-kira 45° — jangan terkembang ke luar","Touch the lower chest":"Sentuh bahagian bawah dada","Press back up, slightly towards the shoulders":"Tolak kembali ke atas, sedikit ke arah bahu","Bar on the front of the shoulders, elbows under and slightly ahead":"Bar di depan bahu, siku di bawah dan sedikit ke hadapan","Squeeze the glutes and brace":"Kecutkan punggung dan kencangkan badan","Tip the head back so the bar travels straight up":"Dongakkan kepala sedikit supaya bar bergerak lurus ke atas","Lock out overhead, head through between the arms":"Kunci di atas kepala, kepala melepasi di antara lengan","Lower back to the shoulders under control":"Turunkan semula ke bahu dengan terkawal","Hinge to about 45°, flat back, arms hanging":"Tunduk pinggul kira-kira 45°, belakang rata, lengan tergantung","Drive the elbows back and squeeze the shoulder blades":"Tarik siku ke belakang dan rapatkan tulang belikat","Bar touches the upper stomach; torso angle doesn't change":"Bar menyentuh perut atas; sudut badan tidak berubah","Lower slowly to straight arms":"Turunkan perlahan hingga lengan lurus sepenuhnya","Jump or step up to the top, chin over the bar":"Lompat atau naik ke atas, dagu melepasi bar","Lower yourself slowly over 3–5 seconds":"Turunkan diri perlahan dalam masa 3–5 saat","At the bottom, step back up and repeat":"Di bawah, naik semula dan ulang","Hands just wider than shoulders, palms forward, hang with straight arms":"Pegang sedikit lebih lebar daripada bahu, tapak tangan ke hadapan, bergantung dengan lengan lurus","First pull the shoulders down away from the ears":"Mula-mula tarik bahu ke bawah menjauhi telinga","Drive the elbows down and back until the chin clears the bar":"Tarik siku ke bawah dan ke belakang sehingga dagu melepasi bar","Lower under control to straight arms":"Turunkan dengan terkawal hingga lengan lurus","Knees down; a straight line from knees to head":"Lutut di lantai; garis lurus dari lutut ke kepala","Hands under the shoulders; a straight line from head to heels":"Tangan di bawah bahu; garis lurus dari kepala ke tumit","Elbows back at about 45°; the whole body lowers as one":"Siku ke belakang kira-kira 45°; seluruh badan turun serentak","Chest just above the floor":"Dada betul-betul di atas lantai","Push the floor away; hips don't sag":"Tolak lantai menjauh; pinggul jangan jatuh","Stand with feet hip-width":"Berdiri dengan kaki selebar pinggul","Take a long step backwards":"Ambil satu langkah panjang ke belakang","Drop straight down: back knee near the floor, front knee over the ankle":"Turunkan badan terus ke bawah: lutut belakang hampir ke lantai, lutut depan di atas buku lali","Push through the front foot to stand back up":"Tolak melalui kaki depan untuk berdiri semula","Forearms down, elbows under the shoulders, start on the knees":"Lengan bawah di lantai, siku di bawah bahu, mula dengan lutut","Lift the knees: head to heels in one line, squeeze stomach and glutes":"Angkat lutut: kepala ke tumit dalam satu garisan, kecutkan perut dan punggung","Breathe normally and hold the position":"Bernafas seperti biasa dan tahan kedudukan","Lie on your back, knees bent, heels close to the seat":"Baring telentang, lutut dibengkokkan, tumit dekat punggung","Press through the heels and lift the hips":"Tekan melalui tumit dan angkat pinggul","Shoulders to knees in one line; squeeze the glutes for 1–2 seconds":"Bahu ke lutut dalam satu garisan; kecutkan punggung selama 1–2 saat","Lower slowly":"Turunkan perlahan-lahan","GREEN LINE = HEAD TO HEELS IN ONE LINE":"GARISAN HIJAU = KEPALA KE TUMIT DALAM SATU GARISAN","DASHED LINE = MID-FOOT (KEEP THE BAR OVER IT)":"GARISAN PUTUS-PUTUS = TENGAH KAKI (KEKALKAN BATANG DI ATASNYA)","Quadriceps":"Kuadrisep","Glutes":"Punggung (gluteus)","Hip & ankle mobility":"Mobiliti pinggul & buku lali","Hamstrings":"Hamstring (otot paha belakang)","Lower back":"Pinggang bawah","Grip":"Genggaman","Chest":"Dada","Triceps":"Trisep","Front shoulders":"Bahu depan","Shoulder-blade control":"Kawalan tulang bahu (skapula)","Core stability":"Kestabilan teras","Upper back":"Belakang atas","Lats":"Lats (otot sayap)","Mid-back":"Belakang tengah","Biceps":"Bisep","Lower-back hold":"Kawalan pinggang bawah","Hip stability":"Kestabilan pinggul","Abs":"Otot perut","Shoulder stability":"Kestabilan bahu","Breathing control":"Kawalan pernafasan","Hip extension":"Lanjutan pinggul","Current level: ":"Tahap semasa:","Beginner version":"Versi pemula","Standard":"Standard","Exercise {n} of 10 · {type}":"Latihan {n} daripada 10 · {type}"," · beginner version":"· versi pemula","The ten exercises at a glance":"Sepuluh latihan sekali pandang","Exercise":"Latihan","Pattern":"Corak","Main muscles":"Otot utama","Sets × reps":"Set × ulangan","A simple beginner week":"Contoh seminggu mudah untuk pemula","Train 2–3 days a week with a rest day between, full body each time:":"Berlatih 2–3 hari seminggu dengan satu hari rehat di antara, seluruh badan setiap kali:","Day A: ":"Hari A:","Squat, bench press (or push-up), row, plank":"Squat, bench press (atau push-up), row, plank","Day B: ":"Hari B:","Deadlift (or glute bridge), overhead press, pull-up (or negatives), lunge":"Deadlift (atau glute bridge), overhead press, pull-up (atau negatif), lunge","Alternate A and B. Do 2–4 sets of each with a weight you can lift with good form and 1–2 reps to spare; when it feels easy, add a little weight or a rep next time.":"Selang-seli A dan B. Buat 2–4 set bagi setiap latihan dengan beban yang boleh diangkat dengan postur baik dan masih ada 1–2 ulangan lagi; apabila terasa mudah, tambah sedikit beban atau ulangan pada kali seterusnya.","Breathing and bracing":"Pernafasan dan pengetatan teras","For standing barbell lifts like the squat, deadlift and press, take a deep breath into your belly before the rep and brace as if someone were about to poke your stomach; hold it on the way down and breathe out after the hard part. For light, high-rep work just breathe normally — don't hold your breath. If you have high blood pressure or heart problems, ask your doctor first.":"Untuk angkatan barbel berdiri seperti squat, deadlift dan press, tarik nafas dalam ke perut sebelum ulangan dan kejapkan otot perut seolah-olah seseorang akan mencucuk perut anda; tahan semasa menurun dan hembus nafas selepas bahagian yang berat. Untuk kerja ringan dan ulangan tinggi, bernafas seperti biasa sahaja — jangan tahan nafas. Jika anda mempunyai tekanan darah tinggi atau masalah jantung, tanya doktor anda dahulu.","Warm up for 5–10 minutes, then do 1–2 light sets with an empty bar or light weight.":"Panaskan badan selama 5–10 minit, kemudian buat 1–2 set ringan dengan bar kosong atau berat ringan.","Bench and squat inside a rack with safety bars, or with a spotter.":"Lakukan bench press dan squat di dalam rak dengan bar keselamatan, atau dengan spotter.","Stop when your form breaks down — form always comes before weight.":"Berhenti apabila postur mula rosak — postur sentiasa lebih utama daripada berat.","Stop for joint pain (not muscle burn) and get it checked by a doctor or physio if needed.":"Berhenti jika sendi sakit (bukan rasa terbakar otot), dan dapatkan pemeriksaan doktor atau ahli fisioterapi jika perlu.","Want to put your strength to the test? See <a href=\"../../hyrox/\">the 8 HYROX stations</a>.":"Ingin menguji kekuatan anda? Lihat <a href=\"../../hyrox/\">8 stesen HYROX</a>.","How many days a week should a beginner train?":"Berapa hari seminggu seorang pemula perlu berlatih?","Two or three full-body sessions with rest days between is plenty. Consistency matters more than frequency.":"Dua atau tiga sesi seluruh badan dengan hari rehat di antaranya sudah memadai. Konsistensi lebih penting daripada kekerapan.","Should I train to failure?":"Adakah saya patut berlatih sehingga gagal?","Beginners don't need to. Leaving 1–2 reps in reserve keeps form clean and injury risk low, and progress is just as fast.":"Pemula tidak perlu. Menyimpan 1–2 ulangan lagi menjadikan postur kekal kemas dan risiko kecederaan rendah, dan kemajuan tetap sama pantas.","Why keep the bar over mid-foot?":"Mengapa bar perlu berada di atas tengah kaki?","In standing barbell lifts mid-foot is your balance point; keeping the bar over it stops the weight pulling you forwards or backwards and makes the lift most efficient.":"Dalam angkatan barbel berdiri, tengah kaki ialah titik imbangan badan; mengekalkan bar di atasnya menghalang berat menarik anda ke depan atau ke belakang dan menjadikan angkatan paling cekap.","Gym basics":"Asas gim","FITNESS · STRENGTH TRAINING FOR BEGINNERS":"KECERGASAN · LATIHAN KEKUATAN UNTUK PEMULA","10 Essential Gym Exercises, With Correct Form":"10 Latihan Gim Penting, Dengan Postur yang Betul","Squat, deadlift, bench press, overhead press, row, pull-up, push-up, lunge, plank and glute bridge — every basic pattern: push, pull, squat, hinge, single-leg and core. The green trail shows the bar path and the dashed line marks mid-foot; choose Beginner to see easier versions.":"Squat, deadlift, bench press, overhead press, row, pull-up, push-up, lunge, plank dan glute bridge — setiap corak asas: tolak, tarik, squat, hinge, satu kaki dan teras. Laluan hijau menunjukkan laluan bar dan garis putus-putus menandakan tengah kaki; pilih Pemula untuk melihat versi yang lebih mudah.","Key exercises":"Latihan utama","Push · pull · squat · hinge · single-leg · core":"Tolak · tarik · squat · hinge · satu kaki · teras","Main muscles, this exercise":"Otot utama, latihan ini","Suggested sets × reps":"Cadangan set × ulangan","A weight you can lift with 1–2 reps to spare":"Beban yang boleh diangkat dengan berbaki 1–2 ulangan","Exercises you have mastered":"Latihan yang telah anda kuasai","Mark each exercise as mastered below":"Tandai setiap latihan sebagai telah dikuasai di bawah","Choose your level (squat, pull-up and push-up have beginner versions)":"Pilih tahap anda (squat, pull-up dan push-up mempunyai versi pemula)","Pick an exercise":"Pilih latihan","Equipment":"Peralatan","How to start":"Cara bermula","Why do it":"Mengapa melakukannya","SIDE 90°":"SISI 90°","Muscles worked":"Otot yang dilatih","Relative involvement":"Penglibatan relatif","For education only; the animations are simplified. Check with a doctor before starting strength training if you have health concerns; beginners should get coaching from a qualified trainer, and always use a spotter or safety bars for heavy lifts.":"Hanya untuk tujuan pendidikan; animasi telah dipermudah. Rujuk doktor sebelum memulakan latihan kekuatan jika anda mempunyai masalah kesihatan; pemula patut mendapatkan bimbingan daripada jurulatih bertauliah, dan sentiasa gunakan spotter atau bar keselamatan untuk angkatan berat.","Gym Exercises for Beginners: 10 Key Movements with Correct Form | KungfuTutor":"Senaman Gim untuk Pemula: 10 Pergerakan Utama dengan Postur yang Betul | KungfuTutor","Learn correct form for 10 essential gym exercises with step-by-step animation: squat, deadlift, bench press, overhead press, bent-over row, pull-up, push-up, reverse lunge, plank and glute bridge — with beginner versions, common mistakes, sets and reps.":"Pelajari postur yang betul untuk 10 senaman gim penting dengan animasi langkah demi langkah: squat, deadlift, bench press, overhead press, bent-over row, pull-up, push-up, reverse lunge, plank dan glute bridge — dengan versi permulaan, kesilapan biasa, set dan ulangan.","Gym Basics — 10 Exercises with Correct Form, Animated":"Asas Gim — 10 Senaman dengan Postur yang Betul, Animasi","What are the best gym exercises for beginners?":"Apakah senaman gim terbaik untuk pemula?","A balanced beginner plan covers a squat, a hip hinge such as the deadlift or glute bridge, a horizontal push (bench press or push-up), a vertical push (overhead press), a pull (row or pull-up), a single-leg move (lunge) and a core exercise (plank).":"Pelan permulaan yang seimbang merangkumi squat, pergerakan engsel pinggul seperti deadlift atau glute bridge, tolakan mendatar (bench press atau push-up), tolakan menegak (overhead press), tarikan (row atau pull-up), pergerakan satu kaki (lunge) dan senaman teras (plank).","How many sets and reps should a beginner do?":"Berapa set dan ulangan yang sepatutnya dilakukan oleh pemula?","Two to four sets of about 8 to 12 reps with a weight you can lift with good form, leaving one or two reps in reserve, two or three times a week.":"Dua hingga empat set, kira-kira 8 hingga 12 ulangan, dengan beban yang boleh diangkat dengan postur yang baik sambil menyimpan satu atau dua ulangan, dua atau tiga kali seminggu.","Should the bar stay over the middle of the foot?":"Dalam angkatan barbel berdiri seperti squat, deadlift dan overhead press, adakah bar perlu kekal di atas tengah kaki?","In standing barbell lifts like the squat, deadlift and overhead press, keeping the bar roughly over mid-foot keeps you balanced and the lift efficient.":"Dalam angkatan barbel berdiri seperti squat, deadlift dan overhead press, mengekalkan bar kira-kira di atas tengah kaki membantu anda kekal seimbang dan menjadikan angkatan lebih cekap.","Women Open":"Terbuka Wanita","the most popular entry division":"kategori permulaan yang paling popular","Women Pro":"Pro Wanita","high-intensity competitive division":"kategori pertandingan berintensiti tinggi","Men Open":"Terbuka Lelaki","Men Pro":"Pro Lelaki","Doubles":"Berpasangan","run together, split every station as you like":"berlari bersama, bahagikan setiap stesen mengikut kehendak","Women":"Wanita","Men":"Lelaki","Mixed":"Campuran","Relay":"Lari berganti","each of 4 runs 2 × 1 km and does 2 stations":"setiap daripada 4 orang berlari 2 × 1 km dan melakukan 2 stesen","Mixed (F / M)":"Campuran (P / L)","SkiErg":"SkiErg","Lats and core power":"Latissimus dan kuasa teras","Stand on the SkiErg base, grab the handles overhead and drive them down while you hinge at the hips and soften the knees, dropping your bodyweight into the pull. Finish with the hands beside the thighs, then ride back up tall. The power comes from the hip hinge, not just the arms.":"Berdiri di tapak SkiErg, pegang pemegang di atas kepala dan tarik ke bawah sambil membengkokkan pinggul dan melembutkan lutut, memindahkan berat badan ke dalam tarikan. Akhiri dengan tangan di sebelah paha, kemudian naik semula dengan badan tegak. Kuasanya datang daripada bengkokan pinggul, bukan hanya lengan.","A judge resets the monitor first. Both feet must stay on the base the whole time — heels may hang off but must not touch the floor; jumping is fine if you land back on the base. After 1,000 m, keep both feet on the base and raise a hand until the judge confirms. Infringements: a warning first, then +15 s each.":"Hakim menetapkan semula monitor dahulu. Kedua-dua kaki mesti kekal di tapak sepanjang masa; tumit boleh tergantung tetapi tidak boleh menyentuh lantai; melompat dibenarkan jika mendarat kembali di tapak. Selepas 1,000 m, kekalkan kedua-dua kaki di tapak dan angkat tangan sehingga hakim mengesahkan. Pelanggaran: amaran pertama, kemudian +15 s setiap satu.","Use 4 × 250 m intervals to find a pace you can hold; drill the hip-hinge-plus-pull timing; don't sprint the first station — save legs for the runs.":"Gunakan selang 4 × 250 m untuk mencari rentak yang boleh dikekalkan; latih masa bengkokan pinggul serta tarikan tangan; jangan pecut di stesen pertama — simpan tenaga untuk larian.","Sled Push":"Tolak Sled","Quads and calf drive":"Kuadriseps dan tujahan betis","Grip the upright poles with straight or slightly bent arms, lean about 45° and drive with short, quick steps on the balls of your feet like a sprint start. Keep the back flat and the core braced, and keep the sled moving — restarting a stopped sled costs the most energy.":"Pegang tiang tegak sled dengan lengan lurus atau sedikit bengkok, condongkan badan kira-kira 45° dan tolak dengan langkah pendek dan pantas menggunakan bahagian depan tapak kaki seperti permulaan pecut. Kekalkan belakang rata dan teras badan dikuatkan, dan biarkan sled sentiasa bergerak — memulakan semula sled yang berhenti paling memenatkan.","Use the lane the judge assigns; sled and athlete start fully inside the Racers Box; it is 4 × 12.5 m and the whole sled must cross each end line before changing direction; never interfere with the next lane. Infringements: a warning, then +15 s each.":"Gunakan lorong yang ditetapkan oleh pengadil; sled dan atlet bermula sepenuhnya di dalam Racers Box; jaraknya 4 × 12.5 m dan seluruh sled mesti melintasi setiap garisan hujung sebelum menukar arah; jangan sekali-kali mengganggu lorong seterusnya. Pelanggaran: amaran, kemudian +15 s setiap kali.","Build with back squats and Bulgarian split squats; drill low, short steps; carpet friction varies by venue, so train heavier than race weight.":"Bina kekuatan dengan back squat dan Bulgarian split squat; latih langkah pendek dan rendah; geseran karpet berbeza mengikut tempat, jadi berlatihlah dengan beban lebih berat daripada beban perlumbaan.","Sled Pull":"Tarik Sled","Grip, back and posterior chain":"Genggaman, belakang badan dan rantai posterior","Stand in the Racers Box, lean back slightly with a solid stance and pull the rope hand over hand so the sled slides to you. Step back to use your bodyweight and legs, and keep the slack rope tidy behind you. When the sled crosses the line, run to the other end and pull it back.":"Berdiri dalam Racers Box, condongkan badan sedikit ke belakang dengan kedudukan kaki yang kukuh, dan tarik tali tangan demi tangan supaya sled meluncur ke arah anda. Undur selangkah untuk menggunakan berat badan dan kaki, dan kemaskan tali yang longgar di belakang anda. Apabila sled melepasi garisan, larilah ke hujung satu lagi dan tarik balik.","Stay standing — no sitting or kneeling pulls; while holding the rope don't step on the front or back line of the Racers Box; keep the rope in your lane (it may run out of the back); the whole sled must pass the 12.5 m line, 4 times. Infringements: a warning, then +15 s each.":"Kekal berdiri — tiada tarikan sambil duduk atau melutut; semasa memegang tali jangan pijak garisan depan atau belakang Racers Box; pastikan tali kekal di lorong anda (ia boleh keluar di belakang); seluruh sled mesti melepasi garisan 12.5 m, sebanyak 4 kali. Pelanggaran: amaran, kemudian +15 s setiap kali.","Rows, pull-ups and dead hangs for grip; sit back and pull with legs and bodyweight, not arms alone; practise stacking the rope behind you so you don't trip.":"Latihan dayung, pull-up dan dead hang untuk genggaman; duduk ke belakang dan tarik dengan kaki serta berat badan, bukan lengan sahaja; latih menyusun tali di belakang anda supaya tidak tersadung.","Burpee Broad Jumps":"Burpee Lompat Jauh","Full-body power and stamina":"Kuasa dan stamina seluruh badan","Hands down, lower until your chest touches the floor, jump or step the feet back in, then broad-jump forward taking off and landing on both feet together. Land straight into the next burpee. Rhythm matters more than distance — a medium jump you can repeat beats a huge one.":"Letakkan tangan ke bawah, turun sehingga dada menyentuh lantai, lompat atau langkah kaki kembali, kemudian lompat jauh ke hadapan dengan melompat dan mendarat dengan kedua-dua kaki serentak. Terus mendarat ke burpee seterusnya. Irama lebih penting daripada jarak: lompatan sederhana yang boleh diulang lebih baik daripada lompatan besar.","Chest must clearly touch the floor every rep; take off and land with both feet together (max 5 cm stagger), no extra steps; hands go down within 30 cm of your front toes; when you come out of the burpee your feet may not pass your fingertips; finish by jumping fully over the line. Using a knee to get up is allowed.":"Dada mesti menyentuh lantai dengan jelas pada setiap ulangan; berlepas dan mendarat dengan kedua-dua kaki serentak (perbezaan maksimum 5 cm), tanpa langkah tambahan; tangan turun dalam jarak 30 cm dari hujung jari kaki depan; apabila bangkit daripada burpee, kaki tidak boleh melepasi hujung jari; tamatkan dengan melompat melepasi garisan sepenuhnya. Menggunakan lutut untuk bangun dibenarkan.","Practise steady EMOM sets; find your most economical jump length; rehearse 1 km run straight into burpee broad jumps.":"Latih set EMOM yang stabil; cari panjang lompatan yang paling jimat tenaga; ulang latihan lari 1 km terus ke lompat jauh burpee.","Rowing":"Mendayung","Leg drive, back pull, stamina":"Tolakan kaki, tarikan belakang, daya tahan","The stroke goes legs → body → arms: push the footplate, swing from a forward lean to a slight lean back, then draw the handle to the lower ribs. Recover in reverse: arms → body → legs. Most of the power comes from the legs.":"Urutan kayuh ialah kaki → badan → tangan: tolak pedal kaki, ayunkan dari condong ke hadapan kepada sedikit condong ke belakang, kemudian tarik pemegang ke rusuk bawah. Semasa kembali, urutannya terbalik: tangan → badan → kaki. Kebanyakan kuasa datang daripada kaki.","A judge resets the monitor; stay seated until 1,000 m is done; you may stop and rest with the handle in its holder, but don't stand or leave the seat until the judge confirms. Damper is preset to 6 and footplates to position 4 — both adjustable.":"Hakim menetapkan semula monitor; kekal duduk sehingga 1,000 m selesai; anda boleh berhenti dan berehat dengan pemegang diletakkan di tempatnya, tetapi jangan bangun atau meninggalkan tempat duduk sehingga hakim mengesahkan. Damper ditetapkan awal kepada 6 dan pedal kaki kepada kedudukan 4; kedua-duanya boleh laraskan.","Use 500 m intervals to learn your sustainable split; aim for about 26–30 strokes per minute; use this station to reset your breathing before the carry.":"Gunakan sela 500 m untuk mempelajari split yang boleh dikekalkan; sasarkan kira-kira 26–30 kayuhan seminit; gunakan stesen ini untuk menetapkan semula pernafasan sebelum membawa beban.","Farmers Carry":"Bawa Beban Petani","Grip and core stability":"Kekuatan genggaman dan kestabilan teras","One kettlebell in each hand, arms hanging by your sides, chest up, shoulders down, core tight, and move with short quick steps. Eyes forward and keep the bells off your thighs. Fast walking or a light jog both work.":"Pegang satu kettlebell di setiap tangan, lengan tergantung di sisi, dada tegak, bahu diturunkan, otot teras diketatkan, dan bergerak dengan langkah pendek yang laju. Pandang ke hadapan dan elakkan kettlebell menyentuh paha. Berjalan laju atau joging ringan kedua-duanya sesuai.","Take and return the bells from the marked box by the station; carry both bells at all times with arms straight by your sides; you may put them down to rest but not move them forward; return them upright in the right box or take a 30 s penalty; using the wrong weight means redoing the station or disqualification.":"Ambil dan pulangkan besi dari kotak yang ditanda di sebelah stesen; bawa kedua-dua besi pada setiap masa dengan lengan lurus di sisi; anda boleh meletakkannya untuk berehat tetapi jangan mengalihkannya ke hadapan; kembalikan dalam keadaan tegak ke kotak yang betul atau dikenakan penalti 30 s; menggunakan berat yang salah bermakna mengulang stesen atau dikenakan diskualifikasi.","Dead hangs and heavy carries for grip; try to go unbroken on race day; short quick steps reduce swing.":"Gantung mati dan bawa beban berat untuk latihan genggaman; cuba teruskan tanpa henti pada hari perlumbaan; langkah pendek yang laju mengurangkan ayunan.","Sandbag Lunges":"Lunge Beg Pasir","Quad and glute endurance":"Ketahanan quad dan glute","Rest the sandbag across the back of both shoulders (on the upper traps), hold it steady, and step forward into alternating lunges, dropping straight down until the back knee touches the floor. Stand up tall and keep moving for 100 m.":"Letakkan beg pasir berat yang ditetapkan di belakang kedua-dua bahu (di atas otot trapezius), pegang kukuh di kedua-dua sisi, dan langkah ke hadapan secara bergilir menjadi lunge, turun lurus sehingga lutut belakang menyentuh lantai. Berdiri tegak dan teruskan bergerak sejauh 100 m.","The back knee must clearly touch the floor each rep; finish each rep standing tall (knees and hips straight); alternate legs; no extra steps between reps; the bag stays on both shoulders — never rested on the floor or anything else (+15 s each time); the front foot must fully cross the finish line and the bag goes back to its area or +30 s.":"Lutut belakang mesti jelas menyentuh lantai pada setiap ulangan; tamatkan setiap ulangan dengan berdiri tegak (lutut dan pinggul lurus); tukar kaki secara bergilir; tiada langkah kecil tambahan antara ulangan; beg mesti kekal di kedua-dua bahu, tidak boleh diletakkan di lantai atau di mana-mana (+15 s setiap kali); kaki depan mesti melepasi garisan penamat sepenuhnya dan beg mesti dikembalikan ke kawasannya, atau penalti 30 s.","Build to 50 m of unbroken walking lunges; stay upright with an even stride; this is the leg-endurance gate before the final station.":"Latih lunge berjalan sejauh 50 m tanpa henti; kekalkan badan tegak dengan langkah yang sekata; ini ialah ujian ketahanan paha sebelum stesen terakhir.","Wall Balls":"Wall Ball","Coordination and willpower":"Koordinasi dan kemahuan","Stand tall holding the ball at your chest, squat until the hips are below the knees, then drive up with the legs and throw the ball to the target above. Catch it and flow straight into the next squat.":"Berdiri tegak sambil memegang bola di dada, cangkung sehingga pinggul berada di bawah lutut, kemudian tolak dengan kaki dan lontarkan bola ke sasaran di atas. Sambut bola dan terus ke cangkungan seterusnya.","Start each set standing tall with the ball — no scooping it off the floor straight into a throw; hips must go below the knees; hit your own target (women 2.70 m, men 3.00 m); catch and go, or let it drop and stand tall before the next rep — no catching off the bounce. Any fault is a no-rep.":"Mulakan setiap set dengan berdiri tegak sambil memegang bola; jangan terus melontar selepas mengambilnya dari lantai; pinggul mesti turun di bawah lutut; bola mesti mengenai sasaran anda sendiri (wanita 2.70 m, lelaki 3.00 m); sambut dan teruskan, atau biarkan bola jatuh dan berdiri tegak sebelum ulangan seterusnya; jangan sambut bola melantun. Sebarang kesilapan tidak dikira (No-rep).","Break it up — 4 × 25 or 5 × 20 with short rests; train squat endurance and breathing rhythm; watch your depth when tired to avoid no-reps.":"Pecahkan kepada beberapa set, contohnya 4 × 25 atau 5 × 20, dengan rehat yang pendek; latih daya tahan cangkung dan irama pernafasan; apabila letih, beri perhatian kepada kedalaman cangkung supaya tidak dikira No-rep.","Base move: double-pole pull":"Pergerakan asas: tarikan dua tiang (Double Pole)","Upper-body pull · coordination":"Tarikan badan atas · koordinasi","Base move: leaning drive":"Pergerakan asas: tolakan condong ke hadapan (Drive)","Leg power · heaviest station":"Kuasa kaki · stesen paling berat","Base move: hand-over-hand pull":"Pergerakan asas: tarikan tali berselang-seli dengan kedua-dua tangan","Grip · posterior chain":"Genggaman · rantaian belakang badan","Base move: burpee + broad jump":"Pergerakan asas: burpee + lompat jauh berdiri","Full-body power · cardio test":"Kuasa seluruh badan · ujian kardio","Base move: legs → body → arms":"Pergerakan asas: kaki → badan → tangan","Full-body pull · breathing reset":"Tarikan seluruh badan · kawal pernafasan","Base move: loaded walk":"Pergerakan asas: berjalan membawa beban","Grip · core stability":"Genggaman · kestabilan teras","Base move: walking lunge":"Pergerakan asas: lunge berjalan (Lunge)","Alternating legs · endurance test":"Kaki berselang-seli · ujian daya tahan otot","Base move: squat + throw":"Pergerakan asas: cangkung + lontar ke atas","Coordination · final push":"Koordinasi · dorongan terakhir","no added load":"tiada beban tambahan","Damper 6 (adjustable)":"Damper 6 (boleh laras)","Lats / upper back":"Latissimus / belakang atas","Cardio":"Kardio"," incl. sled":"termasuk sled","Quads":"Kuadrisep","Calves":"Betis","Grip / forearms":"Genggaman / lengan bawah","Hamstrings & glutes":"Hamstring & gluteus","bodyweight":"berat badan sendiri","Bodyweight":"Berat badan sendiri","Quads / glutes":"Kuadrisep / gluteus","Chest & triceps":"Dada & trisep","Damper 6 · footplate 4":"Damper 6 · pedal pada kedudukan 4"," kettlebells":"kettlebell","Traps / upper back":"Trapezius / belakang atas","sandbag":"beg pasir"," sandbag":"beg pasir","Glute endurance":"Daya tahan gluteus","Balance & core":"Imbangan & teras","Mental grit":"Ketahanan mental","reps":"ulangan"," ball · target ":"bola ubat · sasaran","BOTH FEET STAY ON THE BASE":"KEDUA-DUA KAKI KEKAL DI ATAS PANGKALAN","STAY IN YOUR LANE · 4 × 12.5 m":"KEKAL DI LORONG ANDA · 4 × 12.5 m","STAND UP · STAY INSIDE THE BOX":"BANGUN · KEKAL DI DALAM KOTAK","CHEST MUST TOUCH THE GROUND":"DADA MESTI MENYENTUH LANTAI","STAY SEATED UNTIL 1,000 m":"KEKAL DUDUK SEHINGGA 1,000 m","ARMS STRAIGHT BY YOUR SIDES":"LENGAN LURUS DI SISI","KNEE MUST TOUCH GROUND":"LUTUT MESTI MENYENTUH LANTAI","HIPS BELOW KNEES · HIT THE TARGET":"PINGGUL DI BAWAH LUTUT · KENA SASARAN","Current division: ":"Kategori semasa:","Each of 4 teammates runs 2 × 1,000 m":"Setiap 4 ahli pasukan berlari 2 × 1,000 m","8 × 1,000 m, one before each station":"8 × 1,000 m, satu sebelum setiap stesen","; sled push ":"; tolak sled",", wall ball ":", wall ball","after 1 km":"selepas 1 km","Comes after run {n} of 8 (1,000 m), via the RoxZone":"Datang selepas larian {n} daripada 8 (1,000 m), melalui RoxZone","100 reps":"100 ulangan"," — load":"— beban"," — movement demo":"— demonstrasi pergerakan dan jarak","Division":"Kategori","Sled push":"Tolak sled","Sled pull":"Tarik sled","Farmers carry":"Farmers carry","Lunge bag":"Beg lunge","Wall ball":"Wall ball","What is HYROX?":"Apakah HYROX?","HYROX is an indoor fitness race. Everyone, everywhere, does the same format: run 1 km, complete one functional workout station, and repeat eight times. Because distances, movements and loads are standardised worldwide, a time set in one city compares directly with any other.":"HYROX ialah perlumbaan kecergasan dalam dewan. Semua orang, di mana-mana, menjalani format yang sama: lari 1 km, lengkapkan satu stesen latihan fungsi, dan ulang lapan kali. Oleh kerana jarak, pergerakan dan beban diseragamkan di seluruh dunia, masa yang dicatat di satu bandar boleh dibandingkan secara langsung dengan mana-mana bandar lain.","The transition area between the running track and each station is called the RoxZone. It is easy to ignore, but a few seconds lost finding equipment on each of eight visits can add up to minutes.":"Kawasan peralihan antara trek larian dan setiap stesen dipanggil RoxZone. Ia mudah diabaikan, tetapi beberapa saat yang hilang mencari peralatan pada setiap lawatan daripada lapan kali boleh bertambah menjadi minit.","Loads for every division":"Beban bagi setiap kategori","Sled weights include the sled. All divisions: SkiErg 1,000 m, sled push and pull 50 m each (4 × 12.5 m), burpee broad jumps 80 m, row 1,000 m, farmers carry 200 m, lunges 100 m, 100 wall balls. Women's and men's Doubles/Relay use Women Open / Men Open loads. Source: official HYROX website and the 2026/27 rulebook.":"Berat sled termasuk sled itu sendiri. Semua kategori: SkiErg 1,000 m, tolak dan tarik sled masing-masing 50 m (4 × 12.5 m), burpee broad jump 80 m, dayung 1,000 m, farmers carry 200 m, lunge 100 m, 100 wall ball. Doubles dan Relay wanita serta lelaki menggunakan beban Women Open / Men Open. Sumber: laman web rasmi HYROX dan buku peraturan 2026/27.","Pacing: running is half the race":"Pengurusan kelajuan: larian ialah separuh daripada perlumbaan","The 8 km of running is roughly half your finishing time. The classic mistake is going out too fast on run 1 and arriving at the sled push with empty legs. Run the first four laps at a pace where you can still speak in short sentences, note your lap times, and only push in the second half. The sled push, sled pull and lunges hit the legs hardest, so leave room for them.":"Larian 8 km kira-kira separuh daripada masa penamat anda. Kesilapan klasik ialah memulakan terlalu laju pada larian 1 dan tiba di tolakan sled dengan kaki yang kosong. Larikan empat pusingan pertama pada kelajuan yang masih membolehkan anda bercakap dalam ayat pendek, catatkan masa setiap pusingan, dan hanya tingkatkan kelajuan pada separuh kedua. Tolakan sled, tarikan sled dan lunges paling memberi tekanan kepada kaki, jadi sisakan tenaga untuknya.","Singles, Doubles or Relay?":"Solo, Berpasangan atau Relay?","For a first race, Doubles is a friendly option: you both run the full 8 km but split each station however you like. In the Relay, four teammates each run 2 × 1 km and complete 2 stations — a good fit for friends or workplace teams who want the race atmosphere.":"Untuk perlumbaan pertama, Berpasangan ialah pilihan mesra: anda berdua berlari sepenuhnya 8 km tetapi boleh membahagikan setiap stesen mengikut kesesuaian. Dalam Relay, empat ahli pasukan masing-masing berlari 2 × 1 km dan menamatkan 2 stesen, sesuai untuk rakan atau pasukan pejabat yang mahu merasai suasana perlumbaan.","What are the 8 HYROX stations in order?":"Apakah 8 stesen HYROX mengikut urutan?","SkiErg → Sled Push → Sled Pull → Burpee Broad Jumps → Rowing → Farmers Carry → Sandbag Lunges → Wall Balls, each after a 1 km run.":"SkiErg → Sled Push → Sled Pull → Burpee Broad Jumps → Rowing → Farmers Carry → Sandbag Lunges → Wall Balls, setiap satu selepas larian 1 km.","What if I can't finish a station?":"Bagaimana jika saya tidak dapat menamatkan sesebuah stesen?","Under the rulebook, failing to complete any station in full is a disqualification. You may rest within the station, but you have to finish it.":"Menurut buku peraturan, gagal menyelesaikan mana-mana stesen sepenuhnya akan menyebabkan diskualifikasi. Anda boleh berehat dalam stesen, tetapi mesti menyelesaikannya.","How high is the wall ball target?":"Setinggi manakah sasaran wall ball?","Women (Open and Pro) 2.70 m; men (Open and Pro) 3.00 m.":"Wanita (Open dan Pro) 2.70 m; lelaki (Open dan Pro) 3.00 m.","Are these animations official demos?":"Adakah animasi ini demonstrasi rasmi?","No. The animations are drawn by KungfuTutor to illustrate the key points of each movement; the official HYROX rulebook is the final word on standards.":"Tidak. Animasi ini dilukis oleh KungfuTutor untuk menerangkan perkara utama setiap pergerakan; buku peraturan rasmi HYROX ialah rujukan muktamad untuk piawaian.","HYROX · THE WORLD SERIES OF FITNESS RACING · 2026/27 SEASON STANDARDS":"HYROX · SIRI PERLUMBAAN KECERGASAN DUNIA · PIAWAIAN MUSIM 2026/27","HYROX: The 8 Functional Stations, Explained Interactively":"HYROX: 8 Stesen Fungsi, Dijelaskan Secara Interaktif","Every race is 8 × 1 km runs, each followed by one of 8 functional stations in a fixed order. Pick any station below to see an animated demo, the load for your division, the judging standards and how to train for it.":"Setiap perlumbaan terdiri daripada 8 × larian 1 km, setiap satu diikuti oleh salah satu daripada 8 stesen fungsi dalam susunan tetap. Pilih mana-mana stesen di bawah untuk melihat demonstrasi animasi, beban untuk kategori anda, standard penilaian dan cara berlatih.","Total running (about 50% of race time)":"Jumlah larian (kira-kira 50% masa perlumbaan)","Workout stations (fixed order worldwide)":"Stesen latihan (susunan tetap di seluruh dunia)","Push, pull, squat, lunge, carry and jump":"Tolak, tarik, cangkung, lunge, angkut dan lompat","Reference finish time, this division":"Masa tamat rujukan, kategori ini","Stations you have mastered":"Stesen yang telah anda kuasai","Mark each station as mastered below":"Tandakan setiap stesen sebagai telah dikuasai di bawah","Choose your division (loads and standards update instantly)":"Pilih kategori anda (beban dan standard dikemas kini serta-merta)","Pick a station (in fixed race order)":"Pilih stesen (mengikut susunan perlumbaan tetap)","Distance / reps":"Jarak / ulangan","Main demand":"Tuntutan utama","How to move":"Cara bergerak","Judging rules":"Peraturan penilaian","How to train":"Cara berlatih","Load profile of this station":"Profil beban stesen ini","Relative demand":"Tahap tuntutan relatif","KungfuTutor.com is an independent education site and is not affiliated with HYROX World GmbH; HYROX is a trademark of its owner. Loads and rules are summarised from the official 2026/27 rulebook — always check the latest official rules before racing. Check your health before training and consult a doctor or qualified coach where needed.":"KungfuTutor.com ialah laman pendidikan bebas dan tidak berkaitan dengan HYROX World GmbH; HYROX ialah tanda dagangan pemiliknya. Beban dan peraturan diringkaskan daripada buku peraturan rasmi 2026/27 — sentiasa semak peraturan rasmi terkini sebelum berlumba. Semak kesihatan anda sebelum berlatih dan rujuk doktor atau jurulatih bertauliah jika perlu.","HYROX 8 Stations Explained — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"Penjelasan 8 Stesen HYROX — Panduan Interaktif | KungfuTutor","Interactive HYROX guide: all 8 stations in race order with animated movement demos, official weights for every division (Open, Pro, Doubles, Relay), judging standards and training tips.":"Panduan interaktif HYROX: semua 8 stesen mengikut urutan perlumbaan, dengan demonstrasi pergerakan beranimasi, berat rasmi untuk setiap bahagian (Open, Pro, Doubles, Relay), standard penilaian dan tip latihan.","HYROX 8 Stations — Interactive Movement Guide":"8 Stesen HYROX — Panduan Pergerakan Interaktif","SkiErg 1,000 m, Sled Push 50 m, Sled Pull 50 m, Burpee Broad Jumps 80 m, Rowing 1,000 m, Farmers Carry 200 m, Sandbag Lunges 100 m and 100 Wall Balls, each after a 1 km run.":"SkiErg 1,000 m, Sled Push 50 m, Sled Pull 50 m, Burpee Broad Jumps 80 m, Rowing 1,000 m, Farmers Carry 200 m, Sandbag Lunges 100 m dan 100 Wall Balls, setiap satu selepas larian 1 km.","How heavy is the HYROX sled push?":"Berapa beratkah sled push HYROX?","Including the sled: 102 kg for Women Open, 152 kg for Women Pro and Men Open, and 202 kg for Men Pro.":"Termasuk sled: 102 kg untuk Women Open, 152 kg untuk Women Pro dan Men Open, dan 202 kg untuk Men Pro.","How high is the HYROX wall ball target?":"Berapa tinggi sasaran wall ball HYROX?","2.70 m for women and 3.00 m for men, in both Open and Pro.":"2.70 m untuk wanita dan 3.00 m untuk lelaki, untuk kedua-dua Open dan Pro.","Five Stances":"Lima Kuda-kuda","KUNG FU FOUNDATIONS · THE FIVE BASIC STANCES (WU BU)":"ASAS KUNG FU · LIMA KUDA-KUDA ASAS (WU BU)","The 5 Basic Kung Fu Stances, Explained Interactively":"5 Kuda-kuda Asas Kung Fu, Dijelaskan Secara Interaktif","Stances are the foundation of kung fu: a stable base is what gives punches and kicks their power. Pick a stance to watch it from the front or side, see exactly where the feet go and how the weight is shared, then practise with the built-in stance timer.":"Kuda-kuda ialah asas kung fu: pijakan yang stabil memberi kekuatan kepada tumbukan dan tendangan. Pilih satu kuda-kuda untuk menonton animasinya dari depan atau sisi, lihat dengan tepat kedudukan kaki dan pembahagian berat badan, kemudian berlatih menggunakan pemasa kuda-kuda terbina dalam.","Basic stances (Changquan system)":"Kuda-kuda asas (sistem Changquan)","Horse · Bow · Empty · Drop · Cross":"Kuda · Busur · Kosong · Rendah · Silang","Weight split, this stance (front / back)":"Pembahagian berat badan, kuda-kuda ini (depan / belakang)","Varies by school — common training values":"Berbeza mengikut aliran — nilai latihan lazim","Suggested hold for beginners":"Tempoh tahan yang disyorkan untuk pemula","3 sets per stance, building to 1–2 min":"3 set setiap kuda-kuda, beransur-ansur hingga 1–2 minit","Stances you have mastered":"Kuda-kuda yang telah anda kuasai","Mark each stance as mastered below":"Tandakan setiap kuda-kuda sebagai telah dikuasai di bawah","Choose your level (animation depth updates instantly)":"Pilih tahap anda (kedalaman animasi dikemas kini serta-merta)","Beginner · higher":"Pemula · lebih tinggi","Standard · full depth":"Standard · kedalaman penuh","Pick a stance (in traditional teaching order)":"Pilih kuda-kuda untuk melihat butirannya (mengikut susunan pengajaran tradisional)","Weight (front / back)":"Berat badan (depan / belakang)","Foot distance":"Jarak kaki","Main benefit":"Manfaat utama","How to stand":"Cara berdiri","How to practise":"Cara berlatih","Where it's used":"Digunakan di mana","FRONT 0°":"HADAPAN 0°","RIGHT":"KANAN","LEFT":"KIRI","Foot placement & weight (top view)":"Kedudukan kaki & berat badan (pandangan atas)","↑ facing forward":"↑ menghadap ke hadapan","What this stance trains":"Apa yang dilatih oleh kuda-kuda ini","For education only. Stance details vary between schools — follow your own teacher. Stop if you feel knee or hip pain and seek professional advice.":"Kandungan halaman ini hanya untuk rujukan pendidikan. Butiran kuda-kuda berbeza antara aliran, ikut panduan guru anda sendiri. Berhenti jika anda berasa sakit di lutut atau pinggul dan dapatkan nasihat profesional.","5 Basic Kung Fu Stances: Horse, Bow, Empty, Drop & Cross — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"5 Kedudukan Asas Kung Fu: Horse, Bow, Empty, Drop & Cross — Panduan Interaktif | KungfuTutor","Learn the five basic kung fu stances — Ma Bu (horse), Gong Bu (bow), Xu Bu (empty), Pu Bu (drop) and Xie Bu (cross) — with animated front and side views, foot placement, weight distribution, common mistakes and a stance timer.":"Pelajari lima kedudukan asas kung fu — Ma Bu (kuda), Gong Bu (busur), Xu Bu (kosong), Pu Bu (rendah) dan Xie Bu (silang) — dengan paparan animasi hadapan dan sisi, kedudukan kaki, pengagihan berat badan, kesilapan lazim dan pemasa kedudukan.","The 5 Basic Kung Fu Stances — Interactive Guide":"5 Kedudukan Asas Kung Fu — Panduan Interaktif","What are the five basic kung fu stances?":"Apakah lima kuda-kuda asas dalam kung fu?","Horse stance (Ma Bu), bow stance (Gong Bu), empty stance (Xu Bu), drop stance (Pu Bu) and cross stance (Xie Bu).":"Kuda-kuda kuda (Ma Bu), kuda-kuda busur (Gong Bu), kuda-kuda kosong (Xu Bu), kuda-kuda rendah (Pu Bu) dan kuda-kuda silang (Xie Bu).","How long should a beginner hold horse stance?":"Berapa lama pemula patut menahan kuda-kuda (horse stance)?","Start with three sets of about 30 seconds with good form and build gradually towards two minutes. Stand higher rather than letting the knees cave in.":"Mulakan dengan tiga set kira-kira 30 saat dengan postur yang betul, dan tingkatkan secara beransur-ansur sehingga dua minit. Berdiri lebih tinggi daripada membiarkan lutut masuk ke dalam.","Is horse stance bad for your knees?":"Adakah kuda-kuda (horse stance) buruk untuk lutut anda?","With knees tracking over the toes and a depth you can control, it is a common strength exercise. Pain is a signal to stand higher or stop and seek advice from an instructor or doctor.":"Dengan lutut mengikut arah jari kaki dan kedalaman yang anda boleh kawal, ini ialah senaman kekuatan yang biasa. Kesakitan ialah isyarat untuk berdiri lebih tinggi atau berhenti dan mendapatkan nasihat daripada jurulatih atau doktor.","Horse Stance":"Kuda-kuda Kuda","about 3 foot lengths, parallel":"kira-kira 3 panjang kaki, selari","Thigh and hip endurance":"Daya tahan paha dan pinggul","THIGHS NEAR LEVEL · KNEES OVER TOES":"PAHA HAMPIR MENDATAR · LUTUT DI ATAS JARI KAKI","Feet parallel about three foot lengths apart, toes forward. Bend the knees and sink until the thighs are close to level, pressing the knees out over the toes. Keep the back upright, chin tucked, shoulders relaxed and fists at the waist. Weight sits evenly between both feet.":"Kaki selari, berjarak kira-kira tiga panjang tapak kaki, hujung kaki menghala ke hadapan. Tekukkan lutut dan rendahkan badan sehingga paha hampir mendatar, dorong lutut ke luar ke arah hujung jari kaki. Kekalkan badan tegak, dagu dirapatkan, bahu rileks dan genggaman di pinggang. Berat badan seimbang di antara kedua-dua kaki.","Knees caving inward; leaning forward and sticking the hips out; toes turned out; holding the breath or shrugging. Beginners should stand higher rather than give up good form.":"Lutut terjatuh ke dalam; badan condong ke depan dan punggung dijulurkan; hujung kaki terbuka ke luar; menahan nafas atau mengangkat bahu. Pemula lebih baik berdiri lebih tinggi daripada mengorbankan postur yang betul.","Start with 3 × 30 seconds a day and build to 2 minutes. Breathe naturally and check knee direction in a mirror.":"Mulakan dengan 3 × 30 saat sehari dan tingkatkan kepada 2 minit. Bernafas secara semula jadi dan semak arah lutut di hadapan cermin.","Almost every kung fu style builds on the horse stance: it trains leg strength and a stable base, and it is the starting point for punches and blocks.":"Hampir setiap aliran kung fu dibina atas kuda-kuda: ia melatih kekuatan kaki dan asas yang stabil, serta menjadi titik permulaan untuk tumbukan dan tangkisan.","Bow Stance":"Kuda-kuda Busur","about 4–5 foot lengths long":"panjangnya kira-kira 4–5 panjang kaki","Front-leg support and back-leg drive":"Sokongan kaki depan dan tujahan kaki belakang","FRONT KNEE OVER ANKLE · BACK LEG STRAIGHT":"LUTUT HADAPAN DI ATAS BUKU LALI · KAKI BELAKANG LURUS","Step forward about four to five foot lengths with the front toes turned in slightly. Bend the front knee until the thigh is near level, with the knee above the instep. Straighten the back leg and press it into the floor, back foot turned in to point about 45° forward, and flat. Keep the torso upright and facing forward.":"Langkah ke hadapan kira-kira empat hingga lima panjang kaki dengan hujung kaki depan sedikit dipusingkan ke dalam. Tekukkan lutut depan sehingga paha hampir mendatar, dengan lutut di atas bahagian atas kaki. Luruskan kaki belakang dan tekan ke lantai, kaki belakang dipusingkan ke dalam supaya menghala kira-kira 45° ke hadapan, dan tapak kaki rata. Kekalkan badan tegak dan menghadap ke hadapan.","Front knee past the toes; back heel lifting or back knee bending; both feet on one line like a tightrope, which kills balance; leaning the torso forward.":"Lutut hadapan melepasi hujung jari kaki; tumit kaki belakang terangkat atau lutut belakang ditekuk; kedua-dua kaki berada pada satu garisan seperti berjalan di tali, yang menjejaskan keseimbangan; badan condong ke hadapan.","Hold each side for 30–60 seconds, then add the bow-stance punch: drive the back leg straight and turn the waist as you punch.":"Tahan setiap sisi selama 30–60 saat, kemudian tambah tumbukan kuda-kuda busur: tolak kaki belakang lurus dan pusingkan pinggang semasa menumbuk.","The bow stance is the classic attacking stance: it sends bodyweight forward behind punches and palm strikes.":"Kuda-kuda busur ialah kuda-kuda serangan klasik: ia menghantar berat badan ke hadapan di belakang tumbukan dan serangan tapak tangan.","Empty Stance (Cat Stance)":"Kuda-kuda Kosong (Kuda-kuda Kucing)","about 1–1.5 foot lengths":"kira-kira 1–1.5 panjang kaki","Single-leg strength and balance":"Kekuatan dan keseimbangan satu kaki","FRONT FOOT: TOES ONLY, NO WEIGHT":"KAKI HADAPAN: HUJUNG JARI SAHAJA, TIADA BERAT","Turn the back foot out about 45°, bend the knee and put almost all your weight on the back leg. Place the front foot about one foot length ahead, knee slightly bent, touching down lightly with the ball or toes, heel raised. Keep the body upright — don't sit back and lean.":"Pusingkan kaki belakang ke luar kira-kira 45°, tekukkan lutut dan letakkan hampir semua berat badan pada kaki belakang. Letakkan kaki hadapan kira-kira satu panjang kaki ke hadapan, lutut sedikit ditekuk, sentuh ringan dengan bebola kaki atau hujung jari, tumit diangkat. Kekalkan badan tegak — jangan duduk ke belakang dan condong.","Sneaking weight onto the front foot (you should be able to lift it any time); support knee caving in; leaning back; reaching the front foot too far so it becomes a bow stance.":"Memindahkan berat secara senyap ke kaki hadapan (anda sepatutnya boleh mengangkatnya bila-bila masa); lutut kaki penyokong runtuh ke dalam; condong ke belakang; kaki hadapan dihulur terlalu jauh sehingga menjadi kuda-kuda busur.","Start with a hand on a wall, 20–30 seconds each side. Test: lift the front foot — if your body doesn't move, your weight was right.":"Mulakan dengan satu tangan pada dinding, 20–30 saat setiap sisi. Ujian: angkat kaki hadapan — jika badan tidak bergerak, berat badan anda betul.","Keeping the front leg \"empty\" lets you kick or change step instantly; it appears in both northern and southern styles as a guard and kicking set-up.":"Mengekalkan kaki hadapan dalam keadaan \"kosong\" membolehkan anda menendang atau menukar langkah serta-merta; ia terdapat dalam aliran utara dan selatan sebagai kuda-kuda pertahanan dan persediaan tendangan.","Drop Stance":"Kuda-kuda Rendah","about 4–5 foot lengths wide":"kira-kira 4–5 panjang kaki ke sisi","Hip flexibility and bent-leg strength":"Kelenturan pinggul dan kekuatan kaki yang dibengkokkan","BOTH FEET FLAT · STRAIGHT-LEG TOES TURNED IN":"KEDUA-DUA KAKI RATA · KAKI LURUS, HUJUNG JARI MENGHADAP KE DALAM","Spread the feet wide to the sides. Sink fully into one leg, hips near that heel, knee tracking the toes. Stretch the other leg straight along the floor with the toes turned in. Keep both feet flat and the chest as upright as you can — don't fold forward.":"Renggangkan kaki luas ke sisi. Rendahkan badan sepenuhnya ke satu kaki, pinggul dekat tumit kaki itu, lutut mengikut arah jari kaki. Regangkan kaki yang satu lagi lurus di atas lantai dengan jari kaki menghadap ke dalam. Pastikan kedua-dua kaki rata di lantai dan dada setegak mungkin — jangan membongkok ke depan.","Heel or outer edge of the straight-leg foot lifting; the bent-leg heel coming up; rounding the back; forcing depth until the knee hurts — stay higher until your flexibility allows.":"Tumit atau tepi luar kaki lurus terangkat; tumit kaki yang dibengkokkan turut terangkat; belakang membongkok; memaksa turun sehingga lutut sakit — kekalkan kedudukan lebih tinggi sehingga kelenturan membenarkan.","Warm up the hips and inner thighs first; hold 20–30 seconds each side, or shift slowly from side to side.":"Panaskan badan pinggul dan paha dalam dahulu; tahan 20–30 saat di setiap sisi, atau alihkan perlahan dari sisi ke sisi.","The drop stance is used for low evasions and threading-palm techniques, and is excellent hip-mobility training.":"Kuda-kuda jatuh digunakan untuk elakan rendah dan teknik telapak menyelit, serta latihan mobiliti pinggul yang sangat baik.","Cross Stance (Resting Stance)":"Kuda-kuda Silang (Kuda-kuda Rehat)","legs crossed, back foot behind the front foot":"kaki bersilang, kaki belakang di belakang kaki hadapan","Low balance and hip rotation":"Keseimbangan rendah dan putaran pinggul","FRONT FOOT TURNED OUT · BACK HEEL UP":"KAKI HADAPAN DIPUSING KELUAR · TUMIT KAKI BELAKANG DIANGKAT","Cross the legs and sink: the front foot turns out and stays flat; the back foot sits diagonally behind it on the ball of the foot with the heel raised, back knee tucked close against the outside of the front calf. Sit down towards the back calf and keep the chest upright, slightly forward.":"Silangkan kaki dan rendahkan badan: kaki hadapan dipusingkan ke luar dan kekal rata di lantai; kaki belakang diletakkan secara serong di belakangnya, bertumpu pada bebola kaki dengan tumit diangkat, lutut belakang rapat ke bahagian luar betis hadapan. Duduk ke arah betis belakang dan kekalkan dada tegak, sedikit ke hadapan.","Leaving a gap between the legs; not turning the front foot out so the knee twists; tilting or rounding the body; forcing the sit and straining the knee.":"Meninggalkan ruang di antara kedua-dua kaki; tidak memusingkan kaki hadapan ke luar sehingga lutut terpuntir; badan condong atau membongkok; memaksa duduk dan meregangkan lutut.","Hold onto support at first, 15–30 seconds each side; later practise flowing from bow stance into cross stance.":"Pada mulanya berpegang pada penyokong, 15–30 saat di setiap sisi; kemudian latih peralihan mengalir dari kuda-kuda busur ke kuda-kuda silang.","The cross stance appears in turns, low counters after evasions, and as a finishing posture in forms.":"Kuda-kuda silang muncul dalam pusingan, serangan balas rendah selepas mengelak, dan sebagai postur penamat dalam jurus.","Foundation stance: your root":"Kuda-kuda asas: akar anda","Static hold · leg strength":"Tahan statik · kekuatan kaki","Foundation stance: bend front, drive back":"Kuda-kuda asas: lentur depan, tolak belakang","Attacking stance · forward drive":"Kuda-kuda serangan · dorongan ke hadapan","Foundation stance: empty vs full":"Kuda-kuda asas: kosong lawan penuh","Balance · quick change":"Keseimbangan · perubahan pantas","Foundation stance: low and long":"Kuda-kuda asas: rendah dan panjang","Flexibility · low transitions":"Fleksibiliti · peralihan rendah","Foundation stance: crossed and seated":"Kuda-kuda asas: bersilang dan duduk","Turning · low stability":"Berpusing · kestabilan rendah","FRONT VIEW":"PANDANGAN HADAPAN","KNEE":"LUTUT","Inner thighs":"Otot paha dalam","FRONT KNEE":"LUTUT HADAPAN","BACK KNEE":"LUTUT BELAKANG","Quads (front leg)":"Quadriceps (kaki hadapan)","Calf stretch (back leg)":"Regangan betis (kaki belakang)","SUPPORT KNEE":"LUTUT PENYOKONG","Quads (support leg)":"Quadriceps (kaki penyokong)","Ankle stability":"Kestabilan buku lali","Hip mobility":"Mobiliti pinggul","Inner-thigh stretch":"Regangan paha dalam","Quads (bent leg)":"Quadriceps (kaki yang dibengkokkan)","Ankle mobility":"Mobiliti buku lali","Hip rotation / mobility":"Putaran / mobiliti pinggul","Knee & ankle control":"Kawalan lutut dan buku lali","FRONT":"HADAPAN","Beginner":"Pemula","Weight ":"Berat","Stance {n} of 5 · Pinyin {py}":"Kuda-kuda {n} daripada 5 · Pinyin {py}","Why learn stances first?":"Mengapa belajar kuda-kuda dahulu?","An old kung fu saying tells beginners to \"stand in stance for three years\". Power starts at the ground and travels through the legs and waist to the hands and feet — without a stable base, even fast techniques lack force. The five stances are the foundation of Changquan and most northern styles, and the building blocks of forms such as Wu Bu Quan (Five Stance Fist).":"Ada pepatah kung fu lama yang mengatakan \"berdiri dalam kuda-kuda selama 3 tahun\". Kuasa bermula dari tanah dan mengalir melalui kaki serta pinggang ke tangan dan kaki; tanpa asas yang stabil, teknik sepantas mana pun tidak berkuasa. Lima kuda-kuda ialah asas Changquan dan kebanyakan aliran utara, serta blok binaan jurus seperti Wu Bu Quan (Tinju Lima Kuda-kuda).","The five stances at a glance":"5 kuda-kuda sekilas pandang","Weight splits and distances are common training values; northern, southern and individual schools differ — follow your own teacher.":"Pembahagian berat dan jarak kaki ialah nilai latihan yang lazim; aliran utara, selatan dan setiap perguruan berbeza — ikut guru anda.","Three rules for safe practice":"3 peraturan untuk latihan yang selamat","Knees always track the direction of the toes — never cave in or twist.":"Lutut sentiasa mengikut arah hujung jari kaki — jangan sekali-kali condong ke dalam atau memulas.","Choose a depth you can control: correct shape matters more than going low.":"Pilih kedalaman yang anda boleh kawal: bentuk badan yang betul lebih penting daripada merendah sehingga rendah.","Warm up hips, knees and ankles first; stop if anything hurts.":"Panaskan badan pinggul, lutut dan buku lali dahulu; berhenti jika ada rasa sakit.","Horse (Ma Bu), bow (Gong Bu), empty (Xu Bu), drop (Pu Bu) and cross (Xie Bu).":"Kuda-kuda kuda (Ma Bu), kuda-kuda busur (Gong Bu), kuda-kuda kosong (Xu Bu), kuda-kuda jatuh (Pu Bu) dan kuda-kuda silang (Xie Bu).","Start with about 30 seconds × 3 sets with good form, then build slowly towards 1–2 minutes.":"Mulakan dengan kira-kira 30 saat × 3 set dengan bentuk yang baik, kemudian tambah perlahan-lahan hingga 1–2 minit.","Is horse stance bad for the knees?":"Adakah kuda-kuda kuda tidak baik untuk lutut?","With knees over the toes and a depth you control, it is a common strength exercise. If it hurts, stand higher or stop, and ask an instructor or doctor.":"Dengan lutut di atas jari kaki dan kedalaman yang boleh dikawal, ia ialah latihan kekuatan yang biasa. Jika sakit, berdiri lebih tinggi atau berhenti, dan tanya jurulatih atau doktor.","Who made these animations?":"Siapakah yang membuat animasi ini?","They are drawn by KungfuTutor to show the key points, not an official demonstration of any particular school.":"Animasi ini dilukis oleh KungfuTutor untuk menunjukkan perkara penting, bukan demonstrasi rasmi mana-mana aliran.","Beginner (low kicks)":"Pemula (tendangan rendah)","Standard height":"Ketinggian standard","Strikes with: ":"Serangan dengan:","Technique {n} of 6 · {type} · Pinyin {py}":"Teknik {n} daripada 6 · {type} · Pinyin {py}","First, make a proper fist":"Pertama, buat genggaman tangan yang betul","Roll the four fingers tightly into the palm and fold the thumb across the middle sections of the index and middle fingers — never tuck it inside. Keep the wrist straight so the knuckles line up with the forearm; a bent wrist is the most common beginner injury.":"Gulungkan empat jari rapat ke dalam tapak tangan dan lipat ibu jari melintang pada segmen tengah jari telunjuk dan jari hantu — jangan selitkan di dalam. Kekalkan pergelangan tangan lurus supaya buku jari sejajar dengan lengan bawah; pergelangan tangan yang bengkok ialah kecederaan paling biasa bagi pemula.","The six techniques at a glance":"Enam teknik sepintas lalu","Striking point":"Titik serangan","Height":"Ketinggian","Bend-and-extend kicks vs straight-leg swings":"Tendangan lentur-dan-lanjut vs ayunan kaki lurus","The snap kick, heel thrust and side kick are bend-and-extend kicks: chamber the knee, then extend to strike — the line and striking point are what matter. The front stretch kick is a straight-leg swing: the leg stays straight all the way up, building flexibility and hip strength for higher kicks later.":"Tendangan depan, tendangan tumit dan tendangan sisi termasuk \"tendangan lentur-dan-lanjut\": lentur lutut dahulu, kemudian lanjutkan kaki untuk menyerang; yang penting ialah laluan dan titik serangan. Tendangan regangan depan termasuk \"ayunan kaki lurus\": kaki kekal lurus sepanjang masa naik, untuk membina kelenturan dan kekuatan pinggul bagi tendangan tinggi kemudian.","Warm up hips, knees, ankles and shoulders; never swing hard kicks when cold.":"Panaskan badan pada pinggul, lutut, buku lali dan bahu; jangan sekali-kali ayun tendangan kuat semasa badan sejuk.","Don't snap joints into a hard lock — keep a little give and control the return.":"Jangan kunci sendi dengan kasar — kekalkan sedikit keanjalan dan kawal semasa menarik balik.","Use pads and train under an instructor when hitting targets or working with a partner.":"Gunakan pad dan berlatih di bawah pengawasan jurulatih apabila memukul sasaran atau berlatih dengan rakan.","New to stances? Start with <a href=\"../stances/\">the five basic stances</a> — the punch and palm strike are both done in bow stance.":"Baru dengan kedudukan kaki? Mulakan dengan <a href=\"../stances/\">lima kedudukan asas</a> — tumbukan dan tolakan tapak tangan kedua-duanya dilakukan dalam kedudukan busur.","Snap kick vs heel thrust — what's the difference?":"Tendangan sentak berbanding tendangan tumit — apakah bezanya?","The snap kick points the toes and whips the lower leg out, striking with the tip of the foot; the heel thrust pulls the toes back and pushes the heel out in a straight line.":"Tendangan sentak menegangkan jari kaki dan melecutkan betis ke luar, memukul dengan hujung kaki; tendangan tumit menarik jari kaki ke belakang dan menolak tumit lurus ke luar.","Why does the fist turn palm-down?":"Mengapa penumbuk memusingkan telapak ke bawah?","Starting palm-up at the waist and finishing palm-down lines the knuckles up with the target and locks the arm into a strong structure — the standard Changquan punch.":"Bermula dengan telapak menghadap ke atas di pinggang dan berakhir dengan telapak menghadap ke bawah menjajarkan buku jari dengan sasaran dan mengunci lengan dalam struktur yang kukuh — tumbukan piawai Changquan.","What if I can't kick high?":"Bagaimana kalau saya tidak dapat menendang tinggi?","Use the Beginner (low kicks) level and get the line and balance right first; daily front stretch kicks and hamstring stretches will raise your height over time.":"Pilih tahap Pemula (tendangan rendah) dan betulkan dahulu haluan serta keseimbangan; latihan tendangan depan dan regangan otot paha belakang setiap hari akan meningkatkan ketinggian anda dari masa ke masa.","Punches & Kicks":"Tumbukan & Tendangan","KUNG FU FOUNDATIONS · BASIC HAND AND LEG TECHNIQUES":"ASAS KUNG FU · TEKNIK TANGAN DAN KAKI ASAS","Kung Fu Punches & Kicks: 6 Essential Techniques, Step by Step":"Tumbukan & Tendangan Kung Fu: 6 Teknik Asas, Langkah demi Langkah","Two hand techniques and four kicks — the first lessons of Changquan and most northern styles. Each move is broken into steps: click a step to freeze on it, follow the green trail to see the path of the fist or foot, and watch the red dot for the striking point.":"Dua teknik tangan dan empat tendangan — pelajaran pertama Changquan dan kebanyakan gaya utara. Setiap pergerakan dipecahkan kepada langkah: klik satu langkah untuk membeku pada langkah itu, ikut jejak hijau untuk melihat laluan penumbuk atau kaki, dan perhatikan titik merah untuk titik hentaman.","Basic techniques":"Teknik asas","2 hand techniques · 4 kicks":"2 teknik tangan · 4 tendangan","Striking point, this technique":"Titik serangan, teknik ini","Suggested practice":"Latihan yang dicadangkan","10 slow reps × 3 sets per side, then speed up":"10 ulangan perlahan × 3 set setiap sisi, kemudian tingkatkan kelajuan","Choose your level (kick height updates instantly)":"Pilih tahap anda (ketinggian tendangan berubah serta-merta)","Beginner · low kicks":"Pemula · tendangan rendah","Pick a technique (hands first, then kicks)":"Pilih teknik untuk melihat butiran (tangan dahulu, kemudian tendangan)","Target height":"Ketinggian sasaran","For education only. Details vary between schools — follow your own teacher. Warm up first; when practising with a partner, use pads and train under a qualified instructor.":"Untuk tujuan pendidikan sahaja. Butiran berbeza antara sekolah — ikut guru anda. Lakukan regangan dahulu; semasa berlatih dengan pasangan, gunakan pad dan berlatih di bawah jurulatih yang layak.","Basic Kung Fu Punches & Kicks: 6 Essential Techniques — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"Tumbukan & Tendangan Kung Fu Asas: 6 Teknik Penting — Panduan Interaktif | KungfuTutor","Learn six basic kung fu techniques — straight punch, palm strike, snap kick, heel thrust kick, side kick and front stretch kick — with step-by-step animation, striking points, common mistakes and practice tips.":"Pelajari enam teknik kung fu asas — tumbukan lurus, serangan tapak tangan, tendangan snap, tendangan tolak tumit, tendangan sisi dan tendangan regang hadapan — dengan animasi langkah demi langkah, titik serangan, kesilapan biasa dan tip latihan.","Kung Fu Punches & Kicks — Interactive Step-by-Step Guide":"Tumbukan & Tendangan Kung Fu — Panduan Interaktif Langkah demi Langkah","What is the difference between a snap kick and a heel thrust kick?":"Apakah perbezaan antara tendangan snap dan tendangan tolak tumit?","A snap kick (Tan Tui) whips the lower leg out from a lifted knee with the toes pointed and strikes with the tip of the foot. A heel thrust kick (Deng Tui) pulls the toes back and pushes the heel out in a straight line.":"Tendangan snap (Tan Tui) mengayunkan betis keluar dari lutut yang diangkat dengan hujung jari kaki ditunjuk dan menyerang dengan hujung kaki. Tendangan tolak tumit (Deng Tui) menarik jari kaki ke belakang dan menolak tumit keluar dalam garis lurus.","How do you make a correct kung fu fist?":"Bagaimanakah cara membuat genggaman kung fu yang betul?","Curl the four fingers tightly into the palm and fold the thumb across the middle of the index and middle fingers. Keep the wrist straight so the knuckles and forearm form one line.":"Lipat empat jari rapat ke dalam telapak tangan dan lipat ibu jari melintang di tengah jari telunjuk dan jari hantu. Kekalkan pergelangan tangan lurus supaya buku jari dan lengan bawah membentuk satu garisan.","Should I warm up before practising kicks?":"Patutkah saya memanaskan badan sebelum berlatih tendangan?","Yes. Warm up the hips, knees and ankles and do light stretches first; never swing kicks hard when cold.":"Ya. Panaskan pinggul, lutut dan buku lali serta buat regangan ringan dahulu; jangan sekali-kali menayang tendangan dengan kuat ketika badan masih sejuk.","Straight Punch":"Tumbukan Lurus","Knuckles (fist face)":"Buku lali (permukaan genggaman)","Chest to shoulder height":"Dari dada hingga paras bahu","Waist rotation and straight-line arm drive":"Putaran pinggang dan dorongan lengan lurus","STRAIGHT LINE · SHOULDER DOWN · ELBOW IN":"GARIS LURUS · BAHU TURUN · SIKU KE DALAM","Set a bow stance with both fists at the waist, palms up. Push off the back leg, turn the waist and let the shoulder follow as the fist drives straight out from the waist, twisting palm-down on the way. Power lands on the knuckles as the arm straightens; the other fist stays at the waist. Return along the same line.":"Ambil kedudukan busur dengan kedua penumbuk di pinggang, tapak menghadap ke atas. Tolak dari kaki belakang, pusingkan pinggang dan ikut dengan bahu apabila penumbuk meluncur lurus dari pinggang, memusingkan tapak menghadap ke bawah sepanjang jalan. Kuasa tertumpu pada buku lali apabila lengan lurus; penumbuk satu lagi kekal di pinggang. Tarik balik melalui laluan yang sama.","Arm-only punching with no waist turn; shrugging or flaring the elbow; a curved path; a bent wrist (an injury risk); leaning forward and losing the stance.":"Hanya menumbuk dengan lengan tanpa memusingkan pinggang; mengangkat bahu atau membuka siku ke luar; laluan penumbuk melengkung; pergelangan tangan dibengkokkan (berisiko cedera); condong ke depan dan hilang kedudukan.","Do 10 slow reps to check the line and the twist, then 20 alternating reps each side. Use a mirror to check the fist stays level with the shoulder.":"Buat 10 ulangan perlahan untuk memeriksa laluan dan pusingan, kemudian 20 ulangan selang-seli setiap sisi. Gunakan cermin untuk memastikan penumbuk sentiasa sama tinggi dengan bahu.","The straight punch is the most basic strike and the first lesson in \"power from the ground, through the waist, into the hand\".":"Tumbukan lurus ialah serangan paling asas dan pelajaran pertama untuk memahami \"kuasa dari tanah, melalui pinggang, ke tangan\".","Palm Strike":"Serangan Tapak Tangan","Palm":"Telapak tangan","Heel of the palm":"Pangkal tapak tangan","Chest to chin height":"Dari dada hingga paras dagu","Pushing power and wrist structure":"Kuasa tolakan dan struktur pergelangan tangan","WRIST BENT BACK · FINGERS UP · HEEL OF PALM":"PERGELANGAN DILENTUR KE BELAKANG · JARI KE ATAS · PANGKAL TAPAK","From a bow stance with fists at the waist, open one hand and push it forward from the waist. As it travels, bend the wrist back so the fingers point up and the palm faces forward. Drive from the back leg and waist so the force lands on the heel of the palm, then close the hand and return to the waist.":"Ambil kedudukan busur dengan kedua penumbuk di pinggang. Apabila tangan dikeluarkan, penumbuk bertukar menjadi tapak dan ditolak ke hadapan dari pinggang; pada masa sama, lentur pergelangan ke belakang, jari menghala ke atas dan tapak menghadap ke hadapan. Tolak dari kaki belakang dan pusingkan pinggang supaya kuasa tertumpu pada pangkal tapak. Selepas itu, tukar kembali kepada penumbuk dan tarik ke pinggang.","Not bending the wrist back so the fingers do the pushing; locking the elbow hard; shrugging; pushing with the arm without turning the waist.":"Tidak melentur pergelangan tangan ke belakang sehingga jari yang menolak; mengunci siku dengan kuat; menjongkitkan bahu; menolak dengan lengan tanpa memusingkan pinggang.","20 alternating reps each side; push against a wall or pad to feel force travel from the feet to the heel of the palm.":"20 ulangan berselang-seli setiap sisi; tolak dinding atau pad untuk merasai tenaga mengalir dari kaki ke pangkal tapak tangan.","A palm strike is easier on the hand than a fist; self-defence courses often use it to push an attacker away and create space to escape.":"Serangan tapak tangan lebih mudah untuk tangan berbanding tumbukan penumbuk; kursus pertahanan diri sering menggunakannya untuk menolak penyerang dan mencipta ruang untuk melarikan diri.","Front Snap Kick":"Front Snap Kick","Kick (bend & extend)":"Tendangan (bengkok & lurus)","Tip of the foot (toes pointed)":"Hujung kaki (jari kaki dilurus)","Knee to waist height":"Lutut setinggi pinggang","Quad snap and one-leg balance":"Hentakan kuadriseps dan keseimbangan satu kaki","KNEE FIRST · TOES POINTED · SNAP AND RECOIL":"LUTUT DAHULU · JARI KAKI DILURUS · HENTAK DAN TARIK","Stand with feet together, fists at the waist. Keep the support leg firm. Lift the kicking knee until the thigh is near level, then snap the lower leg out from the knee with the toes pointed, power to the tip of the foot. Recoil straight back to the knee lift before putting the foot down.":"Berdiri dengan kaki rapat, penumbuk di pinggang. Pastikan kaki penyokong teguh. Angkat lutut kaki menendang sehingga paha hampir mendatar, kemudian hentakkan betis ke depan dari lutut dengan jari kaki dilurus, kuasa tertumpu pada hujung kaki. Tarik balik terus ke kedudukan angkat lutut sebelum meletakkan kaki.","Swinging the leg without lifting the knee; snapping the knee into a hard lock (hard on the joint); toes not pointed; leaning far back; slow recoil.":"Mengayun kaki tanpa mengangkat lutut; menghentak lutut hingga terkunci kuat (membebankan sendi); hujung kaki tidak dilurus; badan condong terlalu ke belakang; menarik balik terlalu perlahan.","With a hand on a wall: lift → snap → recoil, 15 per leg. Then practise without support, alternating legs while stepping forward.":"Dengan tangan pada dinding: angkat lutut → hentak → tarik balik, 15 kali setiap kaki. Kemudian latih tanpa sokongan, bergilir kaki sambil melangkah ke hadapan.","The snap kick is the root of Changquan kicking and gives the Tan Tui forms their name; a low snap kick is fast and compact.":"Tendangan snap ialah asas tendangan Changquan dan memberi nama kepada rangkaian bentuk Tan Tui; tendangan snap rendah pantas dan padat.","Heel Thrust Kick":"Heel Thrust Kick","Heel":"Tumit","Waist to chest height":"Pinggang hingga setinggi dada","Hip & leg thrust, core stability":"Kuasa tolakan pinggul & kaki, kestabilan teras","TOES PULLED BACK · POWER TO THE HEEL":"JARI KAKI DITARIK KE BELAKANG · KUASA KE TUMIT","From feet together, lift the kicking knee high with the toes pulled back. Extend hip and knee to drive the heel forward in a straight line until the leg is straight, power on the heel. Keep the chest upright, leaning back only slightly, then bend the knee back in and set the foot down.":"Dari kedudukan kaki dirapatkan, angkat lutut yang menendang setinggi mungkin dengan jari kaki ditarik ke belakang. Lanjutkan pinggul dan lutut untuk menolak tumit ke hadapan dalam garis lurus sehingga kaki lurus, kuasa tertumpu pada tumit. Kekalkan dada tegak, condong ke belakang sedikit sahaja, kemudian bengkokkan lutut ke dalam semula dan letakkan kaki ke bawah.","Pointing the toes so it becomes a snap kick; low knee lift so the foot scoops upward; leaning far back; support heel lifting.":"Hujung kaki dimuncungkan sehingga menjadi tendangan sentak; lutut diangkat terlalu rendah sehingga kaki menyauk ke atas; badan condong terlalu jauh ke belakang; tumit sokongan terangkat.","Push slowly into a kick shield or thick pad, 10–15 per leg; the key is knee up first, then a straight thrust.":"Tolak perlahan ke kick shield atau pad tebal, 10–15 kali setiap kaki; kuncinya angkat lutut dahulu, kemudian tolak lurus.","The heel thrust pushes distance open, much like the Muay Thai teep; in self-defence it can push away someone closing in so you can leave.":"Tendangan tolak ini menjauhkan jarak, serupa dengan teep dalam Muay Thai; dalam pertahanan diri, ia boleh menolak orang yang mendekat supaya anda dapat beredar.","Side Kick":"Tendangan Sisi","Heel & outer edge of the foot":"Tumit & tepi luar kaki","Waist to shoulder height":"Dari pinggang hingga paras bahu","Hip abductor strength and flexibility":"Kekuatan dan kelenturan otot abduktor pinggul","CHAMBER · OPEN THE HIP · HEEL LEADS":"TARIK LUTUT · BUKA PINGGUL · TUMIT MEMIMPIN","Stand side-on, eyes towards the target. Chamber the kicking knee with the foot turned in; pivot the support foot, open the hip and drive the leg out sideways in a straight line, letting the body tilt the other way for balance. Power lands on the heel and the outer edge of the foot. Re-chamber, then set the foot down.":"Berdiri secara sisi, mata memandang sasaran. Angkat lutut yang menendang dengan tapak kaki dipusingkan ke dalam; pusingkan kaki sokongan, buka pinggul dan tendang kaki ke sisi dalam garis lurus, biarkan badan condong ke arah bertentangan untuk imbangan. Kuasa tertumpu pada tumit dan tepi luar kaki. Selepas menendang, tarik lutut semula, kemudian letakkan kaki.","Not pivoting the support foot (strains the knee); kicking with the toes; staying upright so the leg can't extend; dropping the leg without re-chambering.":"Tidak memusingkan kaki sokongan (berisiko tegang lutut); menendang dengan hujung jari kaki; kekal tegak sehingga kaki tidak dapat lurus; menurunkan kaki tanpa menarik semula lutut.","Holding a chair back, do slow side kicks, 10 per leg, through the three phases chamber–extend–re-chamber; add hip stretches.":"Sambil berpegang pada sandaran kerusi, buat tendangan sisi perlahan, 10 kali setiap kaki, melalui tiga fasa: tarik lutut, buka dan tendang, tarik semula; tambah regangan pinggul.","The side kick is among the longest-range, most concentrated kicks, with close relatives in Taekwondo and Karate.":"Tendangan sisi ialah antara tendangan yang paling jauh jangkauannya dan paling tertumpu tenaganya, dengan saudara dekat dalam Taekwondo dan Karate.","Front Stretch Kick":"Tendangan Regangan Hadapan","Kick (straight-leg swing)":"Tendangan (ayunan kaki lurus)","— (flexibility drill)":"— (latihan fleksibiliti)","Goal: toes towards the forehead":"Sasaran: hujung kaki ke arah dahi","Hamstring flexibility and hip-flexor strength":"Fleksibiliti hamstring dan kekuatan fleksor pinggul","BOTH LEGS STRAIGHT · TOES BACK · CHEST UP":"KEDUA-DUA KAKI LURUS · HUJUNG KAKI DITARIK · DADA TEGAK","Stand with feet together, hands on hips or arms out to the sides. Keep the support leg straight; swing the kicking leg up straight with the toes pulled back, aiming towards the forehead, then lower it under control. Alternate legs as you walk forward.":"Berdiri dengan kaki rapat, tangan di pinggang atau lengan dibentang ke sisi. Kekalkan kaki penyokong lurus; ayun kaki yang menendang lurus ke atas dengan hujung kaki ditarik ke belakang, disasarkan ke arah dahi, kemudian turunkan dengan terkawal. Tukar kaki sambil berjalan ke hadapan.","Bending the kicking leg; bending forward to fake the height; support heel lifting or knee bending; slamming the leg down and straining the hamstring.":"Kaki yang menendang dibengkokkan; membongkok ke hadapan untuk menipu ketinggian; tumit penyokong terangkat atau lutut dibengkokkan; menghentak kaki ke bawah sehingga menegangkan hamstring.","Only after a warm-up, 10–20 per leg. Height will come — straight legs and posture matter more. Pair it with daily hamstring stretching.":"Hanya selepas memanaskan badan, 10–20 kali setiap kaki. Ketinggian akan datang kemudian; kaki lurus dan postur lebih penting. Gandingkan dengan regangan hamstring setiap hari.","The front stretch kick opens almost every kung fu class as a warm-up and flexibility drill, laying the groundwork for high kicks.":"Tendangan regangan depan hampir sentiasa dibuka dalam setiap kelas kung fu sebagai pemanasan dan latihan kelenturan, meletakkan asas untuk tendangan tinggi.","Basic hand technique: straight line":"Teknik tangan asas: garisan lurus","Bow-stance punch · waist power":"Tumbukan kuda-kuda busur · kuasa dari pinggang","Basic palm technique: upright palm":"Teknik tapak asas: tapak tegak","Bow-stance palm · wrist bent back":"Tapak kuda-kuda busur · pergelangan tangan dilentur ke belakang","Basic kick: bend-and-extend":"Tendangan asas: bengkok dan lurus","Knee lift · snap · fast recoil":"Angkat lutut · sentak · tarik balik pantas","Basic kick: toes back, heel out":"Tendangan asas: hujung kaki ditarik, tumit ditolak keluar","Thrusting power · creates distance":"Kuasa tolakan · mewujudkan jarak","Basic kick: open-hip side thrust":"Tendangan asas: tendangan sisi dengan pinggul terbuka","Longest-range kick":"Tendangan dengan jangkauan paling jauh","Basic kick: straight-leg swing":"Tendangan asas: ayunan kaki lurus","Flexibility · essential warm-up":"Kelenturan · pemanasan wajib","Bow stance set, fists at the waist":"Pasang kuda-kuda busur, kedua penumbuk di pinggang","Open the hand and drive it forward from the waist — power to the heel of the palm":"Buka tangan dan tolak ke hadapan dari pinggang, kuasa di pangkal tapak tangan","Wrist bent back, fingers up; then return to the waist":"Lentur pergelangan ke belakang, jari ke atas; kemudian kembali ke pinggang","Turn the waist and shoulder; the fist twists palm-down and lands on the knuckles":"Pusingkan pinggang dan bahu; genggaman berpusing telapak ke bawah dan hentam dengan buku jari","Pull straight back to the waist along the same line":"Tarik kembali ke pinggang mengikut laluan yang sama","Stand with feet together, fists at the waist":"Berdiri dengan kaki rapat, kedua genggaman di pinggang","Lift the knee until the thigh is level":"Angkat lutut sehingga paha sama aras","Snap the lower leg out, toes pointed — power to the tip of the foot":"Sentak betis ke hadapan dengan hujung kaki dilurus, kuasa di hujung kaki","Snap straight back to the knee lift":"Tarik pantas kembali ke kedudukan angkat lutut","Lift the knee high and pull the toes back":"Angkat lutut tinggi dan tarik hujung kaki ke belakang","Thrust the heel forward until the leg is straight — power to the heel":"Tolak tumit ke hadapan sehingga kaki lurus, kuasa di tumit","Bend and recover the knee, stay balanced":"Bengkokkan dan tarik semula lutut, kekalkan keseimbangan","Stand side-on, eyes on the target":"Berdiri menyerong, pandangan ke sasaran","Chamber: lift the knee, foot turned in":"Bengkokkan dan angkat lutut, tapak kaki menghadap ke dalam","Open the hip and drive the leg out sideways, body leaning away — power to the heel and outer edge":"Buka pinggul dan tendang ke sisi, badan condong menjauh; kuasa di tumit dan tepi luar tapak","Re-chamber the knee, then set the foot down":"Tarik kaki kembali ke kedudukan angkat lutut, kemudian pijak","Feet together, hands on hips or arms out to the sides":"Berdiri dengan kaki rapat, tangan di pinggang atau dilurus ke sisi","Kick straight up towards the forehead, leg straight, toes pulled back":"Tendang lurus ke atas ke arah dahi, kaki lurus, hujung kaki ditarik ke belakang","Support leg straight, chest upright — lower the leg under control":"Kaki sokongan lurus, badan tegak; turunkan kaki dengan terkawal","STRIKING POINT: ":"TITIK SERANGAN:","Waist rotation":"Putaran pinggang","Shoulder & arm drive":"Tolakan bahu dan lengan","Stance stability":"Kestabilan kedudukan kaki","Wrist alignment":"Kestabilan pergelangan tangan","Pushing power":"Kuasa tolakan","Wrist structure":"Struktur pergelangan tangan","Quad snap":"Letupan kuadrisep","Hip flexors":"Otot fleksor pinggul","Knee control":"Kawalan lutut","Glute thrust":"Tolakan otot gluteus","Hip abductors":"Kekuatan otot abduktor pinggul","Hip flexibility":"Kelenturan pinggul","Lateral core":"Kestabilan teras ke sisi","Hamstring flexibility":"Kelenturan hamstring","Hip-flexor strength":"Kekuatan fleksor pinggul","Support balance":"Keseimbangan sokongan","Core control":"Kawalan teras","Current pace: ":"Kelajuan semasa:","Beginner (slower)":"Pemula (lebih perlahan)","Posture {n} of 24 · {group} · Pinyin {py}":"Postur {n} daripada 24 · {group} · Pinyin {py}","Where the 24-form comes from":"Asal-usul Tai Chi 24 postur","In 1956 China's national sports commission took traditional Yang-style Tai Chi, removed the repetitions and arranged 24 postures from simple to harder — the \"simplified Tai Chi\" form. Because it is short and easy to start, it became the most widely practised Tai Chi routine in the world and a standard for competitions and morning practice in parks.":"Pada 1956, jawatankuasa sukan negara China mengambil Tai Chi gaya Yang tradisional, membuang pengulangan dan menyusun 24 postur dari yang mudah kepada yang lebih sukar: bentuk \"Tai Chi ringkas\". Kerana pendek dan mudah dimulakan, ia menjadi rutin Tai Chi yang paling meluas diamalkan di dunia dan menjadi standard untuk pertandingan serta latihan pagi di taman.","All 24 postures":"Semua 24 postur","Name":"Nama","Pinyin":"Pinyin","Group":"Kumpulan","English names vary between books and teachers; these are common versions.":"Nama Inggeris berbeza-beza antara buku dan guru; ini ialah versi yang lazim.","Learn one group (3–4 postures) at a time before adding the next.":"Pelajari satu kumpulan (3–4 postur) pada satu masa sebelum menambah yang seterusnya.","Move slowly and evenly, keeping the same pace throughout.":"Bergerak perlahan dan sekata, mengekalkan rentak yang sama sepanjang masa.","Breathe naturally — usually in as you open, rise or draw in, out as you close, sink or push. Never hold your breath.":"Bernafas secara semula jadi: biasanya tarik nafas ketika membuka, naik atau menarik masuk; hembus nafas ketika menutup, turun atau menolak. Jangan sekali-kali menahan nafas.","Keep the knees in line with the toes, and only move a foot after the weight has fully shifted off it.":"Pastikan lutut sejajar dengan jari kaki, dan hanya gerakkan kaki selepas berat badan sepenuhnya beralih daripadanya.","Health benefits":"Manfaat kesihatan","Research reviews suggest Tai Chi may help older adults improve balance and lower their risk of falls, and may help flexibility, mood and sleep. It is low-to-moderate intensity and suits most ages; if you have heart, joint or balance problems, check with your doctor first.":"Kajian penyelidikan menunjukkan Tai Chi mungkin membantu warga emas meningkatkan keseimbangan dan mengurangkan risiko jatuh, serta mungkin membantu kelenturan, mood dan tidur. Intensitinya rendah hingga sederhana dan sesuai untuk kebanyakan peringkat umur; jika anda mempunyai masalah jantung, sendi atau keseimbangan, rujuk doktor dahulu.","Want stronger foundations first? See <a href=\"../stances/\">the five basic stances</a> — bow, empty and drop stance all appear in the 24-form.":"Mahu asas yang lebih kukuh dahulu? Lihat <a href=\"../stances/\">lima kuda-kuda asas</a>. Kuda-kuda busur, kosong dan rendah semuanya terdapat dalam 24 postur.","How long does the whole form take?":"Berapa lama keseluruhan rangkaian ini mengambil masa?","Usually about 4–6 minutes; slower practice can take longer.":"Biasanya kira-kira 4–6 minit; latihan yang lebih perlahan boleh mengambil masa lebih lama.","How long does it take to learn?":"Berapa lama masa yang diambil untuk mempelajarinya?","With regular practice many people learn the order in a few weeks to a few months; polishing it takes much longer.":"Dengan latihan yang tetap, ramai orang dapat menghafal urutannya dalam beberapa minggu hingga beberapa bulan; untuk menyempurnakannya memerlukan masa yang jauh lebih lama.","Why do some postures have left and right versions?":"Mengapa sesetengah pergerakan mempunyai versi kiri dan kanan?","Postures such as Wild Horse's Mane, Brush Knee, Repulse Monkey, Cloud Hands and the Shuttles repeat on alternate sides. The animation shows one side — use the Left/Right button for the other.":"Pergerakan seperti Wild Horse's Mane, Brush Knee, Repulse Monkey, Cloud Hands dan Shuttles diulang secara bergilir di sebelah kiri dan kanan. Animasi menunjukkan satu sisi; gunakan butang Left/Right untuk sisi yang satu lagi.","Can these animations replace a teacher?":"Bolehkah animasi ini menggantikan guru?","No. They are simplified flat illustrations to help you remember the order and key points; turning directions, hand details and internal energy are best learned from a qualified teacher.":"Tidak. Ini ialah ilustrasi rata yang dipermudahkan untuk membantu anda mengingat urutan dan perkara utama; arah pusingan, butiran tangan dan tenaga dalaman paling baik dipelajari daripada guru yang berkelayakan.","Tai Chi 24-Form":"Tai Chi 24 Gerakan","INTERNAL ART · SIMPLIFIED YANG-STYLE TAI CHI · CREATED 1956":"SENI DALAMAN · TAI CHI GAYA YANG YANG DIRINGKASKAN · DICIPTA 1956","Tai Chi 24-Form: Every Posture, Animated with a Breathing Cue":"Tai Chi 24 Gerakan: Setiap Pergerakan, Dianimasikan dengan Panduan Pernafasan","The 24-form is the most widely practised Tai Chi sequence in the world and takes about 4–6 minutes. Pick any posture to see it broken into steps; the circle in the top corner swells and shrinks with the in-breath and out-breath. Switch on Play the whole form to follow along from start to finish.":"Tai Chi 24 gerakan ialah rangkaian Tai Chi yang paling ramai diamalkan di dunia dan mengambil masa kira-kira 4–6 minit. Pilih mana-mana pergerakan untuk melihatnya dipecahkan kepada langkah; bulatan di penjuru atas kiri mengembang dan mengecut mengikut tarikan dan hembusan nafas. Hidupkan Play the whole form untuk mengikuti dari awal hingga akhir.","Postures in the form":"Pergerakan dalam rangkaian","In 8 groups, performed in one flowing sequence":"Dalam 8 kumpulan, dilakukan dalam satu urutan yang lancar","Current posture":"Pergerakan semasa","Time for the whole form":"Masa untuk keseluruhan rangkaian","Slow and even beats fast":"Perlahan dan sekata lebih baik daripada laju","Postures you have mastered":"Pergerakan yang telah dikuasai","Mark each posture as mastered below":"Tandakan setiap pergerakan sebagai telah dikuasai di bawah","Pace and playback":"Kelajuan dan main semula","Beginner · slower":"Pemula · lebih perlahan","Standard pace":"Kelajuan standard","▶ Play the whole form (auto-advance)":"▶ Main keseluruhan rangkaian (maju automatik)","Pick a posture (in form order)":"Pilih pergerakan (mengikut susunan rangkaian)","Step by step":"Langkah demi langkah","Name & imagery":"Nama & imej","What this posture trains":"Apa yang dilatih oleh pergerakan ini","For education only; the animations are simplified. Tai Chi is low-to-moderate intensity, but if you have heart, joint or balance problems, check with your doctor first and learn with a qualified teacher where possible.":"Untuk tujuan pendidikan sahaja; animasi telah dipermudahkan. Tai Chi berintensiti rendah hingga sederhana, tetapi jika anda mempunyai masalah jantung, sendi atau keseimbangan, rujuk doktor terlebih dahulu dan belajar dengan jurulatih bertauliah jika boleh.","Tai Chi 24-Form: All 24 Postures with Animation & Breathing Guide | KungfuTutor":"Tai Chi 24 Gaya: Semua 24 Postur dengan Animasi & Panduan Pernafasan | KungfuTutor","Learn the simplified Tai Chi 24-form (Yang style) posture by posture: animated demos of all 24 movements, step-by-step breakdowns, a breathing cue, key points, common mistakes and a play-the-whole-form mode.":"Pelajari gaya Tai Chi 24 ringkas (gaya Yang) postur demi postur: demonstrasi animasi bagi semua 24 pergerakan, huraian langkah demi langkah, isyarat pernafasan, perkara penting, kesilapan lazim dan mod main seluruh gaya.","Tai Chi 24-Form — All 24 Postures, Animated":"Tai Chi 24 Gaya — Semua 24 Postur, Animasi","What is the Tai Chi 24-form?":"Apakah Tai Chi 24 gaya?","A short sequence of 24 postures based on Yang-style Tai Chi, created in 1956 in China to make Tai Chi easier to learn. It usually takes about 4 to 6 minutes to perform.":"Urutan ringkas 24 postur berdasarkan Tai Chi gaya Yang, dicipta pada 1956 di China untuk memudahkan Tai Chi dipelajari. Biasanya mengambil masa kira-kira 4 hingga 6 minit untuk dipersembahkan.","How long does it take to learn the 24-form?":"Berapa lama masa diperlukan untuk mempelajari gaya 24?","Many beginners learn the sequence in a few weeks to a few months of regular practice; refining it takes much longer. Learning one group of postures at a time helps.":"Ramai pemula mempelajari urutan ini dalam beberapa minggu hingga beberapa bulan latihan tetap; memperhalusnya memerlukan masa yang jauh lebih lama. Mempelajari satu kumpulan postur pada satu-satu masa membantu.","Is Tai Chi good for balance?":"Adakah Tai Chi baik untuk keseimbangan?","Research reviews suggest Tai Chi may help improve balance and reduce fall risk in older adults. Check with a doctor if you have health concerns.":"Kajian semakan menunjukkan Tai Chi mungkin membantu memperbaiki keseimbangan dan mengurangkan risiko jatuh dalam kalangan warga emas. Dapatkan nasihat doktor jika anda mempunyai kebimbangan kesihatan.","Commencing Form":"Bentuk Permulaan","Part the Wild Horse's Mane":"Membelah Surai Kuda Liar","White Crane Spreads Its Wings":"Bangau Putih Mengembangkan Sayap","Brush Knee and Push":"Sapu Lutut dan Tolak","Play the Lute (Pipa)":"Memetik Pipa","Repulse the Monkey":"Menghalau Monyet","Grasp the Bird's Tail — Left":"Menggenggam Ekor Burung — Kiri","Grasp the Bird's Tail — Right":"Menggenggam Ekor Burung — Kanan","Single Whip":"Cemeti Tunggal","Cloud Hands":"Tangan Awan","Single Whip (2)":"Cemeti Tunggal (2)","High Pat on Horse":"Tepuk Kuda Tinggi","Right Heel Kick":"Tendangan Tumit Kanan","Strike the Ears with Both Fists":"Pukul Telinga dengan Dua Penumbuk","Turn and Left Heel Kick":"Pusing dan Tendangan Tumit Kiri","Lower Body and Stand on One Leg — Left":"Badan Rendah dan Berdiri Satu Kaki — Kiri","Lower Body and Stand on One Leg — Right":"Badan Rendah dan Berdiri Satu Kaki — Kanan","Fair Lady Works the Shuttles":"Dara Jelita Menganyam dengan Kik","Needle at the Sea Bottom":"Jarum di Dasar Laut","Fan Through the Back":"Kipas Tembus Belakang","Turn, Deflect, Parry and Punch":"Pusing, Tepis, Halang dan Tumbuk","Apparent Close-Up":"Seakan Menutup Rapat","Cross Hands":"Tangan Silang","Closing Form":"Bentuk Penutup","Weight shifting":"Peralihan berat badan","Relaxed breathing":"Pernafasan santai","Full vs empty weight":"Berat penuh dan kosong dibezakan dengan jelas","Focus":"Fokus","Breath coordination":"Penyelarasan pernafasan","Upright posture":"Postur tegak","Side-to-side shifting":"Peralihan ke kiri dan kanan","Waist turning":"Memusingkan pinggang","Backward balance":"Keseimbangan ke belakang","Feet shoulder-width apart, arms hanging naturally":"Kaki dibuka selebar bahu, lengan tergantung secara semula jadi","Slowly raise both arms forward to shoulder height":"Perlahan-lahan angkat kedua-dua lengan ke hadapan setinggi bahu","Bend the knees and gently press the palms down in front of the belly":"Tekuk lutut dan tekan tapak tangan perlahan ke bawah di hadapan perut","Shoulders and elbows sink; knees stay behind the toes":"Bahu dan siku diturunkan; lutut tidak melepasi hujung kaki","Shrugging or raising the arms too high; sticking the hips out or caving the knees as you sink.":"Menjongket bahu atau mengangkat lengan terlalu tinggi; punggung terjojol atau lutut masuk ke dalam semasa menurunkan badan.","The opening: settle the mind and let the breath become natural.":"Pembukaan: tenangkan minda dan biarkan pernafasan menjadi semula jadi.","Hands \"hold a ball\" in front of the chest, weight on the back leg":"Kedua-dua tangan seperti memegang bola di hadapan dada, berat badan di kaki belakang","Step into a bow stance; the front hand parts up to eye level, the rear hand presses beside the hip":"Melangkah ke kuda-kuda busur; tangan depan dibuka ke atas hingga paras mata, tangan belakang menekan di tepi pinggul","Parting hands and bowing the leg finish together; body upright":"Membuka tangan dan membengkokkan kaki selesai serentak; badan tegak","Feet on one line so you wobble; leaning forward; hands arriving before the legs.":"Kaki berada pada satu garisan sehingga goyah; badan condong ke hadapan; tangan sampai lebih awal daripada kaki.","The hands part like combing a galloping horse's mane; done three times, left and right.":"Kedua-dua tangan dibuka seperti menyikat surai kuda yang sedang berlari; dibuat 3 kali, kiri dan kanan.","Follow-step half a step, hands holding the ball":"Ikut langkah separuh langkah, kedua-dua tangan memegang bola.","Sit back into an empty stance; the upper hand rises beside the forehead, the lower hand presses by the hip":"Duduk ke belakang ke kuda-kuda kosong; tangan atas naik di tepi dahi, tangan bawah menekan di sisi pinggul.","Front toes just touch; all the weight sits on the back leg":"Hujung kaki depan hanya menyentuh lantai; seluruh berat badan berada di kaki belakang.","Putting weight on the front foot; lifting the top hand too high and shrugging; puffing the chest.":"Meletakkan berat badan pada kaki hadapan; mengangkat tangan atas terlalu tinggi dan menjongkitkan bahu; membusungkan dada.","Like a white crane opening its wings — one hand up, one hand down.":"Seperti bangau putih membentangkan sayapnya — satu tangan naik, satu tangan turun.","Turn the waist; one hand circles back by the ear, the other comes in front of the chest":"Pusingkan pinggang; satu tangan berputar ke belakang melepasi telinga, tangan yang satu lagi berada di depan dada.","Step and bow; the lower hand brushes past the knee to the hip as the upper hand pushes forward":"Langkah dan bengkokkan lutut; tangan bawah menyapu melepasi lutut ke pinggul manakala tangan atas menolak ke hadapan.","Push, bow and waist settle at the same moment":"Tolakan, kuda-kuda busur dan pinggang kukuh serentak pada masa yang sama.","Shrugging and lunging as you push; brushing too far from the knee.":"Menjongkitkan bahu dan menerkam ketika menolak; sapuan tangan terlalu jauh dari lutut.","One hand brushes the knee while the other pushes; three times, left and right.":"Satu tangan menyapu lutut manakala tangan satu lagi menolak; 3 kali, kiri dan kanan.","Bring the back foot in half a step and shift the weight back":"Bawa kaki belakang masuk setengah langkah dan alihkan berat badan ke belakang.","Front heel touches down in an empty stance; the hands close as if holding a lute":"Tumit kaki hadapan menjejak lantai dalam kuda-kuda kosong; kedua-dua tangan dirapatkan seolah-olah memeluk kecapi.","Front hand at nose height, rear hand near the inside of the front elbow":"Tangan hadapan setinggi hidung, tangan belakang berhampiran bahagian dalam siku hadapan.","Weighting the front foot; hands too far apart or stiff.":"Meletakkan berat pada kaki hadapan; kedua-dua tangan terlalu berjauhan atau kaku.","The shape of someone holding a pipa (Chinese lute), ready to play.":"Bentuknya seperti seseorang memegang pipa (kecapi Cina), bersedia untuk dimainkan.","Turn the waist; the rear hand curls up past the ear":"Pusingkan pinggang; tangan belakang melengkung ke atas melepasi telinga.","Step back; the curled hand pushes forward as the front hand draws back to the waist":"Undur selangkah; tangan yang dibengkokkan menolak ke hadapan manakala tangan hadapan ditarik balik ke tepi pinggang.","When stepping back, the toes land first, then the foot settles":"Apabila mengundur, hujung kaki mendarat dahulu, kemudian kaki diletakkan dengan kukuh.","Stepping back too far; feet on one line; leaning back.":"Mengundur langkah terlalu jauh; kaki berada pada satu garisan; badan condong ke belakang.","Retreating while pushing away, as if fending off a playful monkey; four times, left and right.":"Mengundur sambil menolak, seperti menepis kera yang nakal; 4 kali, kiri dan kanan.","Ward off (peng): bow stance, forearm rounded across the chest":"Tangkis (peng): kuda-kuda busur, lengan bawah membulat merentas dada","Roll back (lu): sit back as both hands draw down and back":"Tarik ke belakang (lu): duduk ke belakang sambil kedua tangan ditarik ke bawah dan ke belakang","Press (ji): one hand on the other wrist, press forward":"Tekan (ji): satu tangan di pergelangan tangan yang satu lagi, tekan ke hadapan","Push (an): sit back, draw the palms in, then push forward":"Tolak (an): duduk ke belakang, tarik tapak tangan ke dalam, kemudian tolak ke hadapan","Ward off, roll back, press and push flow without a break":"Tangkis, tarik, tekan dan tolak dilakukan sebagai 4 gerakan yang mengalir tanpa henti","Sticking the hips out or dropping the head when sitting back; lunging on the push.":"Semasa duduk ke belakang, punggung terjongket atau kepala tunduk; semasa menolak, badan meluru ke hadapan.","Like gently holding a bird by its tail; it contains Tai Chi's four basic energies: peng, lu, ji, an.":"Seperti memegang ekor burung dengan lembut; mengandungi 4 tenaga asas Tai Chi: peng, lu, ji, an.","Turn the body, turn the foot in, hands hold the ball":"Pusingkan badan, pusingkan kaki ke dalam, kedua tangan memeluk bola","Ward off":"Tangkis (peng)","Roll back":"Tarik ke belakang (lu)","Press, then push":"Tekan, kemudian tolak","Same as the left side, mirrored (use the left/right button)":"Sama seperti sebelah kiri, dicerminkan (gunakan butang kiri/kanan)","Losing balance in the turn; not turning the foot in enough.":"Hilang imbangan semasa berpusing; kaki tidak dipusingkan ke dalam dengan cukup.","The mirror image of Grasp the Bird's Tail — Left.":"Pantulan cermin Grasp the Bird's Tail — Kiri.","Shift back; the rear hand forms a hook and extends behind":"Alih berat ke belakang; tangan belakang membentuk kait dan dihulur ke belakang sisi.","Step and bow; the front hand turns and pushes forward":"Melangkah dan membentuk kuda-kuda busur; tangan depan dibalikkan dan menolak ke hadapan.","Hook hand: fingertips together, wrist bent down; push at nose height":"Tangan kait: hujung jari dirapatkan, pergelangan dibengkokkan ke bawah; tolak setinggi hidung.","Arms locked in one stiff straight line; tilting the body.":"Kedua-dua lengan kaku dalam satu garisan lurus; badan condong.","One hand hooked like the tip of a whip, the other pushing — an open, extended posture.":"Satu tangan berkait seperti hujung cemeti, tangan satu lagi menolak — postur terbuka dan terentang.","Weight shifts to one side; upper hand in front of the face, lower hand in front of the belly":"Berat badan beralih ke satu sisi; tangan atas di hadapan muka, tangan bawah di hadapan perut.","Turn the waist; the hands swap high and low, circling like clouds; side-step":"Pusingkan pinggang; kedua tangan bertukar kedudukan atas dan bawah, berputar seperti awan; langkah sisi.","The waist moves the hands; eyes follow the upper hand; toes forward as you side-step":"Pinggang menggerakkan tangan; mata mengikut tangan atas; hujung kaki menghala ke hadapan semasa melangkah ke sisi","Moving only the arms; bobbing up and down; feet too wide.":"Hanya menggerakkan lengan; naik turun; kaki terlalu lebar.","The hands drift continuously like clouds across the sky; three times.":"Kedua-dua tangan mengalir berterusan seperti awan di langit; tiga kali.","From cloud hands, the rear hand forms a hook":"Selepas cloud hands, tangan belakang membentuk kait","Step, bow and push — the same as posture 9":"Melangkah ke hadapan, membongkok dan menolak, sama seperti postur 9","As in posture 9":"Sama seperti postur 9, Single Whip","As in posture 9.":"Sama seperti postur 9.","The second Single Whip, leading into the next group.":"Single Whip kedua, menyambung ke rangkaian pergerakan seterusnya.","Bring the back foot in half a step; open the hook hand":"Bawa kaki belakang ke hadapan setengah langkah; buka tangan kait menjadi tapak","Empty stance; the upper hand pushes forward past the ear, the lower hand rests palm-up by the belly":"Kedudukan kosong; tangan atas menolak ke hadapan melepasi telinga, tangan bawah diletakkan di depan perut dengan tapak menghadap ke atas","Body upright; the pushing hand at eye level":"Badan tegak; tapak tangan yang menolak setinggi mata","Weighting the front foot; leaning as you push.":"Berat badan pada kaki hadapan; badan condong ke hadapan semasa menolak.","Like leaning from the saddle to pat the horse.":"Seperti condong dari pelana untuk menepuk kuda.","Cross the hands in front of the chest and lift the knee":"Silangkan tangan di hadapan dada dan angkat lutut","Open the arms to the sides as the heel slowly presses out":"Buka kedua-dua lengan ke sisi sambil menolak tumit perlahan ke luar","Support leg slightly bent and steady; toes back; power in the heel":"Kaki penyokong sedikit ditekuk dan stabil; hujung kaki ditarik ke belakang; tenaga pada tumit","Bending forward to kick higher; a wobbly support leg; pointed toes.":"Membongkok ke hadapan untuk menendang lebih tinggi; kaki penyokong goyah; hujung kaki tegang.","Arms open, heel kick — a one-leg balance test.":"Lengan dibuka, tendangan tumit: latihan keseimbangan satu kaki.","Draw the leg back to a knee lift; the hands settle above the knee":"Tarik kaki ke atas menjadi angkat lutut; kedua-dua tangan turun ke atas lutut","Step and bow; both fists circle in from the sides to meet in front at head height":"Melangkah dan membongkok; kedua-dua genggaman berputar dari sisi dan bertemu di hadapan setinggi kepala","Fists about a head-width apart; shoulders and elbows sink":"Kedua-dua genggaman berjarak kira-kira lebar satu kepala; bahu dan siku diturunkan","Shrugging, fists touching, leaning forward.":"Bahu terangkat, kedua-dua genggaman bersentuhan; badan condong ke hadapan.","The two fists close in from both sides like twin peaks.":"Kedua-dua genggaman merapat dari kedua-dua sisi seperti dua puncak kembar.","Turn around, cross the hands, lift the knee":"Berpusing, silangkan tangan, angkat lutut","Open the arms and press out with the heel (left side — use the mirror button)":"Buka lengan dan tolak dengan tumit (sisi kiri — gunakan butang cermin)","Settle after the turn before kicking":"Stabilkan badan selepas berpusing sebelum menendang","Kicking before the turn has settled.":"Menendang sebelum pusingan stabil.","The mirror of the right heel kick, with a turn.":"Cermin tendangan tumit kanan, dengan pusingan.","One hand forms a hook as you sink":"Satu tangan membentuk kait semasa anda merendahkan badan","Lower body: drop stance, the front hand threads along the inside of the front leg":"Badan bawah: kuda-kuda rendah, tangan depan menyelit di sepanjang bahagian dalam kaki depan","Stand on one leg: rise and lift the knee, elbow above it (\"golden rooster\")":"Berdiri dengan satu kaki: bangkit dan angkat lutut, siku di atasnya (\"ayam emas\")","Both feet flat in the drop; support leg soft when standing on one leg":"Kedua-dua kaki rata di atas lantai ketika merendah; kaki penyokong lembut ketika berdiri satu kaki","Folding forward in the drop; rising too fast and wobbling.":"Membongkok ke depan semasa merendah; bangkit terlalu cepat dan goyah.","Low then high: from the drop stance up into \"golden rooster stands on one leg\".":"Rendah kemudian tinggi: dari kuda-kuda rendah naik ke \"ayam emas berdiri satu kaki\".","Lower body (right side)":"Badan bawah (sebelah kanan)","Stand on one leg":"Berdiri satu kaki","As the left side, mirrored":"Sama seperti sebelah kiri, secara cermin","Forcing the depth — a higher drop stance is fine.":"Memaksa kedalaman — kuda-kuda rendah yang lebih tinggi juga tidak mengapa.","Mirror of posture 16.":"Cermin bagi postur 16.","Hold the ball, turn and step":"Pegang bola, pusing dan langkah","Bow stance; the upper hand turns to shield above the forehead as the lower hand pushes forward":"Kuda-kuda busur; tangan atas berpusing melindungi di atas dahi manakala tangan bawah menolak ke hadapan","Shielding hand above and in front of the forehead; push at nose height":"Tangan pelindung di atas dan di hadapan dahi; tolak pada paras hidung","Shrugging on the shield; feet on one line.":"Menjungkitkan bahu semasa menahan; kaki berada dalam satu garisan.","The hands go back and forth like a weaver's shuttle; once each side.":"Kedua-dua tangan bergerak ke depan dan belakang seperti kok penenun; sekali setiap sisi.","Follow-step and shift back":"Langkah ikut dan alih badan ke belakang","Empty stance; lean slightly forward as the fingers point down and forward":"Kuda-kuda kosong; condongkan badan sedikit ke hadapan dengan jari menunjuk ke bawah dan ke hadapan","When leaning, keep the head and back in one line":"Semasa condong, pastikan kepala dan belakang dalam satu garisan","Dropping the head and rounding the back; weighting the front foot.":"Menunduk dan membongkokkan belakang; berat badan pada kaki hadapan.","The fingers point down like a needle reaching the sea floor.":"Jari menunjuk ke bawah seperti jarum yang mencecah dasar laut.","Rise and bring both hands up in front of the chest":"Bangkit dan angkat kedua-dua tangan ke hadapan dada","Step and bow; the front hand pushes, the rear hand braces above the head":"Melangkah dan membentuk kuda-kuda busur; tangan hadapan menolak, tangan belakang menahan di atas kepala","Arms open like a fan, spreading from the back":"Lengan terbuka seperti kipas, merebak dari belakang","Push and bow not together; shrugging.":"Tolakan tapak dan kuda-kuda busur tidak serentak; bahu terjongket.","The arms open like a fan from across the back.":"Lengan terbuka seperti kipas dari belakang badan.","Turn around, fist in front of the belly (deflect)":"Pusing, genggam tangan di hadapan perut (tepis)","Step and parry forward with the palm (parry)":"Langkah ke depan dan tangkis dengan tapak tangan (tangkis)","Bow and punch forward, the palm near the inside of the forearm (punch)":"Kuda-kuda busur, tinju ke depan, tapak melekat di bahagian dalam lengan bawah (tumbukan)","Punch with the fist upright; don't force it":"Ketika menumbuk, bahagian celah jari menghadap ke atas; jangan terlalu kuat","Shrugging and lunging on the punch.":"Ketika menumbuk bahu terjongket dan badan meluru ke depan.","Deflect, parry and punch blended into one movement.":"Tepis, tangkis dan tumbuk menjadi satu pergerakan yang bersambung.","Sit back; turn the palms and draw them to the chest":"Duduk ke belakang; pusingkan tapak dan tarik ke dada","Bow forward and push with both palms":"Kuda-kuda busur, tolak kedua-dua tapak ke depan","Don't lean back when sitting back, don't lunge on the push":"Ketika duduk ke belakang jangan condong ke belakang; ketika menolak jangan meluru ke depan","Elbows flaring as the hands draw in; shrugging on the push.":"Siku terbuka ke luar semasa tapak ditarik; bahu terjongket semasa menolak.","Like sealing a door shut — draw in, then push.":"Seperti menutup dan mengunci pintu: tarik dahulu, kemudian tolak.","Turn and circle both hands out to the sides":"Pusing, kedua-dua tangan membentuk lengkung ke tepi dan terbuka","Bring the feet to shoulder-width; the wrists cross in front of the chest":"Rapatkan kaki ke lebar bahu; kedua-dua tangan bersilang di hadapan dada membentuk tanda silang","Arms rounded, wrists crossing in front of the chest":"Lengan dibulatkan, titik silang di hadapan dada","Arms squeezed too tight; shrugging.":"Lengan terlalu rapat ke badan; bahu terjongket.","From cross hands, turn the palms down":"Dari tangan bersilang, pusingkan tapak ke bawah","Slowly lower the palms":"Turunkan kedua-dua tapak perlahan-lahan","Arms by the sides, bring the feet together and stand naturally":"Lengan jatuh di sisi badan, rapatkan kaki, berdiri secara semula jadi","Stand quietly for a moment before walking away":"Berdiri senyap seketika selepas tamat sebelum bergerak","Rushing the close.":"Penutupan terlalu pantas, tergesa-gesa tamat.","The form ends where it began — calm and still.":"Keseluruhan rangkaian tamat kembali kepada ketenangan permulaan.","Group 1":"Kumpulan 1","Group 2":"Kumpulan 2","Group 3":"Kumpulan 3","Group 4":"Kumpulan 4","Group 5":"Kumpulan 5","Group 6":"Kumpulan 6","Group 7":"Kumpulan 7","Group 8":"Kumpulan 8","Bow stance":"Kuda-kuda busur","Empty stance":"Kuda-kuda kosong","One-leg stance":"Kuda-kuda satu kaki","Drop → one leg":"Kuda-kuda rendah → satu kaki","Parallel stance":"Kuda-kuda selari","Side step":"Langkah sisi","Stepping back":"Langkah ke belakang","INHALE ↑":"TARIK NAFAS ↑","EXHALE ↓":"HEMBUS ↓","about shoulder-width, toes turned in":"kira-kira selebar bahu, hujung kaki menghala ke dalam","CENTRELINE":"GARIS TENGAH","Technique {n} of 8 · {type} · Cantonese {py}":"Teknik {n} daripada 8 · {type} · Kantonis {py}","Found in: ":"Terdapat dalam:","What is Wing Chun?":"Apakah itu Wing Chun?","Wing Chun is a close-range southern Chinese martial art (from the Guangdong–Fujian region) known for being simple, direct and economical. It spread worldwide after Ip Man taught it in Hong Kong in the 20th century. Its core ideas are the centreline, attacking and defending at the same time, and developing touch sensitivity through chi sao (sticking hands).":"Wing Chun ialah seni mempertahankan diri Cina selatan jarak dekat (dari wilayah Guangdong–Fujian) yang terkenal kerana kesederhanaan, keterusan dan kecekapannya. Ia tersebar ke seluruh dunia selepas Ip Man mengajarkannya di Hong Kong pada abad ke-20. Idea terasnya ialah garis tengah, menyerang dan mempertahankan diri serentak, serta membangunkan kepekaan sentuhan melalui chi sao (sticking hands).","Centreline theory":"Teori garis tengah","Imagine a vertical line running down the middle of your body. Every Wing Chun hand technique works around it: protect your own centreline and attack the opponent's along the shortest straight path. That is why the elbow stays down and the fist stays directly in front of the body.":"Bayangkan garis menegak yang membelah tengah badan anda. Setiap teknik tangan Wing Chun berfungsi di sekelilingnya: lindungi garis tengah anda sendiri dan serang garis tengah lawan melalui laluan lurus terpendek. Sebab itulah siku kekal di bawah dan penumbuk kekal tepat di hadapan badan.","Cantonese":"Kantonis","Found in":"Terdapat dalam","Romanisations follow common English spellings and vary between schools (e.g. Sao / Sau, Fuk / Fook).":"Romanisasi mengikut ejaan Inggeris yang lazim dan berbeza-beza antara sekolah (cth. Sao / Sau, Fuk / Fook).","A sensible learning order":"Susunan pembelajaran yang munasabah","Get comfortable holding the basic stance relaxed for 2–3 minutes.":"Biasakan diri menahan kedudukan asas dengan santai selama 2–3 minit.","Learn the vertical punch, then build to chain punching.":"Pelajari tumbukan menegak, kemudian tingkatkan kepada tumbukan berantai.","Learn tan, fuk, bong and pak sao through Siu Nim Tao.":"Pelajari tan sao, fuk sao, bong sao dan pak sao melalui Siu Nim Tao.","Start single sticking hands and partner drills with a sifu.":"Mulakan single sticking hands dan latihan berpasangan di bawah bimbingan sifu.","Want to compare? See <a href=\"../strikes/\">basic kung fu punches &amp; kicks</a> — the Changquan punch twists palm-down from the waist, very different from the Wing Chun vertical fist.":"Mahu bandingkan? Lihat <a href=\"../strikes/\">tumbukan &amp; tendangan asas kung fu</a> — tumbukan Changquan memusingkan telapak ke bawah dari pinggang, sangat berbeza daripada penumbuk menegak Wing Chun.","What is the centreline?":"Apakah garis tengah itu?","An imaginary vertical line down the middle of the body. Wing Chun protects your own and attacks the opponent's along the shortest straight path.":"Garis khayalan menegak yang membelah tengah badan. Wing Chun melindungi badan sendiri dan menyerang lawan sepanjang laluan lurus terpendek.","What are the three basic hand shapes?":"Apakah tiga bentuk tangan asas?","Tan Sao, Bong Sao and Fuk Sao, all trained first in Siu Nim Tao.":"Tan Sao, Bong Sao dan Fuk Sao, kesemuanya dilatih dahulu dalam Siu Nim Tao.","Can I learn Wing Chun at home?":"Bolehkah saya belajar Wing Chun di rumah?","You can practise the stance, punches and Siu Nim Tao hand shapes at home, but chi sao and partner work need a sifu and training partners — find a qualified school.":"Anda boleh berlatih kuda-kuda, tumbukan dan bentuk tangan Siu Nim Tao di rumah, tetapi chi sao dan latihan berpasangan memerlukan sifu dan rakan latihan — cari sekolah yang bertauliah.","Wing Chun Basics":"Asas Wing Chun","SOUTHERN KUNG FU · WING CHUN BASICS · FROM SIU NIM TAO":"KUNG FU ALIRAN SELATAN · ASAS WING CHUN · DARIPADA SIU NIM TAO","Wing Chun Basics: 8 Techniques, Step by Step":"Asas Wing Chun: 8 Teknik, Langkah demi Langkah","Wing Chun is built on the centreline: guard your own and attack along the shortest straight path. These 8 techniques come from the first form, Siu Nim Tao, plus the basic kick. Switch on the centreline guide to see whether the fist and elbow stay on line.":"Wing Chun berasaskan garis tengah: pertahankan garis tengah sendiri dan serang sepanjang laluan lurus terpendek. 8 teknik ini datang daripada bentuk pertama, Siu Nim Tao, serta tendangan asas. Hidupkan panduan garis tengah untuk melihat sama ada penumbuk dan siku kekal pada garisan.","1 stance · 2 punches · 4 hands · 1 kick":"1 kuda-kuda · 2 tumbukan · 4 tangan · 1 tendangan","Key point, this technique":"Perkara utama, teknik ini","The three empty-hand forms":"Tiga bentuk tangan kosong","Siu Nim Tao · Chum Kiu · Biu Jee":"Siu Nim Tao · Chum Kiu · Biu Jee","Centreline guide (shows the centreline and the elbow)":"Panduan garisan tengah (menunjukkan garisan tengah dan siku)","Show centreline":"Tunjukkan garisan tengah","Hide":"Sembunyikan","Details differ between lineages (Ip Man, Yuen Kay-San and others)":"Butiran berbeza antara aliran (Ip Man, Yuen Kay-San dan lain-lain)","Pick a technique (in Siu Nim Tao learning order)":"Pilih teknik (mengikut urutan pembelajaran Siu Nim Tao)","Foot placement (top view): toes in":"Kedudukan kaki (pandangan atas): jari kaki ke dalam","↑ facing the opponent":"↑ menghadap lawan","For education only. Wing Chun lineages differ — follow your own sifu, and practise partner drills under a qualified instructor.":"Untuk tujuan pendidikan sahaja. Aliran Wing Chun berbeza-beza — ikutlah sifu anda sendiri, dan berlatih latihan berpasangan di bawah jurulatih yang bertauliah.","Wing Chun Basics: Stance, Vertical Punch, Chain Punch, Tan, Bong, Fuk & Pak Sao — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"Asas Wing Chun: Kedudukan, Tumbukan Menegak, Tumbukan Berantai, Tan, Bong, Fuk & Pak Sao — Panduan Interaktif | KungfuTutor","Learn 8 Wing Chun basics from Siu Nim Tao — Yee Jee Kim Yeung Ma stance, vertical punch, chain punch, Tan Sao, Bong Sao, Fuk Sao, Pak Sao and the front kick — with step-by-step animation and a centreline guide.":"Pelajari 8 asas Wing Chun daripada Siu Nim Tao — kedudukan Yee Jee Kim Yeung Ma, tumbukan menegak, tumbukan berantai, Tan Sao, Bong Sao, Fuk Sao, Pak Sao dan tendangan hadapan — dengan animasi langkah demi langkah dan panduan garisan tengah.","Wing Chun Basics — Interactive Step-by-Step Guide":"Asas Wing Chun — Panduan Interaktif Langkah demi Langkah","What is the centreline in Wing Chun?":"Apakah garisan tengah dalam Wing Chun?","An imaginary vertical line down the middle of the body. Wing Chun techniques protect your own centreline and attack along the shortest, straightest path to the opponent's.":"Garisan menegak khayalan di tengah badan. Teknik Wing Chun melindungi garisan tengah badan anda sendiri dan menyerang sepanjang laluan paling pendek dan paling lurus ke garisan tengah lawan.","What are the three basic hand shapes in Wing Chun?":"Apakah tiga bentuk tangan asas dalam Wing Chun?","Tan Sao (dispersing hand), Bong Sao (wing arm) and Fuk Sao (bridge-on hand), all trained first in the Siu Nim Tao form.":"Tan Sao (tangan penyebar), Bong Sao (lengan sayap) dan Fuk Sao (tangan jambatan), yang semuanya dilatih dahulu dalam bentuk Siu Nim Tao.","Why does the Wing Chun punch use a vertical fist?":"Mengapakah tumbukan Wing Chun menggunakan genggaman menegak?","With the thumb side up, the elbow can stay down behind the fist on the centreline, giving a short, straight and well-supported punch.":"Dengan sisi ibu jari menghadap ke atas, siku boleh kekal di bawah dan di belakang genggaman pada garisan tengah, menghasilkan tumbukan yang pendek, lurus dan kukuh.","Wing Chun Basic Stance":"Kedudukan Asas Wing Chun","Toes in, knees in, hips tucked":"Jari kaki ke dalam, lutut ke dalam, pinggul dikemaskan","Opening of Siu Nim Tao":"Pembukaan Siu Nim Tao","Lower-body structure, centreline awareness":"Struktur badan bawah, kesedaran garis tengah","TOES IN · KNEES GENTLY IN · WEIGHT EVEN":"JARI KAKI KE DALAM · LUTUT SEDIKIT KE DALAM · BERAT SEIMBANG","From feet together, bend the knees and sink. Pivot on the heels to turn the toes out, then pivot on the balls of the feet to push the heels out, ending pigeon-toed. Feet are about shoulder-width, knees squeeze gently inward (the \"goat-clamping\" idea), hips tucked, back upright and weight even. Fists rest at the sides of the chest.":"Dari kedudukan kaki rapat, lentur lutut dan turunkan badan. Pusing pada tumit untuk membuka hujung kaki ke luar, kemudian pusing pada bola kaki untuk menolak tumit ke luar, berakhir dengan jari kaki ke dalam. Kaki kira-kira selebar bahu, lutut dikepit sedikit ke dalam (idea \"mengapit kambing\"), pinggul dikemaskan, badan tegak dan berat seimbang. Penumbuk berada di sisi dada.","Squeezing the knees so hard they ache; sticking the hips out and leaning forward; feet too wide like a horse stance; tense shoulders and a rigid body.":"Mengapit lutut terlalu kuat sehingga sakit; pinggul terjulur ke belakang dan badan condong ke depan; kaki terlalu lebar seperti kedudukan kuda; bahu tegang dan badan kaku.","Open the stance 10 times a day and hold 1–3 minutes, relaxed with natural breathing — this is also how Siu Nim Tao begins.":"Buka kedudukan 10 kali sehari dan tahan 1–3 minit, santai dengan pernafasan semula jadi — inilah juga permulaan Siu Nim Tao.","The stance squares you to the opponent, protects the groin and keeps the centreline; every Wing Chun hand technique grows from this structure.":"Kedudukan ini menjadikan badan betul-betul menghadap lawan, melindungi kawasan kemaluan dan mengekalkan garis tengah; setiap teknik tangan Wing Chun tumbuh daripada struktur ini.","Vertical Punch":"Tumbukan Menegak","Vertical fist, elbow down, on the centreline":"Penumbuk menegak, siku ke bawah, di garis tengah","Siu Nim Tao":"Siu Nim Tao","Straight-line power and elbow structure":"Kuasa garis lurus dan struktur siku","ELBOW DOWN · CENTRELINE · SHOULDER RELAXED":"SIKU KE BAWAH · GARIS TENGAH · BAHU SANTAI","Hold the fist upright (thumb side up) on the centreline in front of the chest, elbow pointing down. Drive the elbow forward along the centreline so the fist travels in a straight line and lands with the bottom three knuckles. Extend almost to straight without locking. Keep the shoulder relaxed — the power comes from the elbow drive and body structure.":"Pegang penumbuk tegak (sisi ibu jari di atas) pada garis tengah di hadapan dada, siku menghala ke bawah. Tolak siku ke hadapan sepanjang garis tengah supaya penumbuk bergerak dalam garis lurus dan mendarat dengan tiga buku jari bawah. Lanjutkan hampir lurus tanpa mengunci. Biarkan bahu rileks: kuasa datang daripada tolakan siku dan struktur badan.","Flaring the elbow out (losing the centreline structure); turning the fist palm-down; shrugging or lunging forward; snapping the elbow into a hard lock.":"Siku terkembang ke luar (hilang struktur garis tengah); memusingkan penumbuk menghadap ke bawah; mengangkat bahu atau menerpa ke hadapan; mengunci siku dengan kuat.","20 slow punches in front of a mirror, checking the fist stays on the centreline and the elbow stays down; then practise on a wall bag.":"20 tumbukan perlahan di hadapan cermin, memeriksa penumbuk kekal pada garis tengah dan siku kekal di bawah; kemudian berlatih pada beg dinding.","The vertical punch takes the shortest, most direct path — the clearest expression of Wing Chun's centreline theory.":"Tumbukan menegak mengambil laluan paling pendek dan paling langsung, ungkapan paling jelas teori garis tengah Wing Chun.","Chain Punch":"Tumbukan Berantai","Fists alternate, rolling on the centreline":"Dua penumbuk bergilir, bergerak di garis tengah","Siu Nim Tao (single) → drills":"Siu Nim Tao (tunggal) → latihan berpasangan","Two-hand coordination and continuous speed":"Koordinasi dua tangan dan kelajuan berterusan","ONE OUT, ONE BACK · ALWAYS ON THE CENTRELINE":"SATU KELUAR, SATU BALIK · SENTIASA DI GARIS TENGAH","Stack both fists on the centreline. Fire the first punch; as the second rolls out over the forearm along the centreline, the first returns underneath. The fists keep cycling like a wheel, so one hand always holds the centreline. Keep the elbows down, shoulders loose and the rhythm even.":"Susun kedua-dua penumbuk pada garis tengah. Lepaskan tumbukan pertama; apabila yang kedua bergulir di atas lengan bawah sepanjang garis tengah, yang pertama kembali di bawah. Penumbuk terus berkitar seperti roda, jadi satu tangan sentiasa memegang garis tengah. Kekalkan siku di bawah, bahu longgar dan irama sekata.","Chasing speed and losing the centreline; arms making circles instead of lines; shrugging and holding the breath; pulling back before the punch arrives.":"Mengejar kelajuan dan kehilangan garis tengah; lengan membuat bulatan dan bukan garis lurus; mengangkat bahu dan menahan nafas; menarik balik sebelum tumbukan sampai.","Start at 1–2 punches a second for 30 seconds, then build speed; use a wall bag and keep breathing.":"Mula dengan 1–2 tumbukan sesaat selama 30 saat, kemudian tingkatkan kelajuan; gunakan beg dinding dan teruskan bernafas.","Chain punching keeps attacks continuous and is one of Wing Chun's best-known techniques for close-range pressure.":"Tumbukan berantai memastikan serangan berterusan dan merupakan antara teknik Wing Chun yang paling terkenal untuk tekanan jarak dekat.","Tan Sao (Dispersing Hand)":"Tan Sao (Tangan Penyebar)","Hand":"Tangan","Palm up, elbow a fist from the body":"Telapak tangan menghadap ke atas, siku sejarak satu genggaman dari badan","Siu Nim Tao, section 2":"Siu Nim Tao, bahagian 2","Arm structure and redirecting force":"Struktur lengan dan pengalihan daya","PALM UP · ELBOW ONE FIST AWAY · SHOULDER DOWN":"TELAPAK KE ATAS · SIKU SEJARAK SATU GENGGAMAN · BAHU JANGAN NAIK","Starting from the centreline, turn the palm up and send the hand forward along it. The elbow settles about a fist's distance in front of the body, forearm angled towards the centre, fingers pointing forward. The outer forearm guides incoming force aside — it doesn't collide with it.":"Bermula dari garis tengah, pusingkan telapak tangan ke atas dan hulurkan tangan ke hadapan sepanjang garisan itu. Siku berhenti kira-kira sejarak satu genggaman di hadapan badan, lengan bawah condong ke tengah, jari menghala ke hadapan. Bahagian luar lengan bawah mengarahkan daya yang datang ke tepi — ia tidak bertembung dengannya.","Elbow too far out or jammed against the body; palm not facing up; shrugging and pushing with force; drifting off the centreline.":"Siku terlalu jauh ke luar atau melekat pada badan; telapak tidak menghadap ke atas; bahu terjongket dan menolak dengan kuat; tangan tersasar dari garis tengah.","Practise the tan–wu–fuk sequence slowly as in Siu Nim Tao, 10 per side, feeling where the elbow sits.":"Latih urutan tan–wu–fuk perlahan-lahan seperti dalam Siu Nim Tao, 10 kali setiap sisi, sambil merasai kedudukan siku.","Tan sao, bong sao and fuk sao are Wing Chun's three core arm shapes; tan sao often redirects a straight punch while you counter at the same time.":"Tan sao, bong sao dan fuk sao ialah tiga bentuk lengan asas Wing Chun; tan sao kerap mengalihkan tumbukan lurus sambil membalas serentak.","Bong Sao (Wing Arm)":"Bong Sao (Tangan Sayap)","Elbow above wrist, forearm slanting to the centre":"Siku lebih tinggi daripada pergelangan, lengan bawah condong ke tengah","Siu Nim Tao, section 3":"Siu Nim Tao, bahagian 3","Shoulder rotation, structure under pressure":"Putaran bahu, struktur di bawah tekanan","ELBOW ABOVE WRIST · WRIST ON CENTRE · SHOULDER LOOSE":"SIKU LEBIH TINGGI DARIPADA PERGELANGAN · PERGELANGAN DI TENGAH · BAHU LONGGAR","Rotate from the shoulder so the elbow turns out and up, higher than the wrist; the forearm slants down to the centreline with the wrist sitting on it. The other hand guards behind on the centreline (wu sao). Bong sao is a pressure-response shape: when force comes, it turns — it never pushes back hard.":"Putar dari bahu supaya siku menghala ke luar dan ke atas, lebih tinggi daripada pergelangan tangan; lengan bawah condong ke bawah ke garisan tengah dengan pergelangan tangan berada di atasnya. Tangan yang satu lagi melindungi di belakang pada garisan tengah (wu sao). Bong sao ialah bentuk tindak balas tekanan: apabila daya datang, tangan berpusing, dan tidak sekali-kali menolak balas dengan kuat.","Forcing with the shoulder; elbow too low so it becomes tan sao; wrist leaving the centreline; the whole body twisting off line.":"Memaksa dengan bahu; siku terlalu rendah sehingga menjadi tan sao; pergelangan tangan keluar dari garisan tengah; seluruh badan berpusing terkeluar dari laluan.","Tan–bong transitions, 20 each way, small and relaxed; later feel it in chi sao (sticking hands).":"Latihan peralihan tan–bong, 20 kali setiap arah, kecil dan santai; kemudian rasakannya dalam chi sao (sticking hands).","Bong sao turns strong incoming force aside and often flows into tan sao or a grab; it's one of the most common shapes in chi sao.":"Bong sao memesongkan daya kuat yang datang, dan selalunya disambung ke tan sao atau tarikan; ia antara bentuk paling biasa dalam chi sao.","Fuk Sao (Bridge-On Hand)":"Fuk Sao (Tangan Tindihan)","Soft wrist hook, elbow in to the centre":"Pergelangan tangan sedikit melengkung, siku masuk ke tengah","Elbow control and touch sensitivity":"Kawalan siku dan kepekaan sentuhan","WRIST SOFTLY HOOKED · ELBOW IN TO CENTRE":"PERGELANGAN TANGAN SEDIKIT MELENGKUNG · SIKU KE TENGAH","Extend the hand forward from the centreline, palm down, wrist softly bent into a hook. Slowly bring the elbow in to the centreline (in Siu Nim Tao this is done very slowly). Fuk sao rests the wrist and forearm on the other person's arm and controls it through elbow position, not by pressing down.":"Hulurkan tangan ke hadapan dari garisan tengah, tapak tangan menghadap ke bawah, pergelangan tangan sedikit melengkung membentuk cangkuk. Perlahan-lahan bawa siku kembali ke garisan tengah (dalam Siu Nim Tao, ini dibuat sangat perlahan). Fuk sao meletakkan pergelangan tangan dan lengan bawah di atas lengan lawan dan mengawalnya melalui kedudukan siku, bukan dengan menekan ke bawah.","Pressing down with force; elbow flaring; a stiff wrist; rushing it in Siu Nim Tao.":"Menekan ke bawah dengan kuat; siku terkembang ke luar; pergelangan tangan kaku; tergesa-gesa dalam Siu Nim Tao.","In section 2 of Siu Nim Tao, extend fuk sao slowly over about a minute, focusing on the elbow and staying relaxed.":"Dalam bahagian 2 Siu Nim Tao, hulurkan fuk sao perlahan selama lebih kurang 1 minit, fokus pada pergerakan siku dan kekal santai.","Fuk sao is the basic contact shape in chi sao, used to feel the direction of force and control the centreline.":"Fuk sao ialah bentuk sentuhan asas dalam chi sao, digunakan untuk merasai arah daya lawan dan mengawal garisan tengah.","Pak Sao (Slapping Hand)":"Pak Sao (Tangan Menampar)","Short slap to the centre, no over-travel":"Tampar pendek ke tengah, tanpa melebihi sasaran","Timing and using both hands at once":"Pemilihan masa dan menggunakan kedua-dua tangan serentak","STOP AT THE CENTRE · OTHER HAND ATTACKS TOGETHER":"BERHENTI DI TENGAH · TANGAN SATU LAGI MENYERANG SERENTAK","With a relaxed open hand, slap from your own side towards the centreline with the palm, knocking the incoming punch off line. Stop around the centre — no wide sweeps. Usually the other hand counter-strikes along the centreline at the same moment.":"Dengan tangan terbuka yang santai, tampar dari sisi anda sendiri ke arah garis tengah dengan tapak tangan, untuk menolak tumbukan yang datang keluar dari laluan. Berhenti di sekitar tengah — jangan sapu luas. Biasanya tangan yang satu lagi membalas serangan sepanjang garis tengah pada masa yang sama.","Slapping too wide past the centre and opening yourself up; a stiff arm; pausing before the counter.":"Menampar terlalu lebar melepasi garis tengah dan mendedahkan diri; lengan kaku; berhenti sebelum membalas.","With a partner at slow speed: one throws a slow straight punch, the other pak saos and punches at the same time, 20 per side.":"Bersama pasangan pada kelajuan perlahan: seorang melontarkan tumbukan lurus perlahan, seorang lagi pak sao dan menumbuk serentak, 20 kali setiap pihak.","Pak sao with a simultaneous punch is one of the most common Wing Chun combinations — defence and attack at the same time.":"Pak sao dengan tumbukan serentak ialah antara gabungan Wing Chun yang paling lazim — pertahanan dan serangan serentak.","Wing Chun Front Kick":"Tendangan Depan Wing Chun","Toes up, heel drives straight, kept low":"Hujung kaki ke atas, tumit menolak lurus, dikekalkan rendah","Chum Kiu, wooden dummy":"Chum Kiu, patung kayu","One-leg balance and straight thrust":"Keseimbangan dengan satu kaki dan tujahan lurus","KNEE UP THE CENTRE · HEEL STRAIGHT OUT · NO LEANING BACK":"LUTUT NAIK DI TENGAH · TUMIT LURUS KE HADAPAN · JANGAN CONDONG KE BELAKANG","From the basic stance with hands guarding the centreline, shift weight to the support leg and lift the knee up the centreline with the toes pulled back. Drive the heel straight out at roughly knee-to-stomach height. Keep the body upright, then re-chamber and set the foot down.":"Dari kedudukan asas dengan tangan melindungi garis tengah, alihkan berat badan ke kaki sokongan dan angkat lutut sepanjang garis tengah dengan hujung kaki ditarik ke belakang. Tolak tumit lurus ke hadapan pada paras kira-kira antara lutut dan perut. Kekalkan badan tegak, kemudian tarik semula lutut dan letakkan kaki ke bawah.","Kicking too high and losing balance; leaning back; kicking with the toes; not re-chambering.":"Menendang terlalu tinggi dan hilang imbangan; condong ke belakang; menendang dengan hujung jari kaki; tidak menarik semula lutut.","Slow kicks with a hand on a wall, 10 per leg, then push into a thick pad; keep the hands on the centreline.":"Tendangan perlahan dengan sebelah tangan pada dinding, 10 setiap kaki, kemudian tolak ke pad tebal; kekalkan kedua-dua tangan di garis tengah.","Wing Chun kicks stay low and direct and are often thrown together with hand techniques — height isn't the goal.":"Tendangan Wing Chun rendah dan lurus, selalunya digabungkan dengan teknik tangan — ketinggian bukan matlamatnya.","Wing Chun root: the \"goat-clamping\" stance":"Asas Wing Chun: kuda-kuda « kepit kambing »","Square body · centreline · stability":"Badan tegak · garis tengah · kestabilan","Signature punch: the vertical fist":"Tumbukan ciri khas: genggaman menegak","Centreline · straight line · short range":"Garis tengah · garis lurus · jarak dekat","Signature technique: chain punching":"Teknik ciri khas: tumbukan berantai","Speed · continuity · coordination":"Kelajuan · kesinambungan · koordinasi","One of the three core arm shapes":"Salah satu daripada tiga bentuk tangan asas","Disperse · redirect · centreline":"Membuka · mengalih · garis tengah","Wing shape · deflect · never force":"Bentuk sayap · mengalih · jangan memaksa","Cover · control · chi sao base":"Menutup · mengawal · asas Chi Sao","Basic hand: slap the punch aside":"Teknik tangan asas: tepis tumbukan lawan ke tepi","Short · fast · counter at once":"Pendek · pantas · balas serta-merta","Wing Chun kick: the front heel kick":"Tendangan Wing Chun: tendangan tumit hadapan","Low · straight · heel power":"Rendah · lurus · kuasa dari tumit","Stand with feet together, relaxed":"Berdiri dengan kedua-dua kaki rapat, santai","Fists to the sides of the chest, bend the knees and sink":"Kedua-dua genggaman di sisi dada, bengkokkan lutut dan rendahkan badan","Pivot on the heels: toes turn out":"Berpusing pada tumit: hujung kaki dibuka ke luar","Pivot on the balls: heels turn out → toes in; knees gently in, hips tucked, weight even":"Berpusing pada tapak kaki: tumit ke luar → kaki membentuk huruf V ke dalam; lutut sedikit ke dalam, pinggul dirapatkan, berat badan sama rata","Stand with feet together":"Berdiri dengan kaki rapat","From the side: knees soft, back upright, hips tucked — no leaning":"Dilihat dari sisi: lutut sedikit dibengkokkan, badan atas tegak, punggung sedikit dirapatkan — tidak condong ke depan","Fist on the centreline in front of the chest, elbow pointing down":"Genggaman di tengah dada pada garis tengah, hujung siku menghala ke bawah","Drive straight out along the centreline, fist vertical (thumb side up)":"Tolak lurus sepanjang garis tengah, genggaman menegak (sisi ibu jari menghadap ke atas)","Land with the bottom three knuckles, shoulder relaxed":"Mendarat dengan tiga buku jari bawah, bahu santai","Return along the same line":"Tarik balik pada laluan yang sama","Both fists stacked on the centreline, ready":"Kedua-dua genggaman bertindih di garis tengah, bersedia","First punch out along the centreline":"Tumbukan pertama dilepaskan sepanjang garis tengah","The rear fist rolls out over the front forearm as the front fist returns":"Genggaman belakang berpusing keluar di atas lengan bawah depan ketika genggaman depan ditarik balik","Keep alternating, like a rolling wheel":"Teruskan bergilir-gilir, seperti roda yang berguling","Hand on the centreline, elbow down":"Tangan di garis tengah, hujung siku menghala ke bawah","Turn the palm up and send it forward along the centreline":"Pusingkan telapak tangan ke atas, tolak ke depan sepanjang garis tengah","Elbow about a fist from the body, forearm angled to the centre — the arm guides incoming force aside":"Siku kira-kira sebuku dari badan, lengan bawah condong ke arah garis tengah — lengan mengalihkan daya datang ke tepi","Circle the wrist and return":"Pusingkan pergelangan tangan dan tarik balik","Both hands guard the centreline (wu sao)":"Kedua-dua tangan melindungi garis tengah (wu sao)","Rotate from the shoulder: the elbow turns out and up":"Pusing dari bahu: siku berpusing ke luar dan ke atas","Elbow above the wrist, forearm slanting down to the centre; the other hand guards behind it":"Siku lebih tinggi daripada pergelangan, lengan bawah condong ke bawah ke arah garis tengah; tangan satu lagi melindungi di belakangnya","Relax back — bong sao deflects, it never pushes hard":"Lembutkan kembali — bong sao mengalihkan, tidak sekali-kali menolak dengan keras","Extend forward, palm down, wrist bent into a soft hook":"Hulurkan ke depan, tapak menghadap ke bawah, pergelangan dilenturkan menjadi kait yang lembut","Bring the elbow in to the centre; the wrist and forearm rest on and control the other arm":"Bawa siku masuk ke garis tengah; pergelangan dan lengan bawah diletakkan di atas dan mengawal lengan lawan","Stay relaxed — don't press down or push":"Kekal lembut — jangan tekan ke bawah atau tolak","Open hand in front of the same-side shoulder, ready":"Tapak tangan terbuka di hadapan bahu sebelah yang sama, sedia","A short, sharp slap with the palm towards the centreline — don't over-travel":"Tampar pendek dan tajam dengan tapak ke arah garis tengah — jangan melampaui terlalu jauh","Clear the incoming punch while the other hand prepares to strike":"Singkirkan tumbukan yang datang sementara tangan satu lagi bersedia menyerang","Return to guard":"Kembali ke posisi pertahanan","From the stance, hands guarding the centreline":"Dari kuda-kuda, kedua tangan melindungi garis tengah","Lift the knee along the centreline, weight onto the support leg":"Angkat lutut sepanjang garis tengah, berat badan dipindahkan ke kaki sokongan","Toes up, drive straight out with the heel at about stomach height":"Hujung kaki ke atas, tolak lurus ke depan dengan tumit setinggi perut","Re-chamber, then settle back into the stance":"Tarik semula ke kedudukan lutut terangkat, kemudian turun semula ke kuda-kuda","RED DASHES = CENTRELINE":"GARIS PUTUS-PUTUS MERAH = GARIS TENGAH","RED DASHES = CENTRELINE · GREEN = ELBOW (DOWN)":"GARIS PUTUS-PUTUS MERAH = GARIS TENGAH · HIJAU = SIKU (BAWAH)","Lower-body structure":"Struktur badan bahagian bawah","Centreline awareness":"Kesedaran garis tengah","Hip & knee control":"Kawalan pinggul & lutut","Elbow structure":"Struktur siku","Two-hand coordination":"Koordinasi dua tangan","Speed endurance":"Ketahanan kelajuan","Redirecting sensitivity":"Kepekaan mengalihkan arah","Shoulder rotation":"Putaran bahu","Structure under pressure":"Struktur di bawah tekanan","Elbow control":"Kawalan siku","Sensitivity":"Kepekaan","Patience":"Kesabaran","Straight thrust":"Tujahan lurus","Upper-body control":"Kawalan badan bahagian atas","When: ":"Bila:","Move {n} of 8 · {type}":"Pergerakan {n} daripada 8 · {type}","The five layers of self-defence":"Lima lapisan pertahanan diri","Most danger can be avoided long before anyone needs to fight. Good self-defence courses put physical moves last:":"Kebanyakan bahaya boleh dielakkan jauh sebelum seseorang perlu bertarung. Kursus pertahanan diri yang baik meletakkan pergerakan fizikal di tempat terakhir:","Stay aware: ":"Sentiasa berwaspada:","Keep your phone down and your music low when walking; notice who is approaching and where the exits are.":"Semasa berjalan, letakkan telefon dan perlahankan muzik; perhatikan siapa yang menghampiri dan di mana pintu keluarnya.","Avoid trouble: ":"Elakkan masalah:","If something feels wrong, change route, cross the road or walk into a busy shop — trust your gut.":"Jika ada yang tidak kena, tukar laluan, melintas jalan atau masuk ke kedai yang ramai — percayalah pada gerak hati anda.","Talk it down: ":"Tenangkan dengan bicara:","Use the fence and say \"No\" and \"Stay back\" clearly and firmly. Don't argue or insult.":"Gunakan kedudukan bertahan dan katakan \"Tidak\" dan \"Jauhkan diri\" dengan jelas dan tegas. Jangan bertengkar atau menghina.","Leave and get help: ":"Beredar dan dapatkan bantuan:","Hand over your wallet or phone if asked — you matter more than things. Head towards people, shout for help and call the police.":"Serahkan dompet atau telefon jika diminta — anda lebih penting daripada barang. Pergi ke arah orang ramai, jerit minta tolong dan hubungi polis.","Defend only if you must: ":"Pertahan diri hanya jika terpaksa:","Only when you cannot get away, use the moves on this page to create a moment — then leave at once.":"Hanya apabila anda tidak dapat melarikan diri, gunakan pergerakan dalam halaman ini untuk mewujudkan peluang — kemudian beredar serta-merta.","The eight moves at a glance":"Lapan pergerakan sepintas lalu","Move":"Pergerakan","When":"Bila","Why these targets?":"Mengapa sasaran ini dipilih?","The chin, nose, knees and shins can stop someone without great strength, and striking with tough surfaces — the heel of the palm, the bottom of the fist, the elbow and the heel — keeps you from hurting yourself. The aim is to stop them for a few seconds so you can leave, not to injure them.":"Dagu, hidung, lutut dan tulang kering boleh menghentikan seseorang tanpa memerlukan kekuatan besar, dan memukul dengan permukaan yang keras — tapak tangan, bahagian bawah genggaman, siku dan tumit — membantu anda tidak mudah cedera. Matlamatnya ialah menghentikan mereka beberapa saat supaya anda boleh beredar, bukan untuk mencederakan.","Only strike pads, kick shields or cushions — never hit your practice partner.":"Hanya pukul pad tangan, perisai tendangan atau alas empuk — jangan sekali-kali memukul rakan latihan anda.","Do escapes slowly and gently, and stop the moment your partner says stop.":"Lakukan teknik melepaskan diri dengan perlahan dan lembut, dan berhenti serta-merta apabila rakan anda berkata berhenti.","End every rep by stepping back and leaving, so getting away becomes a habit.":"Akhiri setiap ulangan dengan melangkah ke belakang dan beredar, supaya melarikan diri menjadi tabiat.","To go further, join a self-defence class with a qualified instructor.":"Untuk belajar lebih lanjut, sertai kelas pertahanan diri bersama jurulatih yang layak.","To build stronger basic strikes and kicks, see <a href=\"../../kungfu/strikes/\">basic punches &amp; kicks</a>.":"Untuk memperkukuh tumbukan dan tendangan asas, lihat <a href=\"../../kungfu/strikes/\">tumbukan &amp; tendangan asas</a>.","What is the most important rule?":"Apakah peraturan yang paling penting?","Avoid the fight and leave early. Awareness, distance and a firm \"No\" prevent far more harm than any technique.":"Elakkan pergaduhan dan beredar awal. Kewaspadaan, jarak dan \"Tidak\" yang tegas mencegah lebih banyak bahaya daripada sebarang teknik.","How do I escape a wrist grab?":"Bagaimana hendak melepaskan diri daripada cengkaman pergelangan tangan?","Don't pull straight back. Bend your elbow, step closer and rip out through the gap between their thumb and fingers, then step back and leave.":"Jangan tarik lurus ke belakang. Bengkokkan siku, rapatkan badan, kemudian keluarkan tangan dengan pantas melalui celah antara ibu jari dan jari lawan, kemudianundur dan beredar.","Is it legal to hit someone in self-defence?":"Adakah sah memukul seseorang untuk mempertahankan diri?","Laws differ, but generally you may only use reasonable and necessary force to protect yourself, and you must stop and leave once you are safe. Check the law where you live.":"Undang-undang berbeza-beza, tetapi umumnya anda hanya dibenarkan menggunakan kekerasan yang munasabah dan perlu untuk melindungi diri, dan mesti berhenti serta beredar apabila sudah selamat. Semak undang-undang di tempat anda.","Does this work if I am small or not strong?":"Adakah ini berkesan jika saya kecil atau tidak kuat?","These moves rely on distance, direction (like the thumb gap) and tough body surfaces rather than strength. Still, nothing is guaranteed — leaving is always the first choice.":"Gerakan ini bergantung pada jarak, arah (seperti celah ibu jari) dan bahagian badan yang keras, bukan kekuatan. Namun, tiada yang dijamin berjaya, jadi beredar sentiasa menjadi pilihan pertama.","Basics":"Asas","PERSONAL SAFETY · BASICS ANYONE CAN LEARN":"KESELAMATAN DIRI · ASAS PERTAHANAN DIRI YANG BOLEH DIPELAJARI SESIAPA SAHAJA","Self-Defence Basics: 8 Simple Moves to Stay Safe":"Asas Pertahanan Diri: 8 Pergerakan Mudah untuk Kekal Selamat","From setting a boundary and keeping your distance to getting free when someone grabs you — every move is animated, with the grey figure showing the other person. Click a step to freeze it. Every move has the same goal: create a moment, then get away and get help.":"Dari menetapkan sempadan dan menjaga jarak hingga melepaskan diri apabila dicengkam, setiap pergerakan dianimasikan, dengan figura kelabu mewakili orang lain. Klik langkah untuk membekukannya. Setiap pergerakan mempunyai matlamat yang sama: mencipta peluang, kemudian beredar dan mendapatkan bantuan.","First rule: if you can leave, leave":"Peraturan pertama: jika boleh beredar, beredarlah","Self-defence is about getting away safely, not winning. Physical moves are a last resort, and you may only use force that is reasonable and necessary — stop and leave as soon as you are safe. Laws differ from place to place, so learn the rules where you live. These animations are an introduction, not a substitute for a real class: train with a qualified instructor and proper pads.":"Pertahanan diri bertujuan untuk beredar dengan selamat, bukan untuk menang. Pergerakan fizikal ialah pilihan terakhir, dan anda hanya boleh menggunakan kekerasan yang munasabah dan perlu — berhenti dan beredar sebaik sahaja anda selamat. Undang-undang berbeza di setiap tempat, jadi pelajari peraturan di kawasan anda. Animasi ini ialah pengenalan, bukan pengganti kelas sebenar: berlatih dengan jurulatih bertauliah dan pad yang sesuai.","Stay aware":"Sentiasa peka","Avoid trouble":"Elakkan masalah","Talk it down":"Redakan dengan bercakap","Leave & get help":"Pergi & dapatkan bantuan","Defend only if you must":"Pertahan hanya jika terpaksa","Basic moves":"Pergerakan asas","2 prevent · 4 strike · 1 escape · 1 defend":"2 mencegah · 4 serang · 1 lolos · 1 pertahan","This move is for":"Pergerakan ini untuk","Safe gap":"Jarak selamat","arm":"lengan","Out of reach of their hands":"Di luar capaian tangan mereka","Moves you have mastered":"Pergerakan yang telah anda kuasai","Mark each move as mastered below":"Tandakan setiap pergerakan sebagai telah dikuasai di bawah","Choose the pace (the animation updates instantly)":"Pilih kelajuan (animasi dikemas kini serta-merta)","Pick a move (best learned in order)":"Pilih pergerakan (paling baik dipelajari mengikut urutan)","When to use it":"Bila hendak digunakan","Why it works":"Mengapa ia berkesan","SIDE VIEW · GREY = OTHER PERSON":"PANDANGAN SISI · KELABU = ORANG LAIN","What this move trains":"Apa yang dilatih oleh pergerakan ini","For education only — not legal advice and no substitute for a real self-defence class. In danger, leave and call the police first. When practising with a partner, go slowly, use pads and train under a qualified instructor.":"Untuk tujuan pendidikan sahaja — bukan nasihat undang-undang dan bukan pengganti kelas pertahanan diri sebenar. Dalam bahaya, beredar dan hubungi polis dahulu. Apabila berlatih dengan pasangan, bergerak perlahan, gunakan pad dan berlatih di bawah bimbingan jurulatih bertauliah.","Self-Defence Basics: 8 Simple Moves to Stay Safe — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"Asas Pertahanan Diri: 8 Pergerakan Mudah untuk Kekal Selamat — Panduan Interaktif | KungfuTutor","Learn eight basic self-defence moves with step-by-step animation: the fence, keeping distance, palm heel strike, hammer fist, elbow strike, low stomp kick, wrist-grab release and head cover — plus how to avoid trouble and get away safely.":"Pelajari lapan pergerakan asas pertahanan diri dengan animasi langkah demi langkah: pagar (the fence), menjaga jarak, tumbukan tapak tangan, tumbukan tukul, serangan siku, tendangan pijak rendah, melepaskan genggaman pergelangan tangan dan melindungi kepala — serta cara mengelak masalah dan beredar dengan selamat.","Self-Defence Basics — 8 Moves, Step by Step":"Asas Pertahanan Diri — 8 Pergerakan, Langkah demi Langkah","What is the most important rule of self-defence?":"Apakah peraturan paling penting dalam pertahanan diri?","Avoid the fight and get away. Awareness, keeping your distance, a firm voice and leaving early prevent far more harm than any strike. Physical moves are a last resort to create a moment to escape.":"Elakkan pergaduhan dan beredar. Kewaspadaan, menjaga jarak, suara yang tegas dan beredar awal jauh lebih mencegah bahaya daripada sebarang tumbukan. Pergerakan fizikal ialah pilihan terakhir untuk mewujudkan peluang melarikan diri.","How do you escape a wrist grab?":"Bagaimana cara melepaskan diri daripada genggaman pergelangan tangan?","Don't pull straight back. Bend your elbow, step a little closer and rip your wrist out through the gap between their thumb and fingers, which is the weakest part of the grip. Then step back and leave.":"Jangan tarik terus ke belakang. Bengkokkan siku, rapat sedikit ke hadapan dan tarik pergelangan tangan keluar melalui celah antara ibu jari dan jari lawan, bahagian paling lemah pada genggaman. Kemudian undur selangkah dan beredar.","Laws differ between countries, but generally you may only use force that is reasonable and necessary to protect yourself, and you should stop and leave as soon as you are safe. Check the law where you live.":"Undang-undang berbeza mengikut negara, tetapi secara umumnya anda hanya boleh menggunakan kekerasan yang munasabah dan perlu untuk melindungi diri, dan hendaklah berhenti serta beredar sebaik sahaja selamat. Semak undang-undang di tempat anda tinggal.","The Fence (Ready Stance)":"Pagar (Kedudukan Sedia)","Prevent":"Mencegah","— (no strike)":"— (tiada serangan)","Someone closes in and things feel wrong":"Seseorang merapat dan keadaan terasa tidak kena","Setting a calm, clear boundary":"Menetapkan sempadan yang tenang dan jelas","HANDS UP · PALMS OUT · FIRM VOICE":"TANGAN DIANGKAT · TAPAK KELUAR · SUARA TEGAS","Step one foot back half a pace and turn slightly side-on, knees soft, weight even. Raise your open hands between chest and chin height, palms out and elbows bent — like signalling \"stop\". Say \"Stay back!\" loudly and firmly. It looks calm to anyone watching, but your hands are already between you and them, ready to block or push.":"Undur satu kaki setengah langkah dan pusingkan badan sedikit ke sisi, lutut lembut, berat badan seimbang. Angkat kedua tangan terbuka antara dada dan dagu, tapak tangan menghadap ke luar dan siku sedikit dibengkokkan, seperti memberi isyarat \"berhenti\". Laungkan \"Berundur!\" dengan kuat dan tegas. Ia kelihatan tenang kepada sesiapa yang memerhati, tetapi tangan anda sudah berada di antara anda dan mereka, sedia untuk menangkis atau menolak.","Raising fists (looks like you want a fight and can escalate it); hands low or in pockets; standing square with feet together so one push knocks you over; speaking quietly or apologising instead of saying \"No\".":"Mengangkat penumbuk (kelihatan seperti mahu bergaduh dan boleh memburukkan keadaan); tangan rendah atau dalam poket; berdiri tegak dengan kaki rapat sehingga satu tolakan sudah menjatuhkan anda; bercakap perlahan atau meminta maaf sebagai ganti berkata \"Tidak\".","In front of a mirror, go from relaxed standing to the fence in one step, saying \"Stay back!\" each time — 10 times each side until it happens without thinking.":"Di hadapan cermin, bergerak daripada berdiri santai ke kedudukan pagar dalam satu langkah, sambil menyebut \"Berundur!\" setiap kali, 10 kali setiap sisi sehingga berlaku tanpa berfikir.","Almost every self-defence course starts here: it is both a message and a guard. Every other move on this page starts from it.":"Hampir setiap kursus pertahanan diri bermula di sini: ia adalah isyarat sekaligus pertahanan. Setiap pergerakan lain di halaman ini bermula daripadanya.","Keep Your Distance":"Jaga Jarak","They keep stepping towards you":"Mereka terus merapat","Spatial awareness and footwork":"Kesedaran ruang dan kerja kaki","MORE THAN AN ARM · SMALL STEPS · FIND THE EXIT":"LEBIH DARIPADA SELENGAN · LANGKAH KECIL · CARI JALAN KELUAR","Stay in the fence and keep more than an arm's length between you. When they step in, take a small step back or back-and-to-the-side — never cross your feet. Keep your eyes on them while using your peripheral vision to find an exit or people, and shout for help.":"Kekal dalam kedudukan pagar dan jaga jarak lebih daripada panjang satu lengan. Apabila mereka melangkah masuk, ambil satu langkah kecil ke belakang atau ke belakang dan ke sisi, jangan sekali-kali menyilangkan kaki. Pandang mereka sambil menggunakan penglihatan sisi untuk mencari jalan keluar atau orang ramai, dan jerit meminta tolong.","Turning your back; big steps or crossed feet that trip you; backing into a corner; retreating silently instead of calling for help.":"Membelakangkan lawan; langkah besar atau kaki bersilang sehingga tersandung; berundur sehingga terpojok; berundur senyap dan tidak memanggil bantuan.","Have a friend walk slowly towards you while you keep the gap with small steps for one minute; then do it again while saying where the exit is.":"Minta rakan berjalan perlahan ke arah anda sambil anda mengekalkan jarak dengan langkah kecil selama 1 minit; kemudian ulang sambil menyebut di mana jalan keluar.","The bigger the gap, the harder you are to reach and the easier it is to leave. The best self-defence never needs a strike.":"Semakin jauh jaraknya, semakin sukar lawan mencapai anda dan semakin mudah anda beredar. Pertahanan diri yang terbaik tidak perlu menumbuk langsung.","Palm Heel Strike":"Tumbukan Pangkal Telapak","Chin or nose":"Dagu atau hidung","They attack and you cannot get away":"Mereka menyerang dan anda tidak dapat melarikan diri","Whole-body pushing power":"Kuasa tolak seluruh badan","FINGERS UP · HEEL OF THE PALM · STRIKE AND RETURN":"JARI MENGHALA KE ATAS · PANGKAL TELAPAK · TUMBUK DAN TARIK","From the fence, bend the rear wrist back with the fingers up and drive the hard base of the palm upward into their chin or nose. Push off the back foot and turn the hips so your body weight goes with it. Pull straight back to the fence, open the distance and leave.":"Dari kedudukan kuda-kuda, bengkokkan pergelangan tangan belakang ke belakang dengan jari menghala ke atas, kemudian tolak pangkal telapak yang keras ke atas ke arah dagu atau hidung lawan. Tolak kaki belakang dan pusingkan pinggul supaya berat badan turut bergerak. Tarik terus kembali ke kedudukan kuda-kuda, jauhkan jarak dan beredar.","Hitting with the fingers (they bend back); arm-only with no body behind it; staying to watch what happens; slow recovery.":"Menumbuk dengan jari (jari akan terbengkok ke belakang); hanya lengan tanpa badan di belakangnya; kekal di situ untuk melihat hasilnya; menarik balik dengan perlahan.","On a pad or a cushion against a wall, 10 strikes each side — focus on landing with the heel of the palm, fingers up, and snapping back to the fence.":"Pada pad atau bantal tebal yang disandarkan pada dinding, 10 tumbukan setiap sisi. Fokus pada sentuhan pangkal telapak, jari menghala ke atas, dan terus kembali ke kedudukan kuda-kuda.","Many self-defence courses teach the palm heel first: it is simple, natural and much less likely to injure your own hand than a punch.":"Banyak kursus pertahanan diri mengajar tumbukan pangkal telapak dahulu: mudah, semula jadi, dan jauh kurang berisiko mencederakan tangan sendiri berbanding tumbukan penumbuk.","Hammer Fist":"Tumbukan Tukul","Reaching arm or face":"Lengan atau muka yang dihulur","They reach out to grab you":"Mereka menghulurkan tangan untuk menangkap anda","Downward striking speed":"Kelajuan tumbukan ke bawah","TIGHT FIST · LITTLE-FINGER SIDE · TOP TO BOTTOM":"GENGGAM ERAT · SISI JARI KELINGKING · DARI ATAS KE BAWAH","Make a tight fist, raise the lead hand above the shoulder, then bring the bottom of the fist (the fleshy little-finger side) down fast onto the reaching arm or face — like banging a table. Let your body weight drop with it. Return to the fence, step back and leave.":"Genggam penumbuk dengan kemas, angkat tangan depan melepasi bahu, kemudian bawa bahagian bawah penumbuk (sisi isi daging jari kelingking) turun dengan pantas ke atas lengan atau muka lawan yang menghulur, seperti memukul meja. Biarkan berat badan turut turun. Kembali ke kedudukan siap sedia, undur dan beredar.","Hitting with the knuckles (an injury risk); a loose fist; a huge wind-up they can see coming; not leaving afterwards.":"Memukul dengan buku jari (berisiko cedera); penumbuk longgar; ayunan besar yang lawan boleh nampak; tidak beredar selepas itu.","On a cushion or pad resting on a table, 10 each side — feel the contact on the bottom of the fist and bend your knees slightly to drop your weight.":"Pada bantal atau pad yang diletakkan di atas meja, 10 kali setiap sisi; rasai sentuhan di bahagian bawah penumbuk dan tekukkan lutut sedikit untuk menurunkan berat badan.","The hammer fist is instinctive — people can do it under stress with no training — and the bottom of the fist is far tougher than the knuckles.":"Penumbuk tukul ialah gerakan semula jadi; orang boleh melakukannya di bawah tekanan tanpa latihan, dan bahagian bawah penumbuk jauh lebih tahan daripada buku jari.","Elbow Strike":"Serangan Siku","Close-range strike":"Serangan jarak dekat","Jaw or side of the face":"Rahang atau sisi muka","They are very close or holding you":"Lawan terlalu dekat atau memegang anda","Short-range hip rotation":"Putaran pinggul jarak dekat","ELBOW LEVEL · TURN THE HIPS · THEN SHOVE AWAY":"SIKU SEPARAS · PUSING PINGGUL · KEMUDIAN TOLAK JAUH","When they are close enough to grab you, fold the arm so your hand is near your own chest, then turn the hips and swing the elbow forward, level, striking the jaw or side of the face with the point of the elbow. Follow with a two-handed shove and get away immediately.":"Apabila lawan cukup dekat untuk menggenggam anda, lipat lengan supaya tapak tangan hampir dengan dada anda, kemudian pusingkan pinggul dan ayunkan siku ke hadapan secara mendatar, memukul rahang atau sisi muka dengan hujung siku. Teruskan dengan tolakan dua tangan dan beredar serta-merta.","Elbow travelling down or up instead of level; arm not folded tight so it becomes a swing; no hip turn; staying to grapple afterwards.":"Siku bergerak ke bawah atau ke atas, bukan mendatar; lengan tidak dilipat rapat sehingga menjadi ayunan; tiada pusingan pinggul; kekal bergelut selepas itu.","Slowly on a pad, 10 each side — elbow at shoulder height, power from the hips; then add the follow-up \"shove → step back\".":"Perlahan pada pad, 10 kali setiap sisi; siku setinggi bahu dan kuasa dari pinggul. Kemudian tambah langkah susulan \"tolak → undur\".","The elbow is one of the hardest parts of the body; when there is no room to extend the arm it works far better than a punch or palm.":"Siku ialah antara bahagian badan yang paling keras; apabila tiada ruang untuk melanjutkan lengan, siku jauh lebih berkesan daripada tumbukan atau tapak tangan.","Low Stomp Kick":"Tendangan Hentak Rendah","Knee or shin":"Lutut atau tulang sendi","They are closing in from about a leg's length away":"Lawan menghampiri dari jarak kira-kira sepanjang sebelah kaki","One-leg balance and thrusting power":"Keseimbangan satu kaki dan kuasa tolakan","KNEE UP · HEEL OUT · KEEP IT LOW · RECOIL FAST":"LUTUT NAIK · TUMIT KELUAR · KEKALKAN RENDAH · TARIK BALIK PANTAS","From the fence, lift the back knee with the toes pulled up and thrust the heel forward and down into their knee or shin. Pull the leg straight back, plant it, then step away. High kicks are easy to catch and easy to fall from, so in self-defence keep every kick low.":"Dari kedudukan kuda-kuda, angkat lutut kaki belakang dengan hujung kaki ditarik ke atas, kemudian tolak tumit ke depan dan ke bawah ke arah lutut atau tulang kering lawan. Tarik kaki lurus ke belakang, letakkan semula, kemudian undur. Tendangan tinggi mudah ditangkap dan menyebabkan kita mudah jatuh, jadi dalam pertahanan diri pastikan setiap tendangan kekal rendah.","Kicking high and getting the leg caught; kicking with the toes (they jam); leaving the leg out; leaning far back and falling.":"Menendang terlalu tinggi dan kaki tertangkap; menendang dengan hujung jari kaki (jari mudah terseliuh); membiarkan kaki terbuka; condong ke belakang terlalu jauh dan jatuh.","Holding a wall or chair, practise \"knee up → heel out → pull back → plant\" slowly, 10 per leg; once balanced, try it on a kick shield.":"Berpegang pada dinding atau kerusi, latih \"lutut naik → tumit keluar → tarik balik → letak\" perlahan-lahan, 10 kali setiap kaki; apabila sudah seimbang, cuba pada kick shield.","Knees and shins are hard to protect; one low kick can stop someone long enough for you to leave.":"Lutut dan tulang kering sukar dilindungi; satu tendangan rendah boleh menghentikan lawan cukup lama untuk anda beredar.","Wrist-Grab Release":"Lepaskan Diri daripada Genggaman Pergelangan Tangan","Escape":"Melepaskan Diri","— (the gap at their thumb)":"— (celah pada ibu jari mereka)","Someone grabs your wrist":"Seseorang menggenggam pergelangan tangan anda","Finding the weak point and exploding out":"Mencari titik lemah genggaman dan keluar dengan pantas","BEND THE ELBOW · STEP IN · OUT THROUGH THE THUMB":"LENTUR SIKU · MASUK SEDIKIT · KELUAR MELALUI IBU JARI","Don't pull straight back — four gripping fingers beat your pull. Bend your elbow and step a little closer, then find their thumb: the gap between thumb and fingers is the weakest part of any grip. Rip your wrist out through that gap, leading with the elbow. Once free, go straight to the fence and get away.":"Apabila digenggam, jangan tarik lurus ke belakang — empat jari yang menggenggam lebih kuat daripada tarikan anda. Lenturkan siku dan masuk sedikit, kemudian cari ibu jari lawan: celah antara ibu jari dan jari telunjuk ialah bahagian paling lemah bagi mana-mana genggaman. Lepaskan pergelangan tangan melalui celah itu, dengan siku memimpin. Sebaik sahaja bebas, terus kembali ke kedudukan dan undur.","Pulling straight back; a straight arm, using only the wrist; turning towards the fingers instead of the thumb; staying put after you are free.":"Tarik lurus ke belakang; lengan lurus, hanya guna pergelangan tangan; memusing ke arah jari, bukan ibu jari; kekal di tempat selepas bebas.","Have a friend hold your wrist lightly; slowly find the thumb side and turn out, 10 times each side, then let them grip harder as you improve. Go gently — don't twist each other's wrists.":"Minta rakan memegang pergelangan tangan anda dengan perlahan; cari sisi ibu jari secara perlahan dan pusingkan keluar, 10 kali setiap sisi, kemudian biarkan mereka genggam lebih kuat apabila anda semakin mahir. Lakukan dengan lembut — jangan memulas pergelangan tangan masing-masing.","A wrist grab is one of the most common situations; this release needs technique, not strength, so it works for smaller people too.":"Cengkaman pada pergelangan tangan ialah antara situasi yang paling biasa; teknik lepasan ini memerlukan kemahiran, bukan kekuatan, jadi ia juga berkesan untuk orang yang lebih kecil.","Head Cover":"Perlindungan Kepala","Defend":"Pertahan","— (protect the head)":"— (lindungi kepala)","A sudden punch comes at your head":"Tumbukan mengejut datang ke kepala anda","Protecting the head under surprise":"Melindungi kepala dalam keadaan terkejut","ARMS FRAME THE HEAD · CHIN DOWN · LEAN IN · SHOVE":"LENGAN MEMBINGKAI KEPALA · DAGU KE BAWAH · CONDONG KE HADAPAN · TOLAK","When a punch comes suddenly, everyone flinches — hands up, head down. Train that flinch into a real guard: raise both forearms with the hands against the sides or back of your head, elbows forward, chin tucked and body leaning in slightly so your arms and elbows take the impact. The moment it stops, shove them away with both palms, step back, leave and get help.":"Apabila tumbukan datang secara tiba-tiba, semua orang tersentak — tangan diangkat, kepala tertunduk. Latih refleks itu menjadi pertahanan yang sebenar: angkat kedua-dua lengan bawah dengan tapak tangan di sisi atau belakang kepala, siku ke hadapan, dagu dirapatkan dan badan sedikit condong ke hadapan supaya lengan dan siku menyerap hentakan. Sebaik sahaja ia berhenti, tolak mereka dengan kedua-dua tapak tangan, undur, pergi dan dapatkan bantuan.","Closing your eyes and turning your back; arms too wide so the head is exposed; leaning back (easy to be knocked over); covering and never leaving.":"Menutup mata dan membelakangkan lawan; lengan terlalu lebar sehingga kepala terdedah; condong ke belakang (mudah ditumbangkan); terus melindungi diri tanpa pernah pergi.","Have a friend swing slowly at your head from different angles with a soft glove or pillow; practise cover → shove → step back for a minute at a time.":"Minta rakan mengayunkan perlahan ke arah kepala anda dari pelbagai sudut dengan sarung tangan lembut atau bantal; latih urutan lindung → tolak → undur, seminit setiap kali.","Head injuries are the most dangerous kind; covering first gives you the chance to shove and get away.":"Kecederaan kepala ialah jenis yang paling berbahaya; melindungi kepala dahulu memberi anda peluang untuk menolak dan melarikan diri.","Step one: protect yourself":"Langkah pertama: lindungi diri anda","Side-on · open hands · loud voice":"Badan menyerong · tangan terbuka · suara lantang","Distance is safety":"Jarak ialah keselamatan","They step in, you step back":"Mereka melangkah masuk, anda melangkah ke belakang","Safer for your hand than a fist":"Lebih selamat untuk tangan berbanding penumbuk","Straight from the fence":"Terus dari kedudukan berjaga","Bottom of the fist — knuckles stay safe":"Gunakan bahagian bawah penumbuk — buku jari selamat","Comes down from above":"Dihayun dari atas ke bawah","Best when they are very close":"Paling berkesan apabila mereka terlalu dekat","Hips drive the elbow":"Pinggul menggerakkan siku","Legs are longer and stronger than arms":"Kaki lebih panjang dan lebih kuat daripada lengan","Kick low, never high":"Tendang rendah, jangan sekali-kali tinggi","Use the weak point at the thumb":"Gunakan titik lemah pada ibu jari","Direction beats strength":"Arah lebih penting daripada kekuatan","Turn the flinch into a good guard":"Ubah refleks mengelak menjadi pertahanan yang baik","Protecting the head comes first":"Melindungi kepala adalah yang utama","Someone approaches and their words or body language feel wrong":"Seseorang menghampiri dan kata-kata atau bahasa badannya terasa tidak kena","Step one foot back, turn slightly side-on, raise open hands to chest height":"Undurkan satu kaki ke belakang, pusingkan badan sedikit menyerong, angkat tangan terbuka hingga paras dada","Palms forward, firm loud voice: \"Stay back!\"":"Telapak tangan ke depan, suara tegas dan lantang: \"Berundur!\"","In the fence, watch their hands":"Dalam kedudukan berjaga, perhatikan tangan mereka","They step in…":"Mereka melangkah masuk…","…you step back, keeping more than an arm's length between you":"…anda undur, mengekalkan jarak lebih daripada panjang satu lengan","Look for the exit, shout for help, get ready to leave":"Cari pintu keluar, jerit minta tolong, bersedia untuk pergi","They close in and reach for you — you are in the fence":"Mereka merapat dan mencapai anda — anda dalam kedudukan berjaga","Drive the heel of the rear palm up into the chin, pushing off the back foot and turning the hips":"Tolak tapak tangan belakang ke atas ke dagu, tolak dari kaki belakang dan pusingkan pinggul","Snap straight back to the fence":"Segera kembali ke kedudukan berjaga","Open the distance, leave, get help":"Renggangkan jarak, tinggalkan tempat itu, dapatkan bantuan","Make a fist with the lead hand and raise it above the shoulder":"Genggam penumbuk dengan tangan depan dan angkat ke atas bahu","Bring the bottom of the fist (little-finger side) down onto the reaching arm or face":"Turunkan bahagian bawah penumbuk (sisi jari kelingking) ke atas lengan atau muka yang menghulur","Back to the fence":"Kembali ke kedudukan berjaga","Step back and leave":"Undur dan beredar","They are too close and grab your collar":"Mereka terlalu dekat dan mencengkam kolar anda","Draw the elbow back and load the hips":"Tarik siku ke belakang dan sediakan pinggul","Turn the hips and swing the elbow forward, level, into the jaw":"Pusingkan pinggul dan ayun siku ke depan, mendatar, ke rahang","Shove them away with both palms":"Tolak mereka menjauh dengan kedua-dua tapak tangan","In the fence; they keep closing in":"Dalam kedudukan berjaga; mereka terus merapat","Lift the back knee":"Angkat lutut belakang","Thrust the heel into their knee or shin":"Tolak tumit ke lutut atau tulang kering mereka","Pull the leg back, stay balanced":"Tarik kaki ke belakang, kekal seimbang","Plant the foot, step back, leave":"Pijakkan kaki, undur, beredar","They grab your wrist":"Mereka mencengkam pergelangan tangan anda","Don't pull straight back: bend the elbow and step a little closer":"Jangan tarik lurus ke belakang: bengkokkan siku dan langkah sedikit rapat","Rip the arm out towards their thumb — the gap where the grip is weakest":"Tarik lengan keluar ke arah ibu jari mereka — celah tempat cengkaman paling lemah","Straight back into the fence":"Terus kembali ke kedudukan pertahanan","They swing a punch at your head":"Mereka mengayun tumbukan ke kepala anda","Raise both forearms to frame the head, chin tucked, body leaning in slightly":"Angkat kedua-dua lengan bawah untuk melindungi kepala, dagu dirapatkan, badan sedikit condong ke depan","Shove with both palms to make space":"Tolak dengan kedua-dua tapak tangan untuk mewujudkan ruang","Step back, leave, get help":"Undur, beredar, dapatkan bantuan","SAFE GAP: MORE THAN AN ARM":"JARAK SELAMAT: LEBIH DARIPADA SEPANJANG LENGAN","\"STAY BACK!\"":"\"JANGAN DEKAT!\"","Setting a boundary":"Menetapkan sempadan","Stable stance":"Kedudukan kaki yang stabil","Hand position":"Kedudukan tangan","Voice & confidence":"Suara & keyakinan diri","Spatial awareness":"Kesedaran ruang","Spotting exits":"Mengenal pasti laluan keluar","Calling for help":"Memanggil bantuan","Whole-body power":"Kuasa seluruh badan","Fast recovery":"Pemulihan pantas","Downward drive":"Tujahan ke bawah","Dropping your weight":"Merendahkan pusat graviti badan","Getting away after":"Beredar selepas itu","Thrusting power":"Kuasa tujahan","Fast recoil":"Tarik balik pantas","Finding the weak point":"Mencari titik lemah","Explosive release":"Lepasan eksplosif","Leading with the elbow":"Mendahului dengan siku","Leaving after":"Beredar selepas itu","Cover reflex":"Refleks melindungi diri","Guard structure":"Struktur kedudukan","Shoving away":"Menolak menjauh","Escape & get help":"Melarikan diri & dapatkan bantuan","What is Krav Maga?":"Apakah Krav Maga?","Krav Maga (Hebrew for \"close combat\") is a self-defence system developed in Israel that borrows practical movements from boxing, wrestling and other fighting arts. It has no competition rules: training focuses on real situations — reacting fast, using the body's natural reflexes, defending and countering together, and getting away safely.":"Krav Maga (bahasa Ibrani bermaksud “pertempuran jarak dekat”) ialah sistem pertahanan diri yang dibangunkan di Israel, yang meminjam pergerakan praktikal daripada tinju, gusti dan seni mempertahankan diri lain. Tiada peraturan pertandingan: latihan memberi tumpuan kepada situasi sebenar, iaitu bertindak balas dengan pantas, menggunakan refleks semula jadi badan, mempertahankan dan membalas serentak, serta beredar dengan selamat.","Three core principles":"Tiga prinsip utama","Defend and counter together: ":"Pertahan dan balas serentak:","Don't block and then hit — do both at once to spend less time on the back foot.":"Jangan tangkis dahulu baru pukul. Buat kedua-duanya serentak supaya kurang masa berada dalam kedudukan bertahan.","Continuous motion (retzev): ":"Pergerakan berterusan (retzev):","Once you must fight back, keep going without pausing until you can escape.":"Apabila terpaksa membalas, teruskan tanpa henti sehingga anda boleh melarikan diri.","Scan and leave: ":"Imbas dan beredar:","The goal is getting home safe, not winning. Every move ends with scanning and leaving.":"Matlamatnya ialah pulang dengan selamat, bukan menang. Setiap pergerakan berakhir dengan mengimbas sekeliling dan beredar.","Strike only pads, shields or protective gear.":"Pukul hanya pad, perisai atau peralatan pelindung.","In choke and grab drills, the partner rests their hands lightly — no real squeezing.":"Dalam latihan cekik dan genggam, rakan hanya meletakkan tangan dengan ringan. Tiada cekikan sebenar.","End every drill by backing off, scanning and leaving.":"Tamatkan setiap latihan dengan berundur, mengimbas sekeliling dan beredar.","To go further, join a Krav Maga class with a qualified instructor.":"Untuk meneruskan lagi, sertai kelas Krav Maga bersama jurulatih yang layak.","You can also start with <a href=\"../basics/\">self-defence basics</a> for the fence and keeping your distance.":"Anda juga boleh bermula dengan <a href=\"../basics/\">asas pertahanan diri</a> untuk kedudukan pertahanan dan menjaga jarak.","How is Krav Maga different from other martial arts?":"Apakah bezanya Krav Maga dengan seni mempertahankan diri yang lain?","It has no competitions or forms — only real self-defence situations, simple movements and getting out fast.":"Tiada pertandingan atau bentuk. Hanya situasi pertahanan diri sebenar, pergerakan mudah dan keluar dengan pantas.","What do I do if I'm choked from the front?":"Apakah yang perlu saya buat jika dicekik dari depan?","Bring both hands up, hook the thumbs and pluck down and out with your chin tucked, then counter and get away.":"Angkat kedua-dua tangan segera, kaitkan ibu jari, dan tarik ke bawah dan ke luar dengan dagu dirapatkan. Kemudian balas dan beredar.","Does it work for smaller people?":"Adakah ini berkesan untuk orang yang bersaiz lebih kecil?","Krav Maga is designed not to rely on strength — it uses weak points, timing and continuous counters. Still, nothing is guaranteed; leaving is always the first choice.":"Krav Maga direka supaya tidak bergantung pada kekuatan. Ia menggunakan titik lemah, masa yang tepat dan serangan balas berterusan. Namun, tiada apa-apa yang dijamin; meninggalkan situasi sentiasa menjadi pilihan pertama.","Krav Maga":"Krav Maga","SELF-DEFENCE · KRAV MAGA FOR BEGINNERS":"PERTAHANAN DIRI · KRAV MAGA UNTUK PEMULA","Krav Maga Basics: Defend, Counter, Get Away":"Asas Krav Maga: Pertahan, Balas, Beredar","Krav Maga is a self-defence system developed in Israel built on simple, natural movements: defend and counter at the same time, keep going once you fight back, and finish by getting away safely. The grey figure is the attacker; the red ring marks where your counter lands.":"Krav Maga ialah sistem pertahanan diri yang dibangunkan di Israel, berasaskan pergerakan yang ringkas dan semula jadi: pertahan dan balas serentak, teruskan selepas anda membalas, dan akhiri dengan beredar ke tempat selamat. Figura kelabu ialah penyerang; bulatan merah menandakan tempat serangan balas anda mendarat.","If you can avoid it or leave, do. Use only reasonable, necessary force when you cannot get away, and stop and call the police as soon as you are safe. Laws differ from place to place. In training, strike only pads or protective gear — never really hit, choke or kick your partner — and train under a qualified instructor.":"Jika anda boleh mengelak atau beredar, lakukannya. Gunakan hanya daya yang munasabah dan perlu apabila anda tidak dapat beredar, dan berhenti serta hubungi polis sebaik sahaja anda selamat. Undang-undang berbeza mengikut tempat. Semasa latihan, pukul hanya pad atau peralatan pelindung — jangan sekali-kali memukul, mencekik atau menendang rakan anda sebenar-benarnya — dan berlatihlah di bawah jurulatih yang layak.","Core principle":"Prinsip utama","Defend = counter":"Pertahan = balas","At the same time, not one after the other":"Dilakukan serentak, bukan berturut-turut","When to use this move":"Bila hendak menggunakan gerakan ini","Last step of every move":"Langkah terakhir bagi setiap pergerakan","Leave":"Beredar","Scan, then get to safety":"Perhatikan sekeliling, kemudian ke tempat selamat","SIDE · GREY = ATTACKER":"SISI · KELABU = PENYERANG","For education only — not legal advice and no substitute for a real Krav Maga class. In danger, leave and call the police first. When practising with a partner, go slowly, use pads and train under a qualified instructor.":"Untuk tujuan pendidikan sahaja — bukan nasihat undang-undang dan bukan pengganti kelas Krav Maga sebenar. Dalam bahaya, beredar dan hubungi polis dahulu. Apabila berlatih dengan rakan, bergerak perlahan, gunakan pad, dan berlatih di bawah jurulatih yang layak.","Krav Maga Basics: Stance, Defences, Choke Release & Counters — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"Asas Krav Maga: Kedudukan, Pertahanan, Melepaskan Cekikan & Serangan Balas — Panduan Interaktif | KungfuTutor","Learn 8 Krav Maga self-defence basics with animated demos against an attacker: fighting stance, straight-punch burst, inside defence, 360° outside defence, front-choke release, groin kick, knee from the clinch, and breaking away to safety.":"Pelajari 8 asas mempertahankan diri Krav Maga dengan demonstrasi beranimasi terhadap penyerang: kedudukan bertarung, tumbukan lurus pantas, pertahanan dalam, pertahanan luar 360°, melepaskan cekikan depan, tendangan ke bahagian kemaluan, lutut dari kedudukan klinc, dan melepaskan diri ke tempat selamat.","Krav Maga Basics — Defend, Counter, Get Away":"Asas Krav Maga — Pertahan, Balas, Lepaskan Diri","A self-defence system developed in Israel that focuses on simple, instinctive movements: defend and counter at the same time, keep attacking until you can escape, and get away to safety.":"Sistem mempertahankan diri yang dibangunkan di Israel, memberi tumpuan kepada pergerakan yang mudah dan naluriah: mempertahankan diri dan membalas serentak, terus menyerang sehingga boleh melepaskan diri, dan melarikan diri ke tempat selamat.","How do you escape a front choke?":"Bagaimana cara melepaskan diri daripada cekikan depan?","Bring both hands up, hook your fingers over the attacker's thumbs and pluck them down and out while tucking your chin, then counter and get away.":"Angkat kedua-dua tangan, kaitkan jari anda pada ibu jari penyerang dan tarik ke bawah dan ke luar sambil menundukkan dagu, kemudian balas dan larikan diri.","What does retzev mean in Krav Maga?":"Apakah maksud retzev dalam Krav Maga?","Continuous motion: once you have to fight back, you keep moving and striking without pausing until you can escape.":"Pergerakan berterusan: apabila anda terpaksa membalas, teruskan bergerak dan menyerang tanpa henti sehingga boleh melepaskan diri.","Fighting Stance":"Kedudukan Bertarung","When you sense a threat":"Apabila anda merasakan ancaman","Readiness and balance":"Kesediaan dan keseimbangan","SOFT KNEES · LEAN IN · HANDS UP":"LUTUT LEMBUT · CONDONG KE DEPAN · TANGAN ANGKAT","Stand with feet staggered about shoulder-width, knees soft, weight on the balls of the feet and the upper body leaning slightly forward. Hold your hands up in front of your face — open (which looks less aggressive) or closed — with the elbows in and the chin down. From here you can defend, counter or get away at any moment.":"Berdiri dengan kaki diselang-seli kira-kira lebar bahu, lutut lembut, berat badan pada bebola kaki dan badan atas condong sedikit ke depan. Angkat tangan di hadapan muka — terbuka (kelihatan kurang agresif) atau digenggam — dengan siku rapat ke badan dan dagu ditundukkan. Dari sini anda boleh bertahan, membalas atau beredar pada bila-bila masa.","Standing upright with weight on the heels (easy to push over); hands too low; feet on one line; stiffness.":"Berdiri tegak dengan berat badan pada tumit (mudah ditolak jatuh); tangan terlalu rendah; kaki pada satu garisan; badan kaku.","Step from relaxed standing into the stance 10 times, then move forward and back in it for a minute.":"Dari posisi berdiri santai, masuk ke kedudukan bertarung 10 kali, kemudian bergerak ke hadapan dan ke belakang dalam kedudukan itu selama seminit.","Every Krav Maga defence and counter starts from this stance.":"Setiap pertahanan dan balasan dalam Krav Maga bermula daripada kedudukan ini.","Straight-Punch Burst":"Letupan Tumbukan Lurus","When you can't get away and must fight back":"Apabila anda tidak dapat beredar dan terpaksa membalas","Continuous attack":"Serangan berterusan","LEAD · REAR · KEEP MOVING IN · NO PAUSES":"TANGAN DEPAN · TANGAN BELAKANG · TERUS MARA · JANGAN BERHENTI","Krav Maga teaches that once you have to fight back, you keep going: lead punch, rear punch, pressing forward as you strike, so the attacker has no time to recover or hit back — until you can get away safely.":"Krav Maga mengajar bahawa apabila anda terpaksa membalas, anda terus melakukannya: tumbukan lurus tangan depan, tumbukan lurus tangan belakang, sambil menekan ke hadapan ketika memukul, supaya penyerang tiada masa untuk pulih atau membalas — sehingga anda boleh beredar dengan selamat.","Throwing one punch and stopping to look; punching while backing up; pauses between punches; dropping the hands.":"Menumbuk sekali lalu berhenti untuk melihat hasilnya; menumbuk sambil berundur; jeda antara tumbukan; menurunkan tangan.","10 seconds of non-stop punches on pads, 10 seconds rest, 6 rounds, always moving forward.":"10 saat tumbukan tanpa henti pada pad, rehat 10 saat, 6 pusingan, sentiasa bergerak ke hadapan.","This continuous, forward-pressing counter-attack is what Krav Maga calls retzev (\"continuous motion\").":"Serangan balas yang berterusan dan menekan ke hadapan ini dipanggil retzev (“gerakan berterusan”) dalam Krav Maga.","Inside Defence vs Straight Punch":"Pertahanan Dalam menentang Tumbukan Lurus","Their face":"Muka mereka","A straight punch comes at you":"Tumbukan lurus datang ke arah anda","Timing and coordination":"Masa dan koordinasi","LEAD PALM REDIRECTS · REAR HAND PUNCHES AT THE SAME TIME":"TAPAK DEPAN MENGALIH · TUMBUKAN TANGAN BELAKANG SERENTAK","As the straight punch comes, use your lead palm to deflect it to the side from the inside while your body moves slightly off line, and at the same moment fire your rear hand straight into their face. Defence and counter happen together, not one after the other. Then keep striking or get away.":"Apabila tumbukan lurus datang, gunakan tapak tangan depan dari dalam untuk mengalihkannya ke sisi, sambil badan sedikit beralih dari garisan serangan, dan pada masa yang sama lepaskan tumbukan lurus tangan belakang terus ke muka lawan. Pertahanan dan balasan berlaku serentak, bukan satu selepas satu. Kemudian teruskan menyerang atau beredar.","Blocking without countering; a big swatting movement; blocking first and punching after (too slow); closing your eyes.":"Hanya menangkis tanpa membalas; gerakan menepis yang terlalu besar; menangkis dahulu baru menumbuk (terlalu perlahan); memejamkan mata.","Partner throws slow straight punches with gloves; deflect and counter at the same time, 10 each side.":"Rakan melontarkan tumbukan lurus perlahan dengan sarung tangan; alihkan dan balas serentak, 10 kali setiap sisi.","Defending and countering at once is a core Krav Maga principle — it cuts the time you spend on the back foot.":"Mempertahankan dan membalas serentak ialah prinsip teras Krav Maga, yang sangat mengurangkan masa anda berada dalam keadaan bertahan.","360° Outside Defence":"Pertahanan Luar 360°","Swinging or overhead attacks from the side":"Serangan ayunan atau dari atas dari sisi","Reflex and structure":"Refleks dan struktur","FOREARM UP · ELBOW ~90° · COUNTER AT ONCE":"LENGAN BAWAH TEGAK · SIKU ~90° · BALAS SERTA-MERTA","The 360° defence is a family of forearm blocks for curved attacks from any angle — high, side or low. Against a swing from the side, raise the forearm with the elbow bent about 90° so the outside of the forearm meets the attack beside your head, while your other hand punches straight back. The block's height changes with the attack, but the principle stays the same: meet it with the forearm and counter at once.":"Pertahanan 360° ialah keluarga tangkisan lengan bawah untuk serangan melengkung dari mana-mana sudut, tinggi, sisi atau rendah. Terhadap ayunan dari sisi, angkat lengan bawah dengan siku dibengkokkan kira-kira 90° supaya bahagian luar lengan bawah menahan serangan di sebelah kepala, manakala tangan satu lagi terus menumbuk balas. Ketinggian tangkisan berubah mengikut serangan, tetapi prinsipnya sama: sambut dengan lengan bawah dan balas serta-merta.","Blocking with the hand (it gets driven through); the arm too far from the head; blocking without countering; shrinking backwards.":"Menangkis dengan tapak tangan (akan tertembus); lengan terlalu jauh dari kepala; hanya menangkis tanpa membalas; mengecut ke belakang.","Partner swings slowly with a pad from different angles; block with the forearm and counter, 5 reps per angle.":"Rakan mengayunkan pad perlahan dari pelbagai sudut; tangkis dengan lengan bawah dan balas, 5 ulangan setiap sudut.","Real attacks are often big looping swings; the 360° defence lets one principle cover every angle.":"Serangan sebenar selalunya ialah ayunan melengkung yang besar; pertahanan 360° membolehkan satu prinsip meliputi setiap sudut.","Front Choke Release (Pluck)":"Melepaskan Diri daripada Cekikan Depan (Tarik)","Release":"Lepas","Their thumbs → then a knee":"Ibu jari mereka → kemudian lutut","Choked from the front":"Dicekik dari depan","Speed and reaction":"Kelajuan dan reaksi","HOOK THE THUMBS · PLUCK DOWN AND OUT · CHIN DOWN · KNEE":"KAIT IBU JARI · TARIK KE BAWAH DAN KELUAR · DAGU DIRAPATKAN · LUTUT","If someone chokes you from the front with both hands, immediately bring your hands up and hook your fingers over their thumbs from above — the thumbs are the weakest part of the grip — and pluck them down and out hard while tucking your chin and pushing your head slightly forward. As soon as you are free, grab hold and counter with a knee, then shove away, step back and leave.":"Jika seseorang mencekik anda dari depan dengan kedua-dua tangan, segera angkat tangan dan kaitkan jari pada ibu jari mereka — ibu jari ialah bahagian genggaman yang paling lemah — kemudian tarik ke bawah dan ke luar dengan kuat sambil mengecutkan dagu dan menolak kepala sedikit ke depan. Sebaik sahaja bebas, cengkam dan balas dengan lutut, kemudian tolak, undur dan beredar.","Pulling or stepping backwards (it tightens the choke); pulling at the wrists instead of the thumbs; not countering after the release; hesitating.":"Menarik atau mengundur ke belakang (menjadikan cekikan lebih ketat); menarik pergelangan tangan dan bukan ibu jari; tidak membalas selepas bebas; teragak-agak.","Partner rests their hands lightly on your neck (no squeezing); slowly practise hook the thumbs → pluck → knee (no contact), 10 reps.":"Rakan meletakkan tangannya dengan ringan di leher anda (jangan picit); latih perlahan kait ibu jari → tarik → lutut (tanpa sentuhan), 10 ulangan.","A choke leaves you only seconds; this release is simple, fast and needs no strength.":"Apabila dicekik, anda hanya ada beberapa saat; teknik ini mudah, pantas dan tidak memerlukan kekuatan.","Groin Kick":"Tendangan Celah Kelangkang","Groin":"Celah kelangkang","They are a leg's length away":"Mereka berada sepanjang kaki","KNEE UP · SNAP UP · INSTEP OR SHIN · FAST RECOIL":"LUTUT NAIK · HENTAK KE ATAS · KAKI ATAS ATAU TULANG KERING · TARIK PANTAS","From your stance, lift the rear knee and snap the lower leg upward so the instep or shin strikes the groin, then pull the leg back fast and plant it. Step back and leave straight away, or keep countering.":"Dari kedudukan anda, angkat lutut kaki belakang dan hentakkan betis ke atas supaya kaki atas atau tulang kering mengena celah kelangkang, kemudian tarik kaki ke belakang dengan pantas dan letakkannya semula. Undur dan beredar serta-merta, atau teruskan membalas.","Kicking with the toes (they jam); a slow, obvious kick; leaving the leg out; staying put afterwards.":"Menendang dengan hujung jari kaki (jari mudah terseliuh); tendangan yang perlahan dan jelas kelihatan; membiarkan kaki terkeluar; kekal di tempat selepas itu.","On a low-held kick shield, 3 × 10 per leg, fast out and fast back. Never actually kick a training partner there.":"Pada pad tendangan yang dipegang rendah, 3 × 10 setiap kaki, pantas keluar dan pantas kembali. Jangan sekali-kali menendang rakan latihan di situ.","Even a much smaller person can use it to stop an attacker and buy time to get away.":"Walaupun orang yang jauh lebih kecil boleh menggunakannya untuk menghentikan penyerang dan mendapat masa untuk melarikan diri.","Knee from the Clinch":"Lutut dari Klinc","Close-range counter":"Serangan balas jarak dekat","Groin, stomach":"Kemaluan, perut","They are right up against you":"Mereka betul-betul rapat dengan anda","GRAB THE SHOULDERS · PULL DOWN · KNEE UP":"CENGKAM BAHU · TARIK KE BAWAH · LUTUT NAIK","When they are right up against you, grab their shoulders or the back of the neck, pull them down and drive your rear knee up into the groin or stomach at the same time. Repeat if needed, then shove away, step back and leave.":"Apabila mereka betul-betul rapat dengan anda, cengkam bahu atau belakang leher mereka, tarik mereka ke bawah dan serentak naikkan lutut belakang anda ke arah kemaluan atau perut. Ulang jika perlu, kemudian tolak mereka, undur dan beredar.","Lifting the knee without pulling them down; kicking forward instead of driving up; leaning back; hanging on instead of leaving.":"Hanya mengangkat lutut tanpa menarik mereka ke bawah; menendang ke hadapan dan bukannya naik ke atas; condong ke belakang; terus berpaut dan tidak beredar.","3 × 10 per leg on a knee pad or bag; with a partner, light touch or no contact only.":"3 × 10 setiap kaki pada pad lutut atau beg; dengan rakan, hanya sentuhan ringan atau tanpa sentuhan.","When there is no room to punch, the knee is the most natural and powerful counter.":"Apabila tiada ruang untuk menumbuk, lutut ialah serangan balas yang paling semula jadi dan kuat.","Break Away & Scan":"Lepaskan Diri & Imbas","— (leave)":"— (beredar)","After every counter":"Selepas setiap serangan balas","Awareness and judgement":"Kesedaran dan pertimbangan","GUARD UP · BACK AWAY · SCAN · LEAVE AND GET HELP":"SEDIA · UNDUR · IMBAS · BERANGKAT DAN MINTA BANTUAN","Once your counter has stopped them for a moment, don't stay to keep fighting. Keep your guard up, back away to open the distance and turn your head to scan around you — other attackers, weapons, obstacles, the exits. Then move to a safe, busy place, get help and call the police.":"Apabila serangan balas anda telah menghentikan mereka seketika, jangan kekal untuk terus bertarung. Kekalkan sedia, undur untuk memberi jarak dan toleh kepala untuk mengimbas sekeliling: penyerang lain, senjata, halangan, jalan keluar. Kemudian pergi ke tempat yang selamat dan ramai, minta bantuan dan hubungi polis.","Staying to \"finish\" the attacker; turning your back too early; tunnel vision on one person; forgetting to call the police.":"Kekal di situ untuk \"menamatkan\" penyerang; memusingkan badan terlalu awal; hanya fokus pada seorang sahaja; terlupa menelefon polis.","End every drill with three steps back, a scan both ways, and naming the exit out loud.":"Tamatkan setiap latihan dengan berundur tiga langkah, mengimbas ke kiri dan kanan, dan menyebut pintu keluar dengan lantang.","Krav Maga's goal is getting home safe, not winning a fight; scanning and leaving are part of every technique.":"Matlamat Krav Maga ialah pulang dengan selamat, bukan memenangi pergaduhan; mengimbas sekeliling dan beredar ialah sebahagian daripada setiap teknik.","Where everything starts":"Tempat bermula segala-galanya","Ready to defend and strike":"Sedia untuk mempertahan dan menyerang","Non-stop combinations":"Gabungan serangan tanpa henti","Punch while moving forward":"Tumbuk sambil bergerak ke hadapan","Defend and counter at the same time":"Pertahan dan balas serentak","Stops attacks from the outside":"Menahan serangan dari luar","The forearm is the shield":"Lengan bawah ialah perisai","One of the most urgent situations":"Salah satu situasi paling mendesak","Pluck the thumbs, counter at once":"Cabut ibu jari, balas serta-merta","The simplest effective kick":"Tendangan paling mudah dan berkesan","Snaps upward":"Sentakan ke atas","The strongest weapon up close":"Senjata paling kuat dalam jarak dekat","Pull down, drive up":"Tarik ke bawah, tolak ke atas","The last step of every technique":"Langkah terakhir bagi setiap teknik","Is anyone else there?":"Adakah orang lain di situ?","Feet staggered, knees soft, leaning slightly forward":"Kaki berdiri berselang-seli depan dan belakang, lutut lembut, badan condong sedikit ke hadapan","Hands up in front of the face, open or closed":"Tangan diangkat di hadapan muka, terbuka atau dikepal","Chin down, weight on the balls of the feet, ready to move either way":"Dagu ditundukkan, berat badan di bola kaki, sedia bergerak ke mana-mana arah","Fighting stance":"Posisi bertarung","Lead straight punch":"Tumbukan lurus tangan depan","Rear straight punch while you keep moving forward":"Tumbukan lurus tangan belakang sambil terus bergerak ke hadapan","Keep firing without pausing until you have a chance to get away":"Terus menyerang tanpa henti sehingga ada peluang untuk melarikan diri","A straight punch comes in":"Tumbukan lurus datang","The lead palm redirects the punch while the rear hand punches back at the same time":"Telapak tangan depan mengalih tumbukan, manakala tangan belakang membalas dengan tumbukan lurus","Keep countering or break away":"Teruskan membalas atau melepaskan diri","A swinging punch comes from the side":"Tumbukan ayunan datang dari sisi","Raise the forearm to block at the side of the head (elbow about 90°) while the rear hand counters":"Angkat lengan bawah untuk menahan di sisi kepala (siku kira-kira 90°), manakala tangan belakang membalas","Keep striking, then get away":"Terus menyerang, kemudian beredar","They choke you from the front with both hands":"Mereka mencekik leher anda dari depan dengan kedua-dua tangan","Immediately bring both hands up and hook your fingers over their thumbs":"Segera angkat kedua-dua tangan dan kaitkan jari anda pada ibu jari mereka","Pluck them down and out hard, chin tucked, head forward":"Tarik mereka ke bawah dan ke luar dengan kuat, dagu dirapatkan, kepala ke hadapan","Grab hold and counter with a knee":"Cengkam dan balas dengan lutut","Shove away, step back, leave":"Tolak menjauh, undur, pergi","Fighting stance, a leg's length away":"Kedudukan bertarung, sejauh panjang satu kaki","Lift the rear knee":"Angkat lutut kaki belakang","Snap the lower leg up, striking the groin with the instep or shin":"Sentak betis ke atas, serang kawasan pangkal paha dengan batang kaki atau tulang hadapan","Snap the leg back":"Tarik kaki kembali dengan pantas","Plant, step back and leave":"Pijak, undur dan pergi","They are too close":"Mereka terlalu dekat","Grab their shoulders or the back of the neck":"Cengkam bahu mereka atau belakang leher","Pull them down while driving the knee up":"Tarik mereka ke bawah sambil menghayunkan lutut ke atas","Repeat the knee if needed":"Ulang serangan lutut jika perlu","After your counter, they are stopped for a moment":"Selepas balasan anda, mereka terhenti seketika","Keep your guard up and back away":"Kekal berwaspada dan undur menjauh","Turn your head to scan around you: other attackers, weapons, exits":"Toleh kepala untuk memerhati sekeliling: penyerang lain, senjata, jalan keluar","Move to safety, get help and call the police":"Bergerak ke tempat selamat, dapatkan bantuan dan hubungi polis","Readiness":"Kesediaan","Movement":"Pergerakan","Forward pressure":"Tekanan ke hadapan","Reflex":"Refleks","Getting away":"Melepaskan diri","Judgement":"Pertimbangan","Getting help":"Mendapatkan bantuan","Setup (Address)":"Persediaan (Address)","Fundamentals":"Asas","Flat back, soft knees":"Belakang rata, lutut sedikit dibengkokkan","A stable, balanced posture":"Postur yang stabil dan seimbang","HINGE AT THE HIPS · SOFT KNEES · ARMS HANG":"TUNDUK DI PINGGUL · LUTUT LEMBUT · LENGAN MENJUNTAI","Set your feet about shoulder-width apart. Bend forward from the hips (not the waist), pushing your seat back with a flat back and softly bent knees. Let your arms hang straight down from the shoulders to hold the club, with the clubhead just behind the ball. From the front, your upper body tilts slightly away from the target, and your weight is even on both feet.":"Letakkan kaki kira-kira selebar bahu. Tunduk ke hadapan dari pinggul (bukan pinggang), tolak punggung ke belakang dengan belakang rata dan lutut sedikit dibengkokkan. Biarkan lengan menjuntai lurus dari bahu untuk memegang kelab, dengan kepala kelab betul-betul di belakang bola. Dari depan, badan atas condong sedikit menjauhi sasaran, dan berat badan sama rata di kedua kaki.","Rounding the back; bending the knees so much it looks like sitting; standing too far away and reaching for the ball; standing too upright.":"Belakang membongkok; lutut ditekuk terlalu banyak sehingga kelihatan seperti duduk; berdiri terlalu jauh dan mencapai bola; berdiri terlalu tegak.","Hold a club along your spine (touching head, upper back and seat) and hinge to your setup angle 10 times; then check side-on in a mirror.":"Letakkan kayu golf di sepanjang tulang belakang (menyentuh kepala, belakang atas dan punggung bawah), kemudian bongkokkan dari pinggul ke sudut sedia 10 kali; kemudian semak dari sisi di hadapan cermin.","Most swing faults start at setup. The right posture lets the body turn freely and makes the swing repeatable.":"Kebanyakan kesilapan ayunan bermula pada kedudukan sedia. Kedudukan yang betul membolehkan badan berpusing dengan bebas dan ayunan boleh diulang dengan konsisten.","Takeaway":"Takeaway","Swing phase 1":"Fasa ayunan 1","Move together, clubhead low":"Bergerak bersama, kepala kayu kekal rendah","Shoulder-led movement and rhythm":"Pergerakan dipacu bahu dan irama","SHOULDERS LEAD · CLUBHEAD LOW · DON'T RUSH":"BAHU MEMACU · KEPALA KAYU RENDAH · JANGAN TERGESA-GESA","Turn the shoulders, arms and club back together as one piece, keeping the clubhead low to the ground and the wrists quiet. By the time your hands pass your back leg, the shaft is roughly parallel to the ground with the toe of the club pointing up.":"Pusingkan bahu, lengan, dan kayu ke belakang sebagai satu unit, kepala kayu kekal rendah dekat tanah dan pergelangan tangan tenang. Apabila tangan melepasi kaki belakang, batang kayu kira-kira selari dengan tanah dengan hujung kayu menghala ke atas.","Lifting the club with the hands only; hinging the wrists too early; snatching it back too fast; swaying the body away from the target.":"Mengangkat kayu hanya dengan tangan; memusingkan pergelangan tangan terlalu awal; menarik kayu ke belakang terlalu laju; badan bergoyang menjauhi sasaran.","Lay a second club or ruler on the ground behind the ball and let the clubhead track along it for the first foot (30 cm) of the takeaway, 15 times.":"Letakkan kayu kedua atau pembaris di atas tanah di belakang bola dan biarkan kepala kayu mengikutinya sejauh 30 cm pertama semasa takeaway, 15 kali.","The takeaway sets the path and tempo of the whole swing — start it right and the rest follows more easily.":"Takeaway menentukan laluan dan tempo keseluruhan ayunan. Jika permulaannya betul, bahagian seterusnya lebih mudah mengikuti.","Top of the Backswing":"Puncak Backswing","Swing phase 2":"Fasa ayunan 2","Shoulders 90°, back to the target":"Bahu berpusing 90°, belakang menghadap sasaran","Upper-body rotation and flexibility":"Putaran badan atas dan kelenturan","SHOULDERS ~90° · HIPS ~45° · LEAD ARM STRAIGHT":"BAHU ~90° · PINGGUL ~45° · LENGAN DEPAN LURUS","Keep turning until your back faces the target — about 90° of shoulder turn and 45° of hip turn. The wrists hinge naturally, the lead arm stays straight but not stiff, and most of your weight sits on the inside of the back foot. The head stays roughly where it started.":"Teruskan memusing sehingga belakang badan menghadap sasaran, kira-kira 90° pusingan bahu dan 45° pusingan pinggul. Pergelangan tangan melentur secara semula jadi, lengan depan kekal lurus tetapi tidak kaku, dan kebanyakan berat badan berada di bahagian dalam kaki belakang. Kepala kekal lebih kurang di kedudukan asal.","Lifting the arms without turning; bending the lead arm a lot; swaying so the weight goes to the outside of the back foot; overswinging so the club droops.":"Mengangkat lengan tanpa memusing badan; membengkokkan lengan depan terlalu banyak; bergoyang supaya berat badan beralih ke bahagian luar kaki belakang; mengayun berlebihan sehingga kayu melentur ke bawah.","Cross your arms over your chest, turn your back to the target, hold 2 seconds and turn back, 10 times; then do it with a club and pause at the top.":"Silangkan tangan di dada, pusing supaya belakang badan menghadap sasaran, tahan selama 2 saat dan pusing semula, 10 kali; kemudian lakukan dengan kayu dan berhenti di puncak.","The top is where the power is loaded; a full turn gives the downswing room and speed.":"Puncak ialah tempat kuasa dikumpulkan; pusingan penuh memberi ruang dan kelajuan kepada ayunan ke bawah.","Downswing":"Ayunan ke bawah","Swing phase 3":"Fasa ayunan 3","Lower body leads":"Badan bahagian bawah memimpin","Sequencing and explosive power":"Urutan pergerakan dan kuasa letupan","WEIGHT SHIFT · THEN HIPS · THEN ARMS":"ALIH BERAT BADAN · KEMUDIAN PINGGUL · KEMUDIAN LENGAN","The downswing starts from the ground up: shift your weight towards the front foot, then turn the hips towards the target, and let the shoulders and arms follow. As the arms drop, keep the wrist hinge (like cracking a whip) so the stored speed is released just before impact.":"Ayunan ke bawah bermula dari bawah ke atas: alihkan berat badan ke kaki depan, kemudian pusingkan pinggul ke arah sasaran, dan biarkan bahu serta lengan mengikut. Apabila lengan jatuh, kekalkan lenturan pergelangan (seperti merotan), supaya kelajuan yang tersimpan dilepaskan hampir dengan hentaman.","Starting with the hands and shoulders (an over-the-top, slicing path); releasing the wrists too early (\"casting\"); leaving the weight on the back foot.":"Memulakan dengan tangan dan bahu (laluan melibas dari luar ke dalam); melepaskan pergelangan terlalu awal (\"casting\"); membiarkan berat badan kekal di kaki belakang.","Pause at the top for a second, then \"step\" into the front foot before swinging down — 15 slow reps, feeling the hips pull the arms.":"Tahan di puncak selama 1 saat, kemudian \"pijak\" ke kaki depan sebelum melibas ke bawah; lakukan 15 ulangan perlahan, rasakan pinggul menarik lengan.","The right order adds speed link by link until it peaks in the clubhead — why good players look effortless yet hit it far.":"Susunan yang betul menambah kelajuan mata rantai demi mata rantai sehingga memuncak di kepala kelab — itulah sebab pemain handal kelihatan tidak bersusah payah tetapi memukul jauh.","Impact":"Hentaman","Swing phase 4":"Fasa ayunan 4","Hands ahead, weight forward":"Tangan di hadapan, berat ke hadapan","Strike quality":"Kualiti pukulan","HANDS AHEAD · WEIGHT FORWARD · HEAD BEHIND THE BALL":"TANGAN DI HADAPAN · BERAT KE HADAPAN · KEPALA DI BELAKANG BOLA","At impact your hands are slightly ahead of the ball (towards the target) with the shaft leaning forward, roughly 70–80% of your weight is on the front foot, the hips have opened towards the target, and the head is still behind the ball. With irons you strike the ball first, then brush the turf.":"Pada saat hentaman, tangan anda sedikit di hadapan bola (ke arah sasaran) dengan batang kelab condong ke hadapan, kira-kira 70–80% berat badan di kaki hadapan, pinggul telah terbuka ke arah sasaran, dan kepala masih di belakang bola. Dengan besi, anda memukul bola dahulu, kemudian menyapu rumput.","Trying to scoop the ball into the air (flipping the wrists, hands behind the ball); falling back onto the back foot; looking up early to see where it went.":"Cuba menyauk bola ke udara (memusingkan pergelangan, tangan di belakang bola); jatuh ke kaki belakang; mendongak awal untuk melihat ke mana bola pergi.","Put a coin or towel 10 cm in front of the ball and make the club brush that spot after the ball — 20 slow half-swings.":"Letakkan duit syiling atau tuala 10 cm di hadapan bola dan biarkan kelab menyapu titik itu selepas bola — 20 ayunan separuh perlahan.","Everything else in the swing exists to get this instant right; a solid impact position sends the ball straight and solid.":"Setiap bahagian lain dalam ayunan wujud untuk memastikan saat ini betul; kedudukan hentaman yang kukuh menghantar bola lurus dan mantap.","Follow-through & Finish":"Susulan & Penamatan","Swing phase 5":"Fasa ayunan 5","Face the target, hold it":"Hadap sasaran, kekalkan","Balance and a full turn":"Keseimbangan dan pusingan penuh","CHEST TO TARGET · WEIGHT ON FRONT FOOT · BACK TOE DOWN":"DADA MENGHADAP SASARAN · BERAT DI KAKI HADAPAN · HUJUNG KAKI BELAKANG TURUN","After impact let the arms and club extend towards the target and keep turning until your chest and belt buckle face it. In the finish nearly all your weight is on the front foot, the back foot is up on its toe, the club wraps over your shoulder, and you are balanced and still.":"Selepas hentaman, biarkan lengan dan kelab memanjang ke arah sasaran dan teruskan berpusing sehingga dada dan gesper tali pinggang menghadap sasaran. Pada penamatan, hampir semua berat di kaki hadapan, kaki belakang terangkat di hujung jari, kelab melingkari bahu, dan anda seimbang serta tenang.","Stopping at the ball with no follow-through; falling backwards; leaving the back foot flat; wobbling at the finish.":"Berhenti di bola tanpa meneruskan ayunan; jatuh ke belakang; kaki belakang rata di tanah; goyah ketika finish.","After every swing hold your finish for 3 seconds like posing for a photo; if you can't, you are swinging too hard.":"Selepas setiap ayunan, tahan kedudukan finish selama 3 saat seperti bergambar; jika tidak mampu, bermakna anda mengayun terlalu kuat.","The finish is the result of the whole swing: holding it means your weight shift and turn were complete.":"Finish ialah hasil keseluruhan ayunan: dapat menahannya bermakna peralihan berat dan pusingan anda telah lengkap.","Full Swing (Iron)":"Ayunan penuh (iron)","Full swing":"Ayunan penuh","Tempo 3 : 1":"Tempo 3 : 1","Tempo and flow":"Tempo dan aliran","TEMPO: BACKSWING 3 : DOWNSWING 1":"TEMPO: AYUNAN KE BELAKANG 3 : AYUNAN KE BAWAH 1","Join setup, takeaway, top, downswing, impact and finish into one smooth motion. Most good players swing with a tempo of about 3 : 1 — roughly 0.75 s back and 0.25 s down. Switch to \"Real tempo\" to see it at true speed.":"Gabungkan kedudukan sedia, permulaan ayunan, puncak, ayunan ke bawah, hentaman dan finish menjadi satu gerakan yang lancar. Kebanyakan pemain yang baik mengayun dengan tempo kira-kira 3 : 1 — lebih kurang 0.75 saat ke belakang dan 0.25 saat ke bawah. Tukar kepada “Tempo sebenar” untuk melihatnya pada kelajuan sebenar.","Rushing the backswing; hurrying from the top; gripping and tensing everything (tension slows you down); swinging in separate jerky pieces.":"Tergesa-gesa semasa ayunan ke belakang; cepat-cepat dari puncak; menggenggam dan menegangkan segalanya (ketegangan memperlahankan anda); mengayun dalam bahagian terpisah yang tersentak-sentak.","Count \"one-two-three\" going back and \"hit\" coming down, or use a metronome app. Start with a 7-iron and half swings.":"Kira “satu-dua-tiga” ketika ke belakang dan “pukul” ketika ke bawah, atau gunakan aplikasi metronom. Mulakan dengan iron 7 dan ayunan separuh.","Irons are the clubs you use most to hit greens; a steady tempo beats raw strength for good shots.":"Iron ialah kelab yang paling kerap digunakan untuk memukul ke green; tempo yang stabil lebih baik daripada kekuatan semata-mata untuk pukulan yang baik.","Driver Swing":"Ayunan driver","Ball off the front heel, sweep up":"Bola di tepi tumit hadapan, sapu ke atas","Speed and an upward strike":"Kelajuan dan pukulan ke atas","WIDER STANCE · BALL OFF FRONT HEEL · TILT BACK A LITTLE":"KEDUDUKAN LEBIH LEBAR · BOLA DI TUMIT HADAPAN · CONDONGKAN BADAN SEDIKIT KE BELAKANG","With the driver the ball sits on a tee opposite the inside of your front heel; stand a little wider than for an iron and tilt the upper body a bit more away from the target. The swing is the same, but you meet the ball just after the club bottoms out, on the way up — sweep it, don't hit down.":"Dengan driver, bola diletakkan di atas tee sejajar dengan bahagian dalam tumit kaki depan; berdiri sedikit lebih luas daripada iron dan condongkan badan atas lebih jauh daripada sasaran. Ayunannya sama, tetapi anda memukul bola sejurus selepas kepala kelab mencapai titik terendah, semasa ia naik. Sapu bola, jangan pukul ke bawah.","Ball too far back; chopping down like an iron; swinging out of your shoes for distance; lunging the head towards the target.":"Bola terlalu ke belakang; menetak ke bawah seperti iron; mengayun sekuat tenaga untuk jarak sehingga hilang keseimbangan; kepala meluru ke arah sasaran.","Tee the ball a little higher and practise sweeping the ball off without hitting the tee; swing at 80% and hold your finish.":"Pasang tee sedikit lebih tinggi dan latih menyapu bola tanpa mengenai tee; ayun pada 80% kuasa dan tahan kedudukan akhir anda.","The driver is usually your first shot on long holes, aiming for distance and the fairway.":"Driver biasanya pukulan pertama anda pada lubang panjang, bermatlamat untuk jarak jauh dan kekal di fairway.","Chip Shot":"Chip Shot","Short game":"Permainan pendek","Weight forward, hands ahead":"Berat badan ke depan, tangan di hadapan bola","NARROW STANCE · WEIGHT FORWARD · SMALL PENDULUM":"KEDUDUKAN SEMPIT · BERAT KE HADAPAN · AYUNAN KECIL","Stand with a narrow stance, ball slightly back of centre and 60–70% of your weight on the front foot — and keep it there. With quiet wrists, rock the shoulders in a small pendulum: short back, brush down through the ball with the hands ahead. The ball flies low for a short way, lands and rolls to the hole.":"Berdiri dengan kedudukan sempit, bola sedikit di belakang tengah, dan 60–70% berat badan pada kaki depan, dan kekalkannya di situ. Dengan pergelangan tangan yang tenang, goyangkan bahu dalam ayunan kecil: ayunan ke belakang pendek, sapu ke bawah melalui bola dengan tangan di hadapan. Bola terbang rendah untuk jarak pendek, mendarat, dan bergolek ke lubang.","Trying to scoop it up; shifting weight back; a big backswing that decelerates; flicking the wrists.":"Cuba mengangkat bola; berat badan beralih ke belakang; ayunan ke belakang terlalu besar dan perlahan semasa turun; pergelangan tangan dipusing.","Lay a towel on the green as a landing spot and land 10 balls on it from different distances, letting them roll out.":"Letakkan tuala di tepi green sebagai titik mendarat dan mendaratkan 10 bola di atasnya dari jarak berbeza, biarkan bola bergolek keluar.","Most strokes are played near the green; a reliable chip saves more shots than anything else.":"Kebanyakan pukulan dimainkan berhampiran green; chip yang boleh dipercayai menjimatkan lebih banyak pukulan daripada apa-apa lain.","Putting Stroke":"Pukulan Putt","Shoulders rock, head still":"Bahu berayun, kepala tidak bergerak","Line and pace control":"Kawalan arah dan kelajuan","EYES OVER THE BALL · ROCK THE SHOULDERS · EVEN BACK AND THROUGH":"MATA DI ATAS BOLA · GOYANG BAHU · BELAKANG DAN HADAPAN SAMA RATA","Set your eyes directly over the ball, let the arms hang and keep the wrists still. Rock the shoulders like a pendulum while the body and head stay quiet. Make the follow-through about as long as the backstroke, at a smooth even pace, and let the ball roll.":"Letakkan mata betul-betul di atas bola, biarkan lengan jatuh santai dan kekalkan pergelangan tangan tetap. Goyangkan bahu seperti bandul manakala badan dan kepala kekal senyap. Buat susulan ayunan kira-kira sepanjang ayunan ke belakang, dengan rentak yang licin dan sekata, dan biarkan bola bergolek.","Flicking with the wrists; looking up straight away; a long backstroke that slows down; swaying the body.":"Menyentak dengan pergelangan tangan; terus mendongak; ayunan ke belakang panjang yang diperlahankan; badan bergoyang.","Start at 1 m and hole 10 in a row before moving to 2 m; for long putts, practise stopping the ball within half a metre of the hole.":"Mulakan pada jarak 1 m dan masukkan 10 bola berturut-turut sebelum beralih ke 2 m; untuk putt jarak jauh, latih bola berhenti dalam setengah meter dari lubang.","Putts are around 40% of an amateur's strokes; a steady putting stroke lowers scores fastest.":"Putt merupakan kira-kira 40% pukulan pemain amatur; ayunan putt yang stabil paling cepat menurunkan skor.","A good swing starts here":"Ayunan yang baik bermula di sini","Side view for posture · front view for width":"Pandangan sisi untuk postur · pandangan depan untuk lebar","The first move of the swing":"Gerakan pertama ayunan","Low, slow, together":"Rendah, perlahan, bersatu","Where the power is stored":"Tempat tenaga disimpan","Turn, don't lift":"Pusing, jangan angkat","Ground-up sequence":"Urutan dari bawah ke atas","Keep the wrist hinge":"Kekalkan sudut pergelangan tangan","The moment that matters most":"Saat paling penting dalam ayunan","Ball first, then the ground":"Bola dahulu, kemudian tanah","A good finish shows a good swing":"Penamat yang baik menandakan ayunan yang baik","Hold it for 3 seconds":"Tahan selama 3 saat","All five phases joined up":"Gabungkan kelima-lima fasa","Slow back, fast through":"Ayunan naik perlahan, turun laju","The longest club in the bag":"Kayu terpanjang dalam beg","Wider stance, ball forward":"Berdiri lebih lebar, bola di hadapan","The small shot near the green":"Pukulan kecil berhampiran green","Fly it low, let it roll":"Terbangkan rendah, biarkan bergolek","Rolling the ball on the green":"Menggolekkan bola di green","Half your strokes happen here":"Separuh pukulan berlaku di sini","Stand tall, feet together, club behind the ball":"Berdiri tegak, kaki rapat, kayu di belakang bola","Feet about shoulder-width, upper body tilted slightly away from the target":"Kaki kira-kira selebar bahu, badan atas condong sedikit menjauhi sasaran","Setup position":"Kedudukan sedia","Shoulders, arms and club move back together; the clubhead stays low":"Bahu, lengan dan kayu bergerak ke belakang bersama; kepala kayu kekal rendah","Wrists hinge; the club points up to the sky":"Pergelangan tangan melentur; kelab menghala ke langit","Top: back to the target, shoulders turned about 90°":"Puncak: belakang menghadap sasaran, bahu berpusing kira-kira 90°","Top of the backswing":"Puncak ayunan ke belakang","Lower body starts first: weight shifts to the front foot":"Badan bawah bergerak dahulu: berat beralih ke kaki depan","Arms drop with the wrists still hinged — stored power":"Lengan turun dengan pergelangan kekal melentur (simpan tenaga)","Impact: hands ahead of the ball, weight on the front foot":"Hentaman: tangan di hadapan bola, berat di kaki depan","Follow-through: arms extend towards the target":"Susulan: lengan lurus ke arah sasaran","Finish: chest facing the target, balanced on the front foot, back toe on the ground":"Penamat: dada menghadap sasaran, seimbang di kaki depan, hujung kaki belakang mencecah tanah","Setup":"Kedudukan sedia","Top (about 0.75 s)":"Puncak (kira-kira 0.75 saat)","Downswing (about 0.25 s)":"Ayunan turun (kira-kira 0.25 saat)","Balanced finish":"Penamat yang seimbang","Ball slightly back, weight leaning on the front foot":"Bola sedikit di belakang tengah, berat condong ke kaki depan","Small pendulum backswing, wrists barely hinge":"Ayunan kecil seperti bandul ke belakang, pergelangan hampir tidak melentur","Brush down through the ball, hands staying ahead":"Sapu ke bawah melepasi bola, tangan kekal di hadapan bola","Short finish — the ball pops up, lands and rolls":"Penamat pendek: bola melantun ringan, mendarat dan bergolek","Eyes over the ball, arms hanging naturally":"Mata betul-betul di atas bola, lengan terjuntai semula jadi","Rock the shoulders back like a pendulum":"Goyangkan bahu ke belakang seperti bandul","Body still, smooth even pace through the ball":"Badan kekal diam, lepasi bola pada kelajuan sekata","Follow through as far as you swung back; keep the head still":"Teruskan ayunan sejauh ayunan ke belakang; kepala kekal diam","Stand tall holding the club out in front":"Berdiri tegak, pegang kelab di hadapan badan","Hinge forward from the hips, push the seat back, soften the knees, keep the back flat":"Bongkok dari pinggul, tolak punggung ke belakang, lenturkan lutut sedikit, kekalkan belakang lurus","Arms hang straight down from the shoulders; club rests behind the ball":"Lengan terjuntai dari bahu; kepala kelab di belakang bola","RED LINE = SPINE ANGLE (KEEP IT FLAT)":"GARIS MERAH = SUDUT TULANG BELAKANG (KEKALKAN LURUS)","GREEN RING = KEEP THE HEAD STEADY":"BULATAN HIJAU = KEKALKAN KEPALA STABIL","Distance from the ball":"Jarak dari bola","Alignment":"Penjajaran","Shoulder turn":"Putaran bahu","Tempo":"Tempo","Club path":"Laluan kepala kelab","Quiet wrists":"Pergelangan tenang","Weight control":"Kawalan berat badan","Weight shift":"Peralihan berat badan","Wrist lag":"Tenaga tertangguh di pergelangan","Sequencing":"Urutan pergerakan","Impact position":"Kedudukan hentaman","Weight forward":"Berat di hadapan","Wrist position":"Kedudukan pergelangan","Steady head":"Kepala stabil","Full rotation":"Putaran penuh","Club speed":"Kelajuan kelab","Upward strike":"Pukulan ke atas","Stance width":"Lebar kedudukan","Line":"Garisan","Pace":"Tenaga","Stillness":"Ketenangan badan","7-iron":"7-iron","Driver":"Driver","Wedge":"Wedge","Putter":"Putter","Learning (3× slower)":"Pembelajaran (3× lebih perlahan)","Real tempo":"Tempo sebenar","Lesson {n} of 10 · {type} · {club}":"Pelajaran {n} daripada 10 · {type} · {club}","First, the grip":"Pertama, genggamannya","For a right-handed golfer: the left hand goes on first, with the grip running diagonally across the base of the fingers; looking down you should see 2–3 knuckles. The right hand goes below it, palm facing the target, covering the left thumb. The overlap, interlock and ten-finger grips all work — pick the most comfortable. Grip pressure should be about 4–5 out of 10; squeezing tight locks up the arms and slows the club.":"Untuk pemain golf tangan kanan: tangan kiri diletakkan dahulu, dengan pegangan melintang secara serong di pangkal jari; apabila melihat ke bawah, anda sepatutnya nampak 2–3 buku jari. Tangan kanan diletakkan di bawahnya, tapak tangan menghadap sasaran, menutupi ibu jari kiri. Pegangan bertindih, berkunci dan sepuluh jari semuanya boleh digunakan, pilih yang paling selesa. Tekanan genggaman sebaiknya kira-kira 4–5 daripada 10; menggenggam terlalu ketat menyebabkan tangan kaku dan kayu bergerak perlahan.","Club":"Kayu","Where should the ball go?":"Di mana bola sepatutnya diletakkan?","Mid and short irons: middle of the stance or slightly forward.":"Iron tengah dan pendek: di tengah kedudukan berdiri atau sedikit ke hadapan.","Driver: opposite the inside of the front heel, on a tee.":"Driver: sejajar dengan bahagian dalam tumit depan, di atas tee.","Chip: slightly back of centre so the hands are naturally ahead.":"Chip: sedikit di belakang tengah supaya tangan secara semula jadi berada di hadapan.","Putt: slightly forward of centre, eyes directly over the ball.":"Putt: sedikit di hadapan tengah, mata tepat di atas bola.","Two ways to watch a swing":"Dua cara memerhati ayunan","Coaches watch a swing from two angles: face-on (in front of the golfer) for weight shift, head position and the swing arc, and down the line (behind the golfer, looking at the target) for posture and swing plane. Filming yourself from both angles on your phone and comparing with these animations is the cheapest, most effective practice there is.":"Jurulatih memerhati ayunan dari dua sudut: dari depan (di hadapan pemain golf) untuk peralihan berat badan, kedudukan kepala dan lengkung ayunan, dan dari belakang garisan bola (di belakang pemain golf, memandang sasaran) untuk postur dan satah ayunan. Merakam diri sendiri dari kedua-dua sudut menggunakan telefon dan membandingkannya dengan animasi ini ialah latihan paling murah dan berkesan.","Safety and warm-up":"Keselamatan dan regangan awal","Always check nobody is nearby or in front before you swing.":"Sentiasa pastikan tiada sesiapa berhampiran atau di hadapan sebelum mengayun.","Warm up shoulders, hips and back with gentle turns, then start with short clubs and half swings.":"Panaskan bahu, pinggul dan belakang badan dengan pusingan perlahan, kemudian mulakan dengan kayu pendek dan ayunan separuh.","If your back or elbows hurt when you swing, stop and get it checked by a coach or doctor.":"Jika belakang badan atau siku sakit semasa mengayun, berhenti dan dapatkan pemeriksaan daripada jurulatih atau doktor.","Why does my ball curve to the right (a slice)?":"Mengapa bola saya melengkung ke kanan (slice)?","Most often the hands and shoulders start the downswing, so the club cuts across the ball from outside to in with an open face. Practise the lower-body-first sequence (lesson 4) and check your grip isn't too weak.":"Punca yang paling kerap ialah tangan dan bahu bergerak dahulu semasa ayunan turun, menyebabkan kepala kelab memotong bola dari luar ke dalam dengan muka kelab terbuka. Latih urutan \"badan bawah dahulu\" (pelajaran 4) dan pastikan genggaman anda tidak terlalu lemah.","How fast should I swing?":"Seberapa pantas saya patut mengayun?","Ratio matters more than speed: the backswing takes about three times as long as the downswing. Swinging at 80% and holding your finish usually gives the best results.":"Nisbah lebih penting daripada kelajuan: ayunan ke belakang mengambil masa kira-kira tiga kali ganda ayunan ke bawah. Mengayun pada 80% tenaga dan menahan penamat biasanya memberi hasil terbaik.","Does my head really have to stay perfectly still?":"Adakah kepala saya benar-benar perlu kekal sepenuhnya tidak bergerak?","Not perfectly — it moves a little as the body turns. The key is no big sway or bob, and keeping the head behind the ball until impact.":"Tidak perlu sepenuhnya diam. Kepala akan bergerak sedikit apabila badan berpusing. Perkara penting ialah tidak banyak bergoyang ke sisi atau naik turun, dan mengekalkan kepala di belakang bola sehingga hentaman.","SPORTS SKILLS · GOLF FOR BEGINNERS":"KEMAHIRAN SUKAN · GOLF UNTUK PEMULA","The Golf Swing, Step by Step: Setup to Finish":"Ayunan Golf, Langkah demi Langkah: Dari Kedudukan hingga Penamat","The swing broken into six positions — setup, takeaway, top, downswing, impact and finish — then the full iron and driver swings, the chip and the putt. The face-on view (target to the right) shows the swing arc best; the green trail follows the clubhead and the green ring reminds you to keep your head steady. Left-handed? Press L-HAND.":"Ayunan dibahagikan kepada enam kedudukan: persediaan, permulaan ayunan, puncak, ayunan ke bawah, hentaman, dan penamat. Kemudian ayunan penuh dengan iron dan driver, chip, serta putt. Pandangan dari depan (sasaran di sebelah kanan) paling jelas menunjukkan lengkung ayunan. Laluan hijau mengikut kepala kelab, dan cincin hijau mengingatkan anda untuk mengekalkan kepala stabil. Kidal? Tekan TANGAN KIRI.","Swing positions":"Kedudukan ayunan","Setup → takeaway → top → down → impact → finish":"Persediaan → permulaan → puncak → turun → hentaman → penamat","Ideal tempo":"Tempo ideal","About 0.75 s back · 0.25 s down":"Kira-kira 0.75 s naik · 0.25 s turun","Learning · 3× slower":"Pembelajaran · 3× lebih perlahan","Practice drill":"Latihan","Why it matters":"Mengapa ini penting","SIDE":"SISI","R-HAND":"TANGAN KANAN","L-HAND":"TANGAN KIRI","For education only; the animations are simplified. Every body is different — a qualified golf coach can check your swing. Warm up first, and always check nobody is near you before you swing.":"Untuk tujuan pendidikan sahaja; animasi telah dipermudah. Setiap badan adalah berbeza — seorang jurulatih golf yang bertauliah boleh menyemak ayunan anda. Lakukan pemanasan dahulu, dan sentiasa pastikan tiada sesiapa berdekatan sebelum mengayun.","Golf Swing Basics: Setup, Backswing, Impact & Finish — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"Asas Ayunan Golf: Kedudukan, Ayunan Belakang, Hentaman & Penamat — Panduan Interaktif | KungfuTutor","Learn the golf swing step by step with animation: setup posture, takeaway, top of the backswing, downswing, impact and finish, plus the full iron swing, driver, chip shot and putting stroke. Includes tempo, common mistakes and drills.":"Pelajari ayunan golf langkah demi langkah dengan animasi: postur berdiri, gerakan awal (takeaway), puncak ayunan belakang, ayunan bawah, hentaman dan penamat, serta ayunan iron penuh, driver, chip shot dan pukulan putt. Termasuk tempo, kesilapan biasa dan latihan.","Golf Swing Basics — Interactive Step-by-Step Guide":"Asas Ayunan Golf — Panduan Interaktif Langkah demi Langkah","What are the main phases of the golf swing?":"Apakah fasa utama dalam ayunan golf?","Setup (address), takeaway, top of the backswing, downswing, impact and follow-through to a balanced finish.":"Kedudukan awal (address), gerakan awal (takeaway), puncak ayunan belakang, ayunan bawah, hentaman, dan susulan sehingga penamat yang seimbang.","What is a good golf swing tempo?":"Bagaimanakah tempo ayunan golf yang baik?","Many good players swing with roughly a 3 to 1 ratio: the backswing takes about three times as long as the downswing, for example about 0.75 seconds back and 0.25 seconds down.":"Ramai pemain baik mengayun dengan nisbah lebih kurang 3 berbanding 1: ayunan belakang mengambil masa kira-kira tiga kali ganda ayunan bawah, contohnya kira-kira 0.75 saat ke belakang dan 0.25 saat ke bawah.","Where should the ball be in my stance?":"Di manakah bola sepatutnya berada dalam kedudukan berdiri saya?","For a mid-iron, about the middle of the stance or slightly forward; for the driver, opposite the inside of the front heel; for a chip, slightly back of centre.":"Untuk iron tengah, lebih kurang di tengah kedudukan atau sedikit ke hadapan; untuk driver, sejajar dengan bahagian dalam tumit kaki depan; untuk chip, sedikit ke belakang daripada tengah."};
